insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'question', 'Two years non-union in Somerset. Too late to try for the UA apprenticeship?', 'Sorry if this has been asked a hundred times. I posted a while back about making $21 an hour near Manville. I did ask for the review. I got fifty cents and a "we''ll see in the spring."

I like the work and the guys, but I keep thinking about the union apprenticeship. I''m two years in. Would I be starting over at zero? Is there any credit for time already worked, or do they not care? I''d also be risking a paycheck I count on for something I might not get.

Not trying to trash my shop, they''ve been fair in other ways. I just want to know if this is a smart move or a step backward.', 'plumbing', 'Somerset County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-27T13:53:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('d92658e4-e046-5505-8409-5996123426d1', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'call local 9 and ask how they treat prior experience. nobody on here can tell you that for sure.', false, 2, '2026-09-27T14:31:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('27b25573-9451-5e15-9b17-e73ef036dd67', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Not a step backward. Different trade from mine, so take this as general.

Time you''ve already worked counts for something in the interview, because you can talk about real jobs. Whether it shortens the apprenticeship itself is a question for that program, not for me. Some programs have a way to evaluate prior experience and some don''t, and those rules change.

What I''d do: apply while you keep the paycheck. Filling out an application doesn''t require quitting anything. If you get called, then you decide. Stay safe.', true, 14, '2026-09-28T00:55:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f74711f3-ec1f-56b5-ab63-079913aad32d', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'I''ll give you the other side. I went union for a few years and then came back to my father''s shop. The benefits were real and the school was better than anything I got on the job. What I didn''t like was having no say in where I went.

My father used to say a man who takes the first offer never learns what he''s worth. Ask the union your questions, ask your shop what their plan for you is, then compare.', false, 4, '2026-09-28T03:18:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7a48e91b-8643-55c0-b59d-7ce9a6b17317', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'brother you''re 2 years in and they gave you 50 cents. apply. worst case they say no and you still have the job', false, 2, '2026-09-28T03:44:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('026ad6f0-ae8e-5762-b0ba-18530edb91c1', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly 50 cents after two years would bug me too. But don''t hear ''we''ll see'' as a no, small shops get squeezed in the fall. Ask him straight what you''d need to show by spring to get a real bump. If he can''t answer, that''s your answer.', false, 3, '2026-09-28T23:11:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fe099c00-486a-5a9f-9663-1ea87a25d9f3', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I look for when I hire, from the other side of the table: someone two years in who can explain what they did on a job, start to finish. That''s worth more than a certificate. Union or not, keep a record of your work with dates and who supervised you. Whoever you talk to next will ask.', false, 13, '2026-09-29T00:26:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('826707c3-5493-5ca2-81c0-74fc0439c9ef', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, the guys who regret it are the ones who never applied. A form costs you nothing. Keep showing up to the shop until somebody hands you something better. That''s the job.', false, 5, '2026-09-29T02:08:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('deb7fec5-bf9b-5330-9e99-e5e5cc2e7321', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', '26c7eeb4-1f62-5c0a-932b-3cd4f82d559b', 'Local 456, 3rd year, different trade, but I did a year non-union in Linden first. My interview went way better because I actually knew what a box was. Grabbed a Wawa coffee on the way and almost spilled it on my paperwork lol.', false, 2, '2026-09-29T03:02:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e4e5458b-fc25-5963-a94c-9ecbcbd3c6fd', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', '31e0974e-aadd-529c-90fc-0385fc7c46a5', 'saw your raise thread. fifty cents is rough. idk about plumbing but the hvac guys I know who switched said the first year pay hurt and then it didn''t', false, 2, '2026-09-29T09:04:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a003234b-a82b-53fe-9543-d3e761aafd5a', '4adb9733-63cd-5819-ae36-db860dcdfb49', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Thank you all, this is more than I expected. I''m going to call Local 9 this week and ask how prior experience works before I do anything else.

edit: called and left a message, waiting on a callback. Started writing down my last two years of jobs from my phone calendar in the meantime.', false, 1, '2026-09-29T10:16:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'question', 'My shop teacher won''t stop pushing the union application. Why is he so sure?', 'Some context first because it matters. I''m in the electrical program at the Mercer County vo-tech, I''ve been doing weekend helper stuff for a guy in Hamilton since June (mostly carrying, some pulling wire), and my shop teacher brings up the IBEW application basically every class. Like every single class. He hands out the flyer, he talks about the pension, he tells us non-union is a dead end.

The guy I work weekends for is non-union and he''s doing fine. Owns two vans, takes his family to Wildwood every August.

So who''s right? I''m not against the union. I just don''t like being told there''s one answer when I can see with my own eyes there''s at least two.', 'electrical', 'Mercer County, NJ', 28, '2026-08-28T22:00:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('db880f85-553f-54c1-a1f3-9e5d7c1d01b3', 'c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Your teacher has probably watched what the apprenticeship did for students before you, and that''s a fair reason to push it. Structured school, a wage scale that steps up on a schedule, benefits, safety training built in. Those are real.

"Dead end" is too strong, though. Plenty of non-union electricians do well, and your weekend guy is proof. The honest version: the union path is a known path, and a good non-union shop can also be a good path. Apply, keep working weekends, and decide with real offers in front of you. Stay safe.', true, 11, '2026-08-29T12:26:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a2c76995-621a-54ec-86fa-8c76bce48a6a', 'c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly I''m the non-union guy your teacher is warning you about. Own my shop in Long Branch, went to trade school, did fine. But I''ll admit the union guys my age have a pension I don''t. Both things are true. Don''t let either side tell you the other one''s a scam.', false, 4, '2026-08-29T13:58:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1901b815-f9cd-5a15-89bd-33be87d871dc', 'c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', '76ffb6b2-6ae2-5434-982e-39a1a1bf28b2', 'Former teacher here (middle school, not shop). Teachers push the thing they''ve watched work for their students. Doesn''t make it the only thing, but he''s not trying to scam you. Sorry, I know that''s not a real answer.', false, 2, '2026-08-29T15:48:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('65c161fe-e92c-596a-a804-9e3f678f87ab', 'c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', '> he''s not trying to scam you

Fair. I didn''t mean he''s scamming anybody. It''s the "dead end" thing that gets me, because my weekend guy clearly isn''t one.', false, 2, '2026-08-29T22:34:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ea6d582c-6f82-559b-8357-13ddff1210b0', 'c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'I left the union and I half regret it, so take that for what it is. What I miss most is the training. What I don''t miss is sitting by the phone between jobs some years. My father used to say every road has tolls, you just have to know which ones you''re paying.', false, 8, '2026-08-30T03:24:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2e328d8b-b4f1-56a7-a44a-64de47766d37', 'c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I look for when I hire a kid out of vo-tech: shows up, has some hours, can pass a background check. Whether he applied to the union doesn''t come into it. If you end up non-union, ask about school and how raises work before you take the job.', false, 7, '2026-08-30T14:12:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('55d9b2ca-ef57-5892-af35-92f51cd3d6cb', 'c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'Same thing at my school in Queens, except it''s Local 3 every class. The foreman at my weekend job says the same thing yours does.', false, 2, '2026-08-30T14:38:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('286b83d4-63ae-5130-a9b6-6d49f649bfd9', 'c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'non-union in manahawkin, 1 year. i put in for 400 anyway just to see what happens. no harm in having options', false, 2, '2026-08-30T16:44:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a36277ec-f79a-59f8-8aef-7d8be91dca43', 'c9493779-0378-5184-b870-6c476d053a55', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', '4th year in 164... your teacher isn''t wrong and neither is your weekend guy. my foreman says some of the best apprentices he gets came from shops like that... apply and keep the weekend job', false, 2, '2026-08-30T17:28:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'question', 'Cousin in Gloucester County asked me union vs school vs shop. I only know how it works in the city', 'So my cousin is 18, lives in Williamstown, just finished high school and wants to do plumbing. He asked me what to do because I''m the "plumber" in the family now lol.

Problem is I''m a first year in Local 1 in Brooklyn and everything I know is how it works in the city. I told him apply to the union and he asked which one, and I realized I have no idea what covers South Jersey. Also no idea if the county vo-tech down there does adult programs or if he should just call shops. I''d drive down the Turnpike and walk him around myself but I''m on at 6 every day.

Help me not give my cousin bad advice. He''s a good kid, works at a Wawa on the Black Horse Pike right now and hates it.', 'plumbing', 'Brooklyn, NY', 21, '2026-09-21T01:11:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('8361677b-63e6-5f7f-9d7e-4ceabcc4e613', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I''d tell him, from Burlington County. There''s a UA local that covers South Jersey. I believe it''s 322, but have him look it up and confirm; don''t go off a contractor''s memory.

Separately, plenty of shops down here hire helpers straight out of high school, especially commercial and service. Tell him to have a driver''s license and be ready for a background check. Those two things get kids hired more than anything on paper.', true, 32, '2026-09-21T01:51:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9305d98f-0dd3-5a7b-8642-686aa5dbec35', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'Deptford here, 15 minutes away. Plenty of shops. Does he want benefits from day one, or is he okay with cash to start? I did three years of cash and wouldn''t do it again. Appreciate you looking out for him.', false, 2, '2026-09-21T02:43:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fb1f05b3-4500-5ded-8358-78604636d8a5', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, the best thing you can tell him is to stop working at Wawa and start carrying pipe for somebody, anybody, while he figures out the rest. He''ll know in a month whether he even likes it.', false, 6, '2026-09-21T03:26:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7863887a-f754-5959-bb44-5e3ac069b5c5', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'Camden County vo-tech grad here... I think the county schools down here have some adult night programs but I don''t know Gloucester''s specifically. worth a phone call. edit: my old teacher says call the adult ed office directly, not the main number', false, 3, '2026-09-21T09:24:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a6fb4065-32fa-5b46-bf9f-31262e4bf637', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'Appreciate it. 322 sounds right, I''ll have him check. What''s the deal with the background check thing though, is that a union thing or a shop thing', false, 3, '2026-09-21T11:59:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9f48f269-a051-5e5c-a1ef-87978b581e21', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Both, depending. A lot of our public work is in schools, so anyone on those sites has to clear whatever the district requires. Shops that don''t do schools may not care. Tell him to keep his record clean and he''ll never have to think about it.', false, 3, '2026-09-21T23:16:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f6745e96-f2ea-58a4-9bbf-d99e3d402f18', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'One thing nobody''s said: tell him to keep a notebook from the first day. Every job, every date, every boss. My father kept one his whole career, and when I took over the shop it was the most useful thing he left me besides the trucks.', false, 2, '2026-09-22T02:21:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7f2e9842-f295-5848-8031-e07f6816c7a5', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly I''d put trade school on the list too, even though I''m biased. I think there''s a private technical school or two around Blackwood. Costs real money though, so he should get a helper job first and find out if he likes it before signing anything.', false, 4, '2026-09-22T09:00:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('70f28528-30ab-587a-a042-a34ff7d238e1', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', 'af3fcb91-09e6-5441-8d3b-b76ecbc0192e', 'Burlington County, 3 yrs non-union. Agree on the license and background check. Also tell him to buy a decent pair of boots before day one, my first shop sent a kid home for wearing sneakers.', false, 2, '2026-09-22T20:40:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('eb9076be-4de5-5985-be27-83e5f4f166cd', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Good on you for asking instead of guessing. One practical thing: whichever way he goes, he should get his OSHA 10 if he can find a class. It''s cheap or even free in some places, it shows initiative, and it teaches him what not to do on a site. Stay safe.', false, 5, '2026-09-27T13:30:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('03cbde63-70cf-5872-806f-806b539c848d', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Ha... I had a helper from Williamstown once, best kid I ever trained lol. Came from a pizza place. Tell your cousin attitude beats everything down here, and there are shops all along the Black Horse Pike that need helpers.', false, 3, '2026-09-27T23:22:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fe1442c0-0999-5f3c-8d0b-f8ac5619f85f', 'cbc2c52d-ecb4-5300-9ec5-3577b6597b9b', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'update: he called two shops near Glassboro and one wants him to come in Thursday. Also told him about the notebook. Thanks everybody, this was way more than I would''ve known to tell him.', false, 1, '2026-09-27T23:43:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('e26a8906-6959-5d21-8ca0-61c036506d6b', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'question', 'Do any non-union shops actually pay for night school?', 'Follow-up to my shop teacher thread. Assume I go non-union. Everyone keeps saying "find a shop that pays for school." Okay, but do those actually exist around Mercer, or is that just something people say?

The guy I work weekends for told me he''d "think about it" when I asked. I''m not expecting a free ride. I''d just like to know what''s normal to ask for before I graduate and start applying for real jobs, so I don''t ask for something crazy or settle for nothing.', 'electrical', 'Mercer County, NJ', 15, '2026-09-18T17:51:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('9ca4280e-d364-5f77-936e-d82dd0f850fb', 'e26a8906-6959-5d21-8ca0-61c036506d6b', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly they exist, I''m one of them. I pay for night classes for my helpers once they''ve been with me a while, because I''d rather pay for school than keep training new guys. Not every shop does it. Ask in the interview: ''Do you help with school, and when does that start?'' A shop that gets weird about the question just told you something.', true, 17, '2026-09-18T21:33:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2ad9c966-6636-522f-a5b5-f1f94ec78922', 'e26a8906-6959-5d21-8ca0-61c036506d6b', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Mine doesn''t, for what it''s worth, and I didn''t ask before I took the job. I wish I had. Sorry, that''s more of a warning than an answer.', false, 2, '2026-09-20T12:24:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('18246cb4-1e80-52e2-b6ea-32ceaf524c55', 'e26a8906-6959-5d21-8ca0-61c036506d6b', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'My cousin''s shop in Totowa reimburses you after you pass the class, not before, so he had to pay up front and wait. It might be worth asking how they pay, not only whether they pay. I''m still in school myself, so this is secondhand.', false, 1, '2026-09-20T13:36:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('02faa579-f49e-5caa-8237-c7dc2aa088f0', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'question', 'hvac grad here, is it dumb to apply to the ibew too', 'sorry if this is a dumb question. finished the hvac program at the ocean county vo-tech in 24, doing duct work and changeouts around toms river now, applied to the apprenticeship and waiting. my buddy says apply to the electricians too so i have two shots. is that weird to do? would they hold it against me that my schooling is hvac? thanks in advance', 'hvac', 'Ocean County, NJ', 20, '2026-08-12T09:01:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('b61cd932-f707-51bc-98cc-3ba6b6b5a3ea', '02faa579-f49e-5caa-8237-c7dc2aa088f0', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Not dumb and not weird. People apply to more than one program all the time. In the interview, be honest: say you went to school for HVAC, say what draws you to electrical, and show you''ve thought about it. What hurts people is looking like they''d take anything. HVAC is a good background anyway; you''ve already been around controls and disconnects. Stay safe.', true, 6, '2026-08-12T11:26:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dce1c251-df7c-5724-909e-f2898c878f65', '02faa579-f49e-5caa-8237-c7dc2aa088f0', '0068d208-ce11-5170-b467-caa34a717104', 'Local 400 2nd year here, Jackson. A guy in my class did HVAC at a vo-tech before this and he''s honestly the best at controls in the room. Nobody held it against him.', false, 2, '2026-08-12T14:22:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9ee86457-91ab-555f-bff8-a7ab1b0cb3ea', '02faa579-f49e-5caa-8237-c7dc2aa088f0', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: the HVAC side and the electrical side meet at the disconnect and the thermostat wire, and I write up plenty of jobs at exactly that spot. Someone who understands both sides is useful in either trade.', false, 5, '2026-08-13T01:38:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('7b48a5f2-6bd8-5216-9fc1-197dce64950c', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'question', 'Weekend helper job is cutting into my program. Worth it?', 'Senior in an electrical program at a trade high school in Queens. Got a weekend helper job with a small shop in Ridgewood, Saturdays and some Sundays. Good money for me, and the foreman lets me do a little more every week. Problem is my grades slipped and my mom is on me about it. Do the hours matter more than grades if I want an apprenticeship? Or am I screwing myself.', 'electrical', 'Queens, NY', 10, '2026-09-11T02:05:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('dec44390-0090-5158-b04a-286019478e56', '7b48a5f2-6bd8-5216-9fc1-197dce64950c', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'Both matter. When I applied they asked about school and about work, so I would not let either one go. Drop Sundays and keep Saturdays. You still get the experience and your mother calms down. Appreciate you asking before it got worse.', false, 2, '2026-09-11T09:38:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1fd0da91-1984-58d8-8542-4c6956aa267d', '7b48a5f2-6bd8-5216-9fc1-197dce64950c', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'Brother, I did the Army before this. Idk anything about the high school side, but I''ve never met anybody who regretted finishing what they started. Finish the program.', false, 2, '2026-09-11T10:35:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('e3bd963e-294d-51ea-a3a8-12e34b9db087', '86afdff7-a622-5314-99e0-81558cc06b11', 'question', 'Two HVAC offers: big company with a sales quota or a 3-truck shop. Which one?', 'Apologies if this is not the right place. Morris County vo-tech, HVAC, class of ''24. I have been doing boilers and furnaces at a small place, but they are slowing down and I''m looking.

Two offers. One is a big residential company with a lot of trucks and ads everywhere. The pay is a little higher, but the techs I talked to said they are expected to sell maintenance plans and equipment, and there is a number every month. It''s also down 287 every morning. The other is a small shop in Dover, three trucks, the owner still goes on calls, a bit less money, fifteen minutes from me.

I want to learn the trade properly. Which one would you take at my stage? Thanks in advance.', 'hvac', 'Morris County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-29T09:27:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0a6c82df-d605-5fd3-8637-a9b1d71c7b22', 'e3bd963e-294d-51ea-a3a8-12e34b9db087', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Speaking as someone who runs a company and has no patience for quota culture:
- At two years in, who teaches you matters more than the extra dollar
- Ask the big company how much of the pay is commission or spiffs; the base is what you can count on
- Ask the small shop if the owner will put you on installs and service, not just maintenance
- Either way, ask what happens to you in January when the phones are busy and you''re the junior guy

If the small shop answers those well, I''d take it.', true, 17, '2026-09-29T16:21:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('787e3c8f-0e09-5654-8030-72571cfb83c1', 'e3bd963e-294d-51ea-a3a8-12e34b9db087', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'I worked for a big outfit for a year early on, out of Cherry Hill. Learned a lot about talking to customers, not a lot about troubleshooting lol. Small shop if you want to fix things.', false, 5, '2026-09-29T22:45:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e26ea451-07d7-56c8-b3fa-eb0f7f0f9e86', 'e3bd963e-294d-51ea-a3a8-12e34b9db087', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'Sorry if this is obvious, but my buddy works for one of those big outfits and he''s stressed every month about his number. He does make good money though. Depends what you want.', false, 3, '2026-09-30T01:15:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f50e0d50-23ca-5e93-8a33-cc8465119ca3', 'e3bd963e-294d-51ea-a3a8-12e34b9db087', '7faa1a09-27de-5125-aea4-eb8d826c963b', 'came from a call center with quotas. would not do quotas again for an extra dollar. is the small shop offering any school or 608 help? that would decide it for me', false, 2, '2026-09-30T02:52:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('19054142-9f78-5299-87a2-8d75db7ef96f', 'e3bd963e-294d-51ea-a3a8-12e34b9db087', '86afdff7-a622-5314-99e0-81558cc06b11', 'Thank you, this is helpful. I asked the small shop about installs and January, and the owner said I would be on installs with him through the winter. I''m going to take it.', false, 3, '2026-09-30T03:57:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('effdb7a7-209b-5ee7-be3d-a258005510f6', 'b298ceb4-fc38-5b36-b8ff-1ad22e49add8', 'question', 'perth amboy: which ibew local am i even supposed to apply to', '33, left delivery driving this summer, helper at a small shop now. i want to apply to the ibew apprenticeship this year. i live in perth amboy. my coworker says 456, a guy at the supply house says i can apply anywhere i want, and someone online said you have to apply where you live. can i apply to two different locals in the same year? does it matter where i live or where i work? appreciate it', 'electrical', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 13, '2026-08-29T13:00:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('74adba7c-8fd7-5889-963a-969750d91472', 'effdb7a7-209b-5ee7-be3d-a258005510f6', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Jurisdiction is set by each local and it isn''t always obvious from a map, so call the apprenticeship office for the local you think covers Perth Amboy and ask them directly whether you''re in their area.

Whether you can apply to more than one program in the same cycle, and whether it''s where you live or where you work that counts, can differ from program to program. Ask each one. Write down who you talked to and when. Stay safe.', true, 13, '2026-08-30T01:24:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('10689efe-d8c0-52e1-81c7-2cf8a1a2a07a', 'effdb7a7-209b-5ee7-be3d-a258005510f6', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'I had the same confusion in Irvington. I ended up just calling. It took five minutes and they were helpful. Much faster than asking around at the Wawa like I was doing.', false, 1, '2026-08-30T02:36:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bd67dbad-2e15-50b8-9125-5f82a0786347', 'effdb7a7-209b-5ee7-be3d-a258005510f6', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', 'I''m pretty sure you can reapply every year if you don''t get in... that''s what a guy in my 164 class did, took him three tries... don''t give up after one. Thanks in advance for posting how it goes', false, 2, '2026-08-30T09:01:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3935574d-c564-51da-b297-c37c13eba68a', 'effdb7a7-209b-5ee7-be3d-a258005510f6', 'b298ceb4-fc38-5b36-b8ff-1ad22e49add8', 'appreciate it. i meant two different locals at the same time, not applying twice. called this morning anyway, left my number, waiting on a callback. writing down the date like marcus said', false, 1, '2026-08-30T09:22:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'discussion', 'Ranked low twice, got in on the third try. Ask me whatever', 'UA Local 24, first year. I ranked low my first two times. Third time I got the call. I see a lot of people on here worried about their ranking, so ask me what you want. I can only tell you what happened to me. I don''t know how anyone else''s local runs. Between tries I worked for a service and drain shop in Fair Lawn.', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 20, '2026-09-21T01:19:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('b181acbb-abb9-56fb-aa86-faff9429a326', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', 'df0dfff9-4016-5ddb-a8b6-c4029b1e30b2', 'what changed between the 2nd and 3rd try? was it the test or the interview', false, 2, '2026-09-21T10:10:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a97340b3-975f-5ffa-a6be-18a92eece5c6', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'The interview. I had real jobs to talk about the third time. Before that I had nothing.', false, 1, '2026-09-21T10:19:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('80279fdc-c4e8-5b36-9468-79cffd5f3a5c', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '02a13f50-be86-588b-966d-7ae10b7d64cd', 'did you retake the test every time or does the score carry over... asking for me, I''m hvac but thinking about it', false, 2, '2026-09-21T13:45:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c03afb8c-98a8-5fd2-8e10-378ea4bc400c', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'I retook it. Idk if that''s required everywhere. Ask the program directly.', false, 4, '2026-09-21T14:29:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('540a5fd4-7aad-541b-8735-4342bbebb103', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Good for you, kid. Third try means you wanted it. Most people quit after one. That''s the job.', false, 5, '2026-09-22T01:11:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1bc12aa7-86a5-5f79-ac5e-7e55f0c5013f', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '07676d29-9e30-5e27-b903-f9044b52fe4b', 'how long between tries? i applied in the spring down in atlantic county and it feels like forever', false, 1, '2026-09-22T01:45:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9cffc59c-02cc-52f5-9497-32e0a7f28066', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'About a year each time. It felt like forever to me too.', false, 3, '2026-09-28T10:25:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c0e2f2f1-c8e5-5fd4-91ae-7e259d539f63', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'This is the most useful kind of post. One thing for everyone reading: his third interview went better because he had specifics. Bring two or three real jobs you can describe start to finish, including something you got wrong and fixed. Panels remember that. Stay safe.', false, 8, '2026-09-29T02:15:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ad83ed12-d5f0-53ea-92d0-99547a6d631d', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'My foreman on weekends says nobody looks at your grades in the interview. True? Or is he just saying that because his were bad lol', false, 1, '2026-09-29T09:32:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('31d882fc-819a-5fb0-af7e-999633dde516', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'Idk about grades. Nobody asked me about mine in any of the three.', false, 1, '2026-09-29T16:22:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e90b5e8e-53c0-5633-8063-9b523426b6b5', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, congrats. Different local, different city, same lesson. Most of the guys I know who got in late are better for it. They showed up already knowing how to work.', false, 2, '2026-09-30T00:09:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('18f61da1-782c-5f66-ba95-fa06c1b960bb', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '6b3a1896-cd39-5ae1-8351-8817f445313d', 'applied in mercer, waiting. foreman says im wasting my time doing pex and should just stay put. this thread helps lol', false, 1, '2026-09-30T01:17:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('57ba055e-fe74-567b-aa22-2ad88b608c30', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'Local 1 first year here. Got in my first try but I''ll be honest, a lot of luck in that lol. Respect for going three times.', false, 2, '2026-09-30T03:41:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3a42b285-4566-5a08-b580-667915d181ce', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'Sorry if this is a dumb question, did you tell the interviewers it was your third try or do they already know?', false, 4, '2026-09-30T03:47:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('63a042cc-4155-5c7d-98a8-6c89a4c7bc83', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'They knew. I said it before they could. Then I said what I did differently each year.', false, 4, '2026-09-30T09:40:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('517ada86-702e-5b10-a3cd-0621d18f5fab', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '81a78d2a-1f86-5ff4-b4e3-293e5f93bee7', 'Fourth year in 24, also not first try (second). Sorry to jump in, but the ''say it before they do'' thing is good advice, people respect owning it. Congrats, and get ready for school nights, grab a big Wawa coffee for those.', false, 1, '2026-09-30T11:43:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('085569cb-9558-5062-85f9-9bb57f3ceb77', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Good post. My father used to say the second time you knock, they know your face. The third time they know your name.', false, 4, '2026-09-30T23:10:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2539995f-fd35-5d42-b26d-c065d0fa0657', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'good. write your hours down every week starting now. you''ll want them later.', false, 4, '2026-09-30T23:22:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9acc57e0-922b-5d67-b9af-054f1db5e4c3', '78002874-e937-5b1f-b53b-fda4d52a2bd7', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'Will do. Thanks everyone, didn''t expect this many questions tonight.', false, 2, '2026-10-01T09:56:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5a2575fe-5453-5d8f-89b8-b6f74b9fcd1c', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'question', 'does my non-union time count for anything when i apply to the union?', 'started at a non-union hvac shop in paterson in june, paid hourly, no benefits yet. been thinking about applying to a union apprenticeship next time one opens, maybe even electrical, i haven''t decided. question for anyone who''s been through it, brother: does the time i''ve already put in count for anything? like does it get you ranked higher, or skip a year, or nothing? i keep hearing alot of totally different answers. one guy at the supply house said it hurts you because you picked up bad habits lol', 'hvac', 'Passaic County, NJ', 23, '2026-08-22T12:12:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('f7a705da-853e-52d5-a467-55378da41ff1', '5a2575fe-5453-5d8f-89b8-b6f74b9fcd1c', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'In my experience it helps you in the interview, because you can talk about real work and it shows you''ll show up at 6 a.m. Whether it earns credit toward the apprenticeship or changes your score is up to each program''s rules, and those get updated, so ask the one you''re applying to.

As for "bad habits": nobody holds that against a first-year. We retrain everybody. Stay safe.', true, 13, '2026-08-22T14:42:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6ebae26d-5769-5336-b60f-2ce1e975fa1b', '5a2575fe-5453-5d8f-89b8-b6f74b9fcd1c', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Bad habits. Ha. The kid who''s carried water heaters for a year has better habits than the kid who hasn''t carried anything. That supply house guy is full of it.', false, 3, '2026-08-23T00:03:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('eff5bc21-a8d7-53b0-8053-4897d0cf257b', '5a2575fe-5453-5d8f-89b8-b6f74b9fcd1c', 'cee246a3-b9ec-55fd-8ac0-35c06eeed07f', 'took me 2 tries to get on at 164. my first interview i had zero work experience and it showed. second time i''d been at a shop in hackensack for a year and it was a completely different conversation, they asked about jobs and i actually had answers. so for me it counted, just not on paper', false, 2, '2026-08-23T01:36:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('69015874-edd0-50c2-929f-0e9215462f00', '5a2575fe-5453-5d8f-89b8-b6f74b9fcd1c', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'Same question here. I start a helper job in Irvington Monday. Following this one.', false, 1, '2026-08-23T01:53:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c60ba432-9d32-5630-8c13-76bf4a0fa049', '5a2575fe-5453-5d8f-89b8-b6f74b9fcd1c', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, it counts where it matters, in the room. Paperwork is paperwork. Ask the program about credit.', false, 6, '2026-08-23T22:29:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c049d1d4-d140-5eb8-b199-efc0ff39cd47', '5a2575fe-5453-5d8f-89b8-b6f74b9fcd1c', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'sorry to hijack but does it matter if the non-union time is in a different trade? i''m hvac and thinking about applying electrical. thanks in advance', false, 4, '2026-08-23T23:47:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bc89ce97-2ba3-551f-a8ee-63344b13fcf1', '5a2575fe-5453-5d8f-89b8-b6f74b9fcd1c', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Not a hijack... the stuff transfers more than people think. Reading a wiring diagram on a furnace is reading a wiring diagram. I''ve seen HVAC guys go electrical and electricians come over to us, both ways work lol', false, 4, '2026-08-23T23:54:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4e8dc10e-89ea-5f58-aefe-6c8508df6f99', '5a2575fe-5453-5d8f-89b8-b6f74b9fcd1c', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'ok so it counts in the interview, not on paper. makes sense. gonna keep a list of jobs i''ve done so i have stuff to talk about. thanks brother', false, 1, '2026-08-24T01:19:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('a0308c0c-a435-5ca1-a4e7-2903e0af71be', '9fe65554-dd4f-5c8b-9708-65d0c765a948', 'question', 'How does the apprenticeship ranking actually get scored? Test, interview, both?', 'Less than a year in at a non-union plumbing shop near Long Branch. Thinking about applying to the UA next round. Every thread I read says "I ranked low" or "I ranked 180th" but nobody says how the number actually gets made.

Is it the test score plus the interview? Do they add points for experience or school? Idk if it''s the same everywhere or if every local does it different. I just want to know what I can actually work on between now and then instead of stressing about a number I don''t understand.', 'plumbing', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 4, '2026-10-01T23:30:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('badafbfb-1d57-51d6-9c22-44f1c070f366', 'a0308c0c-a435-5ca1-a4e7-2903e0af71be', '81a78d2a-1f86-5ff4-b4e3-293e5f93bee7', 'Sorry if this is long. For me in 24 it was the test first, then an interview, then a ranked list, and from what I understood the score was some mix of those. I never got a breakdown of exact points. What you can work on: the math for the test (practice it), and having real jobs to talk about in the interview. Ask the local you''re applying to whether they explain how they score it. Mine didn''t, at least not that I saw.', true, 7, '2026-10-02T09:55:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('63d1602a-12e2-5390-8fa5-d9c3407acf9d', 'a0308c0c-a435-5ca1-a4e7-2903e0af71be', 'df0dfff9-4016-5ddb-a8b6-c4029b1e30b2', 'somerset vo-tech grad, applied, waiting. my foreman says the interview counts more than the test but not sure he really knows. did anybody here ever get a breakdown? also is it the same for hvac', false, 1, '2026-10-02T10:44:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('eeaee8c3-67fc-5bc2-a5b0-b3a7aa861dcb', 'a0308c0c-a435-5ca1-a4e7-2903e0af71be', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'I''d rather you ask the program than trust a forum on this. When I went through, the aptitude test got you to the interview, and the interview had a big effect on where you landed. That was a long time ago. Each program sets its own scoring, and they''re the only ones who can tell you what''s current. Stay safe.', false, 3, '2026-10-04T16:01:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e13e2370-2be5-590f-b5aa-1b31559b1d14', 'a0308c0c-a435-5ca1-a4e7-2903e0af71be', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, stop trying to game a number. Get good at the work and the number takes care of itself. That''s the job.', false, 4, '2026-10-04T23:31:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d12471e0-5fd4-5ca8-8299-9ac5a76cdf88', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'tip', 'To the kids who ranked low this summer', 'Saw a few of you beating yourselves up over a number. Here''s what I tell my own helpers.

A ranking is one morning of your life. It doesn''t know whether you show up, whether you listen, or whether you can carry a 50-gallon heater up a split-level''s stairs without banging the drywall.

Go get a job with somebody who''ll teach you. Learn to solder, learn to read a boiler, learn to talk to a homeowner without making her nervous. Then apply again with something to say. I''ve hired plenty of kids who never got into anything, and they''re running service calls on their own now.

Don''t quit on it. That''s the job.', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 9, '2026-08-14T17:56:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'question', 'Buddy from my vo-tech class ranked low and says he''s done trying. What do I tell him?', 'Kind of a different one. I''m a 1st year in Local 24, got in my first try, and I know that''s partly luck. My best friend from school applied the same time, ranked way down, and now he''s saying he''s done. He''s going to keep working at the Wawa in Montclair and "figure it out."

He''s better with his hands than me, honestly. I don''t want to be the guy who got in lecturing him, but I also don''t want him to waste a year. What would you have wanted someone to say to you? Or is it better to just leave him alone for a while?', 'plumbing', 'Essex County, NJ', 8, '2026-09-14T01:36:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('884f7bae-13bf-5372-9018-2df18b990f7a', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'I was your buddy... took me two tries. what helped was a guy at my shop saying ''you''re working here anyway, apply again, what''s it cost you.'' no speech, just that', false, 1, '2026-09-14T09:20:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7f8ac5a2-6cd3-54cf-b67d-766d5e705a32', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Don''t lecture him, brother. Get him a job carrying something. Ask your foreman if anybody''s looking for a helper. That does more than any pep talk.', false, 4, '2026-09-15T02:57:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('89c4623c-db8a-5f13-9c12-cbc2c3ddc6a4', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'That''s a good idea. My foreman knows half the shops in Essex County.', false, 2, '2026-09-15T03:56:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('07910dca-4698-553c-b9cf-d50e92075344', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'Did he say why he''s done, or is he just embarrassed? Those are different. I''d let him be embarrassed for a week, then ask him to come help on something.', false, 1, '2026-09-15T10:26:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('715185bd-8478-5c3b-9677-80a27f2a5cfe', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'The useful thing you can do is make the next step small. Not ''reapply,'' just ''come with me Saturday, a buddy''s shop needs a hand.'' Once he''s working near the trade again, the application stops feeling like a verdict on him. Stay safe.', false, 5, '2026-09-16T01:12:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0f2720d4-4640-5342-9060-9f07965d5e53', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', 'e9519c5c-bc39-526e-b419-6fd671e34e37', 'Took me two tries at the test too. The second time is easier because you know what''s coming. Tell him that.', false, 3, '2026-09-16T02:39:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('22696d17-8a1a-5f30-ba47-98f8f1091820', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'tell him once, plainly. then leave it alone and let him decide.', false, 3, '2026-09-17T02:57:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('043cfcd9-4685-5230-8f83-7bc61ab769d5', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'Ranked low twice before I got in. Tell him it''s not the end of anything.', false, 1, '2026-09-17T13:48:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('76feb6f5-5189-5c71-b5c1-e0528ebe36d4', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question: what to say, or whether to say anything? Say one thing, once, and make it an offer instead of advice. Then go back to being his friend.', false, 2, '2026-09-18T02:15:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ee717372-1ef8-5f96-9e9e-5eaa98393ce4', '9e83a746-86af-584f-8726-7ebe98bc8a7b', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'update: brought him to a Saturday side thing with my foreman''s buddy, a basement bathroom in Bloomfield. He was better at it than me lol. Says he''ll ''think about'' reapplying. I''ll take it.', false, 2, '2026-09-18T10:11:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d44a6d3d-93fc-5b32-88de-af240023fa60', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'question', 'Apply right out of high school, or wait a year so I don''t tank the ranking?', 'Third time posting about this stuff, sorry, the shop teacher thread got me thinking. If I apply to the IBEW the first chance I get after I graduate, I''ll walk into the interview with one summer job, weekend helper hours and nothing else. If I wait a year and work full time at a shop, I''d have a full year of real work to talk about.

Logic says wait. My teacher says apply right away, every time, because "you can''t get picked if you''re not in the pile." I see his point, but I also don''t want my first impression to be a weak one if it follows me. Does a bad first interview stick with you, or is every year a fresh start?', 'electrical', 'Mercer County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-18T01:07:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('4495a32d-2e38-5658-aa69-38553ac07d2a', 'd44a6d3d-93fc-5b32-88de-af240023fa60', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Your teacher has the stronger argument. I can''t tell you whether any program keeps notes from a previous interview; ask them. But I''ve never heard anyone say they regret applying early. Apply when you''re eligible, work full time while the process runs, and if you need a second try you''ll have the year of experience anyway. You get both. Stay safe.', false, 6, '2026-09-18T03:11:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b3706359-c5ee-5968-a1a0-e50ef7f8dd7c', 'd44a6d3d-93fc-5b32-88de-af240023fa60', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'From the other end of the age range: I wish I''d applied to anything at 18. Two questions back at you though. What''s the actual downside of applying? And would you take it if they called?', false, 2, '2026-09-18T10:02:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('96465190-e058-5511-9818-c840ec9bd2a5', 'd44a6d3d-93fc-5b32-88de-af240023fa60', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Different trade, but here''s how I''d weigh it:
- Applying costs you a morning and maybe an application fee
- Waiting costs you a year of possible apprenticeship time
- A weak interview at 18 is expected; nobody expects an 18-year-old to sound like a foreman
Apply.', false, 4, '2026-09-18T12:29:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('159be074-be98-500c-aee9-cee54f520143', 'd44a6d3d-93fc-5b32-88de-af240023fa60', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'Brother, I waited eleven years to start because I thought I wasn''t ready. Idk your situation, but don''t wait for ready.', false, 1, '2026-09-18T16:04:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('964ad6d9-afde-514f-b354-719cbc8563bf', 'd44a6d3d-93fc-5b32-88de-af240023fa60', '48b61243-8eaf-5f00-b8aa-9268dc17b5af', 'same advice my boss gave me in tottenville, he said apply every year until theyre sick of you. i''m non-union for now and that''s fine, but i applied anyway brother', false, 1, '2026-09-18T18:16:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('6981c72b-6873-534b-a81e-1cc539784537', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'question', 'Do my vo-tech shop hours count toward anything after I graduate?', 'In the plumbing program at the Middlesex County vo-tech. We do a lot of shop time, plus I help my uncle on weekends (he jokes I''m basically his foreman now lol, I''m not). Ziggy''s been answering my questions on here and he said to ask the people who actually run the programs, which I will, but I want to know what others found. Do the hours in a vo-tech program count toward an apprenticeship or a license later? Or is it just a diploma and a head start?', 'plumbing', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 15, '2026-08-19T10:29:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('495e0a03-9170-57ec-903d-643106ecf1e3', '6981c72b-6873-534b-a81e-1cc539784537', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Speaking as someone who teaches in one: first, ask your program''s coordinator directly, because whatever arrangements exist are specific to your school and to the apprenticeship you apply to. Second, assume nothing transfers automatically. Some apprenticeships may look favorably on a program, and some licensing paths may count certain schooling, but you''ll want it in writing either way. Third, keep every certificate and transcript. Ask me how I know you''ll need them years later.', true, 24, '2026-08-20T00:22:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c6b65df4-62cb-5ee7-8a01-78ce349496c7', '6981c72b-6873-534b-a81e-1cc539784537', 'e9519c5c-bc39-526e-b419-6fd671e34e37', 'My vo-tech didn''t count as hours in 24 as far as I know, but it helped a lot in the interview. Thanks in advance if anyone knows different.', false, 1, '2026-08-20T01:21:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('61d4383a-5b80-56bf-9685-9c47ce895ca9', '6981c72b-6873-534b-a81e-1cc539784537', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'It counts in the way that matters most: you''ll know which end of a torch is hot on your first day. My father used to hire the vo-tech kids over everyone else for exactly that reason. I still do.', false, 6, '2026-08-20T01:41:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('662e64d3-031d-59b8-840c-66cfcce69700', 'aa4aa383-9b0a-5294-809c-62f229f9606e', 'question', 'Private HVAC night program while I''m already working. Worth the money?', 'Less than a year in at a non-union HVAC shop in Woodbridge. Hourly, no benefits yet. A buddy is doing the evening HVAC program at one of the private tech schools and says I should too. He told me they quoted him something like the price of a used car. My boss says I''ll learn more on the truck. Is a private program worth that kind of money if I already have the job? Or should I look at the county school''s adult classes first. Honest answers, brother.', 'hvac', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 8, '2026-10-05T00:50:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d34dd4cd-ef40-5799-9285-04d3506993a8', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'tip', 'Before you sign a private trade school loan, ask these questions', 'Every few weeks a new hire tells me what they owe on a private trade school program, and some of them didn''t need to owe it. I''m not against private schools. Some are good. But ask these before you sign anything:
- What''s the total cost, including tools, books and fees, not the monthly payment
- How many hours are hands-on shop time versus classroom
- What share of graduates are working in the trade a year later, and how do they count that
- Does the county vo-tech or community college near you have an adult program for less
- Would an employer pay for it if you got hired first

If the admissions person gets pushy when you ask, that''s an answer too.', 'other', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 8, '2026-08-18T10:23:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('a665fceb-3bcb-57f6-95e9-93141d8c82a9', 'd34dd4cd-ef40-5799-9285-04d3506993a8', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'All good questions. I''d add one from my side: ask to sit in on a shop class before you enroll, on a normal night. You''ll see in ten minutes whether students are working or watching. Ask me how I know some programs don''t love that request.', false, 5, '2026-08-19T01:03:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c29696df-1b0e-5e59-8373-2b77adfa2f3e', 'd34dd4cd-ef40-5799-9285-04d3506993a8', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I look for when I hire, since it''s related: I don''t check where someone went to school. I check whether they can do the work and whether they show up. A certificate helps you get the interview, not the job.', false, 4, '2026-08-19T23:17:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('df410e67-8a61-5777-b2e9-14fa5febdbfc', 'd34dd4cd-ef40-5799-9285-04d3506993a8', '5ea91175-1b81-51fb-918c-7ad563230535', 'I''m doing the county night HVAC program twice a week... it was a fraction of what the private school quoted me... thanks in advance to anyone who knows if the county ones are any good for electrical too', false, 2, '2026-08-19T23:32:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('aaa4a6b5-1618-572e-a397-d852982cbd61', 'd34dd4cd-ef40-5799-9285-04d3506993a8', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly I''m the guy who went to a private trade school and it worked for me. But I was 19, lived with my parents and had no bills. It''s different math if you''re 35 with rent. I''d push back a little on making it sound like a trap.', false, 1, '2026-08-20T22:54:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b724f3f6-9f02-50f9-aca9-a164ddc4c0ee', 'd34dd4cd-ef40-5799-9285-04d3506993a8', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Fair point, Thiago, and I''m not saying skip them:
- If the cost works and you learn better in a classroom, it can be worth it
- If you can get hired as a helper first, try that before you borrow', false, 1, '2026-08-21T09:44:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('43af9bc4-7b23-5e3b-84b7-fc557535a00e', 'd34dd4cd-ef40-5799-9285-04d3506993a8', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'My father used to say never borrow for something you can get paid to learn. He wasn''t always right, but he was right about that one.', false, 8, '2026-08-24T00:07:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('701122d0-8df4-5905-a641-d260443dfd99', 'd34dd4cd-ef40-5799-9285-04d3506993a8', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'refrigeration side, nobody ever asked where i went to school. they asked if i could find a leak on a walk-in in july. winter is when you learn, and you can learn it for free if you''re on somebody''s truck', false, 3, '2026-08-24T23:16:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('85336f02-653e-5312-9fa5-7c85c17c2e71', 'd34dd4cd-ef40-5799-9285-04d3506993a8', '56ebe677-1060-5479-89c5-55faedf03943', 'I''m taking one night class at the community college to test the waters before I commit to anything. Cheaper than any program and I''ll know by December if I hate it.', false, 1, '2026-08-24T23:49:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('e12577be-b037-5db1-9596-f90ca4d38262', '493faab8-51d6-584c-8d92-65b67edb36f6', 'question', 'My dad is 45 and wants to do the HVAC night program. Too old?', 'Kind of a weird one. I''m in the HVAC program at the Gloucester County vo-tech, and my dad has been helping me study for the 608 at the kitchen table. Now he''s into it. He''s 45, works in a warehouse in Swedesboro, back''s okay, and he''s asking if he''s too old to do the adult night program and switch.

I told him I''d ask people who actually do this. Is 45 too late to start in HVAC? Would anyone hire him as a helper at that age?

edit: he says thanks in advance and that he''s "not that old" lol', 'hvac', 'Gloucester County, NJ', 8, '2026-09-25T21:08:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('85ea6e6b-9a67-565c-b9fb-5dc3ebf68e19', 'e12577be-b037-5db1-9596-f90ca4d38262', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Tell your father this, from someone who hires every year: here''s what I look for when I hire, and age isn''t on the list. Reliability, listening, and a clean driving record. Warehouse guys usually have the first two down. The real question is his body in an attic in July, so have him ride along on a hot day before he quits anything.', false, 9, '2026-09-27T17:24:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('89f26aa0-3010-5498-8b86-853c0efca391', 'e12577be-b037-5db1-9596-f90ca4d38262', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'From my side:
- 45 is not too late; he''d have 20 working years in the trade
- The pay cut is the real issue, so he should know his monthly number first
- The adult night program lets him keep the warehouse job while he finds out
Good on him for studying with you.', false, 8, '2026-09-27T21:59:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('bd7ec97a-bf63-5d41-86e3-b4344de04a82', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'question', '17 and every shop says come back when I''m 18. Is that a real rule?', 'Electrical program at the Essex County vo-tech. Trying to get a weekend helper job. Called five shops around Nutley and Belleville. Three said call back when I''m 18. One said insurance. One hung up. I turn 18 in March. Is that an actual law, or just shops not wanting to deal with a kid? Right now I work Sundays at a Wawa on Franklin Ave. Would rather be on a job.', 'electrical', 'Essex County, NJ', 10, '2026-10-02T10:11:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('fa79f8c0-a0f4-59e9-afb6-e4b66066b3e5', 'bd7ec97a-bf63-5d41-86e3-b4344de04a82', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: there are labor rules about what minors can do on certain kinds of sites and with certain equipment, and insurance carriers can add their own requirements on top. Ask your school whether it runs a co-op or work-based placement; that''s often how students get onto a site properly before 18.', false, 4, '2026-10-04T15:11:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('913074ec-fd2d-5493-9060-4c6562d9b4be', 'bd7ec97a-bf63-5d41-86e3-b4344de04a82', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'Same spot here but plumbing. I only get work because it''s my uncle''s shop lol. My shop teacher says the co-op thing is how most of the seniors get placed.', false, 1, '2026-10-04T19:18:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('aa5ec8bf-51bb-5351-a68e-2af29d635085', 'bd7ec97a-bf63-5d41-86e3-b4344de04a82', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'A few things that may help:
- Ask your program about co-op or work-based learning placements
- Supply houses sometimes hire 17-year-olds for the counter or the warehouse; you''ll learn every part by name
- In March, call the same five shops back. They''ll remember you called', false, 2, '2026-10-05T02:35:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c3dd476d-1c4b-54e6-8cdf-187a989146c9', 'bd7ec97a-bf63-5d41-86e3-b4344de04a82', '86afdff7-a622-5314-99e0-81558cc06b11', 'Apologies if this is off topic, but I worked the counter at a supply house in Morristown at 17 before my first shop job. It helped more than I expected. I knew what everything was called on day one.', false, 3, '2026-10-05T02:44:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0f573cbf-8ef4-585e-b870-3b1dd075fd47', 'bd7ec97a-bf63-5d41-86e3-b4344de04a82', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Call those three back the week of your birthday. I mean it. Persistence is half of why my father let me on the trucks young. The one that hung up, forget them.', false, 3, '2026-10-05T02:58:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('9a54cd03-afee-5210-b2aa-a5aebe0dddd7', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'question', 'Is it dumb to pick electrical just because it''s supposed to pay the most?', 'Everybody at my school says electrical pays the best, so that''s why I signed up for it. Honestly I like the plumbing kids'' projects better. Is the pay difference between the trades actually big in North Jersey? Or is that just something people say at the Wawa? Don''t want to pick the wrong one for the wrong reason and be stuck.', 'electrical', 'Essex County, NJ', 27, '2026-10-03T23:19:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('c0ec05f2-3b57-52e5-aec9-ca12e9d6d09e', '9a54cd03-afee-5210-b2aa-a5aebe0dddd7', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'Plumber obviously, so I''m biased lol. From what I see on the union side the scales are pretty close between the trades, at least up here. Pick the one where you don''t watch the clock. And the Wawa guys don''t know anything, I say that as a Wawa guy.', false, 1, '2026-10-04T03:50:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a073c4ae-b933-5ed9-9369-d1671d7df322', '9a54cd03-afee-5210-b2aa-a5aebe0dddd7', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'Same as him. Pick what you like doing. Idk anyone who stayed in a trade they hated just for the money.', false, 1, '2026-10-04T10:01:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('978d60e1-8919-5cff-8cc5-78b8d49b6aa6', '9a54cd03-afee-5210-b2aa-a5aebe0dddd7', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'How I''d compare them:
- Look up the wage and benefit packages for the locals near you; most post them
- Non-union pay varies more by shop than by trade
- Long term, the money follows whoever gets good and runs work, in any trade
- You''ll get good faster at the one you like', false, 4, '2026-10-05T00:14:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('748e837e-2609-5acc-9061-bb71ce535f0f', 'fb3a0b82-da77-5dd7-9a89-e099391b6ce7', 'question', 'Career switchers keep getting hired over us vo-tech kids. What gives?', 'Not trying to start a war. Two years out of the Essex County vo-tech, plumbing, still mostly doing demo at a shop near Bloomfield. My shop just hired a 35-year-old guy who used to sell cars, and he''s already on fittings while I''m still breaking up cast iron. Second time I''ve seen this. Is it because they think older guys are more reliable? Or am I doing something wrong? Kind of burns, I went to school for this for four years.', 'plumbing', 'Essex County, NJ', 4, '2026-09-27T16:27:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('3481c95b-0eb4-5f68-9611-c54252157cde', '748e837e-2609-5acc-9061-bb71ce535f0f', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'I''ll be straight with you: a car salesman knows how to talk to a homeowner, and he usually knows how to ask for what he wants. That''s often why he moves up faster. It isn''t age, it''s that he probably asked. Go to your lead tomorrow and say, ''I''d like to do the fittings on the next job.'' Your four years of school will show the minute they let you.', true, 7, '2026-09-27T23:30:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2f3687c8-2527-5fc4-968e-290076913248', '748e837e-2609-5acc-9061-bb71ce535f0f', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'Sorry, maybe a dumb take, but the same thing happened at my shop in Bayonne and it turned out the new guy just kept asking. I never asked. Started asking, it got better.', false, 3, '2026-09-28T00:17:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8739e93b-1dfd-50c3-8350-3d34d81f3843', '748e837e-2609-5acc-9061-bb71ce535f0f', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'the car salesman guy probably talks to the boss at lunch lol. your gonna have to do that too, it''s half the job', false, 3, '2026-09-28T00:49:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0d9c927a-22aa-598f-8624-df2d8b95c1f5', '748e837e-2609-5acc-9061-bb71ce535f0f', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'From the owner side:
- Older hires often come in asking about the path, so owners see them as long-term
- Younger hires sometimes look like they''re passing through, even when they aren''t
- Tell your boss your plan; owners invest in people who say they''re staying', false, 6, '2026-09-28T00:59:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a90b8bcf-b5e1-5c15-af5f-43ff1e905bec', '748e837e-2609-5acc-9061-bb71ce535f0f', '9fe65554-dd4f-5c8b-9708-65d0c765a948', 'wait so is it a good idea to just tell your boss you want more? I''ve been scared to, idk if it makes you look pushy, or is that only at some shops', false, 2, '2026-09-28T03:13:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0c761516-2e5c-5957-8ce2-17731dc90586', '748e837e-2609-5acc-9061-bb71ce535f0f', 'fb3a0b82-da77-5dd7-9a89-e099391b6ce7', 'Fair, I never actually asked. Asked today if I could do the fittings on a vanity swap Monday. He said yes. Kind of annoyed it was that easy honestly. Is that how it works everywhere?', false, 3, '2026-09-28T03:27:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'discussion', 'Update: did a ride-along in all three trades. Here''s what happened', 'A while back I posted about being 40 and unable to pick a trade. Joy suggested ride-alongs, and she''s been mentoring me since, so here''s the report.

Plumbing: a day on a repipe in an old Colonial in Metuchen. Loved the problem-solving, hated my knees by 2pm.
HVAC: a changeout in a split-level in Edison in August. The attic was brutal, but the diagnosis part was interesting.
Electrical: a service upgrade in Highland Park, panel swap, PSE&G had to come out to pull the meter. That was the one where I lost track of time.

So I''m leaning electrical, and maybe the low-voltage side later because of my knees. Two questions: did anyone else pick partly because of their body? And is it crazy to plan around knees at 40?', 'other', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 21, '2026-09-17T03:11:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0085cf49-0fb6-5045-9d75-ca397058b5a6', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Proud of you for doing all three. What''s your actual question, though? You already picked. You lost track of time on the panel job. That''s the answer.', false, 8, '2026-09-17T10:19:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('55e5f559-8bb2-5c59-81eb-141e2985ba37', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'Ha. Fair. I think I wanted someone to tell me it''s okay that it''s not plumbing, after you set the whole thing up.', false, 6, '2026-09-17T10:52:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('98c5b167-cda9-54a9-b3e3-0d5d5ba905b2', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'It''s more than okay. I''d rather you pick the right one than mine.', false, 8, '2026-09-17T10:57:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cfb407d0-46ca-55e5-9527-b662b42b7720', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fwiw low voltage is a real trade and your knees will thank you. i''ve been doing bms and fire alarm for 14 years, most of my day is a laptop, a ladder and a ceiling tile. don''t let anyone tell you it isn''t real electrical work', false, 1, '2026-09-17T22:24:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('aa52af88-ddbf-59a7-b8cb-9ebbb21fcc2c', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Planning around your body at 40 isn''t crazy, it''s smart. When I hire someone in their 40s, the ones I keep know their limits and tell me up front. That''s worth more to me than someone who says yes to every attic and gets hurt in a month.', false, 6, '2026-09-18T02:38:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dd46b035-4972-58d5-afa9-b4e005755975', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'e84cafaf-f3fa-5f47-ab1f-78162ab3e2c3', 'this is really cool to read. im in the trades program at the ocean county vo-tech and my foreman at my summer job said the same thing, you know which one when you lose track of time. appreciate it', false, 2, '2026-09-18T09:54:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('37bbb5c7-fd57-54b5-bcc5-e1c6e407a7bc', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', 'did hvac at 40 too. attics in august are no joke. knees ok, back less ok. electrical makes sense, good luck', false, 1, '2026-09-18T17:11:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d2003f9f-8780-5b2d-acdb-7562037e0d3d', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'As a vo-tech kid who thinks about this way too much: a panel swap was the best day of my whole summer too, and the meter pull part is wild the first time you see it.', false, 1, '2026-09-18T20:58:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('97775bfa-e1fb-54f2-8e8a-45dee6c0284c', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', '5ea91175-1b81-51fb-918c-7ad563230535', 'Congrats... I''m still doing the HVAC night classes, I''m 33 and my knees already complain... thanks in advance for posting the follow-up when you start', false, 2, '2026-09-19T14:42:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b6257ebb-6779-5cef-bfa9-547df1337be5', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Good process. If you go electrical and later want low voltage:
- Get your OSHA 10 early
- Ask every shop you interview with whether they do any controls or fire alarm work
- Keep notes on every panel and service you touch', false, 4, '2026-09-19T23:43:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0a1f1778-951a-567f-8de0-3fece282bec5', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', '56ebe677-1060-5479-89c5-55faedf03943', '40 here too, bartending, same three-way choice. This is the most useful thing I''ve read on here. Doing my own ride-along next month because of it.', false, 1, '2026-09-20T03:10:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b69c54bb-6fe2-5b01-a51a-2751dda3bc6c', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Love this. One thing my older students tell me: the first year is harder on the body than any year after, because you''re doing everything the slow way. It gets easier as you get efficient. So don''t judge your knees by one day on a repipe.', false, 12, '2026-09-21T02:55:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('86638723-7b06-5889-a508-5f600d45527e', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', '76ffb6b2-6ae2-5434-982e-39a1a1bf28b2', 'Career switcher too (36, used to teach middle school). Did basically the same thing and electrical won. Sorry for the dumb question, but did they let you actually do anything on the ride-alongs or just watch?', false, 2, '2026-09-28T01:34:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e6c1c703-dbca-5388-969c-229ca14b3961', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'Mostly watching. On the electrical one he had me land a couple of breakers with the power off, after he tested it, him standing right there. Probably why I liked it lol.', false, 4, '2026-09-28T01:46:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b32cdda8-807c-53ab-bb5b-1ef95670c1a1', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Ha, ''the attic was brutal'' is every HVAC guy''s August... respect for trying all three, most people never do lol', false, 6, '2026-09-28T03:36:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b6b88005-13b2-5dea-8f7b-43a1167c54c7', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', '566a4ee6-0294-5f38-93a7-c5e3a7297ddd', '35, woodbridge, ex-bartender, hvac helper now. reading this made me feel better about how i picked. the attic part is very real', false, 1, '2026-09-28T10:13:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d46083d0-3ef4-5fe6-aaab-1b9eee5ab216', '74e792e7-756d-59ca-b879-631f095b9182', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'Appreciate everyone. Not deciding yet: the HVAC startup day last Saturday threw me, more on that in its own post, and I''ll look at the low-voltage side once I know what I''m doing.

edit: two interviews set up already.', false, 2, '2026-09-28T12:33:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('36f036a9-7484-5ac5-bbdd-9b4c61278e14', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'discussion', 'Came in at 26 from restaurant management. Career switchers, ask me.', 'I get the same five questions from switchers, so I''ll take them here. Background: ran a restaurant for a few years, quit at 26, got hired as a helper by a plumber in Jersey City who needed someone who could handle customers. 17 years later I''m a master plumber with a three-person crew doing multifamily and co-ops in Hudson County. I''m not going to tell you it was easy or that it''ll work for you. I''ll tell you what happened to me. Ask.', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 20, '2026-08-10T00:44:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e804baf0-8d6f-5d05-b48b-38324108e70a', '36f036a9-7484-5ac5-bbdd-9b4c61278e14', '8498b67e-8832-52a9-854b-bbe6514f03b3', '36, bartending, woodbridge. how did you handle the pay cut the first year? that''s the whole thing for me', false, 2, '2026-08-10T03:22:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f705ce11-f9d8-5504-8083-804578fbf63d', '36f036a9-7484-5ac5-bbdd-9b4c61278e14', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Badly at first. I''d saved about six months of rent and burned through it in four. What saved me was picking up two shifts a week at a restaurant that first year. Know your number before you quit. Not after.', false, 6, '2026-08-10T23:01:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('951d4967-ca91-520f-a474-74706fc80b2c', '36f036a9-7484-5ac5-bbdd-9b4c61278e14', 'cbe525cf-5b87-54d7-b315-7c60d722e874', 'sorry if this is a dumb question but did anyone treat you differently for starting late? i''m 42 on staten island and i worry about that more than the work', false, 3, '2026-08-11T02:06:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('98df202c-050d-5206-9a1c-213f7c60a86a', '36f036a9-7484-5ac5-bbdd-9b4c61278e14', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Some did. Mostly younger guys who felt competition. The masters who hired me cared that I could talk to a building super without starting a fight. Your age is a skill there. Use it.', false, 3, '2026-08-12T00:22:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('36264ca7-aa38-55b0-921a-ebae07b36eac', '36f036a9-7484-5ac5-bbdd-9b4c61278e14', '9d863d1d-0f6f-5b8c-921d-d473f8721247', 'how long before you stopped feeling like the dumbest person on the job lol', false, 2, '2026-08-12T09:00:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('711f2a7a-affb-54be-ac91-537e7facfaad', '56ebe677-1060-5479-89c5-55faedf03943', 'question', 'How do I put together a resume for a helper job when it''s all bartending?', '40, Perth Amboy, bartending most of my adult life, managed a bar in South Amboy for six years. Taking a night class to test the waters before I quit.

When I start applying for helper jobs, what do I even put on a resume? I''ve got nothing trade-related except fixing stuff at the bar: replaced a few faucets, cleared the floor drains more times than I want to remember, helped the beer guy run new lines to the taps. Do shops even want a resume? Or do you just show up?

edit: thanks everyone, printing one page tonight.', 'other', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 13, '2026-08-17T02:51:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('11af4a37-3142-5f01-87d7-0b33c68fc92b', '711f2a7a-affb-54be-ac91-537e7facfaad', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I look for when I hire a switcher, and a resume is a small part of it. One page. Put the bar management job first and say what you were responsible for: opening and closing, staff, cash, handling problems. That tells me you''re reliable and can deal with people. Then one short line about the hands-on work. Bring it in person if you can, early morning, and ask for the owner. A lot of small shops don''t read email.', true, 15, '2026-08-18T00:40:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9ec0b142-c04c-5f83-8e7b-e4d45d6d1f95', '711f2a7a-affb-54be-ac91-537e7facfaad', '8498b67e-8832-52a9-854b-bbe6514f03b3', 'ex bartender too. i just walked in with a printed page at 7am. got hired at the second place. dont overthink it', false, 4, '2026-08-26T00:38:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9f5fde91-5ac5-5ac6-97a6-d6e466fd5a6c', '711f2a7a-affb-54be-ac91-537e7facfaad', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Bartenders make good helpers, I''ve had two. You already know how to keep a crowd calm and stay on your feet for ten hours. Say that. My father used to say the trade can be taught and the attitude can''t.', false, 14, '2026-08-26T01:38:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('095d138e-7884-566e-adf8-2d5d9f7f3ea3', '711f2a7a-affb-54be-ac91-537e7facfaad', '049e3011-0b6d-5ddf-ad0e-83e84339599a', 'call center to trades here. had the same question last month. one page, in person, worked for me.', false, 2, '2026-08-26T02:20:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('19e23ff0-5d56-5f5e-9866-005fc3fc90bb', 'ea9bf166-53e3-541b-9f3a-28d296966e19', 'question', '28, woman, calling plumbing shops in Gloucester County. Two hung up on me.', 'Left insurance claims a few weeks ago. Want to do plumbing. Have been calling shops around Glassboro and Pitman for a helper job. Two hung up after I said my name. One said they don''t really have a bathroom on the jobs, hon. One was nice and said call back in October. I know some of this is just shops being shops, but it''s hard not to take it personally. Any women here who got in this way? What worked? Should I just show up in person instead? Appreciate it.', 'plumbing', 'Gloucester County, NJ', 19, '2026-10-01T01:10:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('280de00b-2b9c-5deb-a6b7-51e4a5242787', '19e23ff0-5d56-5f5e-9866-005fc3fc90bb', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Show up in person. Early, in work clothes, with a one-page sheet. It''s harder to hang up on someone standing at your counter. I got the same comments at 26. The ones who said dumb things weren''t shops I wanted to work for anyway. The one who hired me cared that I came back twice. Call the nice one back in October like they said, and mention that you called before.', true, 12, '2026-10-01T16:05:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fe879ea1-5fd8-5410-8900-216f2573695e', '19e23ff0-5d56-5f5e-9866-005fc3fc90bb', 'af3fcb91-09e6-5441-8d3b-b76ecbc0192e', 'Burlington County, 3 years. The bathroom thing is so dumb, every job has a porta john or a Wawa down the road. Keep calling. There are good shops down here that hire women, mine''s one of them, they just don''t advertise it.

edit: also ask at the supply house counter. They know which shops are decent.', false, 2, '2026-10-01T17:43:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('820b253b-da3c-531c-8f82-a67ad7772b00', '19e23ff0-5d56-5f5e-9866-005fc3fc90bb', '07676d29-9e30-5e27-b903-f9044b52fe4b', 'plumbing, pleasantville, vo-tech grad. only girl in my class. got hired by the 4th shop i walked into. the first 3 were weird about it. keep going', false, 1, '2026-10-02T01:08:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('55bf4d4e-a525-5206-b433-f6cde088ddab', '19e23ff0-5d56-5f5e-9866-005fc3fc90bb', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'Deptford here. Appreciate you posting this. Were the ones that hung up small one-man outfits or bigger shops? Not asking for names. The bigger ones around here are usually better about it.', false, 2, '2026-10-02T10:30:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7a01681e-45c3-50e5-a9ee-173b46f4dd17', '19e23ff0-5d56-5f5e-9866-005fc3fc90bb', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'When you walk in, ask for the owner by name if it''s on the truck or the sign. My father hired two of his best people because they came in and asked for him, not for ''whoever''s hiring.''', false, 10, '2026-10-04T14:00:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('396656d8-0b46-5a0e-a011-a1b97929e772', '5a5af8e2-ab77-5d69-b65c-21d56be38ca8', 'question', 'can i try a trade part time on weekends before i quit my day job?', '34, voorhees, wife is supportive but honestly nervous about me taking a pay cut with a kid on the way. i work a desk job monday to friday that pays the bills. is there any way to do helper work on saturdays for a couple months to see if i even like it before i quit? or do shops not want part time guys? i''d do anything, carry stuff, clean up, whatever. not really looking for money, more like a test drive. thanks in advance', 'other', 'Camden County, NJ', 3, '2026-08-14T16:30:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('8db9346d-b07d-5acc-9848-c0cae5121a55', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'question', 'First real paycheck in the apprenticeship. What tools are actually worth buying now?', '1st year in Local 24, mostly commercial bathrooms so far. Got the tool list at the start and bought the basics. Now I''ve got a couple real paychecks and I''m tempted to go nuts at the big box store. What did you actually end up using every day in your first year that wasn''t on the list? And what''s a waste of money until later? I spend enough at Wawa already, trying to be smart about this.', 'plumbing', 'Essex County, NJ', 11, '2026-08-30T00:55:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('70ac721c-dfc9-5d03-b884-18f9562bd96d', '8db9346d-b07d-5acc-9848-c0cae5121a55', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, buy what you reach for, and borrow twice before you buy anything else. First year, you want good channel locks in two sizes, a decent tubing cutter, a level that isn''t junk, and a headlamp. Anything with a battery can wait until you know what your shop doesn''t supply. And put your initials on all of it. Things walk on commercial jobs. That''s the job.', true, 10, '2026-08-30T03:27:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2c28aa06-79a7-5ebc-8fc7-f59030277b3e', '8db9346d-b07d-5acc-9848-c0cae5121a55', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First, a good headlamp. Second, knee pads you''ll actually wear. Third, a tape measure you like holding. Students always skip the knee pads and regret it by 30. Ask me how I know.', false, 3, '2026-08-30T10:13:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('73c21aaa-25ac-5a60-b68e-c50f9485f281', '8db9346d-b07d-5acc-9848-c0cae5121a55', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Different trade, same rule: buy safety glasses you''ll actually keep on your face. If they fog or pinch, you''ll take them off, and that''s when something finds your eye. Spend money there first. Stay safe.', false, 2, '2026-08-31T01:06:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('392c86a4-0c8d-5871-aab0-1b5c92b47b1f', '8db9346d-b07d-5acc-9848-c0cae5121a55', '2f048a7b-273e-574a-911a-7232a6136051', '4 yrs in, my biggest waste was a fancy cordless set i bought my first year when the shop already had everything on the trucks. dont do that lol', false, 4, '2026-08-31T09:02:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d8814428-5d4a-5b1a-a9e4-fc841c06caa4', '8db9346d-b07d-5acc-9848-c0cae5121a55', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'brother get a decent bucket organizer and stop carrying stuff in your pockets. took me 6 months to learn that one', false, 2, '2026-08-31T10:29:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('033a1163-a20f-5745-b09e-d586a6daebd1', '8db9346d-b07d-5acc-9848-c0cae5121a55', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'Okay so headlamp, knee pads, glasses, initials on everything, and no battery stuff yet. My wallet thanks you guys.', false, 1, '2026-08-31T12:54:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', '02a13f50-be86-588b-966d-7ae10b7d64cd', 'question', 'New kid at my shop showed up in running sneakers. What boots do I tell him to get?', 'So we hired a new helper last week... nice kid, 18, straight out of school... and he shows up to a basement in Hackensack in white running sneakers. Boss sent him to buy boots on his lunch and he came back with the cheapest pair in the store, which I get, he doesn''t have money yet. I''m two years in so the boss told me to ''help him out.'' What do you all tell a brand new guy about boots? Steel toe vs composite, waterproof, do they need to be 8 inch... and is there a budget pair that won''t wreck his feet by October? I already bought him a Wawa coffee, I''m not buying him boots lol', 'hvac', 'Bergen County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-24T09:23:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('059fc7ba-978d-53dc-b8a7-253a760eb63c', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Waterproof, safety toe, good sole, and comfortable enough that he doesn''t take them off at lunch. The cheap ones are fine for a month while he figures out what his feet hate. Then he buys a real pair. Tell him to try them on at the end of the day when his feet are swollen.', false, 7, '2026-09-25T00:43:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('006c5e48-7cac-5106-b579-346a9f0b3d66', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'If he''ll be anywhere near electrical work, look for the EH (electrical hazard) rating on the label, and check whether your shop or the GC has a site rule on safety toes; commercial sites usually do. Composite toe is lighter and doesn''t get as cold in winter. Beyond that, fit matters more than brand. A boot that''s half a size wrong ruins a ten-hour day. Stay safe.', false, 3, '2026-09-25T02:19:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5745588e-c1b0-5618-a928-16d62ee023b2', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'I''m still in school so I can''t speak to brands, but our shop teacher made everybody buy boots the first week and said the same thing about trying them on at the end of the day. I got mine at a store on Route 23 in Wayne. Sorry, I''m over-explaining again, it''s a habit.', false, 1, '2026-09-25T10:24:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('987f5980-5f7d-55f3-997f-16c15467abae', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First, safety toe. Second, a sole that grips a wet basement floor, because that''s where he''ll live all winter. Third, wool-blend socks, two pairs. Students blame the boot when it''s really the cotton socks. Ask me how I know.', false, 11, '2026-09-25T12:45:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('673f8336-6421-5b01-80c1-be38c69e0c59', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'waterproof. he will stand in a walk-in drain pan at some point. july or january, doesn''t matter, wet feet all day is the worst', false, 2, '2026-09-27T20:16:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('17914540-e182-5353-b807-11b69dc58d84', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'sorry if this is dumb but do the 8 inch ones actually matter or is 6 fine? i got 6 and my ankles are fine so far. thanks in advance', false, 1, '2026-09-27T23:24:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('22d1b87c-e81a-51b9-b8a7-cef3d13d24fe', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', '8 inch if he''s on ladders or uneven ground a lot. 6 is fine for bathrooms. That''s just what my journeyman told me.', false, 4, '2026-09-27T23:58:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ba43d628-ca0b-501d-92fe-f91278e5bb71', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'clifton, under a year in. i got the cheap ones at first like your kid and my feet were destroyed by the end of august. switched to a better pair and it was definately like a different job. tell him to save up for it, it''s the first thing worth spending on', false, 1, '2026-09-28T03:28:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d8ea515c-a12e-53ca-acc6-e25aec45340a', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'idk why everyone sleeps on insoles. cheap boots plus a good insole gets you through till payday', false, 3, '2026-09-28T10:28:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6027e277-1232-5d95-aa65-91236e75edf6', 'dbd9fc84-817f-5f07-97a2-a0296f3442e4', '02a13f50-be86-588b-966d-7ae10b7d64cd', 'This is great... sending him the thread lol. Insoles plus the cheap ones for now, real pair by October... thanks all', false, 2, '2026-09-28T10:34:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('ad4e6f1f-d989-53a4-9c4a-062ae4428952', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'question', 'Starting at a new shop Monday after 3 years at the cash place. What should I bring?', 'Took Rui''s advice from my cash-pay thread. Lined up a new shop in Pitman before I gave notice, left on good terms, start Monday. Real payroll, they do service and boilers, five minutes off 55. Three years in, but I''ve never started somewhere new as anything but a kid. What do I bring day one? My own tools or wait and see? And how do I handle it if they treat me like a first-year when I''m not?', 'plumbing', 'Gloucester County, NJ', 8, '2026-09-21T01:18:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('12292730-6084-5897-a9ef-5d93e8e92551', 'ad4e6f1f-d989-53a4-9c4a-062ae4428952', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Congratulations on doing it the right way. Bring your hand tools, clean and organized, and your PPE. Leave the big stuff home until you see what''s on the trucks. On the first-year thing: expect it for a week or two. They need to see how you work before they hand you anything. Show them, don''t tell them. Ask on day one who you report to and what they expect by the end of the first month. Stay safe.', true, 19, '2026-09-21T23:50:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('37a3fb4f-435d-556b-ba38-587330d7f90e', 'ad4e6f1f-d989-53a4-9c4a-062ae4428952', '9d863d1d-0f6f-5b8c-921d-d473f8721247', 'congrats. also pack a lunch the first week, you never know where you''ll end up lol', false, 1, '2026-09-22T09:30:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7bc32933-55d0-5892-9c31-2d526564c035', 'ad4e6f1f-d989-53a4-9c4a-062ae4428952', '5ea91175-1b81-51fb-918c-7ad563230535', 'Congrats... I''m way behind you but this is the kind of update I like reading... good luck Monday', false, 3, '2026-09-22T10:36:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('930c674e-7a71-52fe-bdb8-8246694ee528', 'ad4e6f1f-d989-53a4-9c4a-062ae4428952', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'same thing when I started in Local 1 after doing non-union stuff for a summer. they made me prove it for a couple weeks then it was fine. don''t get offended, just be good lol', false, 2, '2026-09-22T11:13:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'discussion', 'Worst tool you ever bought as an apprentice?', '4th year in 164... cleaning out my tool bag this weekend and found a ''professional'' 47-piece screwdriver set I bought my first month. Used two of them. Ever. My foreman laughed at me then and he''s still laughing. What''s the worst tool you bought when you were starting out... so the first-years reading this don''t make the same mistake. Appreciate it', 'electrical', 'Bergen County, NJ', 17, '2026-09-19T18:45:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('4f36ddef-cdf7-53b7-a30f-93b9e2a9a376', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'A pipe threader I bought used from a guy in Lodi my second year. Weighed more than me, I used it twice, and it sat in my mother''s garage for a decade. Kid, rent the big stuff.', false, 2, '2026-09-20T02:44:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b407f2f3-30c9-5e69-aedb-0e47e5f29757', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'A cheap non-contact voltage tester. It told me a circuit was dead when it wasn''t. I learned to test with a meter I trust, and to check the tester on a known live source before and after. That one isn''t funny; buy the good meter.', false, 6, '2026-09-20T02:51:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4bccccff-522b-5eb5-b6af-5d5205151462', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'that''s the one my foreman yells about too... test the tester first', false, 1, '2026-09-20T10:25:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f1f6d5ce-a7a0-5d21-bfd7-a5d49ba3c0b4', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'Sorry if this is a dumb one, but a ''universal'' refrigerant gauge set from an online deal. The hoses leaked from day one.', false, 2, '2026-09-20T11:19:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3d2227a0-fea3-56bc-9e81-06d74d7a39a0', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First place goes to the students who buy the giant rolling toolbox before they''ve had one day on a job. Second place, anything with ''kit'' in the name. Ask me how I know: I bought both.', false, 2, '2026-09-21T02:27:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1f132484-22b7-58e5-b7df-522dd7b9df5d', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'a ''contractor grade'' drill from a discount bin. smoked in a week drilling a joist in paterson, brother. never again', false, 2, '2026-09-21T09:41:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('054f425f-571d-5b19-a682-bb3be031a2e8', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', 'cee246a3-b9ec-55fd-8ac0-35c06eeed07f', 'a big fancy wire stripper with like eight functions because a video said it was the only one you''d ever need, and my journeyman just uses a basic pair and a knife, and now i do too', false, 1, '2026-09-21T12:36:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('46e11ec3-5e7f-5d70-9bb9-be1a8dd386a6', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'sorry if this is dumb but is a conduit bender worth buying yourself or does the shop always have them? mine always does but i keep seeing guys with their own. thanks in advance', false, 2, '2026-09-21T12:43:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('120db23b-d6a6-59b3-8519-4a7560e64ad6', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'shop should have benders... buy your own once you know which size you bend the most. appreciate it', false, 2, '2026-09-21T19:33:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e06b04b4-27c7-50e1-886f-681c05b11191', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'a headlamp so bright it blinded the guy I was working with every time I looked at him lol. Union City basements are dark but not that dark', false, 1, '2026-09-26T10:13:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('65bafdd7-55b7-5674-a9d0-0184b82411e8', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly a $300 laser level my first year, to hang a few fixtures straight in Asbury. A $15 torpedo level did the same job. Learn on the cheap version first.', false, 10, '2026-09-26T13:18:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6e999f31-42e2-5b83-8847-2390f912a4b3', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'a label maker. kidding, the label maker is the best tool i own. fwiw every low voltage guy will tell you that', false, 5, '2026-09-26T16:10:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5c0bf3d3-2ba4-519e-af6e-cc6af7bb5dd8', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'A ''pro'' drain snake from the big box store. Kinked the first day lol. Now I use the shop machine.', false, 2, '2026-09-26T18:19:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('735de83d-bb76-5272-863a-df64880500d6', '1cd7897d-1c2b-542e-9ec1-ce151fea551e', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'this thread is going to save me money. was literally about to buy a 40 piece screwdriver set. appreciate it, thanks in advance for more', false, 2, '2026-09-26T19:05:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('4e5ec037-22fc-5080-b018-c7004345e20f', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'question', 'Got called for the Local 3 interview after a year of waiting. What do they look for?', 'Apex grad, working non-union in the Bronx for two years while I waited. I got the letter this week: I have an interview. I have been preparing with my mentor here, but I want to hear from more people.

What did your interview look like? What do they want to hear from someone who already has some field experience? I do not want to sound like I know everything, but I also do not want to undersell the two years I put in. Appreciate any advice.

edit: interview is Monday, not next week. I misread the letter.', 'electrical', 'Bronx, NY', 8, '2026-09-11T02:01:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('80decf41-2167-5849-89d2-a80a1c2d7065', '4e5ec037-22fc-5080-b018-c7004345e20f', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, you already know what I think, but for everyone else reading: the format changes, so I''m talking about what matters, not what the room looks like.

Be on time. Dress clean and simple. Answer the question they asked. When they ask about your year, give one real job start to finish and one mistake you made and what you learned. Don''t trash your current shop. And leave an hour early, the trains have been a disaster.', true, 18, '2026-09-13T20:15:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('26000940-94dd-5c78-b9aa-777e06c972fd', '4e5ec037-22fc-5080-b018-c7004345e20f', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'Good luck. Please post how it goes, I''m a year or two behind you.', false, 2, '2026-09-13T22:18:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f60ee285-f2a3-54d3-bad0-fcd34e4f90d6', '4e5ec037-22fc-5080-b018-c7004345e20f', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fwiw i interviewed for a different program years ago and the thing that helped most was having a couple of questions for them at the end. shows you care what happens after you get in', false, 3, '2026-09-14T00:10:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fbebdf3d-38e6-558e-98aa-e8797091c1fd', '4e5ec037-22fc-5080-b018-c7004345e20f', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'sorry if this is dumb but do they ask technical questions or just about you? asking for when i apply in jersey. thanks in advance', false, 2, '2026-09-14T01:42:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('14c5b8d0-0cdd-5cc9-8f1f-732a324c18b8', '4e5ec037-22fc-5080-b018-c7004345e20f', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'From what people told me, mostly about you and your work, but I am not sure. I will report back after.', false, 3, '2026-09-14T09:37:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c27c5d96-e7d5-5c0a-bd03-8a3ea1f865e7', '4e5ec037-22fc-5080-b018-c7004345e20f', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different in a lot of ways, but an interview is an interview everywhere. I hire helpers for my shop, and what I always remember is whether they could explain something simple clearly. Practice explaining a job out loud to someone who isn''t in the trade.', false, 2, '2026-09-14T23:09:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f68af5f9-922a-5cee-bbc6-ff7cef59566b', '4e5ec037-22fc-5080-b018-c7004345e20f', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'Army guy here, interviews are just inspections with chairs. Clean shoes, short answers. Idk if that translates but it worked for every job interview I''ve had.', false, 1, '2026-09-15T02:13:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b5a7bdb8-fe22-55c7-a3c7-887e7777cb64', '4e5ec037-22fc-5080-b018-c7004345e20f', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'update: had it. Mine felt like mostly questions about my work and why electrical. I talked about a service change we did in Throggs Neck and the time I mislabeled a panel. Felt okay. Now I wait again. Appreciate everyone here, and dreb especially.', false, 2, '2026-09-15T09:12:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('05e30a35-301f-5c1b-b3db-c0c8f1acf9ff', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'question', 'Parents want college. Would City Tech''s electrical program count for anything with Local 3?', 'So, some background so this makes sense. I''m in the electrical program at a trade high school in Queens (I live in Bay Ridge, so it''s a long ride every morning). My shop teacher keeps pushing the union application. My parents want me to go to college, period. I found out City Tech in downtown Brooklyn has electrical-type associate degrees, and I''m wondering if that''s a middle ground that makes everybody happy. Would a degree like that help a Local 3 application, or would I just be two years older applying with the same chances? Has anyone done City Tech and then gone union? Thanks in advance.', 'electrical', 'Brooklyn, NY', 7, '2026-07-24T22:54:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'discussion', 'Local 1, Local 3, Local 638: how did you actually get in? Roll call', 'Since everybody keeps asking me how I got into Local 1 like I''m some expert lol. I''m a first year. I got in, I don''t fully know why, and I''m not going to pretend I know how it works this year. So let''s just do a roll call. If you''re in Local 1, Local 3, Local 638, or you tried and didn''t get in, say how it went for you: how many tries, what you were doing before, what you''d tell somebody applying now. Non-union people welcome too, half of Brooklyn is non-union and doing fine. No ''my uncle said'' stories, only what happened to you.', 'other', 'Brooklyn, NY', 10, '2026-09-21T00:39:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('7684d1f9-7e52-5c74-8b84-c42e68439541', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Local 3, 21 years. Got in on my first try after two years with a small contractor in Queens. Different world back then. What I''d tell anyone now: follow the official site and nobody else, and keep working while you wait.', false, 4, '2026-09-21T02:28:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8cac0acf-4895-59f1-a039-0a46b3b870ad', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'ccf9dc60-958f-5461-ad1b-ad7dd180a037', 'non union apprentice in flatbush... applied to 3 twice, didn''t get in either time... still at it, brother. thanks in advance to anyone with tips for a third try', false, 2, '2026-09-21T03:07:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('61ffbbca-884d-5195-ab74-afa01cbbb33a', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'Apex grad, working non-union in the Bronx, and I had my Local 3 interview last week. Waiting on results. Appreciate the roll call idea.', false, 1, '2026-09-21T03:12:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2ec2b335-15e8-50ad-8045-be9d8f45dc3f', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'good luck man, post when you hear, we''re all rooting for you', false, 2, '2026-09-21T09:04:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ae8e7a86-7f1d-5de3-a293-82a5b14a0ec1', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different from what people assume: a lot of the gas and brownstone work in Brooklyn is done by non-union shops like mine. 26 years, never union, licensed master, no regrets. The union is a great path. It isn''t the only one.', false, 3, '2026-09-21T14:13:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3ed3da69-60c3-51ff-8c44-1c8a6893f142', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'Jersey side but same idea: UA Local 24, first year, first try. I think timing and luck were a big part of it. Commercial bathrooms all day lol', false, 1, '2026-09-21T16:02:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('346ecbf3-1fc6-50c2-a5a1-c92a7dc1878a', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'Local 24 first year, third try. Ranked low the first two times.', false, 2, '2026-09-21T17:55:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6aa326a4-16e0-5f55-9620-72a9b5465ecf', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', '393b9bbb-e88d-53b5-be6e-c1c847014fa4', 'Apex grad, plumbing. Applied to Local 1, waiting. Working service and drain calls out of Canarsie meanwhile. My foreman says don''t hold my breath.', false, 1, '2026-09-21T19:38:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c2f512a0-b6c6-5888-a0dd-704a207e666c', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'Army, then a non-union helper job in Ozone Park, 35 now. Haven''t applied yet. Idk if I''m too old for the list, brother.', false, 2, '2026-09-21T22:54:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c20bd23e-8021-5cb4-8e1f-9b385520783c', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Not too old. We''ve had plenty of guys start in their 30s. Check the age rules on the official site, don''t guess.', false, 3, '2026-09-21T23:11:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1160f93e-665d-51c1-a532-89abf388ebfd', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'b8fa619e-10c3-53ee-8438-f4471618c6ee', '34, Bronx, left a desk job. Working for a non-union plumber in Fordham. My mentor on here says non-union in the city can be a good career too, and so far he''s right.', false, 2, '2026-09-22T00:13:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('453ad132-7072-59ab-82cb-2e7e0eca1e3c', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', '48b61243-8eaf-5f00-b8aa-9268dc17b5af', 'staten island, non-union helper out of tottenville. applied to 3 once, didn''t get the call. trying again. boss says the ferry commute would kill me anyway lol brother', false, 3, '2026-09-22T02:06:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b9fea796-6a83-5ffd-9beb-d615c4a93206', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'Jersey guy reading along... 164, got in on the second try. same lesson as everyone, keep working while you wait', false, 3, '2026-09-22T02:19:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('42bedc57-6fb6-5d70-b352-f130f0391153', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'cbe525cf-5b87-54d7-b315-7c60d722e874', '42, staten island, helper at a non-union shop. wasn''t even going to try the union at my age, but this thread has me wondering if i should. sorry if that''s a dumb thing to say', false, 1, '2026-09-22T10:10:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a5421c8d-14ab-595c-aef3-89b2885d91a0', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'not dumb. guys in my class are all ages. call and ask, worst case they say no lol', false, 1, '2026-09-22T21:28:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e7f5a8ba-39ac-5e25-bb59-ac2e90cad37f', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'Trade high school kid from Bay Ridge here, haven''t applied to anything yet, just reading every single one of these and taking notes, sorry for over-explaining, but it''s really useful to see how different everyone''s path was. Thanks in advance to everyone who posted.', false, 3, '2026-09-22T23:35:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f8310562-d78f-5bf0-9762-b1545fb1acb2', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'Same as the Bay Ridge kid. Still in school in Queens, reading all of this. There''s a Local 3 guy on here who answers everybody, so I''m getting a lot of good advice already.', false, 3, '2026-09-23T09:45:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d00bb75e-6bbb-5f7d-b494-281989016324', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'Bayonne, non-union helper, about a year in. Haven''t applied anywhere yet. Reading every one of these before I do, brother.', false, 1, '2026-09-26T23:30:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7e2fba30-3b0e-5614-806b-7d66ebbbd819', 'ac4670e5-b2d4-5833-9cb3-3100e1b27014', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'This blew up lol. Thanks everybody. Short version from all of you: keep working, apply anyway, check the official site, and non-union is real too.', false, 2, '2026-09-27T10:01:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('2874ad19-aa79-514a-8aac-a06236f2e60b', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'question', 'Could I apply to a Jersey IBEW local instead of Local 3? Aunt lives in North Bergen', 'Queens kid, still in an electrical program. Local 3 is the dream but everybody knows how hard it is. My aunt lives in North Bergen and said I could stay with her after I graduate.

Dreb already told me jurisdiction is a "call them and ask" thing, which I will. But for the Jersey people: if I moved to Hudson County, would I just apply to whatever local covers there like anybody else? Is it dumb to move states for an apprenticeship? My foreman on weekends says I''m overthinking it.

edit: not trying to skip the line anywhere, just want options.', 'electrical', 'Queens, NY', 10, '2026-09-28T23:58:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('f493bdee-88e3-548a-859a-0b44cf17bc10', '2874ad19-aa79-514a-8aac-a06236f2e60b', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', '164 2nd year, Teaneck... I''m pretty sure Hudson is 164 too but please call and check, don''t go off me. A couple of guys in my class moved here from out of state... it''s not dumb if you''re actually going to live here. Thanks in advance for updating us', false, 4, '2026-09-29T10:14:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7f93babf-729a-5a8c-9096-2a5c59d015c0', '2874ad19-aa79-514a-8aac-a06236f2e60b', 'fe2e3539-023d-5301-8ea8-24dd54954171', 'I''m in the Hudson County vo-tech and I live in North Bergen, so this is my town lol. Your aunt''s neighborhood is fine, close to the buses into the city too if you change your mind, sorry I''m over-explaining, but parking is terrible here, don''t bring a car.', false, 1, '2026-09-29T11:46:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ef6421f4-c609-5336-b2a6-9f818d7e952c', '2874ad19-aa79-514a-8aac-a06236f2e60b', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'I grew up in Jersey and work in Brooklyn, so I''ve lived both sides. In the city it''s different on licensing, on unions, on everything down to the permits. If you move, commit to Jersey for the long run. As far as I know apprenticeships don''t move easily between locals, and your career grows where you train.', false, 3, '2026-09-29T22:37:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('37f8e2e4-43fb-57df-b7e9-1bcc0d006d0f', '2874ad19-aa79-514a-8aac-a06236f2e60b', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'What I said before, brother: call and ask. And whichever side you pick, half my guys come through the tunnels every day and complain about it every day. You''ll be fine.', false, 1, '2026-09-29T23:21:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7da4dc87-9839-5b36-a37d-040d0d4fa360', '2874ad19-aa79-514a-8aac-a06236f2e60b', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'Mercer kid, totally different part of the state, but my cousin moved from Philly to Trenton for the same reason, and he said the local wanted proof he actually lived here, a lease or bills in his name or something like that, I don''t remember exactly. So if you do it, do it for real and keep your paperwork.', false, 1, '2026-09-29T23:58:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5193f868-4276-5da0-a22a-5f7919c12897', '2874ad19-aa79-514a-8aac-a06236f2e60b', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'Nutley, Essex vo-tech. Same boat but the other way around, I keep thinking about Local 3. Grass is greener I guess.', false, 2, '2026-09-30T01:54:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e77bf3d3-a79f-5dc4-91aa-80792d2b056a', '2874ad19-aa79-514a-8aac-a06236f2e60b', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'Makes sense. Going to call both and ask about residency before I say anything to my aunt. Thanks all.', false, 1, '2026-09-30T02:07:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('21cee5c5-b02c-53be-813b-768cbdea3e28', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'question', 'What kind of math is on the aptitude test, and how did you study?', 'Getting ready for the Local 3 application whenever it opens next. I''m okay at math but not great. What was actually on the aptitude test when you took it? Algebra? Reading? Mechanical stuff? And what did you use to study? My shop teacher has an old practice packet but it''s from like 2015 and half the pages are photocopies of photocopies.', 'electrical', 'Queens, NY', 22, '2026-09-18T16:40:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('ffa1729b-5730-54bc-91ec-df5c27dc95d7', '21cee5c5-b02c-53be-813b-768cbdea3e28', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, mine was math and reading, 21 years ago, so don''t plan around my memory. Look at what the official site says the test covers now, and if they name a test or a practice guide, use that one. Then do algebra and fractions until it''s boring. Work on reading speed too; people run out of time.', true, 24, '2026-09-20T18:45:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9e5c26b1-b96d-509c-81a1-c6a45fc470aa', '21cee5c5-b02c-53be-813b-768cbdea3e28', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'I''m in New Jersey and haven''t taken one yet, but our shop teacher in Wayne had us do practice algebra and reading comprehension out of a library book for civil service and apprenticeship tests. I''m over-explaining, but the library route is free, which my parents appreciated.', false, 4, '2026-09-20T20:01:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3fe8b456-47e5-5d7c-b3bf-8946c243073a', '21cee5c5-b02c-53be-813b-768cbdea3e28', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'never took one, went straight to a shop. idk if that helps but you dont need the test to have a career lol', false, 2, '2026-09-20T20:59:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6171f317-c307-5c66-a3e1-da9c609e049f', '21cee5c5-b02c-53be-813b-768cbdea3e28', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'The shop teacher down the hall from mine has a newer packet I think, I''ll ask him which room and tell you, sorry if that''s over-explaining, thanks in advance', false, 1, '2026-09-27T19:59:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('a7bbf204-0302-55de-9a8d-25d3da026c6d', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'discussion', 'Hiring two first-year apprentices this fall. Ask me what I look for.', 'I run a mechanical company in Burlington County: HVAC and plumbing, mostly schools and warehouses, a lot of it prevailing-wage public work. I hire apprentices every year and this fall I need two. I''m not posting a job here, and I won''t take applications through this site. But I get asked the same questions every time I interview, so ask them here and I''ll answer honestly. Fair warning: our jobs are on public schools, so there''s certified payroll, background checks, and early starts. That isn''t for everyone, and that''s fine.', 'hvac', 'Burlington County, NJ', 23, '2026-08-12T03:00:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('4da6a270-e588-5606-ab25-60a94b3fb903', 'a7bbf204-0302-55de-9a8d-25d3da026c6d', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'Camden County vo-tech grad, 2 years in... what''s the biggest reason you don''t hire someone after the interview? edit: or don''t keep them after the first month', false, 1, '2026-08-12T09:35:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('368f9d70-5f11-5d66-864b-10c1e65853e1', 'a7bbf204-0302-55de-9a8d-25d3da026c6d', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Interview: they can''t tell me why they want this trade, or they badmouth their last boss. First month: lateness. I''ll teach anybody who''s there at 6. I can''t teach someone who isn''t.', false, 5, '2026-08-12T14:56:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6b6d6330-6036-5bce-ab89-57e068c8c944', 'a7bbf204-0302-55de-9a8d-25d3da026c6d', '5ea91175-1b81-51fb-918c-7ad563230535', '33, Cherry Hill, left a warehouse... doing the county HVAC night classes but no field experience at all... would you even look at someone like me? Thanks in advance', false, 2, '2026-08-12T18:23:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('974fe93f-0b26-57b0-af6b-01111492d3a7', 'a7bbf204-0302-55de-9a8d-25d3da026c6d', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Yes. Warehouse people know how to work a shift and follow a safety rule. Get your driver''s license squared away if it isn''t, take an OSHA 10 if you can, and apply. That''s more than a lot of applicants bring.', false, 2, '2026-08-12T21:01:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('672f3776-0723-5b17-a1ef-8e1055ec6068', 'a7bbf204-0302-55de-9a8d-25d3da026c6d', 'af3fcb91-09e6-5441-8d3b-b76ecbc0192e', 'Burlington County here too. Can confirm the 6am thing is real, I''ve driven past school job sites around Mount Laurel at 5:45 and the trucks are already there lol', false, 3, '2026-08-13T02:34:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('dd5d5b7d-5f80-5dcb-bb59-d14907494cb4', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'discussion', 'low voltage is a way in, and nobody at the vo-tech ever mentions it', 'small rant, then useful info. every year i meet vo-tech kids who''ve only heard about two options: line-voltage electrician, union or non-union. nobody tells them about building automation, fire alarm, security, data.

i''ve been in bms and fire alarm 14 years, somerset and middlesex mostly. it''s a real trade. you still need to understand electricity, you still work under codes and permits, and in nj fire alarm work has its own licensing as far as i know, so check what applies to the work you''d be doing.

the pay is fine, a lot of the work is indoors, and your knees last longer. fwiw if you like troubleshooting more than pulling wire, look at it. ask me anything.', 'electrical', 'Somerset County, NJ', 17, '2026-09-22T22:09:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('85336706-0d8f-599e-817c-c156eb51c3d7', 'dd5d5b7d-5f80-5dcb-bb59-d14907494cb4', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'this is me, 3 years non-union in garfield doing emt and bending and i like the troubleshooting part way more. how do you even get hired into controls with no controls experience? appreciate it', false, 1, '2026-09-23T03:11:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f5bc02a5-f89c-5ef4-a395-469982185435', 'dd5d5b7d-5f80-5dcb-bb59-d14907494cb4', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'a lot of integrators hire installers from line-voltage shops because you already know how to be on a site. call the controls companies near you and ask if they take apprentices or installers. fwiw the first year is a lot of pulling cable and labeling, same as anywhere', false, 2, '2026-09-24T01:40:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3c4aa60e-6856-58c1-a4ce-1b176560be02', 'dd5d5b7d-5f80-5dcb-bb59-d14907494cb4', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Agree it''s a real trade, and plenty of our journeymen end up in controls. One gentle correction for the kids reading, though: don''t skip the line-voltage fundamentals to get there. The best controls people I''ve worked with could also wire a motor starter. Learn both if you can. Stay safe.', false, 8, '2026-09-24T09:44:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7eb9c183-a5ee-5b56-99b7-5fede8a0bfe4', 'dd5d5b7d-5f80-5dcb-bb59-d14907494cb4', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fair, marcus, i agree with that. the best ones can do both', false, 3, '2026-09-25T01:56:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ef91e968-208e-5a6e-a05f-546a94d22419', 'dd5d5b7d-5f80-5dcb-bb59-d14907494cb4', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'residential remodels in manahawkin, 1 year. never heard of bms until this post. is there any of that work down the shore or is it all up north', false, 2, '2026-09-25T10:21:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('2db1faa8-f6b3-5aff-903f-e78df36b5e07', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'tip', 'Before application season: get your paperwork together now, not the week it opens', 'Every year I watch people scramble for documents the week an application opens. Don''t be that person.

I can''t tell you what any specific program requires; each apprenticeship posts its own list, and you should go by that. But in my experience the usual suspects are proof of age, your high school diploma or equivalent, sometimes a transcript, a driver''s license, and for veterans, discharge paperwork. Some of those take weeks to get.

Request your transcript now. Find your birth certificate now. If your license is suspended, deal with it now. None of this is exciting. All of it has cost people a year. Stay safe.', 'electrical', 'Morris County, NJ', 11, '2026-08-04T22:58:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('488357cc-e7ad-5eb5-bce1-fbbcac460af6', '2db1faa8-f6b3-5aff-903f-e78df36b5e07', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'This is timely. I had no idea where my high school diploma was. I graduated in 2008. Requested a copy this morning.', false, 1, '2026-08-05T01:10:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('560d773c-e2f5-59cb-ab77-088508e568b9', '2db1faa8-f6b3-5aff-903f-e78df36b5e07', 'a500e8c1-fe10-5f2f-a33e-6f510dd05201', 'UA Local 9, 3rd year. Agree on the transcript, mine took almost a month to come from my old school. Thanks in advance to whoever reads this and starts now.', false, 1, '2026-08-05T10:39:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('43d8a61b-5e9b-54f6-b8b8-1a83ecf19a76', '2db1faa8-f6b3-5aff-903f-e78df36b5e07', 'ac073e3f-468a-564a-9831-abbcb2c2a679', 'sorry, dumb question... does a vo-tech certificate count as the diploma or is that separate', false, 2, '2026-08-05T17:56:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4a15506c-7e03-555b-80e6-9ca51ec8a4ad', '2db1faa8-f6b3-5aff-903f-e78df36b5e07', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Not dumb. They''re usually separate; the diploma is the high school credential, and the vo-tech certificate is extra. Bring both. Check the program''s list to be sure.', false, 11, '2026-08-05T21:09:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d0250eef-c664-5be0-b982-6040a141d1c2', '44b08815-50e0-53ab-b9bd-7782549d0da7', 'question', 'No car and no license yet. Can I still get hired as a helper?', 'Vo-tech student in Newark, haven''t picked a trade yet. Want a summer and weekend helper job. Problem: I don''t have my license yet (road test is in September) and I don''t have a car. Every listing says valid driver''s license required. Is that a dealbreaker? Could I get to a shop on the bus and ride with the crew? My friend''s dad is a foreman for a builder and he says no shop will take me. I work at a Wawa right now so I need to know if it''s worth trying.', 'other', 'Essex County, NJ', 8, '2026-08-09T00:08:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('c62dd2e3-b75a-5cbb-a79c-c825ff860efa', 'd0250eef-c664-5be0-b982-6040a141d1c2', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, a lot of shops want the license because you''ll drive the van eventually, and their insurance cares. But if you show up at the shop at 6:30 every day on the bus, somebody will notice. Get the license in September. That''s the job.', false, 5, '2026-08-09T02:23:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('45dbdec7-afa3-564c-9818-e4469da20dda', 'd0250eef-c664-5be0-b982-6040a141d1c2', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'I hired a kid once who took two buses from Newark to Kearny every morning for a year before he got his license. Best helper I had that decade. My father would have hired him on the spot too. Ask shops near a bus line, and tell them your road test date.', false, 4, '2026-08-09T02:46:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b1fc2cb4-7ceb-5337-82c5-4166f0a4a8ae', 'd0250eef-c664-5be0-b982-6040a141d1c2', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'no car here either my first 4 months in union city lol. boss picked me up at the light rail some days. it works if you''re close to the shop', false, 2, '2026-08-09T09:06:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('7e901570-94ed-5311-b9b2-99e3775ed1ae', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'question', 'Do union apprenticeships drug test now that weed is legal in Jersey?', 'Asking for real, not trying to be funny lol. I''m at a non-union shop in Union City, nobody''s ever tested me. Thinking about applying to the IBEW next year. I smoke sometimes on weekends, it''s legal now. Do they test before you start? Random? Does legal even matter for that? Not looking for a lecture, just want to know what I''m walking into so I''m not dumb about it.', 'electrical', 'Hudson County, NJ', 11, '2026-08-02T23:09:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('52a8bd03-13c7-50d6-90e2-50e810f6c39e', '7e901570-94ed-5311-b9b2-99e3775ed1ae', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Fair question, no lecture. I can''t speak to any program''s current policy; ask them directly or read their application materials.

From the job side: a lot of the sites we work on, especially big commercial and data centers, have their own testing rules regardless of state law, and contractors follow the site''s rules. Legal at home doesn''t mean allowed on a site. If you want the job, plan as if you''ll be tested. You''re working around energized equipment. Stay safe.', true, 12, '2026-08-03T02:31:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cd0d0a8f-47ad-579a-b462-f9c3edb2c471', '7e901570-94ed-5311-b9b2-99e3775ed1ae', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: state law on cannabis and an employer''s safety policy are two different questions, and the second one is the one that decides whether you work on Monday.', false, 9, '2026-08-03T03:54:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2fc40b4d-507c-58f3-b0e8-23587fbc5563', '7e901570-94ed-5311-b9b2-99e3775ed1ae', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'Union City too. My shop tested me at hiring four years ago. Just depends on the shop lol.', false, 1, '2026-08-03T09:59:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2ae76e3d-145e-51bb-a9e7-c51c461e2550', '7e901570-94ed-5311-b9b2-99e3775ed1ae', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'idk about the union but every gc site i''ve been on in passaic county had a policy posted in the trailer. read it', false, 2, '2026-08-03T12:31:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('9217873d-c7e2-5c9f-b705-dc9afa73228b', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'question', 'How do I explain to my parents that the trades aren''t a step down?', 'This needs some background. I''m in the electrical program at the Passaic County vo-tech, and I''m good at it. My parents are both accountants in Wayne and they want me to go to a four-year college. They''re not mean about it, they just think trades are what you do if college doesn''t work out.

I want to apply to an apprenticeship and work. I''ve tried explaining, but I end up sounding like a kid who doesn''t want to study. How did any of you have this conversation with your parents? What actually convinced them, if anything did?

I''m writing this from the Wawa parking lot on Hamburg Turnpike because I didn''t want to have this argument again tonight.', 'electrical', 'Passaic County, NJ', 7, '2026-09-24T22:45:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('5c822604-bece-586f-a6d4-b3c42a8268c3', '9217873d-c7e2-5c9f-b705-dc9afa73228b', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'I have this conversation with parents every semester at open house. First, show them a plan, not a feeling: the apprenticeship, the school hours, the pay scale, the license at the end. Accountants love a plan. Second, point out that apprentices are generally paid while they train, which a lot of parents don''t realize. Third, invite them to talk to someone in the trade. Ask me how I know that last one works.', false, 10, '2026-09-25T01:14:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('41c1b259-caa0-53cb-a9cc-2264f609ca4d', '9217873d-c7e2-5c9f-b705-dc9afa73228b', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly my parents wanted college too. What changed it was my first paycheck, and then my second year when I was already ahead of my cousin who had loans. I''m not saying college is bad. I''m saying show them the numbers and give it a year.', false, 2, '2026-09-25T16:26:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('72b9df41-3565-5c08-816f-782e75b6facf', '9217873d-c7e2-5c9f-b705-dc9afa73228b', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'I''ve got a version of this with my grandmother, who thinks electricians are ''just labor,'' and what finally got her was when I fixed the hallway light that two handymen couldn''t figure out, and I explained how a three-way works while I did it, which is maybe a lot, but she stopped saying ''just labor.''', false, 2, '2026-09-25T17:17:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8b57eb32-1b07-5357-896d-e9418abb1c62', '9217873d-c7e2-5c9f-b705-dc9afa73228b', '63579434-616f-5a6d-8f1f-281437382d7a', 'Same here, brother. Asbury Park, HVAC program. My parents want Rutgers. Bookmarking this for the next time it comes up at dinner.', false, 1, '2026-09-28T02:00:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('894151f1-804d-5228-84ce-cfde6d0d2e2e', '9217873d-c7e2-5c9f-b705-dc9afa73228b', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fwiw my parents wanted college too and i did two semesters before switching. if yours like degrees, some colleges may give credit for apprenticeship coursework, check what exists near you. it can make the conversation easier', false, 9, '2026-09-29T02:31:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1931d577-f0e2-5a17-b629-8f685fd1d0f8', '9217873d-c7e2-5c9f-b705-dc9afa73228b', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'my parents were the opposite lol, they were happy I wasn''t going to college. but my foreman (well, my uncle) told my mom about the pension stuff and that''s what she cared about', false, 2, '2026-09-29T09:15:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('154b5458-0e2c-54ab-a0f3-df6cb28169db', '9217873d-c7e2-5c9f-b705-dc9afa73228b', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'My father used to say there''s no shame in any work you do well. Show them you''re going to do it well. Parents mostly want to know you''ll be okay.', false, 4, '2026-09-30T00:15:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('60a9a692-4206-59d5-948b-895007c70771', '566a4ee6-0294-5f38-93a7-c5e3a7297ddd', 'question', 'is there even a union route for residential hvac in nj?', 'sorry if this is a dumb one. 35, left bartending, started as a helper at an hvac shop in woodbridge this year. everyone talks about the ibew and the plumbers union but i never hear about an hvac union. is there one for residential service in nj, or is it all commercial? and would i be better off just staying non-union and getting my hours and my 608?', 'hvac', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 15, '2026-08-11T09:09:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('f38e4c70-3657-5b56-b484-59e595d094d0', '60a9a692-4206-59d5-948b-895007c70771', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'As I understand it:
- There are union routes into HVAC in NJ, mostly through the pipe trades and the sheet metal side, and they lean commercial
- Residential service in NJ is mostly non-union shops like mine
- Either way, get your 608 now and track your hours; the HVACR license has experience requirements, so check the board for details
Call the locals directly if commercial interests you.', true, 10, '2026-08-12T00:49:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('42e28f1b-b911-531b-bf93-e3fa5928d437', '60a9a692-4206-59d5-948b-895007c70771', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'local 9 has hvac service guys. commercial mostly. call them.', false, 6, '2026-08-12T01:56:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4ab7ce52-f641-5205-90b3-ffb9e20411c9', '60a9a692-4206-59d5-948b-895007c70771', '4c3c92ef-9ba5-56b3-90e4-5341be547a4a', '3rd year non-union in asbury park, rooftops on strip malls along 35. i looked at the union stuff and decided to stay put for now, my boss says he''ll help with license prep when i''m closer. appreciate it, good question', false, 3, '2026-08-12T09:30:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8f6e2e42-6808-5460-a5e7-43c7edf8eaad', '60a9a692-4206-59d5-948b-895007c70771', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'refrigeration down the shore is mostly non-union shops too. if you like the cold side, a restaurant refrigeration guy will take a helper in the winter. winter is when you learn', false, 3, '2026-08-13T00:07:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('4c6f0a10-8e57-5614-a2e0-22192da74ca3', '049e3011-0b6d-5ddf-ad0e-83e84339599a', 'question', 'pre-apprenticeship programs: worth it or a waste of 10 weeks?', '31, voorhees, left a call center last year. general labor right now. a nonprofit in camden runs a free 10-week pre-apprenticeship program, construction basics, osha 10, some math, and they say they help with union applications. free is good. but 10 weeks without a paycheck is not. anyone done one? did it actually help?', 'other', 'Camden County, NJ', 10, '2026-08-17T02:33:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0095fdd4-020e-514e-a1b6-388f9c2cd106', '4c6f0a10-8e57-5614-a2e0-22192da74ca3', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'So this one time in AC... I worked with a kid who came out of a program like that, and he was ahead of the other helpers on safety and math from day one lol. Not every program is the same though. Ask them how many people from the last class got hired and where. If they can''t answer, skip it.', true, 32, '2026-08-17T23:08:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('975756ce-30e9-5941-bb30-2ea69a9f9e14', '4c6f0a10-8e57-5614-a2e0-22192da74ca3', '5ea91175-1b81-51fb-918c-7ad563230535', 'Cherry Hill here... I looked at the same kind of thing before I did the county night HVAC classes... couldn''t do 10 weeks unpaid either... thanks in advance if anyone knows a weekend version', false, 0, '2026-08-18T00:39:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('46335bb9-6ced-58be-80eb-09d9bf66e815', '4c6f0a10-8e57-5614-a2e0-22192da74ca3', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: the OSHA 10 alone is worth having, and a structured program can help with the math on aptitude tests. Whether it gets you into an apprenticeship faster depends on whether the program actually works with the apprenticeship programs. Ask for specifics.', false, 8, '2026-08-18T01:04:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('45716d6b-14b5-5e64-b7eb-7a0ec5d2ba32', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'tip', 'From the inspection side: whose license belongs on a heat pump swap', 'I get some version of this question every week this time of year, so I''ll put it in one place. Not legal advice; your local construction office has the final word.

As I understand the current rules, a condenser or heat pump replacement in NJ usually touches more than one subcode. The mechanical work goes on a permit from a contractor holding the HVACR license. The new disconnect, the whip and any circuit changes are electrical work, which means an Electrical Contractor pulls that permit or the work is done under one. Some companies have both licenses in-house. Plenty don''t, and that''s where I see trouble: the HVAC crew runs a new circuit because the panel was right there, and nobody pulled the electrical.

The HVACR license is also newer than a lot of people assume. If I remember right it became required around 2014, so you''ll still meet techs who talk like it doesn''t exist.

If you''re a helper and you don''t know whose license a job is under, it''s a fair thing to ask. And find out which edition of the code the permit falls under; it changes what I look for.', 'hvac', 'Ocean County, NJ', 3, '2026-08-10T16:02:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', 'eb2e65c4-6237-58c3-874e-6d74de571429', 'question', 'electrician here, is the 608 worth getting or is that an hvac thing', '164 2nd year. we just wrapped a condo job in weehawken with like 40 mini split heads and the hvac sub was short guys. their foreman asked if any of us had our 608 so we could help with the line sets lol. nobody did.

is it worth it for an electrician to get? my thinking is more and more of the work is heat pumps and it cant hurt on a resume. but i also dont want to be the guy doing another trade''s work and getting a talk from the steward.

edit: not trying to become an hvac guy, just curious if it opens doors', 'hvac', 'Hudson County, NJ', 4, '2026-09-09T02:02:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('c6f80393-02f5-52c4-beea-a834dcad7abe', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'So this one time in AC... we had an electrician on a hotel job who had his 608 and it saved us a whole afternoon, he could hook up gauges while we were stuck on the roof lol. Cheap test. Never hurts to have.', false, 3, '2026-09-10T00:48:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7c001b15-91a7-5f0a-b22c-cc93db2295c6', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'you need a license for side jobs anyway, there was a whole thread about doing outlets for neighbors', false, 2, '2026-09-10T02:31:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a3e1ebee-fdda-5522-ab2f-372f03074264', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'get it if you want. having a card doesn''t make you a refrigeration guy. i''ve cleaned up after plenty of guys with a card and a cheap set of gauges', false, 3, '2026-09-10T09:59:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('73f4533a-08d5-5a97-807b-ae4e8057218a', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Two separate things are getting mixed up here.

First, the 608 is an EPA certification to buy and handle refrigerant. As far as I know it doesn''t license you to do HVAC work in New Jersey; that''s the HVACR license, and on a union job there''s also the question of whose work it is. Second, it doesn''t hurt to have. Some of my electrical students take it and none of them have regretted it.

Ask your steward before you help with line sets, not after.', false, 11, '2026-09-11T00:10:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e9037a78-7b9d-576a-8c4e-40010552ad58', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'She''s right on the steward thing... I was thinking like a non-union shop where everybody does everything. Different world on a union job.', false, 6, '2026-09-12T12:22:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4b117892-445a-5259-92cc-33f10c5deffa', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Plumber''s view: never had it, never needed it. But heat pump water heaters are showing up in my buildings now, so I''m watching this.', false, 6, '2026-09-12T22:42:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('73ec8ac8-4a2d-595e-a0b5-136b378ee740', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'heat pump water heaters are gonna be a mess for a few years. everybody thinks the other trade is supposed to know them', false, 9, '2026-09-13T00:39:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('606fdc18-434a-5dc6-836b-19dbdbfe3c41', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'my bad, reread it and you meant on the job not side work. my shop does maybe 5 mini splits a year, definately going to ask if they''d pay for the test', false, 3, '2026-09-13T02:02:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('76abde2c-60e4-5630-aaeb-5bcee9040265', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Whoever takes it: keep the card somewhere you can find it. The supply house counter will usually ask to see it before they sell you refrigerant.', false, 5, '2026-09-13T02:18:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('54371aa4-45c5-5641-9e39-90e0a1acaa8d', '60495a22-6112-53b1-a3a0-f96883c01915', 'eb2e65c4-6237-58c3-874e-6d74de571429', 'update: steward said getting the card is fine, touching the line sets on our jobs is not lol. taking it anyway over the winter', false, 1, '2026-09-13T03:13:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('506c8059-ce00-5133-af65-a6bd52be281c', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'question', '4 years in and the license on the van isn''t my boss''s. do my hours count?', 'Service tech, 4 years, shop in Union City. Found out last month the master license on the trucks belongs to my boss''s uncle. Uncle is retired in Florida lol. Boss runs everything.

Starting to think about the master down the road. Do my 4 years even count if the guy who actually supervised me isn''t the licensed one? Not trying to get anybody in trouble. Just don''t want to find out in 3 more years that none of it counts.', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 8, '2026-08-18T00:20:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('22aab326-26db-56da-8a75-ca89a7f12af3', '506c8059-ce00-5133-af65-a6bd52be281c', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, this is the question to ask now and not at year eight.

Last I checked, the board wants your experience under a licensed master, documented, and the application asks who supervised you. If the licensed guy has been in Florida the whole time, you''ve got a problem proving that, and from what I understand your boss might have a bigger one.

I''m not going to guess how the board treats your situation. Call them and ask in general terms, no names. Meanwhile keep your own records: dates, jobs, who was on site. That''s the job.', true, 4, '2026-08-18T00:53:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('92a98f71-14e4-523d-9e65-76e6d5803aa7', '506c8059-ce00-5133-af65-a6bd52be281c', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'electrical side but my instructor says the same thing... get your hours in writing every year while people still remember you', false, 2, '2026-08-18T02:08:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4d3d5a0e-950b-576f-ad44-e9fab0880e1b', '506c8059-ce00-5133-af65-a6bd52be281c', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Second the records, and keep every W-2 and pay stub too. When my students apply for anything that asks for experience, the paper trail is always what''s missing, never the skill.', false, 3, '2026-08-18T03:13:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('84aac576-ac1c-54a5-8044-e269fe7e7d2a', '506c8059-ce00-5133-af65-a6bd52be281c', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'Sorry to jump in. Following this, because I never once thought to ask whose license my shop in Bayonne runs under.', false, 2, '2026-08-18T09:45:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('f0807430-b077-57c8-ba2b-98e56918fb49', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'question', 'Where do people in the city actually sit for the 608?', 'Two years in, non-union electrical shop in the Bronx. We''ve started doing a lot of PTAC and through-wall unit replacements in apartment buildings, and my boss wants two of us to have the 608 by the end of the year.

Searching online gets me a hundred sites and I can''t tell which ones are legit. Some say online with a webcam, some say you have to go in person. Is there a supply house or a school in the city people use? Or is the online one fine? Appreciate it.', 'hvac', 'Bronx, NY', 9, '2026-08-19T01:53:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('401a46f2-c954-5527-bf94-e7f1936cfa0d', 'f0807430-b077-57c8-ba2b-98e56918fb49', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First, make sure whoever you test with is an EPA-approved certifying organization. EPA keeps a list; check it before you pay anybody. Second, how the test is given depends on the organization and the type. Some offer remote proctoring, some only do it in person, and Type I has its own rules. Ask them directly what''s proctored.

Plenty of supply houses host test days too. Call the counter at the one your shop already uses.', false, 11, '2026-08-19T03:47:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c799f74b-8c2f-5894-b370-6016ece85d58', 'f0807430-b077-57c8-ba2b-98e56918fb49', '76ffb6b2-6ae2-5434-982e-39a1a1bf28b2', 'sorry to hijack, but does an electrical helper even need it for PTACs? the shop i''m helping at down in Galloway does a few and nobody there has one', false, 2, '2026-08-19T03:53:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7d6fa3dc-86d8-5973-ac9e-72299ee03130', 'f0807430-b077-57c8-ba2b-98e56918fb49', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'Appreciate it. Found one on the list that does remote, booked it for next month.

edit: update for anyone in the Bronx, passed Core and Type I on the first try. Going for Type II in the spring.', false, 4, '2026-08-19T10:16:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'question', 'Can a 17 year old take the 608, and does it ever expire?', 'Senior in a trade program in Queens, electrical track. I live in Bay Ridge so it''s two trains every morning, which is why I''m typing this at 6am. Our program lets you take the 608 at the end of the semester if you want, it''s optional. My shop teacher keeps saying anything that comes with a card is worth having for the union application.

Two questions. I''m 17, is there an age limit? Someone in my class said you have to be 18. And if I get it now and don''t use it for years because I go electrical, does it expire? Don''t want to pay for something I have to redo.

Thanks in advance.', 'hvac', 'Brooklyn, NY', 14, '2026-08-09T23:07:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e227aea6-c944-51da-b1e6-a418795e61d8', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Not that I know of on the age thing... I''ve had high school kids on ride-alongs who already had theirs. Mine''s from forever ago and still good lol.', false, 5, '2026-08-10T02:11:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d206af75-e5b8-56d5-a481-7602af006d00', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'card doesn''t expire as far as i know. the rules around refrigerant change though, so don''t assume what you learned in school is still the rule when you''re 30', false, 3, '2026-08-10T09:03:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('38204f5d-e045-562b-8466-ef9890ffaa01', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'Ok that''s good to hear. So the guy in my class saying 18 is wrong? He sounded really sure, he said his cousin wasn''t allowed to take it.', false, 3, '2026-08-10T10:27:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6765a28b-f7f6-558c-81fb-229a65c1c7db', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First, I''m not aware of any federal age minimum for the 608, and I have students who are 17 sit for it every year. Second, a certifying organization can have its own policies, so ask whoever''s giving yours; that might be what happened to the cousin. Third, last I checked the certification itself doesn''t expire.

Keep the card and a photo of it on your phone. Replacing a lost one is a hassle.', true, 6, '2026-08-11T02:00:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('11697954-8c8b-51fe-a599-078a34cd3c6e', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'Thank you, that makes sense. I''ll ask my teacher which organization the program uses before I sign up.', false, 1, '2026-08-11T10:27:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b8150588-3b9c-5bc6-93ec-8fa99b32ec31', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'study the recovery and leak repair stuff. that''s what got half my helpers, not the science', false, 2, '2026-08-11T14:15:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ca96da52-06f9-5595-899d-e701a80a0944', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'And hey... electrical guys who understand refrigeration are worth a lot on service calls. Half our no-cools are a contactor or a capacitor lol', false, 5, '2026-08-12T00:48:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('52e36802-838d-5f79-ba64-9f9905600944', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'hec is right about that. The best service techs I''ve trained could read a wiring diagram before they could braze.', false, 4, '2026-08-12T01:54:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('eaf24b44-a1e7-5729-a243-2830441856f8', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'update: asked my teacher, no age limit with the one our program uses. Signed up for December. Thanks everyone.', false, 1, '2026-08-12T02:15:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9037e379-087e-578a-a8b0-b78e4a1a7b8c', '1ea03970-5e27-56d6-8dd7-b8bf6d177b0f', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'good. winter is when you learn, so do the practice tests over break', false, 5, '2026-08-13T00:29:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('11d570b2-b711-52e6-bcff-02c2f1045d67', '0e1f3b61-0ba4-56b9-9844-cea31e8e2deb', 'question', 'sorry if this is dumb, but what do you call an electrician after 4 years in NJ?', 'Sorry if this is a dumb question. About six weeks into my first job as a helper in Brick (non-union). An older guy at my shop says he''s a journeyman, the boss is "the contractor," and when I asked what I''ll be in 4 years nobody could give me a straight answer. One guy said NJ doesn''t have a journeyman license at all, another said it does but nobody bothers.

So what am I working toward? Is it just the contractor license, or is there something in between? I''d like to know what to keep track of now instead of finding out later.', 'electrical', 'Ocean County, NJ', 7, '2026-10-02T10:18:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('017153c9-7e25-5dee-8133-e71f2cf8dc3d', '11d570b2-b711-52e6-bcff-02c2f1045d67', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'I asked my teacher this exact thing last year at the vo-tech. He said the one that matters in NJ is the Electrical Contractor license, because that''s the one that pulls permits. He wasn''t sure about the journeyman part either, which honestly didn''t help me much.', false, 1, '2026-10-02T13:44:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d00e4d0c-b697-5757-a089-6eb5688bc8e2', '11d570b2-b711-52e6-bcff-02c2f1045d67', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Good question, not a dumb one.

In the union you top out as a journeyman wireman, but that''s a classification in our agreement, not a state license. On the state side, the license you need to pull permits and run jobs yourself is the Electrical Contractor license, from the Board of Examiners of Electrical Contractors.

Whether NJ has a journeyman-level state credential for electricians, and what it would do for you, read the board''s page or call them. I''ve never needed one on a union job, so I''m the wrong person to say. What to track now: your hours, who you worked under, and what kind of work it was. Stay safe.', true, 30, '2026-10-04T23:55:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6eca6967-774d-5951-bf53-7fe4a29bc1e6', '11d570b2-b711-52e6-bcff-02c2f1045d67', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Same structure on the HVAC side, which might help it make sense:
- The license that runs work is the contractor/master license (HVACR for us, EC for you)
- Everything before that is experience you''ll have to document
- The board''s page lists the experience routes; read it yourself, the rules have changed over the years', false, 10, '2026-10-05T02:23:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('b04c9a1e-d546-5ab7-86b3-df5378cedd64', '0068d208-ce11-5170-b467-caa34a717104', 'question', 'guy in my apprenticeship class does mini-split installs on weekends. is that legal?', 'Not snitching on anyone, just curious, and I''ll probably over-explain this. There''s a guy in my 400 class, 2nd year like me, who does mini-split installs on weekends for cash. He says it''s fine because the units come pre-charged and he just "hooks them up," and he does the electrical himself because he''s "basically an electrician." He makes more on Saturdays than I make all week lol.

I''m not about to start doing it. But is any of that actually allowed in NJ without a license? I know electrical side work is a no from the other thread, but does the HVAC part need its own license too?', 'hvac', 'Ocean County, NJ', 17, '2026-09-28T01:51:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('39309cdd-f545-56e9-9505-3432110e90cb', 'b04c9a1e-d546-5ab7-86b3-df5378cedd64', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Short version, as I understand it: that''s two licenses he doesn''t have. The electrical is Electrical Contractor work. The mechanical side of a mini-split, the line sets, flaring, pulling a vacuum, opening the valves, falls under the HVACR license, and handling refrigerant takes a 608 on top of that. Pre-charged doesn''t change who''s allowed to install it.

Check with Consumer Affairs if you want it from the source. And he''s one bad flare away from a fire or a lawsuit. Stay safe.', false, 6, '2026-09-29T02:42:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('31b348f1-d825-5174-85fd-65115964f748', 'b04c9a1e-d546-5ab7-86b3-df5378cedd64', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'wait so even the pre charged ones need the hvac license? i figured that was the whole point of pre charged. guess not', false, 2, '2026-09-29T09:17:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('0ddccd9f-34cd-552e-ba05-8ae7f998514e', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'question', 'my boss doesnt have an hvacr license, is that a problem for me?', 'few months in as a helper now, same residential shop in paterson. was filling out paperwork for a supply house account and saw the license number on our estimates is under some other guy''s name, not my boss. boss is the owner and does all the installs himself, i''ve never met the other guy.

is that normal? does the owner have to be the one with the license? and does any of this matter for me brother, like does my time count toward my own license later if the licensed guy is never on the job', 'hvac', 'Passaic County, NJ', 5, '2026-09-09T16:18:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('51daf23b-dbca-5a59-a86c-e1448f2842e2', '0ddccd9f-34cd-552e-ba05-8ae7f998514e', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Plumbing side has the same problem, kid. A license holder who never shows up is how shops get in trouble. When HVAC licensing started, around 2010 I think, half the shops up here scrambled to find somebody licensed to put on paper.', false, 4, '2026-09-09T23:04:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d5a84b93-e149-5549-a0c0-0c880648d4ba', '0ddccd9f-34cd-552e-ba05-8ae7f998514e', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Ziggy, I think it was later than that. The law came first and the license requirement kicked in a few years after; I remember it as around 2014. Check the board''s page before anyone quotes either of us.

To your questions, as I understand NJ''s rules:
- The business needs a licensed Master HVACR Contractor, and that person is supposed to actually supervise the work
- It doesn''t have to be the owner
- Whether your hours count depends on documenting work under that licensee; ask the board how they want it shown', true, 17, '2026-09-10T02:57:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8e0e4772-a197-5498-871d-4f06006bb65a', '0ddccd9f-34cd-552e-ba05-8ae7f998514e', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', '> I remember it as around 2014

Could be. It''s your license, not mine, you''d know. Listen to Kash on this one, kid.', false, 5, '2026-09-10T03:48:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1db9ef30-227a-5472-aa4a-2afb5772ca2d', '0ddccd9f-34cd-552e-ba05-8ae7f998514e', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'From the owner side: I hold both licenses partly so nobody ever has to wonder whose name is on a job. When I''m hiring, I tell people up front whose license they''ll be working under. If your boss gets uncomfortable when you ask, that tells you something.', false, 6, '2026-09-11T00:26:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8c5f10ba-5bd4-5e5b-a4ce-a044c58ae7bd', '0ddccd9f-34cd-552e-ba05-8ae7f998514e', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'our contractor''s license number is on every truck door. pretty sure plumbing shops have to do that, i think hvac too? if it''s not on the van that''s weird', false, 4, '2026-09-11T01:22:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('916ea45e-75d0-5152-a57a-fe8a6ed91640', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'tip', 'Don''t cut a line set on demo until someone certified has recovered it', 'Saw this twice this summer on fit-outs, so I''m posting it for the electrical apprentices.

You''re demoing a space, there''s an old split system or a rooftop unit coming out, and someone hands a first-year a pair of cutters and points at the copper. Don''t. Unless someone with a 608 has recovered the refrigerant and told you it''s done, that line set may still be charged. Cutting it vents refrigerant, which as I understand it is illegal, and at close range it can freeze-burn your hands and face.

Ask the GC or the HVAC sub, "has this been recovered?" and get a name. It''s the same as LOTO: you don''t assume it''s dead because somebody said it probably is. Glasses and gloves either way. Stay safe.', 'hvac', 'Morris County, NJ', 2, '2026-08-28T10:26:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('5c593467-803e-5469-8d55-74651f007782', '916ea45e-75d0-5152-a57a-fe8a6ed91640', 'b298ceb4-fc38-5b36-b8ff-1ad22e49add8', 'appreciate this. i was literally handed cutters for this exact thing on a job in edison last month and the hvac guy yelled before i cut. now i know why', false, 2, '2026-08-28T15:12:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('44e78c35-8ba4-5fc4-815b-1ff37a8984a9', '916ea45e-75d0-5152-a57a-fe8a6ed91640', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Agreed. Not legal advice, but the venting rules are federal, so this is the same in every town. On the electrical side, that same demo is where I find abandoned circuits left live in the ceiling. Verify dead before you cut anything, copper or wire.', false, 8, '2026-08-30T16:23:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9507a035-285a-54a7-852e-9dc5be5625ef', '916ea45e-75d0-5152-a57a-fe8a6ed91640', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Adding one for the apprentices: if you''re the one who recovered it, tag it with your name and the date. The next person can''t see what you did.', false, 4, '2026-08-31T02:45:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('0f26629a-2668-55c4-9db1-9e20928d3863', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'question', 'Started an hours log like people said. What should actually be in it?', 'Sorry if this has been covered. After reading the thread about what license you have when you top out, I started keeping a log. Two years at my shop now, so I already feel behind.

Right now it''s a notebook: date, job, hours, what I did. Is that enough? Do I need my boss to sign something? Should I go back and reconstruct the last two years from my pay stubs, or is that pointless? I''d rather overdo it now than find out later it''s useless.

edit: I mean for a master plumber license someday, in NJ.', 'plumbing', 'Somerset County, NJ', 10, '2026-09-28T23:16:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('34f6ed18-e997-54b1-bf44-b873f236d4bc', '0f26629a-2668-55c4-9db1-9e20928d3863', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'reconstruct it. pay stubs and a calendar get you most of the way. towns, not customer addresses.', false, 5, '2026-09-29T00:27:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('48d17db3-9165-5607-ac35-d3da54991d7d', '0f26629a-2668-55c4-9db1-9e20928d3863', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, you''re ahead of most guys, not behind. The notebook''s fine.

What the board cares about, last I checked, is that the work was under a licensed master and who that was. So write your boss''s name and license number in the front. Once a year, ask him to sign a summary while he still remembers you. Keep your W-2s forever.

What the application actually wants on paper, read it on the board''s page. Don''t build the whole system off what an old guy says on the internet. That''s the job.', true, 19, '2026-09-29T22:14:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0c5bb811-1035-50ca-ad8c-aee06461dc83', '0f26629a-2668-55c4-9db1-9e20928d3863', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'What I''ve seen hold up for my techs:
- One line per week is enough; daily is nice but people quit
- The type of work matters as much as hours (service, rough-in, boilers)
- Photograph the pages every month; notebooks die in vans', false, 3, '2026-09-29T23:44:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b3e926e7-266e-53b3-adc2-79bfd23b6686', '0f26629a-2668-55c4-9db1-9e20928d3863', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'union side the apprenticeship tracks our hours but i keep my own anyway, i do it in the car at the wawa before work. foreman says the union''s records are good but yours are better lol', false, 1, '2026-09-30T00:37:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('93683405-e501-55c7-8731-aa55899c7a31', '0f26629a-2668-55c4-9db1-9e20928d3863', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'doing this for electrical too after reading this. does it matter if its in an app or does it have to be paper', false, 1, '2026-09-30T00:48:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('58eba5d3-826e-55db-a4b2-86cd1d2860ea', '0f26629a-2668-55c4-9db1-9e20928d3863', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Thank you, this is exactly what I needed. Going through two years of pay stubs this weekend. On the app question, I''m doing both, paper and photos.', false, 1, '2026-09-30T03:25:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('7e6bcf1b-c439-5300-861e-c00f43bd41d2', 'ef1df32c-a982-5124-b412-10efc20b8e86', 'question', 'Got my 608 in school. What''s the actual road to an HVACR license?', 'Morris County vo-tech ''24, passed my 608 Universal senior year, first job now at a residential shop out of Parsippany. At school everyone talked about the 608 like it was the finish line, and now my lead says it''s basically the entry ticket and the real license is years away.

So what''s the road? Is there a journeyman HVAC license in NJ or is it straight to master? How many years, and does my vo-tech time count for anything? I get coffee at Wawa with my lead every morning and he just says "you''ll figure it out."', 'hvac', 'Morris County, NJ', 7, '2026-08-24T02:02:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('9b39dbc7-9adb-554e-82d0-947531e82813', '7e6bcf1b-c439-5300-861e-c00f43bd41d2', '7180834c-9f0f-5d01-a84e-72ced4209a2c', 'following... same question for plumbing. does school count? does it matter if you''re non union?', false, 1, '2026-08-24T09:57:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7fe561bf-b4a9-5e68-871c-272f6bfcb207', '7e6bcf1b-c439-5300-861e-c00f43bd41d2', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'As I understand NJ''s setup, and please verify on the board''s page:
- The license that matters is the Master HVACR Contractor license; I''m not aware of a separate journeyman HVACR license
- There are a few experience routes, mostly years working under a licensed contractor, sometimes with an apprenticeship or schooling counting toward it
- There''s an exam with a business and law section, not just trade questions
- I won''t quote you the years; they''re on the board''s page and I''d rather you read them there

Start documenting now. The 608 was the right first step.', true, 12, '2026-08-24T13:59:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ef0587ac-ca32-5202-934f-f45b7dbd17b9', '7e6bcf1b-c439-5300-861e-c00f43bd41d2', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Plumbing''s the same idea, kid, different board. Nobody should be quoting you numbers off the top of their head, including me. Read it yourself, print it, and write the date on the printout.', false, 5, '2026-08-25T02:45:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2415311b-f8da-5f25-85d3-9199e76e01bd', '7e6bcf1b-c439-5300-861e-c00f43bd41d2', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'my union school might count toward stuff? not sure honestly, my instructor said ask the board too lol', false, 2, '2026-08-25T10:21:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'discussion', 'I''m not hiring HVAC helpers without a 608 anymore. Fair or not?', 'Hiring two helpers for the heating season. This year I''m making the 608 a requirement to interview, not something we''ll get to after you start. My reasons:
- It''s cheap and you can study for it on your own time
- It shows me you''ll finish something without being chased
- I can send you to the supply house or put you on a recovery job on day one
- The last three helpers I hired who were "planning to take it" never did

I can see the other side: someone who''s never been around equipment doesn''t know what half the test is talking about. Tell me if I''m wrong.', 'hvac', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 14, '2026-09-27T14:14:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('9d75b165-0608-579d-bc85-0c9202baba45', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', 'fair. got mine before i applied anywhere, at 40. took two weekends', false, 2, '2026-09-27T16:41:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8bd1b696-71bd-5304-8e97-07b6545f1f36', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'kind of chicken and egg though? i''m studying for it now and half of it is stuff i''ve never seen in person. took my shop 4 months to even let me hold the gauges. how are you supposed to know it before anyone hires you?', false, 1, '2026-09-27T17:14:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1c5410ad-98f0-5900-b9fa-87e5288927ce', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'I''ll take the other side a little.

First, I agree it shows follow-through. Second, passing the test isn''t the same as understanding it; I''ve had students with a card who couldn''t tell you which way the refrigerant flows. Third, you''ll lose good career switchers who are working another job and can''t study and job hunt at the same time. Make it a 90-day requirement and you get both.', false, 8, '2026-09-27T17:29:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('80c3a452-195a-559c-9f9b-2fc0112dd405', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Fair point on the switchers. But in my experience the 90-day promise is exactly what doesn''t happen.', false, 7, '2026-09-28T01:21:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('131d8233-6822-56bb-8e4b-914e48110471', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Plumbing apprentice, sorry to jump in from another trade. Does anyone do this for plumbing helpers? Require something before you start?', false, 1, '2026-09-28T09:41:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9d65b1fd-8f20-5a20-9e27-b398af46f4ee', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'electrical side my first job wanted osha 10 and a license and that was it lol. drivers license i mean', false, 1, '2026-09-28T10:06:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('533be2bc-d656-56b8-98eb-65e2ee2dd79f', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Kash, how many of those three would have stayed anyway? Sometimes the missing card is a symptom, not the cause. I''ve hired summer help too, ask me how I know.', false, 3, '2026-09-28T23:44:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bf98a88c-4216-5212-a660-3d11c960de65', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Two left inside six months. One is still with me and is a good tech, card or no card. So you have a point.', false, 1, '2026-09-29T00:28:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6aa3125f-a800-5f73-8f2c-81225aecf06b', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'so if i pass it by november am i hireable lol. asking for me', false, 1, '2026-09-29T10:19:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5fa84acd-ef74-5a84-b92d-211ad50fbb3c', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Yes. And put it at the top of the resume, not the bottom.', false, 4, '2026-09-29T10:40:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7aff51f8-fe43-5b85-8caf-6e2466dac172', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', '^ correction to mine, two weekends plus a retake on type 2. still worth it', false, 1, '2026-09-29T20:13:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('53f6f96f-471c-5616-a316-8196916e88ea', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Update on my question: asked my boss, he doesn''t require anything, but he said he''d pay for a code class if I asked. So I asked. Starting in October.', false, 2, '2026-09-29T20:23:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ba8eabc4-ac1b-50a2-9746-5e518e7340db', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Good. That''s how it works most of the time. You ask.', false, 3, '2026-09-29T21:27:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5927a6ff-6e29-5a26-b15b-5212c2c89750', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'is the 608 worth it for electrical guys? sorry if thats off topic', false, 1, '2026-09-30T02:39:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d8e81c22-fc67-5f23-a857-8b68e86a690c', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'theres a whole thread on that one, a 164 guy asked it in the summer', false, 1, '2026-09-30T11:22:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('48deaaab-b6ce-52f1-b885-fc1377b262cc', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'update: I''m going with ms_almonte''s version. Card required within 90 days of starting, and we pay the test fee if you pass on the first try.', false, 1, '2026-10-01T00:37:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2d96eed9-6c35-5b43-9195-a6ecd5863798', 'f73675e2-903c-5e21-8991-df7a3704e235', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'ok thats actually a good deal. studying tonight, practice tests until core is boring', false, 1, '2026-10-01T01:19:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('35771995-5af9-513a-bd5f-8f32eec54e9e', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'question', 'Honestly thinking about adding an HVACR license to my electrical shop', 'Honestly didn''t think I''d be asking this after 22 years. Half my calls down here involve heat pumps now. A lot of the raised houses went all-electric in the Sandy rebuilds, and I''ve been doing the circuits and handing the customer off to an HVAC guy I''ve known forever. He''s retiring in the spring.

So I''m weighing getting the HVACR license myself versus hiring someone who has it. Anyone here hold both an EC and an HVACR? Could I even meet the experience requirement at this point, or am I starting from zero? Kash, I''m looking at you.', 'hvac', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 11, '2026-09-11T09:23:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('ce15e6c4-d161-5c01-9607-3b70e21c8340', '35771995-5af9-513a-bd5f-8f32eec54e9e', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Happy to help, with the usual caveat that the board''s page is the authority, not me:
- Your electrical years almost certainly don''t count as HVACR experience; as far as I know it''s trade-specific
- Hiring or partnering with a licensed Master HVACR Contractor is the faster route, and plenty of shops do it
- If you go for it yourself, there''s a business and law part on the exam, which you''ve already been through once for your EC
- Price the insurance before you decide; adding mechanical work changes your policy', false, 11, '2026-09-14T01:14:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5ac45bc9-adf3-5c18-93d0-1cd25bc5e35b', '35771995-5af9-513a-bd5f-8f32eec54e9e', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'This is interesting to me because I still haven''t picked a trade. If a guy who''s been an electrician this long is moving toward heat pumps, should someone starting out just pick HVAC? Or is electrical smarter since the heat pumps need it anyway?', false, 5, '2026-09-14T01:58:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3984b6ca-4418-5cd2-b2d3-ae87761280ce', '35771995-5af9-513a-bd5f-8f32eec54e9e', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly? Either. The guys who understand both sides are the ones I''d hire tomorrow. Pick the one you''d still like doing in a crawlspace in August.', false, 9, '2026-09-14T10:27:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('80f45f5b-3d67-5c52-adea-543502a771b8', '35771995-5af9-513a-bd5f-8f32eec54e9e', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'Career switcher here too. The shop I''m helping at does the electrical for two HVAC companies, and both of them are always short. I''d assumed the license side was simpler than this.', false, 3, '2026-09-19T22:31:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9d1c9f62-16bf-5e5a-b995-319575d7e22e', '35771995-5af9-513a-bd5f-8f32eec54e9e', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'our hvac teacher at the mercer vo-tech says the same thing, everything''s going heat pump. glad i picked electrical then lol, they can''t run without us', false, 1, '2026-09-19T22:49:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('bd01aaf4-7ef1-58cc-ab8c-283ae434ad11', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'tip', 'Jersey guys on city jobs: start your master''s paperwork now, not at year ten', 'Half my crew in Midtown comes through the tunnel from Jersey. Every year one of the older guys decides he wants his NYC master electrician license and then spends months chasing people he worked for ten years ago for signatures.

From watching them go through it: the DOB wants years under a licensed master electrician, documented with experience affidavits signed by the masters you worked for, plus proof like tax records. I keep hearing seven and change for the years. Don''t trust me on the number, read the DOB licensing page.

Never went for it myself. Happy as a journeyman. But if you think you might, brother, get the paper while people still pick up the phone.', 'electrical', 'Queens, NY', 40, '2026-09-13T19:28:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('9dd9cd11-9792-528c-af92-eeefa74ab762', 'bd01aaf4-7ef1-58cc-ab8c-283ae434ad11', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'does city time count toward the jersey EC license too... or do you basically have to pick one', false, 2, '2026-09-13T22:25:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9ab3679e-d71a-52d6-b5dd-bf1016fed575', 'bd01aaf4-7ef1-58cc-ab8c-283ae434ad11', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'I''ll take the Jersey side of that. I can''t speak for how the NJ board weighs out-of-state work; that''s a question for them directly. What I''d do is document it the same way for both, so you''re covered whichever way you go. Stay safe.', false, 3, '2026-09-14T00:07:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1240e931-a517-5126-9b64-4a9e36047e06', 'bd01aaf4-7ef1-58cc-ab8c-283ae434ad11', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'what he said. keep one set of records, fill out whatever forms each side asks for', false, 4, '2026-09-14T01:14:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('21c2e0e9-02d8-5943-8235-e41e2f28231a', 'bd01aaf4-7ef1-58cc-ab8c-283ae434ad11', 'cee246a3-b9ec-55fd-8ac0-35c06eeed07f', '1st year in 164, we''ve done a couple city jobs already through the tunnel (lincoln tunnel at 6am is its own punishment btw). does a 1st year even need to think about this yet or is that way too early', false, 1, '2026-09-14T10:13:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('13f3a638-d4ad-5a6a-b0b7-bedf499ae37f', 'bd01aaf4-7ef1-58cc-ab8c-283ae434ad11', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Never too early... so this one time in AC... had a tech who''d spent six years at a shop that closed, and he couldn''t prove a single one of them when he wanted to test. Paperwork is free when it''s fresh lol.', false, 5, '2026-09-15T00:18:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b7c4d9c2-d10b-5f01-aa1f-3f73309e897d', 'bd01aaf4-7ef1-58cc-ab8c-283ae434ad11', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Same thing I tell my students on the Jersey side. First, keep every W-2. Second, get the name and license number of whoever supervises you. Third, write it down the week it happens, not the year.', false, 6, '2026-09-15T03:06:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9c726f0d-0381-5914-8356-5306726cc158', 'bd01aaf4-7ef1-58cc-ab8c-283ae434ad11', '330afa2d-de1f-58bc-aedf-c06a7bea2cac', 'Non-union in Morris County, never worked in the city. Does it go the other way too, would NJ time count for the NYC license? And who signs if your boss is a contractor, not a master?', false, 1, '2026-09-15T09:39:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bc2ba951-7936-562b-a649-5bb21a0528e8', 'bd01aaf4-7ef1-58cc-ab8c-283ae434ad11', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'brother, that''s a DOB question, not mine. what I know is they want it signed by masters, and Jersey doesn''t call anybody a master electrician. ask them before you count on it', false, 4, '2026-09-16T00:30:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('4739eea2-eaed-55b0-a4f5-9e15a9d63a7e', '2f048a7b-273e-574a-911a-7232a6136051', 'question', 'is the nj journeyman plumber license worth getting or do people skip to master', 'sorry if this is basic. 4 years in, service and repipes, north bergen and the walkups around there. my boss says the journeyman license is a waste of money and i should just save up the time for master. a guy at the supply house said he wouldnt hire anybody without at least the journeyman.

who''s right? does the journeyman actually let you do anything you can''t do now? i want to move toward commercial eventually if that changes the answer', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 9, '2026-08-19T09:18:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('3a3e4622-59d7-50ad-b0cd-a97c3f9c2646', '4739eea2-eaed-55b0-a4f5-9e15a9d63a7e', '1d393be9-5524-5be0-bb30-924bfb46f3c2', 'my foreman says get it. union side it comes up when you top out. not sure what it does for non union', false, 2, '2026-08-19T11:01:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5e72f536-2fe3-567b-ac69-6568d65a7238', '4739eea2-eaed-55b0-a4f5-9e15a9d63a7e', 'd680c878-f79d-58ae-9875-7e9bdf0efa31', 'brother my boss said the same thing as yours. then said it again when i asked for a raise lol. how much is the test even, and is it the same place you take the master?', false, 3, '2026-08-19T11:14:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('838859e9-304a-5fcc-8af0-5d75f0126859', '4739eea2-eaed-55b0-a4f5-9e15a9d63a7e', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Not my trade, so take this as general advice from an owner:
- Commercial shops and GCs ask about credentials more than residential ones, in my experience
- A license your current boss doesn''t value can still matter to the next boss
- What it lets you do legally is a question for the plumbing board, not the supply house counter, and not me', false, 7, '2026-08-19T14:24:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('01850499-af8a-50f5-8858-a070751105b4', '4739eea2-eaed-55b0-a4f5-9e15a9d63a7e', '9d863d1d-0f6f-5b8c-921d-d473f8721247', 'my night class instructor said the journeyman is what lets you work without a master standing right over you. didnt say it like he was sure though lol', false, 1, '2026-08-19T19:34:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('21ac3fd9-c3e9-539c-b4d2-4388e3f1caf8', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'question', 'Failed the DWV rough because we tested with air and the inspector wanted water?', 'Sorry if this is a basic one. We failed a plumbing rough today on a basement bathroom in Hillsborough. We had the DWV on air, gauge was holding, and the inspector said he wanted a water test and wouldn''t look at it. My boss was annoyed but said this town has always been like that, and the next town over takes air with no problem.

Is that a code thing or an inspector thing? I''d like to understand it before the retest Thursday instead of just doing what I''m told.

edit: filled the stack, passed Thursday. Still curious about the why if anyone knows.', 'plumbing', 'Somerset County, NJ', 15, '2026-07-26T15:27:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'question', 'Do plumbers need the 608 for heat pump water heaters?', 'We installed our first two heat pump water heaters this month, both in basements in Somerset County, and now my boss says we should both get the 608 "just in case." I always thought the 608 was strictly an HVAC thing.

From what I can tell the units come sealed from the factory and we''re just doing the water, the condensate and the venting clearances (an electrician did the circuit). So when would a plumber ever need it? Warranty work? If the compressor side ever needs service? I apologize if this is obvious to the HVAC people here.', 'plumbing', 'Somerset County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-11T16:15:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('5fad449c-ed4b-5ab0-be93-7e6c1fd30e27', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'installing a sealed unit, as far as i know you never open the refrigerant side, so no card needed for that. the day it needs a repair on the sealed system, somebody needs the card. probably not you, but your boss isn''t wrong either', true, 13, '2026-09-14T01:11:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1fb4ec7e-6588-5c51-bb5d-418abe529bac', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Your boss is smart, kid. These are going in everywhere. Get the card, it''s cheap, and you''ll be the one he sends.', false, 2, '2026-09-15T02:21:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('08d9f0a0-97bf-5c5d-b9e5-3ff18d007505', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different in the details but the same in principle. I''ve put in a handful in Bay Ridge. The plumbing is plumbing. If you ever open the refrigerant circuit you need certification, and some manufacturers want a certified tech for warranty work. The install manual usually says.', false, 3, '2026-09-15T02:39:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('793f79b2-7158-5600-9dc7-fe923fac715b', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'The shop I just started at does these too. Do they count as small appliances for the 608? Is that Type I?', false, 2, '2026-09-15T02:57:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('310b69c2-9f77-5d6b-874a-ce9f5312168c', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'depends on the charge and how it''s built. a lot of them are, from what i''ve seen, but read the nameplate and the manual before you go by me', false, 12, '2026-09-15T09:25:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e00e2af8-6873-5fb9-8526-aeab1975917e', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'Did two in Union City. Customer asked if it was the AC thing lol. Took 10 minutes to explain.', false, 2, '2026-09-15T10:25:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bd60c24c-c366-5d17-b3b3-719623f113cb', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'This is the kind of thing that keeps making me think I should learn plumbing and HVAC both. Is that a thing? A plumber with a 608?', false, 2, '2026-09-15T11:13:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6b423bed-a01d-5212-b539-9f31bd04ba2d', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'It''s a thing. Pick one trade first, kid, and get good at it. The card takes a couple of weekends. The trade takes ten years.', false, 3, '2026-09-15T11:53:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('23a1fb0a-7f70-5c37-a559-99006ee308de', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'my union school just mentioned these last week, said they''re coming into the curriculum. nobody said anything about the 608 though', false, 1, '2026-09-15T17:02:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('75fef573-5c63-558a-8052-6f910401b711', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'I''d add the condensate. Most of the problems I''ve heard about on these are condensate, not refrigerant. Pitch it, trap it if the manual says to, and know where it ends up.', false, 3, '2026-09-16T02:26:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e799fe28-a476-5493-9590-f27f20fdd29d', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Thank you all. So: installing doesn''t need it, repairing the sealed side does, and it''s cheap enough to get anyway. Signing up for Core and Type I.', false, 8, '2026-09-16T03:02:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('98b61e7f-81e0-5fbb-8c7f-fb3987c92486', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'do universal. you''ll want it the first time somebody hands you a mini split', false, 6, '2026-09-16T09:40:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6c439beb-672b-5fad-a536-2067c63b4462', '0f3e762d-48ae-57f8-9c7c-45984ed6d680', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'Same. Signing up for Universal, new boss said he''d cover it. Appreciate it.', false, 3, '2026-09-16T12:08:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5655cf0d-8767-59e1-a1bf-90469291b88e', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'question', 'Boilers: plumbing license or HVACR license?', '1st year, UA Local 24. My shop does a lot of hot water boiler work in Bergen in the winter. Someone at school said that once the HVACR license came in, boilers became an HVAC thing and plumbers can''t touch them. My foreman laughed at that.

Idk who to believe. Who''s allowed to do hydronic heat in NJ: plumbers, HVACR contractors, or both? Short answer is fine.', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 5, '2026-08-24T01:04:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('6d63e311-029b-51da-8c5b-81e80b3d986e', '5655cf0d-8767-59e1-a1bf-90469291b88e', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'I''ve wondered the same. My boss is a master plumber and does boilers all the time and has never mentioned needing anything else. But I''d ask the board rather than take his word or mine.', false, 3, '2026-08-24T09:37:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e7444ee9-ea21-515c-8bf8-ca0bd6a4919f', '5655cf0d-8767-59e1-a1bf-90469291b88e', '7180834c-9f0f-5d01-a84e-72ced4209a2c', 'following... my shop does boilers too and nobody has an hvac license that i know of. is that a problem or no? sorry if dumb q', false, 1, '2026-08-24T18:12:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('6b8e255c-6517-51a4-bfb5-fc155a153616', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'discussion', 'same drawings, two towns... two different answers on the rough', '4th year in 164. foreman has us on two retail fit-outs right now, one in hackensack and one a couple towns over in paramus. same drawings, same crew, same everything. one inspector passed our rough no problem... the other wrote up the exact thing the first one signed off on. foreman just shrugged and said every town is its own country.

isn''t the code supposed to be the same everywhere in NJ? how does that even happen', 'electrical', 'Bergen County, NJ', 9, '2026-08-18T00:56:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('42daa723-daed-51ee-b996-b48b04f0bd60', '6b8e255c-6517-51a4-bfb5-fc155a153616', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'The code is statewide; the UCC adopts one set of subcodes for everybody. The people enforcing it are local, and some sections leave room for judgment, so two good inspectors can read the same sentence differently.

What I''d do: ask the one who wrote it up for the code section, politely, and bring it to your foreman. If it''s a real disagreement, the construction official in that town can sort it out. Also look at the permit dates. Permits filed at different times may not be under the same code edition.', false, 4, '2026-08-18T22:58:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5a3bf987-3e33-58bd-a2fd-f60d8a936709', '6b8e255c-6517-51a4-bfb5-fc155a153616', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly that''s every week for me down the shore. Every town has its thing. You learn what each one looks at and you do it that way. Not worth the fight unless it''s actually wrong.', false, 3, '2026-08-19T00:54:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('e51493b7-01de-5bf4-a902-bf9ba7a5b5e2', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'question', 'Does a like-for-like water heater swap need a permit in NJ?', 'Sorry, another one from me. A customer in Manville asked us to swap a 40-gallon gas water heater, same spot, same venting. My boss said "we''ll pull a permit" and she acted like we were trying to pad the bill. Her last plumber never pulled one.

Is a straight swap actually permit work in NJ, or does it count as maintenance? And if it''s a permit, who inspects it, the plumbing inspector or someone for the gas? I want to be able to explain it next time instead of just standing there.', 'plumbing', 'Somerset County, NJ', 12, '2026-09-27T23:29:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0e2b5385-f64c-5964-aecf-971ac3b49074', 'e51493b7-01de-5bf4-a902-bf9ba7a5b5e2', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, and plumbing isn''t my subcode, but I can tell you how the UCC generally works. Ordinary maintenance is a short, specific list, and as far as I know replacing a water heater isn''t on it. Many construction offices treat a water heater swap as permit work, sometimes under a quicker category where you can start right away and the inspection follows. The gas connection and the venting are part of what gets looked at.

Call the town''s construction office for how they handle it. And your boss is right.', true, 8, '2026-09-28T16:48:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1a4a1cc3-67c3-5ef7-bfd6-0e5fa8743638', 'e51493b7-01de-5bf4-a902-bf9ba7a5b5e2', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'my shop pulls one every time... and customers complain every time lol. we tell them the inspection protects them, not us', false, 3, '2026-09-29T09:29:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('629f7aa3-a863-52ba-8a18-0d64f809b19a', 'e51493b7-01de-5bf4-a902-bf9ba7a5b5e2', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Same on the HVAC side with furnace swaps. How I explain it to customers:
- The permit is about the gas and the venting, not the tank
- A bad vent on a gas water heater is a carbon monoxide problem
- It''s its own line on the invoice so nobody thinks it''s padding', false, 3, '2026-09-30T02:35:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ce5f57f2-327c-58c5-aa28-374dac8cce9c', 'e51493b7-01de-5bf4-a902-bf9ba7a5b5e2', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', '> a carbon monoxide problem

That''s the line I''ll use with customers. Thank you.', false, 3, '2026-09-30T10:11:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8d3fc318-e00f-5b40-9906-c0bc512934ce', 'e51493b7-01de-5bf4-a902-bf9ba7a5b5e2', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'my uncle swapped his own in hamilton last year and nobody pulled anything. not saying it''s right, just saying most people have no idea this is a thing', false, 1, '2026-09-30T16:13:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('df019ee0-75b5-5ccc-a1dd-f8beb68feb05', 'e51493b7-01de-5bf4-a902-bf9ba7a5b5e2', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'does the same go for electric water heaters? since theres no gas or vent', false, 1, '2026-10-01T02:40:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6ea06421-2a74-5d42-a7e9-a3a6bc21cb03', 'e51493b7-01de-5bf4-a902-bf9ba7a5b5e2', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Generally still permit work as far as I know, and the electrical connection gets looked at. Same answer: ask the local office how they handle it.', false, 3, '2026-10-01T02:47:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('b9acba68-d532-5eac-8f21-86922d71d22f', '330afa2d-de1f-58bc-aedf-c06a7bea2cac', 'question', 'Failed rough-in for ''cable not secured.'' How close to the box is close enough?', 'First year non-union, Denville. Failed the rough on a basement finish today. Inspector circled a bunch of runs and wrote "cable not secured within required distance of box," plus something about stacking cables under one staple. My lead was out sick so I did most of those runs myself, which is great.

How close does the staple have to be to the box? And is two cables under one staple really a fail, or did I just get a picky inspector? I want to fix it right before Friday.', 'electrical', 'Morris County, NJ', 25, '2026-09-30T01:21:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('65483516-0d19-5d5c-b267-1ac2142bc234', 'b9acba68-d532-5eac-8f21-86922d71d22f', '02a13f50-be86-588b-966d-7ae10b7d64cd', 'we failed a rough last month too... ours was the duct sealing at the boots, inspector wanted mastic on every joint. same kind of thing?', false, 2, '2026-09-30T03:50:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e2482e2b-040d-5e11-a95d-b0fcfa574eee', 'b9acba68-d532-5eac-8f21-86922d71d22f', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'think he means electrical cable not ducts lol. our teacher said 12 inches from the box but idk the exact rule', false, 2, '2026-09-30T09:24:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5fddc21d-3939-56c8-888e-2822ede3fb6f', 'b9acba68-d532-5eac-8f21-86922d71d22f', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'For NM cable, the editions I''ve enforced want it secured within 12 inches of a box and at intervals of no more than 4 1/2 feet after that, with exceptions for things like fishing through finished walls. Check which code edition is in effect for your permit, but that part hasn''t changed in a long time.

On two cables under one staple: it depends on the staple. Some are listed for two cables stacked flat and some aren''t. Look at the box they came in. If the listing doesn''t allow it, it''s a fair write-up.', true, 11, '2026-10-01T00:11:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('46c210ce-8001-531a-9172-701c9b27f04b', 'b9acba68-d532-5eac-8f21-86922d71d22f', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Agree with Dale. And since your lead was out: next time, it''s fine to ask the shop for someone to look over your runs before the inspector does. A second set of eyes beats a red tag. Stay safe.', false, 6, '2026-10-02T00:29:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8a4e7cd2-b78b-59ea-9435-44de000a0cb3', 'b9acba68-d532-5eac-8f21-86922d71d22f', '330afa2d-de1f-58bc-aedf-c06a7bea2cac', 'update: restapled everything closer to the boxes, switched to staples rated for two, passed Friday. thanks Dale and Marcus, learned more from this than the whole week', false, 3, '2026-10-02T10:04:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('a6cc97ba-03e7-56c0-ab15-872c303014e3', '48b61243-8eaf-5f00-b8aa-9268dc17b5af', 'question', 'staten island, could work nj or the city. which license path makes more sense', 'live in tottenville. outerbridge is right there so i could work jersey or the city. right now i''m a helper at a small non union shop that does both, boss is licensed in nj and does some city jobs with a guy who has his city license.

long term i want my own license. brother which one do people go for when they live right on the line. nj contractor or nyc master. is one way easier or is that a myth. not trying to put 7 years into the wrong one', 'electrical', 'Staten Island, NY', 12, '2026-09-20T01:29:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('ee41c84e-a6a1-5dad-95a0-d35cc1d02a24', 'a6cc97ba-03e7-56c0-ab15-872c303014e3', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'Grew up in Jersey, licensed in the city, so I''ve thought about this. I can only speak to plumbing, but in the city it''s different: the master license wants years of documented experience under a licensed master, with affidavits, and the exams are their own thing. I''d guess electrical is similar in spirit, but read it. Jersey is a different board with its own rules, and I won''t pretend I know their current requirements. Neither side is the easy one.

Pick where you want to work most of the next ten years, and document every job on both sides in the meantime. Read the DOB''s licensing page and the NJ board''s page side by side.', false, 3, '2026-09-20T23:54:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3daf8016-699d-534f-9ee0-30e775b23aa8', 'a6cc97ba-03e7-56c0-ab15-872c303014e3', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'electrical in the city, same idea. years under a master, affidavits, check the DOB page. and brother, think about the commute. the outerbridge is fine till it isn''t', false, 4, '2026-09-21T02:18:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6d835979-8de7-5a63-8cc7-ba080c114f7f', 'a6cc97ba-03e7-56c0-ab15-872c303014e3', 'ccf9dc60-958f-5461-ad1b-ad7dd180a037', 'flatbush non union here... my boss says pick the city if you want commercial and jersey if you want houses. no idea if thats true brother lol', false, 2, '2026-09-21T09:56:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'question', 'Failed Core by a couple questions, passed Type II. Do I retake everything?', 'plumbing apprentice in brooklyn. took the 608 on a saturday because my uncle does hvac and won''t stop saying every card helps. passed type II, failed core by like two questions lol. the proctor said something about only retaking the part i failed but i was too annoyed to listen.

do i redo the whole thing or just core? does the type II pass count for anything if i don''t pass core? kind of salty about it not gonna lie', 'hvac', 'Brooklyn, NY', 8, '2026-09-21T23:25:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('831f0bc7-01ff-5b8a-9c66-29369428e1a9', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Been there... well not me, half my crew lol. From what I remember you only retake the section you failed, and the Type II pass doesn''t do anything for you until Core is passed too. Ask the organization that tested you how long they hold the passing score.', false, 7, '2026-09-22T16:48:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('adc07feb-8356-5333-acd1-cb86ba4ffd42', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'hec has it right as far as I know. The sections are scored separately, so you should only need to retake Core, but you aren''t certified for Type II until you''ve passed Core as well. Ask your certifying organization about their retake rules and the fee, because those vary.

And treat Core like vocabulary, not logic. It''s the regulations, the dates, the safety and recovery rules. You either know them or you don''t.', true, 12, '2026-09-22T20:14:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('07dd7b7d-4b57-59a8-b159-c8c595284172', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'ok so just core. thats less bad. still salty lol', false, 2, '2026-09-22T21:03:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('71abcfda-8492-5edb-bb54-686188ec4b7f', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'local 24 1st year, i failed core the first time too!! got it the second time. the practice tests are the move', false, 1, '2026-09-23T02:18:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('30b14249-02b0-5c14-9726-07363d3fb87f', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'Why''s a plumber taking the 608 lol. Serious question, never needed it once.', false, 2, '2026-09-23T10:15:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2d20f566-6680-55ba-8f97-d4347095e73a', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'my uncle. long story. also heat pump water heaters, there''s a whole thread about it', false, 3, '2026-09-23T11:45:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a8f42a68-62cc-5a7e-8a6f-379af8fb9478', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'cherry hill here... my vo tech made us take it senior year and i failed core too lol. it''s the dates that get you', false, 2, '2026-09-29T00:06:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bde2ada4-cbe7-5f50-8ef3-8ca2b281be58', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', '8498b67e-8832-52a9-854b-bbe6514f03b3', 'bartender brain. i''d fail core too, dates are not my thing', false, 2, '2026-09-29T15:40:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d5508b28-dae2-56ad-9766-006f0fadd6e8', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Quick tip for the retake... read every question twice. Core loves the ''which of these is NOT'' questions', false, 7, '2026-09-29T18:48:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6cff9f28-8954-5142-92de-4854fe02149e', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Second hec''s tip. Most of my students who fail Core miss the NOT questions, not the hard ones.', false, 5, '2026-09-29T21:54:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b73df709-71b8-5d8b-ac4a-38481a6d5713', 'b521dd38-18e1-556d-bdc2-69da5724ddd1', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'update: retook core this weekend, passed. type II is official now. the NOT questions were exactly it lol', false, 2, '2026-09-29T22:50:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('341a49e1-9f56-5ae3-aa1e-0f9439c63ed2', 'b8fa619e-10c3-53ee-8438-f4471618c6ee', 'question', 'Helper in the Bronx: what''s the DOB gas qualification and do I need it?', 'I''m 34, switched over from warehouse management this spring, and I''m a helper at a small plumbing shop in the Bronx. A lot of our work is gas lines in old multifamily buildings. My foreman keeps saying I''ll "need my gas card" before he can let me do more than carry pipe, and that the boss''s master license isn''t enough on its own.

What is the gas qualification exactly? Is it a test, a course, both? Can a helper get it, or do you need years first? And is it part of working toward a master plumber license, or totally separate? Trying to figure out what to do first.', 'plumbing', 'Bronx, NY', 14, '2026-07-29T23:59:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('474ad19e-0ada-5346-8f2f-7ac9559bf624', '341a49e1-9f56-5ae3-aa1e-0f9439c63ed2', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different from anything I knew growing up in Jersey. As I understand the current rules, gas work has to be done by a licensed master plumber or by someone working for one who holds a DOB gas work qualification. Getting the qualification means an approved training course, and there''s more than one level of it. I won''t quote you hours or prerequisites; they''ve been adjusted since it started, and the DOB''s page has the current list.

It''s separate from the master license. The master is years down the road and needs documented experience with affidavits. The gas qualification is what lets you actually work on gas for a licensed master in the meantime. Ask your foreman which course the shop uses.', true, 37, '2026-07-30T22:16:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('732a6ceb-1536-57b1-b385-89328e109ca6', '341a49e1-9f56-5ae3-aa1e-0f9439c63ed2', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'One more thing, since you asked what to do first: the time you''re putting in now should count toward the master later if it''s under a licensed master and you can document it, as far as I know. Start a log this week. Dates, buildings, who supervised you.', false, 2, '2026-07-31T01:47:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4f02c329-61e5-5023-966c-d7b7997f8d08', '341a49e1-9f56-5ae3-aa1e-0f9439c63ed2', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Jersey guy. Never run into a card like that on our side, kid. Over here it''s the license, master plumber or HVACR depending on the equipment, as far as I know. Different world over the bridge.', false, 6, '2026-08-03T01:57:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3240b62f-99a3-5f4a-8aca-2c381b236d6a', '341a49e1-9f56-5ae3-aa1e-0f9439c63ed2', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'electrician, but it''s the same story in the city with everything. far as I know DOB wants a card for it, and arkady knows that side better than me. get the card, brother', false, 3, '2026-08-03T02:29:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dffa5a8f-2738-5c02-8df1-b9efe92c5998', '341a49e1-9f56-5ae3-aa1e-0f9439c63ed2', '393b9bbb-e88d-53b5-be6e-c1c847014fa4', 'my foreman sent me to the course my second month. a few long saturdays. worth it', false, 1, '2026-08-03T11:55:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('407aa6f8-7f03-5175-abea-7c06034634bd', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'question', 'what''s actually on the business and law part of the EC exam', '4 years doing service and panel swaps out of little falls. not taking the EC exam tomorrow, i know i need my experience squared away first, but i want to start on the business and law side now since that''s the part nobody at my shop can tell me anything about. my boss took his like 20 years ago and says "it''s common sense, don''t worry about it." idk, that''s what people said about every test i ever failed.

what''s on it? nj law stuff like contracts and liens, or general business? open book? anyone take it recently', 'electrical', 'Passaic County, NJ', 3, '2026-09-17T02:54:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('7c1cdd9b-dbcb-5cad-bc8f-d630a1c1ef41', '407aa6f8-7f03-5175-abea-7c06034634bd', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly when I took mine that part was open book and the trade part was the hard one. Bring the reference book, tab it up, you''ll be fine.', false, 2, '2026-09-17T10:17:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e3a40016-094f-5820-89a6-59a5cd10b0dc', '407aa6f8-7f03-5175-abea-7c06034634bd', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'I''d be careful with that, Thiago. When I took it, some sections allowed references and some didn''t, and I''m sure the format has changed since. The testing company publishes a candidate bulletin that lists what''s covered and which references are allowed. That''s the only document I''d trust.

From memory, business and law covered NJ licensing rules, contracts, liens, insurance, payroll and tax basics, and record keeping. Read the bulletin before you buy a single book.', true, 7, '2026-09-17T15:12:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d6d7c56b-1f0e-5318-ab8d-25bb0db53b1b', '407aa6f8-7f03-5175-abea-7c06034634bd', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Fair. Dale''s right, that was a long time ago for me. Read the bulletin.', false, 4, '2026-09-17T16:42:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('98e60aa3-259b-5e55-9419-df571ebb1028', '407aa6f8-7f03-5175-abea-7c06034634bd', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Ours on the HVACR side had a business and law section too. What helped me:
- Read the candidate bulletin first, then buy only the references it lists
- Practice tabbing the books; if references are allowed, the clock is the real enemy
- The law part is less common sense than people say, especially liens and contracts', false, 6, '2026-09-18T02:16:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('34378e0c-2e4b-5f33-a266-29878c6e2b26', '407aa6f8-7f03-5175-abea-7c06034634bd', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'ok so bulletin first, then books. found the bulletin, it''s way longer than i expected lol. thanks', false, 4, '2026-09-18T15:53:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('76e5aee6-e2f0-525c-934e-1667041cb3e1', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'question', 'Homeowner pulled his own permit and wants us to do the work under it', 'Started at a new shop a few weeks ago, Gloucester County, service and repipes. Better place, actually sends me to school. Today a homeowner in Washington Township told my boss he''d already pulled the plumbing permit himself to "save money" and just wanted us to do the work. Boss said no and walked away from a decent job.

Is that a real rule or is my boss being stubborn? Can a homeowner even pull a plumbing permit in NJ? And if he can, why can''t a licensed shop just work under it?', 'plumbing', 'Gloucester County, NJ', 4, '2026-09-14T09:45:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('cb05fd69-70c9-5916-92b3-08e72cfe469a', '76e5aee6-e2f0-525c-934e-1667041cb3e1', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Your boss isn''t being stubborn. My father used to say the permit is your name on the job. As I understand it, a homeowner can pull a permit for work on his own single-family house that he lives in, when he''s doing the work himself. Once he hires a contractor, the contractor is supposed to pull it under his own license. Working under the homeowner''s permit doesn''t take your boss''s license off the line if something goes wrong.', false, 5, '2026-09-14T22:59:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('009fc034-0717-5b85-9dfa-2509851b8bb4', '76e5aee6-e2f0-525c-934e-1667041cb3e1', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice. That matches how I''ve seen it handled across the subcodes: the homeowner permit is for a homeowner doing his own work. Call the local construction office if you want it from them; most will explain it in two minutes.', false, 3, '2026-09-14T23:54:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('074a9802-4b8c-5676-9024-a995199cb879', '76e5aee6-e2f0-525c-934e-1667041cb3e1', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question, whether to be mad at your boss? Don''t be. He just kept his license clean.', false, 2, '2026-09-15T01:57:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('16d10c7e-2352-5ad7-aa4d-ba97ec594b0f', '76e5aee6-e2f0-525c-934e-1667041cb3e1', 'd680c878-f79d-58ae-9875-7e9bdf0efa31', 'brother my old cash shop used to do exactly this lol. one of the reasons i left. good on your boss', false, 1, '2026-09-15T09:28:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c2a991ae-63a4-5aa7-9633-d567da0371a3', '76e5aee6-e2f0-525c-934e-1667041cb3e1', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'Appreciate it. Told my boss what you all said and he laughed and said now you know why I walked.', false, 1, '2026-09-15T10:26:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'question', 'My first-year thinks he''s just a laborer. How do I tell him what''s normal?', '4th year in 164. foreman paired me with a first-year on a warehouse fit-out in secaucus about 2 months ago... good kid, shows up, doesn''t complain on the job. but at lunch he told me he thinks he''s being used as a laborer. material, gang box, sweeping, fire watch. he''s thinking about quiting.

problem is i half agree with him. i don''t want to lie and say it''s all fine. i also don''t want to go over the foreman''s head for him.

what do i actually tell him... what''s normal at 2 months and what isn''t? and is it my place to say something to the foreman? appreciate it', 'electrical', 'Bergen County, NJ', 39, '2026-09-22T00:17:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('075f48de-731a-5a2f-afba-6703ad740b6d', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Tell him the truth, kid. The first months are carrying stuff, and the way out is being good at carrying stuff. He knows where everything is, has the next thing in his hand before the journeyman asks.

Then tell him the other truth: if it''s still only material at a year, he should say something. Different trade, same job.', false, 9, '2026-09-22T02:05:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4b4a0064-5f19-5e80-acdd-32e4f17b6262', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I look for when I hire, and what I''d want a 4th year doing for my first-years: give him one real task a day that you can check. Pull a run, terminate a row of devices, label a panel schedule. Then tell the foreman what he did right, by name.

You''re not going over anyone''s head. You''re vouching for him. Foremen move the first-years somebody vouches for.', true, 11, '2026-09-22T16:24:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('47d1354d-d1ca-5b1b-b56c-6524d3de77c6', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', '> give him one real task a day that you can check

that part i can actually do... foreman lets me run my own little area so i can hand him stuff', false, 2, '2026-09-22T17:09:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e8ce83de-1e69-50ee-ac01-3eb7ad63d8ea', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question? How to talk to him, or whether to talk to the foreman? Talk to him first. When you go to the foreman, go to say he''s ready for more, not to complain for him.', false, 9, '2026-09-23T00:33:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e7d9efce-fc07-5921-8aab-756f8e6bca3f', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '2f048a7b-273e-574a-911a-7232a6136051', 'my first year i would''ve killed for a 4th year who even noticed me lol. sorry, not super helpful, but the fact you''re asking means he''s lucky', false, 5, '2026-09-23T01:54:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('392fe546-a5c8-5042-af91-8de5c14c709f', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, half my first-years think they''re laborers because the job is a tower and they''re on the material hoist all week. Tell him a building gets built in order. Right now the order is material. In two months it''s pipe and wire. That''s how big jobs go.', false, 7, '2026-09-23T03:44:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e1bde0c2-cb94-5d60-aa7e-9ecd7d1bd00e', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'eb2e65c4-6237-58c3-874e-6d74de571429', '2nd year in 164 and i was the gang box guy for like 5 months on my first job lol. then one day the journeyman handed me the bender and never took it back', false, 4, '2026-09-23T09:39:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3fd3af99-93fe-5ed1-bb6a-111ee3eabc20', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly the union side and the small-shop side look different here. In a shop like mine a first-year is doing real work by week three because there''s nobody else. On a big job you can sit in material for months. Neither one is wrong, but he should know that''s the trade-off he picked.', false, 3, '2026-09-24T01:54:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5597fdd4-e9ef-569f-b28f-c085d115456b', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'My father used to say the apprentice who complains at the lunch table is still learning, the one who complains to the foreman is gone. Tell him to bring it to you, not the table. Lunch table talk travels.', false, 9, '2026-09-24T10:06:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('33faf340-fabe-5552-b8f5-e2e51473bc5d', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'I was that guy a few weeks ago, plumbing side. What helped was someone telling me the actual red flags instead of just ''it''s normal.'' Then I asked for something specific and got it.', false, 4, '2026-09-24T10:46:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('632e5eb8-a66d-5b3c-bb3c-4e61deca268e', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'ok so what are the red flags, straight up? so i can tell him something real and not just ''hang in there''', false, 3, '2026-09-24T12:13:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('844f6189-5cd4-516b-bb9f-b36fd04eabf7', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Nobody explains anything even when he asks. Still nothing but material at a year. Paid off the books. No talk about school. He''s in the Local, so school and paper are handled. That leaves the first two. At two months, neither one is true yet from what you''re saying.', false, 5, '2026-09-25T01:02:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0350b4ac-cfc0-5c90-88e4-e8e765e53d18', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'From the inspection side: have him walk with you when the inspector comes through. A first-year who hears why something passes or fails learns more in twenty minutes than in a week of material runs.', false, 2, '2026-09-25T09:25:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ed49cf20-a1ad-50f3-ac4a-1a8e2e6b1e31', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'lol at ''used as a laborer.'' we''re all laborers until someone trusts us with something. the trick is not acting like it''s beneath you', false, 4, '2026-09-25T12:59:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fa109053-d4c1-59f5-bb71-7080f390d0ca', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Mostly agree with hudson. But if he''s asking, he cares. Don''t make him feel dumb for asking. That''s how you lose the good ones.', false, 2, '2026-09-28T02:11:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('60e1f328-7594-5cd7-a62b-f1c610569ef6', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'sounds like your foreman is the problem tbh. i''d tell him to find a different shop that actually lets him work', false, 1, '2026-09-28T03:02:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3f0d3a2a-d9ed-5a8f-b55b-83c0257b4130', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'he''s not at a shop... we''re both in the local, he can''t just switch shops lol. but i get what you mean', false, 2, '2026-09-28T21:46:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0b5e2ff4-b85c-5066-af49-381b2a2c3c85', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '7180834c-9f0f-5d01-a84e-72ced4209a2c', 'first-year here (plumbing, 5 months)... honestly just hearing a 4th year say ''this is normal and here''s when it isn''t'' would help me more than anything. tell him what you''d want to hear', false, 3, '2026-09-29T00:21:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a6b29619-b955-5b65-9d1d-d7ad322f7f91', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'One more, since you''ll top out soon: this is part of the job now. Teaching the first-year is what makes a good journeyman. Foremen notice who the first-years want to work with.', false, 2, '2026-09-29T02:00:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fdd4753b-cfe5-5d4b-98e2-2bb487fbe33d', 'e5929067-c29c-5679-b6e4-9ac5e8e6c044', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'update: told him basically what Haddad and Ziggy said, the red flags and the one-task thing. had him terminate a whole row of receptacles yesterday and i checked every one with him. foreman walked by and saw. kid was smiling at lunch for once... appreciate everybody', false, 2, '2026-09-29T10:17:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5a460a3f-0cf4-56d6-8899-f24a7ce8058b', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'question', 'Senior-year co-op has me sweeping and doing the Wawa run. Ask the school to move me?', 'Vo-tech senior in Essex County, electrical. Our co-op started in September, I''m placed with a small contractor in Nutley three afternoons a week. So far it''s been sweeping, carrying boxes of fittings up from the van and going to Wawa for the guys. Two weeks of that.

My shop teacher said if the placement is bad we can ask to switch. I don''t want to look like I''m complaining. Is two weeks too early to say something?', 'electrical', 'Essex County, NJ', 12, '2026-10-04T01:03:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('b9913959-b115-568a-828f-2429514d7eb3', '5a460a3f-0cf4-56d6-8899-f24a7ce8058b', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'I''ve taken co-op students. Here''s what I look for: does the kid ask what we''re doing tomorrow. Before you go to the school, ask your lead that, and ask to carry the tools for that task, not just the material. If it''s still only sweeping in a month, then talk to your co-op coordinator. They''d rather move you than lose you.', false, 6, '2026-10-04T22:19:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('33c0402c-dc30-5fb7-ba12-5c33c890de8c', '5a460a3f-0cf4-56d6-8899-f24a7ce8058b', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'Apex grad. Did basically the same thing in the Bronx for my first few months. Two weeks is early. Give it a few more before you burn the placement.', false, 1, '2026-10-05T00:58:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c1a85d77-12ff-524c-8792-f9ed26304b65', '5a460a3f-0cf4-56d6-8899-f24a7ce8058b', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'brother i''m 35 and i swept for 3 months when i switched. idk if that makes you feel better or worse', false, 1, '2026-10-05T01:15:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0d811f8c-7fcc-5665-b462-4d27c0049397', '5a460a3f-0cf4-56d6-8899-f24a7ce8058b', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'Career switcher, about six weeks into my first helper job. My lead told me the sweeping is where you learn where everything goes in a house. He wasn''t wrong. I can find a panel in a split-level in about ten seconds now.', false, 1, '2026-10-05T01:37:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5a2d55f6-9e8f-5025-bf2c-c0907a5cd701', '5a460a3f-0cf4-56d6-8899-f24a7ce8058b', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'wawa runs and sweeping are how everybody starts. ask one question a day. two weeks is too early to call it', false, 2, '2026-10-05T02:11:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('92c67012-4cc2-5e60-b4df-b2ff252bac3b', 'e9519c5c-bc39-526e-b419-6fd671e34e37', 'question', '3rd year and still running material while the 1st years hang pipe', '3rd year in 24. on a big commercial job in hackensack, and the foreman has me on material and fire watch while two first years are cutting in hangers and risers. is it because he thinks i''m good at material? do i ask him or go to the steward? don''t want to make it a thing. thanks in advance', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 4, '2026-08-30T15:11:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('c129a133-5f15-57b4-8b95-dc62d5fdd073', '92c67012-4cc2-5e60-b4df-b2ff252bac3b', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Ask the foreman first, kid, not the steward. The steward is for when it''s a problem, and this isn''t a problem yet. Some foremen keep the reliable guy on material because he''s reliable. Tell him you want time on the pipe before you top out. That''s the job, but you can still say something.', false, 9, '2026-08-31T23:26:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0a012e53-0698-5b94-bd0b-bc2cdcb9575d', '92c67012-4cc2-5e60-b4df-b2ff252bac3b', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'From the contractor side: the foreman may not even have noticed. Big jobs have a lot going on. Ask for something specific, like ''can I get on the risers next week,'' and he''ll probably say yes.', false, 5, '2026-09-01T10:12:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'question', 'Saturday helper job is all carrying, and my parents want me doing SAT prep instead', 'I''ll try to give the full picture. I''m in the electrical program at the Passaic County vo-tech, senior year. All summer and now on Saturdays I''ve been helping a residential electrician out of Wayne. It''s mostly carrying, sweeping, holding the ladder, and the occasional Wawa run. I like it anyway, and he''s a good guy.

My parents want college. They say if I''m "just carrying boxes" I should quit and spend Saturdays on SAT prep instead. Part of me thinks they have a point, because I''m honestly not learning a lot of electrical yet.

Is carrying boxes at 16 worth anything? Or am I wasting time I could use on school?', 'electrical', 'Passaic County, NJ', 8, '2026-09-25T21:38:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('f9eb2f85-3808-577f-beee-d1cdab0dd411', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, your parents aren''t wrong that school matters, and you''re not wrong that the job matters. Every one of us started carrying. Don''t quit because it''s carrying. Quit if he''s not teaching you anything when you ask.', false, 8, '2026-09-26T14:10:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f4b780af-8738-5827-a2a7-c9730c132732', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'carrying is how they find out if you show up... you showing up on saturdays at 16 is already more than most people do', false, 1, '2026-09-26T20:28:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('748f98dd-942a-59fc-b692-c10080a3eb76', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different with summer helpers, and I''d guess Jersey has its own rules too: there are limits on what a minor is allowed to do on a job, and insurance has opinions. So it may not be him holding you back. Ask him what he''s allowed to let you do at your age.', false, 7, '2026-09-26T23:29:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bf3ca13f-18fa-5cb4-a4a8-70886c305e31', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'That''s a good point I hadn''t considered. He did say something about insurance once and I thought he was just saying it. I''ll ask him next Saturday.', false, 2, '2026-09-27T02:46:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8bb7e89a-b1ac-58e3-82a1-0e750c888c74', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'vo-tech grad here. the summer job i had before senior year is honestly why i got hired out of school, the boss called my summer guy. so it counts even if its sweeping', false, 2, '2026-09-27T12:58:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c366ed1a-1f12-50c6-9da6-cab40b2ec02f', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'my parents wanted college too lol. now i''m in Local 1 and my mom tells everyone at church about it. they come around', false, 2, '2026-09-27T13:29:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('aa548909-2750-5a8d-8144-a8def22ec378', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', 'b298ceb4-fc38-5b36-b8ff-1ad22e49add8', 'for what it''s worth i did college and then switched at 33. not saying don''t go, just saying the trade will still be here. appreciate you asking this, wish i had at your age', false, 1, '2026-09-27T13:37:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('360f96b1-a9d2-531a-bed7-34a352de6de5', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Talk to your parents with facts. Most apprenticeship programs I know of want a high school diploma and solid algebra, and they look at your grades, so school is part of this plan, not against it. Show them you know that. Then keep the Saturday job if you can keep your grades up.

And whatever you''re doing on site, glasses and boots every time, even for sweeping. Stay safe.', true, 11, '2026-09-28T02:35:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('79e2dab2-c239-5705-9e1d-61279cf3d711', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'Thank you. I''m going to show my parents this thread, which may or may not help my case.', false, 0, '2026-09-28T02:51:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4a97d18c-33c1-571e-854a-c64ee00efd4b', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Show them the part about keeping your grades up, kid. That''s the part parents read.', false, 2, '2026-09-29T01:49:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ff0c1c0f-0b06-5f44-9d70-920fc136e3e4', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'same situation in hamilton except my dad''s a plumber and STILL wants me to go to college lol. you''re not alone', false, 1, '2026-09-29T03:39:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('072c21f2-6668-57dc-953a-29a175accae6', 'f0630f66-c319-54a6-be6d-0476675c235a', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'update: kept the job. Parents agreed as long as my grades stay where they are. He let me make up whips for two condenser disconnects last Saturday (nothing live, and he checked every one). Small thing but it felt huge.', false, 2, '2026-09-29T09:53:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d0738716-c187-5369-ac46-5d9734e45788', '0068d208-ce11-5170-b467-caa34a717104', 'question', 'Eight months pulling wire in the same warehouse. Do I ask to be moved?', '2nd year in 400. Since February I''ve been on one warehouse job off Route 537 near Jackson. It''s huge, so it''s been pulling wire, more pulling wire, some terminations, a lot of lift time. I''m not complaining about the work exactly, I''m getting good at it and the crew is fine.

But my buddy from the same class has been on three different jobs, a school, a strip mall and some service work, and he talks about stuff I''ve never touched. Am I falling behind by staying on one job? Is it normal to ask to be moved, or does that look like I''m not a team player?', 'electrical', 'Ocean County, NJ', 2, '2026-08-30T00:32:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('a85eeb86-1fcb-5633-b96e-c96d909ca750', 'd0738716-c187-5369-ac46-5d9734e45788', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', 'same thing happened to me in 164... 9 months on one job in secaucus. our training people told us you can ask about seeing different work, some locals care about rotation more than others... ask yours, at least that''s how they explained it to us', false, 2, '2026-08-30T02:16:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ef567521-9f0c-5d08-82f4-a00983789786', 'd0738716-c187-5369-ac46-5d9734e45788', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Not bad for you. Long jobs teach things short ones don''t, like how a big job is sequenced. Ask anyway, politely, when the job''s winding down.', false, 6, '2026-08-31T01:07:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('56f88cea-781c-5be9-9ebe-4943686d5ac2', 'd0738716-c187-5369-ac46-5d9734e45788', '76ffb6b2-6ae2-5434-982e-39a1a1bf28b2', 'sorry if this is dumb, but isn''t a long job a good thing? steady checks? i''m brand new, non-union and i''d definately take 8 months in one building over driving to 4 towns a day', false, 1, '2026-08-31T02:13:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5a575935-e74e-5226-966e-d493d2449f46', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'question', 'the GC keeps borrowing me for drywall cleanup on our remodel jobs', 'helper at a small electrical shop, residential remodels around manahawkin and the island. on the last two jobs the gc has been grabbing me when my boss isn''t there. "hey can you help carry this drywall out," "can you sweep the kitchen for the tile guy." i say yes because i don''t want to be rude, and then i''m behind on my own stuff.

is this normal? how do i say no to a gc without it getting back to my boss wrong

edit: told my boss. he was not happy with the gc. pretty sure that''s handled now.', 'electrical', 'Ocean County, NJ', 5, '2026-08-30T13:07:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('289357e6-6eb7-502c-b0fc-956c78f2e12c', '5a575935-e74e-5226-966e-d493d2449f46', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question? Whether it''s okay, or how to say no? It''s not okay if your boss doesn''t know about it. Tell your boss and let him tell the GC. Not your fight.', false, 7, '2026-08-31T00:15:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0315f308-a645-51c9-8d98-153fedea5e3b', '5a575935-e74e-5226-966e-d493d2449f46', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Your boss is paying you, kid. The GC isn''t. If the GC wants a laborer he can hire one. Tell your boss tonight, not the GC tomorrow.', false, 3, '2026-08-31T01:02:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('4d25e617-d0d2-5433-b107-721fd76aeb25', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'tip', 'Inspectors notice which helpers are paying attention', 'Something I''ve noticed from the inspection side, for anyone stuck in the material-and-cleanup months.

The helpers who come along on inspections and actually listen are the ones I later see running jobs. Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: if your boss lets you, be there when the inspector walks the rough. Ask what he''s looking at. Ask which code edition is in effect for that permit, and then go read the section he wrote up. Bring the permit card and the plans without being asked.

You''ll carry material for months no matter what. Spend twenty minutes of it learning what passes and why. It''s the cheapest education on the job.', 'electrical', 'Ocean County, NJ', 34, '2026-07-27T17:12:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('eec34092-0fa2-5632-965e-f4c91fd072fd', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'question', 'Old cash boss won''t write a letter confirming my two years', 'Before I got into the Local I worked two years for a plumber in Garfield. All cash, every Friday. Now people keep telling me prior experience can matter later, either for credit somewhere or for a license someday. I asked him for a short letter saying what I did and when.

He won''t do it. Says he "doesn''t do paperwork." Not angry about it, just no.

idk what to do. Is it even worth chasing? Or do those two years just not exist now?', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 5, '2026-09-24T17:22:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('81cee999-76eb-559b-8cad-79bdc76f6538', 'eec34092-0fa2-5632-965e-f4c91fd072fd', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'This is the trouble with cash. He won''t sign because a letter is paper showing he had an employee. My father put everybody on the books and used to say that''s what lets you sleep at night.

What you can do: write your own record now while you still remember it. Jobs, towns, rough dates, what you did. Keep texts, photos of you on jobs, anything with a date on it. Whether any of it counts for anything, ask your apprenticeship now and the board later. Don''t assume either way.', true, 12, '2026-09-24T23:33:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ccc2f912-f4c9-5817-806a-ec56d4ad830b', 'eec34092-0fa2-5632-965e-f4c91fd072fd', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'I have a lot of texts from him with job addresses and times. idk if that counts for anything.', false, 3, '2026-09-25T02:12:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('58976180-4aa5-5c4e-98bf-34d1896bdf28', 'eec34092-0fa2-5632-965e-f4c91fd072fd', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Keep them, kid. Screenshots, backed up somewhere that isn''t your phone. Whether they count is for somebody else to decide, but you can''t use what you deleted.', false, 2, '2026-09-25T02:47:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3095d6e8-1eb7-54ea-877f-14bae768270b', 'eec34092-0fa2-5632-965e-f4c91fd072fd', '88487bcb-3ea0-505b-a1b4-eb9fd79161ef', 'my old boss did the exact same thing. i stopped asking. been fine so far, 3 years in now. does it actually matter for union guys though?', false, 1, '2026-09-25T09:50:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('660f9448-93cc-5f5c-87e5-d83ae28e4fcf', 'eec34092-0fa2-5632-965e-f4c91fd072fd', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly don''t burn him over it either. He''ll say no to a letter, but he might pick up the phone if somebody calls him someday to ask about you. Small state.', false, 11, '2026-09-26T12:14:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4d9e5c87-089b-5f73-9760-e3deb4f0991e', 'eec34092-0fa2-5632-965e-f4c91fd072fd', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'brother just go work for a shop that pays on the books, problem solved', false, 2, '2026-09-26T16:42:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('39fb3623-ec92-5a57-93ff-0c3b15598270', 'eec34092-0fa2-5632-965e-f4c91fd072fd', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'I am in the Local now. This is about the two years before that.', false, 1, '2026-09-26T21:07:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ad636b79-8c8f-5a4d-afcf-fa2f349b6f2c', 'eec34092-0fa2-5632-965e-f4c91fd072fd', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'Is this why my shop teacher keeps telling us to keep a log from day one? I genuinely thought it was just a school assignment.', false, 0, '2026-09-26T23:04:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('3bf9d935-27f7-5af4-8a43-521176964a1f', '8498b67e-8832-52a9-854b-bbe6514f03b3', 'question', 'saturdays with a plumber for cash while i still bartend. dumb idea?', '36, woodbridge. still bartending nights, doing the night class. a plumber i know from the bar offered me saturdays, cash, carrying and helping on repipes. my mentor on here said keep a log of everything i do from day one so i started one.

question is whether cash saturdays are worth anything or if i''m just wearing myself out. not trying to quit the bar until i know.', 'plumbing', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 11, '2026-10-05T02:51:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('05663658-6b75-52c8-af1f-733978c2e9be', '3bf9d935-27f7-5af4-8a43-521176964a1f', '8b6662c7-cfe4-56bc-ba9e-b7cdcd78d855', 'Did basically that before I got hired, brother. It helped because I could say I''d actually been on jobs. Thiago told me to get on with a real shop as soon as I could, though, and he was right about that.', false, 2, '2026-10-05T03:11:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('036ade8e-2daa-5d61-b146-2b1bedc65b21', '3bf9d935-27f7-5af4-8a43-521176964a1f', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Not dumb, kid. It''s a smart way to test it before you quit the bar. Just know cash Saturdays don''t cover you if you get hurt, and they probably won''t count for much on paper. Treat it like a tryout.', false, 5, '2026-10-05T03:27:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('2a3230aa-f1a6-5433-aeff-b444ddd18997', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'question', 'Weekend boss pays cash and says Local 3 is a waste of five years', 'I asked about the Local 3 application here a while back. Update and a new question. I''ve been working weekends for an electrician in Ridgewood, cash. He found out I''m planning to apply and now he''s offering me full time when I graduate, more cash than I''d make as a first-year apprentice he says, and he keeps telling me the union is a waste of five years.

Money''s good for my age. But is cash going to hurt me later? He says "nobody checks."', 'electrical', 'Queens, NY', 6, '2026-10-01T01:59:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('2acbda03-0eab-590d-8630-22ca6d8e6faa', '2a3230aa-f1a6-5433-aeff-b444ddd18997', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different from Jersey on the license side, but this part is the same: if you ever want a license, the DOB wants experience you can document, and in my experience "cash, nobody checks" doesn''t document anything. Also ask him what happens if you get hurt. Off the books, that''s on you.

Apply to the Local anyway. You can always say no to them later. You can''t always get back in line.', true, 16, '2026-10-01T03:01:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0a89f9fd-ccfd-5e3d-b37d-7b4f7ef05e17', '2a3230aa-f1a6-5433-aeff-b444ddd18997', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'I''m non-union (Bronx shop, the Queens one starts next week) while I wait on 3, but I''m on the books. Big difference. If he really wants you full time, he can put you on payroll.', false, 1, '2026-10-01T03:22:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('63d083c7-3eef-5e8c-854a-4590a1e055f5', '2a3230aa-f1a6-5433-aeff-b444ddd18997', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fwiw ''nobody checks'' is what people say right up until somebody checks. take the money for now if you need it, but keep the application in', false, 7, '2026-10-02T00:06:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('32bd9460-79e7-5c3c-bafb-9e21b0268811', '2a3230aa-f1a6-5433-aeff-b444ddd18997', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'Similar age and situation here in Jersey. My teacher says anything off the books is basically invisible later. Not sure that''s literally true, but he says it a lot.', false, 2, '2026-10-02T09:11:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('65e1f225-4bdd-5c89-9990-b5ef5dafe580', '2a3230aa-f1a6-5433-aeff-b444ddd18997', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'keep applying. you can''t get the time back later. nobody i know who applied regrets it, even the ones still waiting', false, 2, '2026-10-02T09:17:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('2c537ba7-6fa3-589b-aa39-68e8d0323dbe', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'tip', 'From the hiring side: why a paper trail matters more than you think', 'Here''s what I look for when I hire, and it''s not what most young guys expect.

When someone tells me they have three years of experience and all of it was cash, I usually believe them. But I can''t verify it, and on our public jobs everybody goes on certified payroll from day one, so I''m starting them at zero on paper whether I like it or not.

The applicants who stand out walk in with something I can check: pay stubs or W-2s, a 608 card, a letter from a past employer, a log of jobs with dates and who they worked under. It doesn''t have to be fancy. It has to exist.

If you''re getting paid cash right now, start that log tonight. Nobody''s coming to build it for you later.', 'hvac', 'Burlington County, NJ', 12, '2026-09-25T02:08:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('701493b3-b2f9-51f1-82c5-433d7f966baf', '2c537ba7-6fa3-589b-aa39-68e8d0323dbe', '86afdff7-a622-5314-99e0-81558cc06b11', 'Sorry if this is a basic question, but does a log I keep myself count for anything with you, or does it need to be signed by someone? Thanks in advance.', false, 1, '2026-09-25T09:43:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('285108a6-dd05-59f5-8aec-33663f79418a', '2c537ba7-6fa3-589b-aa39-68e8d0323dbe', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: a log you keep yourself helps you remember. A supervisor''s signature or a pay stub is something someone else can check. For a license, read what the board actually asks for before you assume either one is enough.', false, 5, '2026-09-27T23:47:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('02aa2b20-54a3-57bf-926b-42d5f9cb49b6', '2c537ba7-6fa3-589b-aa39-68e8d0323dbe', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'kept every pay stub since school in a folder in the truck. guess i''m doing one thing right', false, 2, '2026-09-28T02:50:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'e9519c5c-bc39-526e-b419-6fd671e34e37', 'question', 'foreman wants me on his weekend side jobs for cash. allowed if I''m in the Local?', 'foreman on my job does bathrooms on weekends and asked if i want to make extra cash saturdays. good guy, taught me a lot this year. two questions. is that even allowed being in the local? and if something goes wrong, whose license is it on? he says he has his master''s so it''s fine. he also says he pulls permits "when it needs one." thanks in advance', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 14, '2026-09-21T02:40:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('4510fe11-259d-55bf-8316-9c6912abd163', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly that''s two questions. Whether the Local cares, ask your business agent or read your agreement. I''m non-union and won''t guess at that one. Whose license: if he''s a master running it as a real business, with permits and insurance, that''s one thing. If it''s cash and no permits, it''s on him and on you.', false, 5, '2026-09-22T02:59:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1da948cb-3e9c-5de1-924f-3edfed9df17a', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'e9519c5c-bc39-526e-b419-6fd671e34e37', 'the ''when it needs one'' part is what''s bugging me. idk what that means honestly', false, 1, '2026-09-22T10:28:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3f0d1327-dbb8-531b-b185-43b4059c4aa2', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'It means sometimes he doesn''t pull one, kid. Think about what that means for the helper who was there.', false, 6, '2026-09-22T12:09:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('33db63d8-d5f1-5b68-b984-e1090fc5d7b1', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: whether a job needs a permit is decided by the code and the town, not by the plumber''s opinion of the job. Bathroom work that moves or adds fixtures typically needs one where I''ve worked. If an inspector never sees it and something fails, the homeowner''s insurer will ask who did the work, and your name comes up as the guy who was there.', true, 9, '2026-09-23T00:46:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c43904af-8c64-5226-a704-7e397b737134', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'guys in 164 talk about this all the time... ask the steward quietly. some locals are a lot stricter about side work than people think. don''t find out the hard way', false, 3, '2026-09-23T01:06:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('38019e96-eabd-5cc8-87db-bbca3ded0a7c', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'I was in the union a few years and I''ll admit I did some Saturdays back then. Not proud of all of it. The money''s good until you''re the one on the job that floods the downstairs neighbor.', false, 3, '2026-09-23T03:19:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ae6be411-c4ca-5be2-ba4a-5a532a8cb0a4', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'not plumbing but my boss in clifton offered the same kind of thing for weekend ac installs. i asked kash about it (he''s my mentor on here) and he basically said if it''s not on the company''s books and insurance, don''t. so i didn''t. not sure if it''s the same for union guys tho, or if it''s worse', false, 2, '2026-09-23T09:05:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fd2cf089-e256-58bd-a74a-0ee20e681760', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', '1st year in 24 here. Our instructor brought this up in class, actually. Said read the bylaws and ask. Didn''t say yes or no, just said ask.', false, 2, '2026-09-23T11:36:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f9806dfe-bbf2-5de6-b449-a713305bac17', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'ask the hall. then do what they say. never needed the saturday money that bad in thirty years', false, 4, '2026-09-23T22:15:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6ee51375-4735-54ae-9bf1-212f3e438692', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'e9519c5c-bc39-526e-b419-6fd671e34e37', '> never needed the saturday money that bad

fair. i''m not desperate, just tempted. he''s a good guy, that''s the hard part', false, 2, '2026-09-23T23:48:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('722ee98c-1ee9-5d7b-858a-600e85055dc6', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question: is it legal, or how do you say no to a guy you like? The second one''s easier than you think. ''Can''t, I''ve got stuff Saturdays.'' He''ll ask somebody else.', false, 2, '2026-09-24T01:54:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7361ce8a-813d-546b-a5d9-30158ee454f3', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'i do side work for cash all the time, nobody cares. just dont tell anyone lol', false, 1, '2026-09-24T03:10:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f5fa120c-71dd-53c8-aacd-64ae7dea9a2d', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Respectfully, ''nobody cares'' is what everyone says until something goes wrong. I''d rather he hear it here than from an insurance adjuster.', false, 2, '2026-09-24T09:38:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('76165cab-c812-56e8-84b5-adc63cfb7a36', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', '81a78d2a-1f86-5ff4-b4e3-293e5f93bee7', '4th year in 24. sorry, not trying to pile on, but a guy a couple years ahead of me did weekends with a foreman and when one of those jobs leaked, guess who got blamed. not the foreman.', false, 5, '2026-09-24T09:43:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('09a190be-8514-55fc-8be5-61fbf93d2dfc', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'That''s the part people miss. When something goes wrong, the helper is the easiest one to point at.', false, 7, '2026-09-25T02:58:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4f80cd6a-929d-5cc8-b8d9-5376b48e5a00', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'And a foreman who''s good to you on the job doesn''t stop being your foreman on Saturday. Say no nicely and he''ll respect it. That''s the job.', false, 2, '2026-09-25T03:13:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('214d015a-9150-5a60-a2f3-c174ee5c5844', '1fe422ad-b630-5f57-a28b-93703d139175', 'e9519c5c-bc39-526e-b419-6fd671e34e37', 'update: asked the steward, quietly. he pointed me to the part of the agreement that covers it and told me to read it myself. read it. not doing it. told my foreman i''m busy saturdays, he said no problem and moved on. thanks everyone', false, 1, '2026-09-25T09:59:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('76e1d91b-6101-501a-a953-0a62e8eccf0e', 'aa4aa383-9b0a-5294-809c-62f229f9606e', 'question', 'Thirty hours on the check, the rest cash. Normal?', 'Started at a residential HVAC shop in Woodbridge in the spring. Boss puts 30 hours a week on my paycheck and pays the rest in cash on Fridays. Says it''s "better for both of us." Some weeks that''s 15 hours cash.

Is it better for me, brother? I''d like to know before tax time, not after.', 'hvac', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 3, '2026-10-03T15:06:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e085b8ee-d639-513c-bccb-4d355e168c97', '76e1d91b-6101-501a-a953-0a62e8eccf0e', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Not normal at any shop I''d want to work for, and as I understand it, not legal either. Here''s what I''d think about. The cash hours probably aren''t covered if you get hurt on them. Your W-2 will show less than you earned, which matters for a car loan, an apartment, unemployment. Only the paper hours are easy to prove later. And taxes on the cash are still your problem.

Talk to a tax preparer before April. Not a contractor, including me.', true, 11, '2026-10-03T20:44:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bfea9dc1-0888-5c52-9b1c-72386866ba43', '76e1d91b-6101-501a-a953-0a62e8eccf0e', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly I see this a lot down the shore. ''Better for both of us'' usually means better for him. Doesn''t make him a bad guy, but you should know what you''re giving up.', false, 4, '2026-10-03T23:25:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('891e6d0d-be9c-5d3b-b738-61cf8f80c084', '76e1d91b-6101-501a-a953-0a62e8eccf0e', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Sorry to jump in, I''m in a similar spot (not the cash part, just no benefits yet). Is there a polite way to ask a boss to put everything on the check without it turning into a whole thing?', false, 3, '2026-10-04T02:23:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'question', 'gave my two weeks and now my boss barely talks to me', '3 years at a small shop in garfield. boss is decent but wouldn''t pay for school and i got tired of waiting. got an offer from a bigger shop in paramus that does. gave my two weeks monday.

since then he barely talks to me and i''m getting every crawlspace job on the board lol. the new shop''s owner knows him from the supply house on 46 so i''m worried about what he says.

did i mess up? how do i get through the two weeks without burning it. small state, everyone knows everyone. thanks in advance', 'electrical', 'Bergen County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-23T09:38:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('7cb407db-4b77-5779-bd3d-37cd7e8304f9', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'You didn''t mess up. My father used to say a boss who''s hurt that you''re leaving is a boss who thought you were worth keeping.

Finish the two weeks better than you started. Clean van, labeled panels, notes on every job you''re leaving open so the next guy isn''t lost. On your last day, shake his hand and thank him for three years. He''ll be talking about you at the supply house either way. Give him something good to say. I left the union badly once and I still hear about it.', true, 9, '2026-09-24T01:40:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8ca539c4-5b15-597e-9702-1b4f66700c5e', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'lol the crawlspace jobs. classic. he''s seeing if you''ll quit early so he doesn''t have to deal with it. don''t give him that', false, 2, '2026-09-24T01:53:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('51c50260-62f4-55db-80f2-7cc78221b38f', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question? You know how to get through two weeks. Show up. The real one is whether he''ll badmouth you. Maybe. Your work will talk louder.', false, 2, '2026-09-24T02:55:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('021cf4f4-1baf-58d8-b40f-06650513a7a9', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', '> Your work will talk louder

appreciate it. yeah i think i''m mostly worried the new guy hears something before i even start', false, 1, '2026-09-24T10:22:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('75553047-84c1-584e-8fdd-da5f458c3a2c', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly in a small state the new owner already called somebody about you before he made the offer. If he''d heard anything bad, you wouldn''t have the offer.', false, 2, '2026-09-25T00:22:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f07a69fa-9855-5bfd-961e-f8bef3631244', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'also bergen, also a small shop. how did you even bring up leaving? asking for a friend (me). sorry if thats off topic', false, 1, '2026-09-25T01:20:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('71f3808e-6f3f-5cc7-bce5-58f9b9b50d45', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'told him in the morning at the shop before we left, not on a job and not by text. said thanks for 3 years, i want my schooling paid for and they offered. that''s it. he said ''ok'' and walked out lol', false, 2, '2026-09-25T10:30:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b1a75bfc-efb1-5de3-97d5-43ff1fb2b318', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'That''s how it should be done. In person, early, short. The ''ok'' and walking out is his problem, not yours. I''ve had people leave my company exactly that way, and I''ve hired two of them back since.', false, 6, '2026-09-26T14:31:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('560e6dda-2229-57de-bab9-55a59e94c342', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Something nobody''s mentioned: crawlspaces are a safety job, and a bad two weeks is when people rush. GFCI on your cords, check what''s live before you go in, lock out what you''re working on, and don''t let being angry make you careless. Stay safe.', false, 8, '2026-09-26T23:18:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a77ae378-e68d-57e7-afb2-b6e27dcd346a', 'c49ba2f4-f97c-5e53-a344-bde5ab9cedb7', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'update: last day was friday. he warmed up the last few days, bought lunch, told me to call him if the new place doesn''t work out. start in paramus monday. appreciate everyone in here', false, 1, '2026-09-27T03:28:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'question', 'Boss calls late September ''boiler cleaning month.'' What am I actually doing?', 'About 7 months in at the shop out of Bayonne. Boss says starting next week it''s boiler cleanings and fall service every day until it gets cold, mostly old one-pipe steam in Bayonne and JC, some hot water. Joy told me to ask for one new thing a week so this is me asking ahead of time.

What actually happens on a fall service for an old steam boiler? What should I be watching so I''m not just the guy holding the light? brother I''ve seen maybe three steam boilers up close.', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 10, '2026-09-23T09:39:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('9b106dcf-7173-58c4-bceb-4b2956492aa8', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Fall service on steam is about making sure January is boring, kid.

Your lead will look at the water line in the gauge glass, check the low-water cutoff and flush it if it''s the kind you flush, look at the pressure control and the pigtail under it, check the burner and the flue, and look for leaks on the near-boiler piping. You''ll be holding the bucket and the light. Watch the order he does it in and ask why after, not during.', true, 10, '2026-09-24T01:28:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cc7d0f85-c2b1-5548-8448-c6c0bb701ed0', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First, bring a notebook. Second, write down the make and model of every boiler and what the water looked like in the glass. Third, ask your lead what "normal" is for that one, because every old steam system has its own normal. Ask me how I know.', false, 4, '2026-09-25T00:47:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f71ff982-efca-5756-a4f5-6088fc6c3e3f', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'what''s a pigtail? sorry. is that the loop thing under the gauge?', false, 1, '2026-09-25T02:06:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c8aea8f2-5b77-54fc-a109-728471b4490f', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'That''s the one. It protects the control from live steam. Old ones clog up with crud, which is why we look at them every fall. You''ll see.', false, 4, '2026-09-26T12:22:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dce83265-9d63-5292-9c96-5288e6e3d452', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'we barely see steam down here in cherry hill... mostly hot water and forced air. honestly jealous, sounds like you learn more up there', false, 1, '2026-09-26T21:22:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3fcd8503-4fc8-507d-a31c-c8515507276a', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Two years in and I''ve done maybe four steam boilers around Manville. What surprised me was how much the homeowner knows about their own system. Ask them what it does when it''s acting up.', false, 1, '2026-09-26T22:46:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6976658e-7e45-551a-bc5c-b0bd0bbd30d4', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'Is it true you''re never supposed to add water to a steam boiler while it''s hot? My teacher said that once and I wasn''t sure if it was a rule or a saying.', false, 1, '2026-09-27T09:11:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e6822393-06b6-56cb-9a26-8d4eeb8027ae', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'It''s a real rule. Feeding cold water into a hot boiler that''s run low can crack it, or worse. That''s why we teach people to stop and find out why it''s low before anything else. On a fall service your lead handles that, not the helper.', false, 7, '2026-09-27T09:37:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e16335b6-430a-5e63-82fa-8edc0b37b967', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'electrical guy here... the amount of boiler room wiring in bayonne that''s older than me is scary. watch where your hands go near the burner controls', false, 3, '2026-09-27T12:07:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('07b26f38-6cc7-57ab-b02a-a72178caedfd', '9c5f33f5-7dad-5095-8391-cd7aa070526b', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'update: 6 cleanings this week with my lead. held a lot of buckets. he let me do the gauge glass on the last one while he watched. the pigtails were exactly as gross as Ziggy said', false, 1, '2026-09-27T12:23:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('00f91842-b195-5201-abe3-41d17720283a', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'discussion', 'What was your first no-heat call like?', 'Shop just put the winter emergency list on the board and my name is on it with a journeyman starting in November. Mostly service and drain work up to now, Fair Lawn and around. Not scared exactly. idk. Curious what your first one was like, the real version. Was it the boiler, the customer, or just being tired?', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 13, '2026-09-21T16:28:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('f63c9e76-77a4-5b51-8d86-b124d79be3fc', '00f91842-b195-5201-abe3-41d17720283a', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'So this one time in AC... ok it was Haddonfield, not AC lol. 3am, lady swearing the heat was broken. house had two thermostats and she was turning up the one for the AC. check what''s actually calling for heat before you open anything', false, 5, '2026-09-21T23:01:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ae0abe8b-3229-5d0a-a77c-cbeb444bb3e1', '00f91842-b195-5201-abe3-41d17720283a', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'had my first one last week in bay ridge, first cold night of the season. steam. the lady had painted over every air vent in the apartment. 3 hours lol. never forget it', false, 2, '2026-09-22T00:09:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8a9cff6f-c571-55f9-b8cc-34cc7df73b9a', '00f91842-b195-5201-abe3-41d17720283a', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'i''m on the list this year too in clifton. kash told me to ask if i can ride with a senior guy for the first few nights before i''m on my own, going to ask my boss this week', false, 1, '2026-09-22T00:21:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6cd3976f-8626-5450-9fef-25326ce519bc', '00f91842-b195-5201-abe3-41d17720283a', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Cold, tired, and somebody''s grandmother watching you work. You''ll be fine, kid. Take the customer seriously, take the call seriously, and call your lead before you guess. That''s the job.', false, 4, '2026-09-22T00:54:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('a7999985-6504-5a41-b617-203e1464b454', 'df0dfff9-4016-5ddb-a8b6-c4029b1e30b2', 'question', 'first cold night and the phones blew up. what do you check on a boiler that sat all summer', 'first night in the 40s and our board went crazy, 11 no-heat calls before noon. foreman sent me out with a journeyman on 4 of them. two were the thermostat. what else is usually wrong on startup week? and is there a order you guys go in or is it just experience. bound brook, mostly hot water boilers and some steam', 'plumbing', 'Somerset County, NJ', 8, '2026-09-16T01:30:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('8a7cf76d-8ea7-57f7-bf7d-5b7eff399b65', 'a7999985-6504-5a41-b617-203e1464b454', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Fall startup calls we see every year around now:
- Thermostat batteries died over the summer, or it''s still set to cool
- Service switch got turned off for the summer
- Pilot out on older standing-pilot boilers
- Low pressure on hot water systems nobody looked at since spring
- Circulator stuck after sitting all summer
Check the simple things first, in that order, and do a combustion and CO check before you leave. A callback on startup week costs more than the call.', true, 12, '2026-09-16T23:50:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d2942276-7c72-5a0e-81e5-fd24a43767a3', 'a7999985-6504-5a41-b617-203e1464b454', 'df0dfff9-4016-5ddb-a8b6-c4029b1e30b2', 'the thermostat one got us twice today lol. foreman said the same, check the stat before you open anything', false, 1, '2026-09-17T02:11:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f8b4a5b6-333a-53f8-ad34-90fb1443d5c5', 'a7999985-6504-5a41-b617-203e1464b454', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'Ziggy told me basically the same thing in another thread, simple stuff first. My uncle''s phone hasn''t stopped ringing all week either.', false, 1, '2026-09-17T03:29:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d0274e29-023c-55db-a91c-b2a0bd8285cc', 'a7999985-6504-5a41-b617-203e1464b454', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'Circulators. Two stuck ones this week, one in Deptford and one in Woodbury. Appreciate the list.', false, 4, '2026-09-17T09:41:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c878a6ad-f242-5ccf-96a9-b8cecd6392a9', 'a7999985-6504-5a41-b617-203e1464b454', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'electrical side but over-explaining as usual: my teacher says half the no-heat calls his old shop in hamilton ran were a tripped breaker or a service switch somebody flipped thinking it was a light. so check that too before anyone opens the boiler', false, 2, '2026-09-21T09:13:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('ebccf4f5-3d36-55cb-85c4-8501787b43f7', '493faab8-51d6-584c-8d92-65b67edb36f6', 'question', 'First furnace we fired this fall filled the house with burning smell. When is that normal?', 'Doing a co-op this fall with a residential shop in Glassboro, mostly furnace and boiler tune-ups. First furnace we fired today, the house filled up with that burning dust smell and the homeowner freaked out, thought it was a gas leak. My lead stayed calm and talked to her, and it went away after a few minutes.

How do you tell the difference between the normal first-fire smell and something actually wrong? I don''t want to be the guy who says "that''s normal" and it isn''t.

edit: asked my lead about the readings. CO in the flue was where he wanted it and zero in the house. makes a lot more sense now.', 'hvac', 'Gloucester County, NJ', 16, '2026-09-28T00:16:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('5dff6460-cfa4-5744-813b-f1db16128a63', 'ebccf4f5-3d36-55cb-85c4-8501787b43f7', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Good instinct. First, dust burning off a heat exchanger smells like hot dust and fades in minutes. Second, gas has that rotten-egg smell and that is never normal: you stop, get everyone out, and call the gas utility or 911 from outside. Third, a combustion analyzer and a CO meter answer the question your nose can''t. Your lead should be testing every tune-up. Ask him to walk you through the numbers.', true, 13, '2026-09-28T03:48:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8435bf3d-0f5f-5930-b4ca-0f0798c91f03', 'ebccf4f5-3d36-55cb-85c4-8501787b43f7', '493faab8-51d6-584c-8d92-65b67edb36f6', 'he did test it, i just didn''t know what the numbers meant. going to ask him tomorrow', false, 5, '2026-09-28T10:30:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('adf0cef0-7070-5c14-8f9a-5ba3907421cd', 'ebccf4f5-3d36-55cb-85c4-8501787b43f7', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'So this one time in AC... ok Sewell lol, same thing, lady called the fire department on the first fire of the year. they came, smelled dust, left. better she calls than doesn''t', false, 8, '2026-09-29T00:04:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b4a2cafa-8947-5221-84f4-87fb9880944d', 'ebccf4f5-3d36-55cb-85c4-8501787b43f7', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'What I tell my techs on fall tune-ups:
- Tell the homeowner before you fire it that there may be a dust smell for a few minutes
- Change the filter first so you''re not burning off a summer of dust
- Test CO in the flue and in the living space, and write the numbers on the ticket', false, 4, '2026-09-29T09:09:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c21482f9-1843-5ee9-b155-98bd832f008c', 'ebccf4f5-3d36-55cb-85c4-8501787b43f7', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'brother we had the same thing in paterson last week. my lead opened a window and just talked to her the whole time. that''s half the job i think', false, 3, '2026-09-29T14:36:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('eb2246df-f4c7-5e3a-b1f7-aeceec2d7cf6', 'ebccf4f5-3d36-55cb-85c4-8501787b43f7', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'One more: ask whether the house has working CO alarms. Not legal advice, but NJ has CO alarm requirements for many homes, and a startup call is a good time to make sure theirs actually work.', false, 5, '2026-09-29T18:29:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e9fee0d3-24bf-5f0e-a4ce-566e3404defc', 'ebccf4f5-3d36-55cb-85c4-8501787b43f7', '15a35d13-ce46-5ce0-8883-c803eafa1f49', 'First week at my new job and we did tune-ups every day. Telling them about the smell before you fire it saved me from this exact situation twice already.', false, 1, '2026-09-29T19:32:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('efaf3ac6-bf80-57f2-966b-9226acb3111f', 'ebccf4f5-3d36-55cb-85c4-8501787b43f7', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'your nose is a tool. the meter is the answer. trust the meter and you sleep fine', false, 2, '2026-09-29T21:52:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('53df17ee-1d8d-5d99-9f8b-6a84a50fca9c', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'question', 'Electrical helper here. Boss says we get no-heat calls in winter too?', 'About a month into my first helper job (residential electrical, Irvington and around). My lead mentioned that once it gets cold we''ll get calls from people whose boiler or furnace "has no power," and that half the time it''s something electrical.

I assumed no-heat was an HVAC or plumbing call. What are electricians usually finding on these? And where''s the line between our job and the heating guy''s? I don''t want to be the new guy poking at a burner.', 'electrical', 'Essex County, NJ', 5, '2026-09-13T01:59:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('fe3380df-6fb0-508a-9887-c1e683b524d9', '53df17ee-1d8d-5d99-9f8b-6a84a50fca9c', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly most of them are simple: a service switch somebody turned off, a tripped breaker, a thermostat wire that got chewed or cut during a remodel, a bad transformer feeding the controls. The electrician''s job is to prove power is getting where it''s supposed to, and stop there if it''s the heating side. Test, don''t guess, and don''t start replacing HVAC parts you weren''t called for.', true, 10, '2026-09-14T01:44:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fd0f7843-7739-59ab-b275-2a1416bf2fa2', '53df17ee-1d8d-5d99-9f8b-6a84a50fca9c', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'From the HVAC side, first: tell the homeowner you''re there for the electrical, not the boiler. Second, if your side checks out, say so and let them call the heating company. Electricians who start adjusting burner controls make my life harder.', false, 3, '2026-09-14T09:23:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5cd916e9-f476-57ee-aa0d-e5344f603ebf', '53df17ee-1d8d-5d99-9f8b-6a84a50fca9c', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'got called in once behind an electrician who swapped a whole thermostat when the problem was a blown fuse on the control board lol. know what you''re looking at or don''t touch it', false, 5, '2026-09-15T01:49:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('be8c19db-953a-57e6-b748-84058b4489a7', '53df17ee-1d8d-5d99-9f8b-6a84a50fca9c', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'That helps. So the line is: confirm power to the equipment and the controls, then hand it off. Marcus already has me testing everything before I touch it, so at least that part''s a habit.', false, 2, '2026-09-15T02:39:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1b66fc4c-1253-5f61-8681-9af557af3387', '53df17ee-1d8d-5d99-9f8b-6a84a50fca9c', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'That''s the line. And when you find the switch at the top of the basement stairs turned off, don''t laugh in front of the customer. Laugh in the truck.', false, 4, '2026-09-15T22:44:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('4b0a4bd8-b2b7-51ce-b939-9b06ebdc45da', '5ea91175-1b81-51fb-918c-7ad563230535', 'question', 'Night class starts oil burners next month. Anyone still run a lot of oil down here?', 'Doing the night HVAC program at the county vo-tech twice a week... we start the oil burner unit next month. I have never seen an oil burner in person, my house and everyone''s I know is gas. Is oil still a big part of the work in Camden County, or is it mostly a North Jersey and Morris County thing at this point? Trying to figure out how hard to study it. Thanks in advance.', 'other', 'Camden County, NJ', 10, '2026-08-16T14:34:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'discussion', 'Ride-along update from the 40-and-undecided guy: leaning HVAC after startup day', 'Update from the 40-and-undecided guy. After my first round of ride-alongs I leaned electrical, but Joy said to do a second day in whatever I was least sure about, so last Saturday I went out with an HVAC shop doing boiler and furnace startups.

The HVAC day was the one where I didn''t check my phone once. Ten houses, every one different, and the tech explained everything while he worked. My knees were fine in the basements. An attic in August would probably be another story.

For people who picked HVAC: what made you sure? And is the heat-season-then-AC-season thing as brutal as it sounds?', 'other', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 31, '2026-09-29T01:56:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('a70b7cd9-526c-5882-b8c5-329321217606', '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', 'did it at 40 too. the not checking your phone thing is how i knew. summers are brutal, winters are long, spring and fall you catch your breath. worth it for me so far', false, 2, '2026-09-29T10:30:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('685a1809-6851-5fe4-8967-62914f03a2b9', '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'From the owner side, what HVAC looks like across a year around here:
- Spring and fall: maintenance, installs, the steady money
- Summer: no-cool calls, long days, attics
- Winter: no-heat calls, on-call rotations
- Heat pumps are blurring that, more year-round install work than when I started
If startup day felt right, most of the year feels like that, just louder.', false, 6, '2026-09-30T00:46:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('635fa950-5156-5979-960c-a17014c879f7', '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First, the phone thing is real, I''ve watched students light up the same way. Second, ask that shop what their July looks like and believe them. Third, look at the night program at your county vo-tech so you''re not walking in cold. Ask me how I know that matters.', false, 3, '2026-09-30T01:12:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5b5e2b5e-0b95-5683-9d92-5956e4c99773', '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', '> ask that shop what their July looks like

The owner said almost the same thing. His words were "come back in July if you still want it." I''d rather not wait that long, honestly.', false, 2, '2026-09-30T02:47:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d6e5b35e-d486-5366-8713-8d192e650630', '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', '9fe65554-dd4f-5c8b-9708-65d0c765a948', 'plumbing guy here so i''m biased lol, but did the plumbing ride along not click at all? or was it just the day you got? idk, alot of days are just drains', false, 2, '2026-09-30T09:27:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('543a0afd-5b97-550e-94f9-b1d47f20a56a', '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'Honestly it was a day of drains. The guy was great. I just didn''t light up. Maybe that''s unfair to plumbing.', false, 1, '2026-09-30T10:36:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('24d326d2-5958-5539-9e30-5a311005697a', '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Not unfair. A day of drains would scare off plenty of people who''d make good plumbers. But you picked the day that felt right, and that counts for something. You can fake liking a job for a week, not for a whole career.', false, 5, '2026-10-02T02:42:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5c0c7eca-8b89-5388-a874-2a6fe3301db9', '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fwiw if the troubleshooting is the part you liked, keep controls in the back of your mind too. thermostats, zoning, boiler controls, bms on the commercial side. low voltage is a real trade and it''s easier on the knees', false, 3, '2026-10-03T12:02:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5a6c7b08-0534-52db-830b-383756bf986d', '620e35ba-a7a2-5220-99e1-31e930bb0d5e', '56ebe677-1060-5479-89c5-55faedf03943', 'Also 40, also undecided, also Middlesex. Bartending nights and testing the waters with a night class. This thread is basically my life. If you pick HVAC, please post how the first month goes.', false, 1, '2026-10-03T12:49:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('6337ccdd-7619-572c-b765-0b536e33e76b', '86afdff7-a622-5314-99e0-81558cc06b11', 'question', 'Oil-to-gas conversion in Rockaway and the customer keeps asking me about her buried tank', 'Sorry if this is basic. I''m on my first oil-to-gas conversion with my lead, an old split-level in Rockaway. The homeowner keeps asking me, not my lead, what happens to the buried oil tank in the side yard and whether we take it out. I told her I''d find out.

I honestly don''t know whose job that is or what the rules are, and I don''t want to tell her something wrong. My lead says there are a lot of these up here in Morris County. Thanks in advance.', 'hvac', 'Morris County, NJ', 10, '2026-09-28T16:29:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('391d50f3-dd13-5ccc-ba69-9027a6f2274f', '6337ccdd-7619-572c-b765-0b536e33e76b', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Good call not answering. How I''d handle it:
- Tank removal or abandonment is its own specialty, not the HVAC contractor''s, at least at my company
- From what I understand, the town will want a permit for it and some situations involve soil testing; that''s not something to guess at in a driveway
- Tell her to call a tank company and her town''s construction office, and that her insurance company and any future buyer will care about the paperwork
- Your job is the new equipment, the gas piping, and disconnecting the oil supply to the old burner properly
Point her to the right people. Don''t become the tank expert.', true, 19, '2026-09-28T21:55:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c90c2489-2a3f-5fd3-8989-09ba6b7cdcfa', '6337ccdd-7619-572c-b765-0b536e33e76b', '81a78d2a-1f86-5ff4-b4e3-293e5f93bee7', 'rockaway is full of these. half the houses on my street had tanks pulled before they sold. sorry not that helpful, just confirming your lead is right lol', false, 2, '2026-09-28T22:11:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6e2498c3-7f4d-56df-93e0-a571280db9ac', '6337ccdd-7619-572c-b765-0b536e33e76b', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Up in Morris and Sussex you''ll see more buried tanks than you ever wanted to, kid. A leaker can turn into real money for a homeowner. Never guess on that question.', false, 8, '2026-09-29T09:23:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d5dd4c11-c3eb-5172-b0a9-f74c4357e7cb', '6337ccdd-7619-572c-b765-0b536e33e76b', '86afdff7-a622-5314-99e0-81558cc06b11', 'Thank you, this helps a lot. I told her to call the town and a tank company and wrote it on the ticket. My lead said that''s what he would''ve told her.', false, 1, '2026-09-29T09:37:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('f679fa1c-5fff-5756-8013-bf7da748cce4', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'tip', 'Last week of September: what I want my helpers doing before the phones start', 'Every year the last week of September is the calm before the phones. Here''s what I tell my helpers.

Stock your truck like it''s January. Fittings for the old stuff, not just the new stuff. Nipples, unions, gauge glasses, pigtails, a couple of the controls we always end up needing.

Know where every shutoff is on your regular customers'' boilers before it''s dark at five.

Test your flashlight, your CO meter, your combustion analyzer. Get your boots resoled now, not the first wet week.

And sleep. On-call season is long, kid. The guy who''s rested at 2am does better work than the guy who''s been up since Tuesday. That''s the job.', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 14, '2026-09-13T13:31:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('08c10c74-c242-5a3b-a399-567555b27ad9', 'f679fa1c-5fff-5756-8013-bf7da748cce4', '7180834c-9f0f-5d01-a84e-72ced4209a2c', 'the boots one... mine already have a hole in them. ordering new ones tonight. thanks zig', false, 2, '2026-09-13T16:19:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4858006e-928f-5139-8e52-2b10087c5033', 'f679fa1c-5fff-5756-8013-bf7da748cce4', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'I''d add one, Ziggy, and push back on one. Add: update your customers'' contact info now, half my building supers changed this year. Push back: don''t stock every control on every truck. Two on the lead truck is plenty. The rest is money sitting on a shelf.', false, 11, '2026-09-13T21:03:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8aa1f3bd-1331-5c93-bda2-fe4508168471', 'f679fa1c-5fff-5756-8013-bf7da748cce4', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Fair. My trucks, my bad habit. Two on the lead truck it is. Don''t tell my guys I said that.', false, 5, '2026-09-17T03:19:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d3247247-bd74-5bcf-856a-ac05e346628f', 'f679fa1c-5fff-5756-8013-bf7da748cce4', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'My uncle''s truck is a disaster right now. Sending him this. He''s going to pretend he didn''t read it.', false, 1, '2026-09-17T10:15:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('54165981-007b-532f-98bd-4cf435079713', 'f679fa1c-5fff-5756-8013-bf7da748cce4', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'My father used to say the truck tells the customer who you are before you open your mouth. He was right, and mine still doesn''t look like his did.', false, 6, '2026-09-17T12:35:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('112d2afd-c8ae-5c06-aa77-3dcae42f9408', 'f679fa1c-5fff-5756-8013-bf7da748cce4', '9d863d1d-0f6f-5b8c-921d-d473f8721247', 'night class guy, not on a truck yet. writing all this down for when i am lol', false, 3, '2026-09-17T13:58:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('9c14094a-cf4a-5c4e-84d4-95a5cbf9dfc6', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'question', 'panel was labeled wrong and the outlet was still hot after i flipped the breaker', '1 yr in, non union shop in bergen. changing a kitchen receptacle in fair lawn today. boss said kill the kitchen circuit so i flipped the one labeled kitchen. went to pull the device and my tester lit up. still hot. turns out the kitchen counter was on the one labeled "dining" and nobody ever fixed the panel schedule.

i didn''t touch anything but i''m pretty shook. i did test thank god, that''s the only reason i''m posting this and not in the er. what should i have done different? sorry if dumb', 'electrical', 'Bergen County, NJ', 29, '2026-09-17T11:17:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('72d6c7fc-5d02-5e5a-89ac-9a011df2a4ce', '9c14094a-cf4a-5c4e-84d4-95a5cbf9dfc6', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'You did the most important thing right: you tested. Never trust a panel label. What I''d add: check your tester on a known live source before and after, so you know it actually works. Lock out and tag the breaker you turned off, even in a house. And tell your boss about the labeling so the customer gets it fixed.

This isn''t a dumb question. This is the question. Stay safe.', true, 16, '2026-09-17T23:44:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1fc6d79b-3d7f-58a7-a317-549636c79165', '9c14094a-cf4a-5c4e-84d4-95a5cbf9dfc6', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'our teacher in queens literally says ''the label is a suggestion.'' glad you tested. did your tester go off right away or only when you got close to the device?', false, 2, '2026-09-18T01:37:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9b2cb06b-9a93-5b41-9b60-2a160e8ab749', '9c14094a-cf4a-5c4e-84d4-95a5cbf9dfc6', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'New helper here, a few weeks in. Marcus told me the same thing about checking the tester on something live first. I didn''t really understand why until I read this.', false, 1, '2026-09-18T09:00:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('73141ef3-fd42-570e-b971-2a791d247e25', '6b3a1896-cd39-5ae1-8351-8817f445313d', 'question', 'got dizzy pulling galvanized out of an attic in the heat. foreman was mad i didn''t say something', 'demo day on an old cape in hamilton, like 97 out. foreman had me pulling old galvanized out of the attic for a bathroom reno. after maybe an hour i got dizzy and noticed i''d stopped sweating, which i thought was a good thing lol. foreman made me sit in the truck with the ac on and drink water. felt fine after a while.

he was mad i didn''t say something sooner. was it actually a big deal or is he overreacting', 'plumbing', 'Mercer County, NJ', 9, '2026-08-02T23:38:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e109219a-12ea-5019-9183-c6481d9f31c9', '73141ef3-fd42-570e-b971-2a791d247e25', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Your foreman is right, and he may have done you a real favor. Dizziness and stopping sweating in that kind of heat are warning signs of heat illness, and it can get serious fast. Next time: water before you''re thirsty, breaks out of the attic, and tell someone the moment you feel off. If someone gets confused or stops sweating, that''s a call for medical help, not a break.', false, 3, '2026-08-04T02:27:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('632e6a1f-8d06-5626-ad3f-f03e0458a98f', '73141ef3-fd42-570e-b971-2a791d247e25', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'stopping sweating is not good lol. it''s bad. watched a guy go down in a condenser room on the boardwalk one july. your foreman did the right thing. listen to him', false, 4, '2026-08-04T02:33:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d74cfa51-2d4f-513a-9981-3360e8795d6f', '73141ef3-fd42-570e-b971-2a791d247e25', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'What we do on summer attic days:
- Attic work first thing in the morning, done before 11 if possible
- Two people, one stays where he can see the other
- Water and electrolytes in the truck, not "I''ll grab something later"
- Anyone can stop the job if they feel off, no questions asked', false, 5, '2026-08-04T10:09:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('05f0d96f-dd9c-5598-820f-f66c3644e3b9', '73141ef3-fd42-570e-b971-2a791d247e25', 'af3fcb91-09e6-5441-8d3b-b76ecbc0192e', 'not to scare you but this happened to me my first july in burlington. went home thinking i was fine and felt terrible for two days. say something early. edit: early, not after', false, 1, '2026-08-04T11:36:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f818143a-accb-5390-8dc6-69bd8c4f0881', '73141ef3-fd42-570e-b971-2a791d247e25', '4c3c92ef-9ba5-56b3-90e4-5341be547a4a', '3rd summer in attics. the thing nobody tells you is drink water the night before too. appreciate this thread, sending it to our new guy', false, 1, '2026-08-04T16:05:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'discussion', 'CO meter went off before I hit the bottom of the basement stairs', 'service call in a 4-family in union city, water heater "making a smell." basement door was shut. my CO meter started going off before i got to the bottom of the stairs. flue pipe had come apart at the chimney.

got out, got the tenants out of the first floor, called the gas company from the sidewalk. they shut it down. the super was mad at ME lol.

4 years in and never had my meter go off like that. how many of you actually carry one, and actually turn it on?', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 16, '2026-09-07T23:16:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('25ab6f35-fd88-5605-afd4-dc0b1fe95ac1', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'You did it right. Got out, got people out, called it in. The super being mad is the super''s problem. I''m in those buildings every week. Every one of my guys carries a meter, clipped on and turned on, before they open the basement door.', false, 7, '2026-09-08T03:34:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2b9222bb-5c2b-5397-9cef-de4c46cbb477', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'turned on before the door is the part. i usually forget to turn mine on till i''m already down there lol. not anymore', false, 1, '2026-09-08T09:59:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c27d763b-43cf-55ee-8e31-71507099423a', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Glad you''re okay. What you did is the right order: get out, get others out, call the utility or 911 from outside, and don''t go back in until it''s been cleared. A personal CO meter is PPE, same as your glasses. Bump test or check it the way the manufacturer says, so you know it works when you need it. Different trade, same rule. Stay safe.', true, 36, '2026-09-08T12:08:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b4cc3d68-ad39-54cc-8002-289153ef26f1', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '0b536e7d-7d15-52d5-ae52-959dc9ae15ec', 'how often are you supposed to calibrate them? mine came with the job and idk if anyone has ever done it. foreman probably doesn''t know either', false, 4, '2026-09-08T21:33:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bd1b9269-7de7-504c-b913-a9411a5b1e59', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First, follow the manufacturer''s calibration and bump-test schedule. It''s in the manual and it''s not optional. Second, a cheap meter that works beats an expensive one sitting in the truck. Third, if nobody knows when yours was last checked, assume it hasn''t been. Ask me how I know.', false, 7, '2026-09-08T22:04:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1c374b75-ba61-52d5-a951-88884a4b8cc9', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'we got ours from the shop this summer... nobody told us anything about bump testing. going to ask monday', false, 2, '2026-09-08T23:20:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('56f2a7e5-c479-5b98-9b2b-a8276fe78718', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Scary one. My father had a call like that in Harrison years ago. What I''d tell a young guy: if the meter goes off, open it up, let it air out, and once the meter clears, fix the flue and get on with it.', false, 9, '2026-09-09T00:05:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('74614be5-f1d8-5063-8e93-f1bd8a62f19d', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Respectfully, Rui, I wouldn''t tell a young guy that. Get out first. Let the gas company or the fire department clear the building and find the source. Then you come back. Airing it out and going back to work is how good mechanics end up in the hospital.', false, 2, '2026-09-09T03:49:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('748b3c8f-b28f-58aa-850b-56f0f96893e0', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'You''re right, Ziggy. I said that wrong. Out first, utility or fire department, then the work. Thanks for catching it.', false, 5, '2026-09-09T10:14:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ca25cb0f-bb80-5a38-94e5-8f6260166280', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '07676d29-9e30-5e27-b903-f9044b52fe4b', 'pleasantville. had my meter go off in a crawlspace last winter with no gas appliance anywhere near me. turned out to be the neighbor''s generator. you never know', false, 2, '2026-09-15T20:44:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cf5c74b1-2a79-583b-85e2-be80e5ef7d70', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: once you''re allowed back in, make sure the building''s CO alarms are there and working. A flue that came apart at the chimney may also mean somebody did work without an inspection. Worth noting on your ticket.', false, 5, '2026-09-15T23:23:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6599e2b2-bcae-543b-bd26-f5883bbc9262', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'What every one of my techs carries on every call:
- Personal CO meter, on, before entering the basement
- Combustion analyzer on any fuel-burning work
- The gas utility''s emergency number saved in the phone
And they''re trained to leave first and diagnose second.', false, 12, '2026-09-16T00:27:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6bdbc43e-65f7-55a6-b40b-462e97649c40', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '2f048a7b-273e-574a-911a-7232a6136051', 'north bergen, same kind of buildings. sorry, dumb question, but how did the super blame you? you''re the one who found it', false, 1, '2026-09-16T03:32:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('37478ec8-db64-537c-8246-6da4e814f04e', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'he said i ''broke it'' when i was looking at it lol. the gas company guy told him it had been off the chimney a while. he shut up after that', false, 1, '2026-09-16T03:48:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8b346d63-d267-5719-afcc-9a879c54baec', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'So this one time in AC... hotel kitchen, the exhaust fan was dead and everyone had headaches and blamed the heat lol. my meter was the only reason we figured it out. carry it everywhere', false, 2, '2026-09-17T01:20:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e39e178c-c90f-5e4a-a6fb-d4645aa332cc', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'bayonne helper here, about 7 months in. i don''t have a meter, my lead does. should i buy my own or is that overkill?', false, 2, '2026-09-17T03:58:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('03394be2-6b98-571e-a11f-903a739235f6', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Not overkill. Buy your own. Your lead won''t always be standing next to you.', false, 5, '2026-09-17T22:08:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('062fccab-68bb-5c71-9f2e-8b3238b1ab6a', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'Sorry if this is off topic, but this is why I hate those basements with the door shut. Bayonne and JC are full of them. Glad you''re okay.', false, 1, '2026-09-18T00:06:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2bea96b4-1362-52f0-90ab-316a7cafbdf7', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'electrical guy, also union city. didn''t know we should carry these too. we''re in those basements for panels all the time. ordering one', false, 1, '2026-09-18T00:34:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e03b8992-e7ac-53c1-9313-71188a6f1f49', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Yes, you should. Electricians spend plenty of time in rooms with fuel-burning equipment, and the meter doesn''t care what trade you''re in.', false, 4, '2026-09-21T01:21:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e5c5cd50-5cb0-5c5f-be09-446a421b5645', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'f335afa5-2456-517f-bd3e-8c28f1aaa9ec', 'our instructor made all of us buy one first year and honestly i thought it was a racket. not anymore after reading this one', false, 1, '2026-09-21T10:11:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dd91ce3a-017a-5254-8eb0-5ba6acb49115', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '0b536e7d-7d15-52d5-ae52-959dc9ae15ec', 'update on mine: asked the foreman, he had no idea when it was last checked. shop is getting new ones this week', false, 1, '2026-09-21T11:12:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0727456a-0e11-5733-9ca2-2f9bd2c320bc', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'appreciate everybody. went back to that building today. new flue, CO alarms in the basement now. super even said thanks. kind of', false, 1, '2026-09-21T13:56:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5d68fff2-ae83-58c1-b2b2-e1a6e044c90b', '76fec270-043e-5e68-907c-d9ae1e6781b3', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'follow up: asked about bump testing like ms almonte said. nobody at my shop knew either lol. we''re doing it now', false, 1, '2026-09-21T14:24:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('72dd1ffc-d794-5372-a335-50c865dfb50d', 'd680c878-f79d-58ae-9875-7e9bdf0efa31', 'question', 'slid down a hot roof to the gutter on a one-story. you guys tying off for that?', 'on a roof in toms river tuesday putting a boot on a vent stack for an addition on a split level. low pitch, one story side, figured no big deal. shingles were so hot my boot just let go and i slid on my butt to the gutter. gutter held. didn''t go off the edge. boss laughed. i didn''t. are you guys tying off on a one story roof? is that overkill brother', 'plumbing', 'Ocean County, NJ', 9, '2026-08-16T14:25:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0177e523-25f7-544e-bc9c-f4f0e326d95e', '72dd1ffc-d794-5372-a335-50c865dfb50d', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: fall protection requirements depend on the height and the work, not on how easy the roof looks, and residential roofs are where a lot of serious falls happen. Ask your boss what the shop''s fall protection plan is. If there isn''t one, that''s your answer.', false, 6, '2026-08-16T23:54:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4745a334-30d0-5457-8c8f-db5201e23dba', '72dd1ffc-d794-5372-a335-50c865dfb50d', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Not overkill, kid. A one-story fall puts guys out for a year. Hot shingles in summer are like ice. Proper fall protection, a ladder that''s set right, and somebody on the ground. Your boss laughing is the part that worries me.', false, 25, '2026-08-17T00:50:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'question', 'Felt a tingle in a wet crawlspace in Manville. What do you check before going under a house?', 'Crawlspace job in Manville last week, replacing a section of drain under an old ranch. There was an inch of water down there from the storms. The work light was on an extension cord plugged into a garage outlet, no GFCI. Halfway through, the light flickered and I felt a tingle in my hand where I was holding the light and kneeling in the water. I got out right away.

The cord had a nick in it. I''m fine. My boss said I should have checked the cord, and he''s right, but I also had no idea the garage outlet wasn''t GFCI protected.

What do you all do before going into a wet crawlspace? I''d like a routine instead of luck.', 'plumbing', 'Somerset County, NJ', 7, '2026-09-11T17:00:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('6f47f4a0-b029-5108-b08e-541dedbd666e', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'First: you got out. That was the right call. A tingle in a wet space is a warning, not a nuisance.

Before any wet crawlspace: GFCI protection at the source, or a portable GFCI at the plug, and test it every time. Inspect the whole cord, end to end. Use lights rated for damp locations. And if there''s standing water and anything electrical involved, the job can wait until it''s dry. Stay safe.', true, 9, '2026-09-12T16:27:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5b142c60-3bd8-54a1-bb70-245e30dde583', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'I didn''t know portable GFCIs were a thing. Ordering one tonight.', false, 1, '2026-09-12T19:07:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('990ca446-c0b8-5007-903b-6953307d287a', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Ground-fault protection for temporary power on a job is a standard requirement, and a garage outlet in an older house may well predate GFCI. Don''t assume any outlet in an older house is protected. Test it.', false, 7, '2026-09-12T21:01:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8bd50921-2a08-5536-8ff4-48f50741d495', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly after Sandy we did hundreds of crawlspaces down here, and that''s the one thing I drilled into every helper. Portable GFCI on every cord, every time. Water under a house is a different job.', false, 2, '2026-09-12T21:20:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5ff3b31e-0741-5d07-b84d-99532a58067e', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '8537b87b-2917-5fba-aac2-8e516880bdaf', 'sorry dumb q but does a gfci actually stop you from getting shocked, or does it just stop it from killing you lol', false, 1, '2026-09-12T22:01:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ec924589-76d6-58cc-9c28-bfaa9de76f50', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fwiw it doesn''t stop the first bit of current. it trips fast enough that it usually isn''t dangerous, so you might still feel something. that''s why you also fix the cord and stay out of the water', false, 3, '2026-09-13T01:30:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('44579e46-d6cd-585d-9127-ec0e30a09c75', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '31e0974e-aadd-529c-90fc-0385fc7c46a5', 'bound brook here, everything flooded that same week. idk how many crawlspaces we''ve been in since. glad you''re ok', false, 1, '2026-09-13T09:07:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('441b1b90-8c82-5083-9404-770dfed4a067', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Crawlspace routine at my company:
- Look before you crawl: water, wiring, animals, smell
- Portable GFCI and a cord you''ve inspected
- Someone outside who knows you''re in there
- Phone or radio on you
- If it smells like sewage or gas, nobody goes in yet', false, 3, '2026-09-14T00:04:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f4e233dc-ffb9-5200-afb8-a6aca5898608', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', '1st year here. Our instructor calls crawlspaces confined spaces ''in spirit.'' Not sure that''s the official definition, but it stuck with me.', false, 2, '2026-09-14T01:56:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cd249c59-4810-5302-bb79-4dd61d1495cd', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Careful with that one. Whether a space counts as a permit-required confined space is a specific determination, and some crawlspaces could qualify depending on the hazards. On our jobs the competent person makes that call. Your instructor''s instinct is right, though: treat it with that respect.', false, 5, '2026-09-15T01:42:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('aaaf6f14-5350-5c1b-83b5-32a8d1e71325', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'vo-tech electrical guy here, over-explaining: a nicked cord plus wet ground means you were the path. that''s literally what our teacher draws on the board every year. glad you''re not the example now', false, 2, '2026-09-15T09:49:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5203853f-2fa4-594c-add3-2f2b4f8788c3', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', '> you were the path

That''s a sentence I won''t forget anytime soon.', false, 3, '2026-09-15T10:57:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e87584fc-60e7-52e1-9bff-6f1344237580', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'your boss is right about the cord. you''re right nobody told you about the outlet. both true. now you know', false, 3, '2026-09-16T00:06:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('185dd1e5-40c5-5160-87c1-b62e38fbdd2b', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', 'ed01b27e-7f0b-586c-bcb9-397a7d11f3fe', 'Every sump call in a finished basement after a storm, I think about this. Appreciate you posting it. Buying a second portable GFCI for the van.', false, 8, '2026-09-16T02:09:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('eaa7fdd2-8dbd-5830-a206-7b189b86627d', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'You asked what we do. Look first, test the GFCI, tell someone. You know all that now. The thing I''d add: say no when it''s not safe yet, even to your boss.', false, 6, '2026-09-17T01:26:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d1f5b913-ce3e-5d4d-b2b6-4d5d9633d41b', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', 'df0dfff9-4016-5ddb-a8b6-c4029b1e30b2', 'bound brook. foreman made us start carrying portable gfcis after one of our guys got bit last year. didnt think about why until now', false, 2, '2026-09-17T13:07:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('820fc857-c2c8-54cf-ad3a-a16738b89ba7', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'Did a flooded crawlspace in Deptford after the August storms. Didn''t think twice about the cord. I will now. Appreciate it.', false, 1, '2026-09-17T14:04:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('37b301a8-5c7a-54bb-8d47-eb8073886db9', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'One more: if you ever take a real shock, even if you feel fine afterward, tell someone and consider getting checked out. Some injuries don''t show up right away.', false, 4, '2026-09-17T22:24:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ce584075-e12e-551e-93f8-cc173bda11d6', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Thank you. I hadn''t thought about getting checked. I felt fine, but I''ll mention it to my doctor anyway.', false, 1, '2026-09-17T22:54:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('652d5cec-4af1-59c8-a2a8-48c239ad833a', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '7ae3dcf8-1c9a-56f2-bc63-f1efe2a2d403', 'bound brook too, hvac. we had a whole unit on this in school and i still almost did the same thing last month lol. saved this', false, 0, '2026-09-18T00:33:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('49489af7-c279-586d-8c71-973411639dc2', '70c12aa5-415f-54a3-8c28-16c22ac39528', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'update: the shop bought portable GFCIs for every truck after I showed my boss this thread. Small win.', false, 3, '2026-09-18T02:12:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5fae92d6-baee-59ed-99a1-e88b366a5ae3', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'question', 'Rung cracked on the homeowner''s old wooden ladder during my ride-along', 'Quick one from the electrician ride-along. Our ladder was on the other truck and the homeowner insisted we use her old wooden extension ladder from the garage. I went up first to look at a soffit light and a rung cracked under my foot. I caught myself, nothing happened. The electrician just said "that''s why we don''t use customer ladders" and moved on. Is that an actual rule people follow, or did he just say it because I almost fell?', 'other', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 10, '2026-10-05T00:35:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('7801ae1c-492c-59f8-ba43-3f72f134d252', '5fae92d6-baee-59ed-99a1-e88b366a5ae3', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'It''s a real rule at every good shop I''ve known. You don''t know how a customer''s ladder was stored, what it''s rated for, or what''s cracked. Your own ladder, inspected, set at the right angle, on stable ground. He was teaching you something. Take it.', false, 6, '2026-10-05T01:19:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dc2f5c7b-7793-5223-8b32-386a614dbdf8', '5fae92d6-baee-59ed-99a1-e88b366a5ae3', '8498b67e-8832-52a9-854b-bbe6514f03b3', 'almost the same thing happened to me on a step stool at the bar lol. not the same at all but i get it. glad you''re ok, keep posting these ride along stories', false, 2, '2026-10-05T02:15:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('e759ee61-d1ec-5f8a-b0b0-66e85b97f6ea', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'tip', 'Heat wave week: 14 no-cool calls in two days and what I keep telling new techs', 'So this one time in AC... ok it''s this week, not one time lol. 14 no-cool calls Monday and Tuesday between Cherry Hill and Washington Township. Half were dirty filters and clogged condensate lines, a couple capacitors, one frozen coil the homeowner "fixed" by turning the thermostat down to 60.

What I keep telling my new guys on ride-alongs... check airflow before you even think about the charge. Check the condensate before you blame the unit. Drink water in the truck between every call, not when you''re already dizzy. And if the attic is an oven, do the attic part first thing in the morning and come down for air often. Nobody gets a medal for passing out over an air handler.

What are you guys seeing this week?', 'hvac', 'Camden County, NJ', 17, '2026-08-22T13:01:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('75f59b41-1d4e-5256-994e-0c4d50c92bd8', 'e759ee61-d1ec-5f8a-b0b0-66e85b97f6ea', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'walk-ins down here. every restaurant on the boardwalk calls at 4pm on a saturday when the box hits 50. dirty condensers, every one. winter is when you learn, summer is when you survive', false, 6, '2026-08-23T00:10:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('983dd940-0c4d-5c78-ad24-98e4db4a26fb', 'e759ee61-d1ec-5f8a-b0b0-66e85b97f6ea', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'first summer brother... 3 frozen coils this week in paterson, all filters. my lead makes me check airflow first every single time now', false, 0, '2026-08-23T03:07:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c91f36b4-ca18-5b87-8413-1bc37f73433a', 'e759ee61-d1ec-5f8a-b0b0-66e85b97f6ea', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Same here in Middlesex. What I''d add for the new techs:
- Write down what you found, even on the easy calls; patterns show up
- Don''t promise same-day on a part you don''t have on the truck
- Heat-wave callbacks cost more than the calls did', false, 5, '2026-08-23T10:27:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3a2f7b58-8370-5368-b331-44cf495b7ca5', 'e759ee61-d1ec-5f8a-b0b0-66e85b97f6ea', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Kash with the callbacks lol. he''s right though... the heat wave callback is the one that eats your saturday', false, 2, '2026-08-24T02:43:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3abf1a82-2531-5f68-a3fd-e480b812ac09', 'e759ee61-d1ec-5f8a-b0b0-66e85b97f6ea', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'toms river. capacitors and clogged drains all week. drank like 6 waters yesterday and still got a headache. thanks for the reminder', false, 1, '2026-08-24T09:53:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('56730198-8370-590d-b044-aab1740cfbf0', 'e759ee61-d1ec-5f8a-b0b0-66e85b97f6ea', '3839ca6e-9b97-5146-a0ce-e1221e0f3b8e', 'pemberton, running calls solo this summer. the come down for air thing, my shop doesn''t really do that. should i bring it up? thanks in advance', false, 1, '2026-08-24T10:36:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2bedca3b-cb00-58e6-b11c-20b814e7f47f', 'e759ee61-d1ec-5f8a-b0b0-66e85b97f6ea', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Bring it up... nicely lol. Say you want to go up with someone and take turns. Most bosses say yes when you put it that way', false, 12, '2026-08-25T01:50:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ff50502f-0c51-52ab-ab69-a8e19f55fd5b', 'e759ee61-d1ec-5f8a-b0b0-66e85b97f6ea', '4ba5185c-1185-5ec2-ac92-cea31f2ca143', 'lakewood, first summer. the thermostat down to 60 thing happened on literally our first call monday lol. is that why the coil freezes or is it the filter mostly?', false, 1, '2026-08-25T02:55:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('3ad42076-77aa-55e0-82a3-d3ab0e8e04e0', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'question', 'Route 1 at 6am in my mom''s car for a $17/hr summer job. Ask about travel or suck it up?', 'Over-explaining as usual. Got a summer job with an electrical contractor whose shop is in North Brunswick, and the jobs are all over Middlesex and Mercer. I live in Hamilton and I don''t have my own car, so I''m borrowing my mom''s. Route 1 at 6am is a parking lot from the Quaker Bridge area up, and when I take the Turnpike instead the tolls add up fast. Gas is killing me too. I make $17 an hour.

Is it normal for a shop to pay nothing for travel for a summer kid? Should I ask, or just suck it up until school starts?', 'electrical', 'Mercer County, NJ', 15, '2026-08-05T23:33:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('f7ec9c38-1ce2-575a-aede-a7696e4be298', '3ad42076-77aa-55e0-82a3-d3ab0e8e04e0', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Normal for a summer kid, unfortunately. My father never paid travel for helpers, and I swore I''d change that when I took over. I only half did. What you can ask: can you meet at the job instead of the shop, or ride in with a guy who lives near you. Owners say yes to that a lot more often than to money.', false, 2, '2026-08-06T02:28:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c225b9b4-d39a-535e-b0eb-445e03019a86', '3ad42076-77aa-55e0-82a3-d3ab0e8e04e0', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Small thing, but your toll cost depends a lot on E-ZPass and the time of day. Run your real route through the toll calculator instead of guessing. And ask about meeting at the job. Commute time is easier to fix than pay.', false, 7, '2026-08-06T09:45:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('febdd11f-5ad3-552a-8fc1-4bd1f6d2d45e', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'question', 'boss offered me the van home but it''s GPS tracked with no personal stops', 'boss offered to let me take the van home starting next month. catch is gps tracking, no personal stops, not even wawa on the way in lol, and i''d be on the emergency list some weekends. saves my car and gas money. but it kind of feels like a leash. do you guys take the van home? worth it? thanks in advance', 'electrical', 'Bergen County, NJ', 3, '2026-09-15T00:53:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('48e49bfc-9a8a-52dc-86af-a662799c8cbb', 'febdd11f-5ad3-552a-8fc1-4bd1f6d2d45e', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'GPS is normal now, most shops have it. Whether it''s worth it depends on how often they''ll call you out. Ask how weekend calls get paid before you say yes.', false, 3, '2026-09-15T09:41:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a1664052-7b8f-5224-b747-1a2bccc25bb4', 'febdd11f-5ad3-552a-8fc1-4bd1f6d2d45e', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'i take my shop''s van home in clifton. honestly the gas savings alone is like a raise. they don''t care about a coffee stop on the way in though, ask if wawa counts lol', false, 3, '2026-09-15T15:58:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e54b4a6c-5481-5a6c-a412-31bcec619627', 'febdd11f-5ad3-552a-8fc1-4bd1f6d2d45e', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'My guys take the trucks home. From the owner side, kid: a truck at your house means I can send you straight to a job at 7, or to a no-heat call at night. The no-stops rule is about insurance and about customers seeing my truck parked outside a bar. A coffee on the way in I don''t care about, but ask yours. Get the rules in writing so nobody argues later.', false, 6, '2026-09-15T16:48:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1b62a581-688a-50e7-b7b4-bd158eaac999', 'febdd11f-5ad3-552a-8fc1-4bd1f6d2d45e', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'One thing to ask while you''re at it: who''s insured if you''re in an accident on the way home. Not legal advice, but that''s a question for your boss and his insurance agent, not something to guess at.', false, 8, '2026-09-15T18:39:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('167925e5-0b5c-5d57-a6be-de6ccecabd42', '48b61243-8eaf-5f00-b8aa-9268dc17b5af', 'question', 'staten island guy, job offer in woodbridge. worth paying the bridge toll home every day?', 'tottenville, staten island. working for a small shop on the island, boss is decent but won''t pay for school. got an offer from a shop in woodbridge that does pay for school. it''s like 15 min over the outerbridge without traffic. the bridge going into jersey is free i think, it''s coming back into the city that costs money and it''s not cheap. so every day i''d pay to come home lol.

also if i ever want a nyc license someday, does jersey work even count? sorry for over explaining brother', 'electrical', 'Staten Island, NY', 18, '2026-08-20T09:49:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('3c720ef4-bfa4-56fa-950f-61ce9ef8e65a', '167925e5-0b5c-5d57-a6be-de6ccecabd42', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different, and you''re asking the right question early. Last I checked, the DOB wants documented experience, and whether out-of-state work counts depends on the license and how it''s documented. Read the DOB''s own requirements for your trade before deciding based on that. School paid for and a shorter commute than most guys on Brooklyn jobs? Woodbridge sounds good to me.', false, 9, '2026-08-20T12:07:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3350dd83-b83b-5d31-9d2e-f1917aa73d53', '167925e5-0b5c-5d57-a6be-de6ccecabd42', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, guys on my crew pay way more in tunnel tolls every day. One bridge toll home to get your school paid for? Take it. Just don''t count on the Outerbridge being 15 minutes. It isn''t.', false, 4, '2026-08-21T00:01:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8dfafa32-e4c4-5780-9fa7-dd7e4868e7b3', '167925e5-0b5c-5d57-a6be-de6ccecabd42', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'Career switcher in Irvington, different situation, but my commute''s 35 minutes each way on a good day. School being paid for is worth a lot of tolls from what everyone told me here.', false, 1, '2026-08-21T00:43:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('54e7d2c5-a077-5444-88ca-4012039c36e7', '167925e5-0b5c-5d57-a6be-de6ccecabd42', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Two different questions. Tolls: ask the new shop whether they reimburse, some do. License: think about where you want to be working in ten years and follow that board.', false, 3, '2026-08-21T02:41:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4c769853-ff18-5d88-89c7-480b802ff471', '167925e5-0b5c-5d57-a6be-de6ccecabd42', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'manahawkin here. some weeks i drive the parkway an hour each way to jobs. a 15 minute bridge sounds like a vacation honestly', false, 1, '2026-08-21T09:05:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9be20607-05c9-5f22-8c16-160a0e80a8a4', '167925e5-0b5c-5d57-a6be-de6ccecabd42', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Another angle: a shop that pays for school is investing in you, and that usually shows up in how they train you on the job too. I''d weigh that more than the toll. And give yourself extra time on that bridge in the winter.', false, 6, '2026-08-22T14:04:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('a038bdb1-1bb4-5391-8969-41566909c22f', 'fb3a0b82-da77-5dd7-9a89-e099391b6ce7', 'question', 'three Hoboken parking tickets in four days and my boss won''t cover them', 'Shop sent me to a brownstone job in Hoboken for two weeks. No driveway, no permit, and the parking enforcement is out at 8am sharp. Three tickets in four days. Boss says parking is part of the job and he won''t pay them. Is that normal or is he full of it? And how are you guys parking in Hoboken and JC with a van full of material?', 'plumbing', 'Essex County, NJ', 21, '2026-08-31T00:06:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('eab375d1-0ba6-5b02-b2c6-65aac651c1d0', 'a038bdb1-1bb4-5391-8969-41566909c22f', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question: who pays, or how to park? Who pays: at my shop, if I sent you there, the parking is on me. Not every shop does that. How to park: before the job, have the GC or homeowner ask the city about contractor permits or temporary no-parking signs, unload and move the van, and walk from a lot. Hoboken doesn''t care that you have a van.', false, 10, '2026-08-31T01:10:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('aca913c2-80d2-5cff-845a-8db904b25c05', 'a038bdb1-1bb4-5391-8969-41566909c22f', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'cherry hill guy so idk hoboken at all... but 3 tickets in 4 days would be my whole week''s lunch money lol. at least ask him to split them', false, 2, '2026-08-31T09:52:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('53c0d258-313e-5ae9-b466-104a2552f055', 'cbe525cf-5b87-54d7-b315-7c60d722e874', 'question', 'starting next week in brooklyn and they want me driving my own car to jobs', 'starting as a helper next week, 42, career change. the shop is in brooklyn and they want me to drive my own car to jobs around brooklyn and the island. verrazzano toll every time i cross (the resident discount helps i think), plus parking in bay ridge and park slope. about gas they said "we''ll see." sorry if this is a dumb question but is it normal to ask about mileage before you even start? i don''t want to seem difficult before day one', 'plumbing', 'Staten Island, NY', 5, '2026-10-02T02:32:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('00156c36-817d-5c1d-9497-63ea731b0cd0', '53c0d258-313e-5ae9-b466-104a2552f055', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Not dumb. Ask before you start, it''s easier now than six months from now. Keep it simple: "How do you handle tolls and mileage when I use my car for jobs?" A good shop has an answer. "We''ll see" isn''t an answer yet, so ask again before your first day.', true, 20, '2026-10-02T02:57:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c97ae2fd-da07-5d8d-9aef-9ffc91562b98', '53c0d258-313e-5ae9-b466-104a2552f055', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'I drive my own car to jobs around Somerset County and didn''t ask when I started. Two years later I''m only now getting ready to bring up mileage. Ask now. I wish I had.', false, 1, '2026-10-02T09:25:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7ab5939f-60df-5e8c-8c5b-8345b884147b', '53c0d258-313e-5ae9-b466-104a2552f055', '8498b67e-8832-52a9-854b-bbe6514f03b3', '36 here, also switching. had the same worry about seeming difficult. everyone told me asking isn''t difficult, it''s normal. good luck next week', false, 2, '2026-10-02T09:47:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('56080fd2-0b68-5c01-8afb-7a5a6d1b1bcb', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'question', 'Bronx shop landed a Midtown high-rise. Driving in, or the 6 train with my tools?', 'My non-union shop in the Bronx got a three-month job on a high-rise in Midtown. First time I''ll be working in Manhattan. Driving in means the congestion charge plus parking, and the foreman says garages near the job cost about as much as a car payment. Taking the subway means carrying my tools on the 6 at 5:30am.

How do you guys do it? Does anyone''s shop actually pay for parking in the city? Appreciate it.

edit: shop says they''ll cover parking for the lead only. subway it is.', 'electrical', 'Bronx, NY', 5, '2026-07-31T02:57:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('70d67439-bb18-571b-993e-f262c1a8237a', '56080fd2-0b68-5c01-8afb-7a5a6d1b1bcb', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, I''ve been doing this 21 years. Nobody drives to Midtown unless the company pays. Your gang box stays on the job and you carry a small bag. Get there early, because the freight elevator line is the real commute. Find out day one where the shanty is and who runs the hoist. And for what it''s worth, the 7 is worse than the 6.', true, 13, '2026-08-02T16:42:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7f214c1c-0aa1-59cd-9e69-814f30c835ec', '56080fd2-0b68-5c01-8afb-7a5a6d1b1bcb', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'Gang box stays on the job, that makes sense. I''ve been carrying my whole bag home every night like an idiot. Appreciate it.', false, 1, '2026-08-02T18:51:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('adb607ec-7be6-5b77-aa75-220349aa356f', '56080fd2-0b68-5c01-8afb-7a5a6d1b1bcb', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different from Jersey shops: plenty of NYC shops don''t pay parking at all, and some pay a garage for the lead only, like yours. Ask before every new job. Don''t assume either way.', false, 5, '2026-08-03T00:33:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('aeb906af-0eb6-57e4-b9fb-f5a704215ae6', '56080fd2-0b68-5c01-8afb-7a5a6d1b1bcb', '393b9bbb-e88d-53b5-be6e-c1c847014fa4', 'Apex grad, plumbing. My foreman takes the R in with a small bag too. Once you do it a week it''s fine. The 5am train is basically all trades anyway.', false, 3, '2026-08-03T02:15:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8e2d7e88-87d8-53bc-8cfe-ed3ba55f9899', '56080fd2-0b68-5c01-8afb-7a5a6d1b1bcb', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'jersey guy here, union city. how do they even get material up a high-rise if nobody drives in? do trucks just block the whole street?', false, 3, '2026-08-03T02:42:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('500f9330-7543-55bb-9e81-cc629eb5d543', '56080fd2-0b68-5c01-8afb-7a5a6d1b1bcb', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Deliveries are scheduled, usually early, with a loading area and a time slot for the hoist. On the city jobs I did back in my union days, miss your slot and you wait half a day. The city teaches you patience whether you want it or not.', false, 9, '2026-08-11T02:58:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('28076ded-a7c4-52e6-81ac-c58cc36dbf08', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'tip', 'For the Jersey guys walking onto my Midtown job late: tunnels, PATH, and DOB inspection days', 'Brother, this is for the Jersey guys I keep watching walk in at 6:58 with a coffee from the tunnel line.

One: leave earlier than you think. The Lincoln on a random Tuesday will eat 40 minutes for no reason.

Two: the PATH or the bus plus a walk beats driving unless the company pays the garage, and most don''t.

Three: on inspection days, the inspector sees your area before he sees your work. Clean, covers on, panels labeled, no open boxes you can''t explain. In my experience an inspector who walks into a mess starts looking harder. I''ve watched good work get picked apart because the floor looked like a dumpster.

Get in early on inspection day. That''s all I''ve got.', 'electrical', 'Queens, NY', 12, '2026-09-09T23:03:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('592d22cd-cb52-5a04-89ee-aec2c0521ea9', '28076ded-a7c4-52e6-81ac-c58cc36dbf08', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'union city, i can see the helix from my window and on days the shop sends me into the city i still leave at 5. the lincoln is a coin flip every morning lol', false, 2, '2026-09-10T00:46:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3a51ead3-5324-5cfe-b57d-a0fde37a28b4', '28076ded-a7c4-52e6-81ac-c58cc36dbf08', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different from Jersey on inspection day too: more people walking the job, more paperwork on the wall. Same rule as yours though. A clean area buys you patience.', false, 4, '2026-09-10T02:23:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8e26dbdb-735b-5bf5-8b06-fcf799d87eb9', '28076ded-a7c4-52e6-81ac-c58cc36dbf08', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Same on the Jersey side. Inspection day is also a safety day: covers on, nothing energized left open, everyone in their PPE. An inspector notices a crew that works safe.', false, 1, '2026-09-10T03:03:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0414d7a3-447f-57da-977b-32a1d6332e5f', '28076ded-a7c4-52e6-81ac-c58cc36dbf08', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'Took your gang box advice from my Midtown thread over the summer. Now it''s the inspection day advice. Appreciate it.', false, 7, '2026-09-10T03:45:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fc97b1f1-fdf3-5790-8aa2-313d871bbf11', '28076ded-a7c4-52e6-81ac-c58cc36dbf08', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', '164 guy, not in the city... but my cousin''s in 3 and commutes from teaneck. he says the same thing, the bus beats driving most days... and a wawa stop is not an option lol', false, 2, '2026-09-10T10:05:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cf04925e-9403-5c13-b9d4-e04ba4879b98', '28076ded-a7c4-52e6-81ac-c58cc36dbf08', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Your cousin''s right. The bus and a walk beat sitting in the helix with your engine running, every time.', false, 11, '2026-09-11T02:13:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('732bcc13-f424-5b24-a469-09b6744a517d', '28076ded-a7c4-52e6-81ac-c58cc36dbf08', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'Queens trade program, applying to 3 this round. Writing all of this down for when I''m on a job like that someday.', false, 2, '2026-09-11T09:17:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d065b6b7-9dee-5e10-9347-744d73b16972', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'discussion', 'Boardwalk''s slow after Labor Day. That''s when I take a helper.', 'boardwalk''s quiet now. july was brutal, walk-ins dying every afternoon, ice machines, a whole freezer of shrimp at a place i won''t name. now it''s slow and that''s when i take a helper along.

people think summer is when you learn. summer is when you run. winter is when you learn. you''ve got time to open things up, explain them, let you braze something without a restaurant owner standing over you yelling about his fish.

if you''re down here, atlantic or cape may, and curious about refrigeration, ask around the shops in october. we''re all slower and nicer. a little.', 'hvac', 'Atlantic County, NJ', 28, '2026-09-13T16:38:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('48f9b89c-2591-59dd-99f2-451e80dd2cd6', 'd065b6b7-9dee-5e10-9347-744d73b16972', '85d3dc63-b215-52ad-b741-7bace7266d53', 'egg harbor brother, residential hvac 1 yr. never touched refrigeration. is it worth asking even with zero commercial experience?', false, 2, '2026-09-13T18:04:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c5d16286-ef0e-5e2b-8e35-07c77bbc5589', 'd065b6b7-9dee-5e10-9347-744d73b16972', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'yes. nobody down here had commercial experience before somebody gave them some. have your 608, show up on time, don''t be scared of the cold', false, 3, '2026-09-13T19:02:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('18aaad74-2c0b-5884-85e2-e44139985673', 'd065b6b7-9dee-5e10-9347-744d73b16972', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'tnguyen''s right... I did casino chillers in AC for years and the winters were where I actually learned the big stuff. summers you just survive lol', false, 7, '2026-09-14T00:48:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('7e686769-2a08-50b7-9429-1d245ff4335b', '4c3c92ef-9ba5-56b3-90e4-5341be547a4a', 'discussion', 'crane day at a middle school, finished the rooftop swaps the night before teachers came back', 'long one sorry. our shop had rooftop unit swaps at a middle school near asbury, 4 units, and they had to be done before teachers came back. crane day was a 5am start, roof was already hot by 9. i was on tag lines and the curb adapters. foreman was strict about the swing zone, nobody under the pick, nobody on the edge without being tied off, and honestly after hearing stories in here i didn''t mind.

last unit got wired and started up at like 9pm the night before the teachers'' first day. sat on the tailgate after with a gatorade and just looked at it lol.

3rd year and it''s the first job where i felt like i actually built something. appreciate the crew i''m on.', 'hvac', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 7, '2026-08-09T23:15:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d1700801-9333-53d7-9a94-7184139ebf10', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', 'question', 'journeyman has me on the morning wawa run and ''forgets'' to pay me back', 'so this is a dumb one... 2nd year in 164, my journeyman has me do the wawa run every morning before we start. coffee, his hoagie for lunch, sometimes for 3 guys. he always says he''ll get me back friday... friday never comes lol. it''s like $20-30 a week. i like him, he teaches me a lot. do i say something or is this just part of being the apprentice? thanks in advance', 'electrical', 'Bergen County, NJ', 18, '2026-08-30T18:13:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e5862ea6-96e5-5a7c-bda0-44af36a68542', 'd1700801-9333-53d7-9a94-7184139ebf10', '02a13f50-be86-588b-966d-7ae10b7d64cd', 'the wawa run is tradition... the not paying you back part is not tradition lol. your getting played. $30 a week is real money on an apprentice check', false, 1, '2026-08-31T00:13:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a06c86ae-fa07-5162-9639-2a46e2921a8d', 'd1700801-9333-53d7-9a94-7184139ebf10', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Say something. ''Hey, can you get me back today, I''m short this week.'' Said with a smile, on a Friday. And up here it should be QuickChek, but that''s another thread.', false, 3, '2026-08-31T01:35:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ad4a5c79-0ded-5afd-8114-63899c679357', 'd1700801-9333-53d7-9a94-7184139ebf10', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'lol my first lead owed me like $200 in coffee by christmas lol. finally said something and he paid me in one lump and bought me a pork roll egg and cheese every day for a week. say something', false, 3, '2026-08-31T03:44:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('098c95f9-f3aa-50c8-a516-81460a7cc1ac', 'd1700801-9333-53d7-9a94-7184139ebf10', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Getting coffee is a normal part of being the newest guy on a crew. Paying for it out of your own check isn''t. On my crews the apprentice runs and the journeyman pays up front. Suggest that: ''Give me the cash before I go and I''ll get everything.'' Nobody has to feel called out.', false, 8, '2026-08-31T09:09:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('33f03082-7b08-5fbe-97b5-b376818fc876', 'd1700801-9333-53d7-9a94-7184139ebf10', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', 'update: did the ''give me the cash first'' thing monday... he laughed, handed me a twenty and said ''about time you asked.'' thanks everyone', false, 2, '2026-08-31T11:18:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('e3c5e260-b34e-5acc-86eb-f0eb5ebba898', '63579434-616f-5a6d-8f1f-281437382d7a', 'question', 'Weekend helper offer at $17/hr while I finish vo-tech. Fair or lowball?', 'I''m in the HVAC program at the county vo-tech, graduating next year. A residential shop near Neptune offered me Saturdays plus some days over winter break at $17 an hour, mostly carrying equipment and cleaning up after installs. My cousin says that''s a lowball. My teacher says take anything that gets me hours.

I care more about the experience than the money, but I also don''t want to get taken advantage of. Is $17 reasonable for a student with zero hours?

edit: I first wrote that it was cash. It''s on the books, I misread the text.', 'hvac', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 5, '2026-08-16T01:15:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('7e6c7b90-a360-592d-9305-781f25390aab', 'e3c5e260-b34e-5acc-86eb-f0eb5ebba898', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'the rate matters less than whether anyone teaches you. on the books is the right answer.', false, 3, '2026-08-16T03:24:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f5cd8915-29d5-5ecb-a47e-0b3aaa3656d7', 'e3c5e260-b34e-5acc-86eb-f0eb5ebba898', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'From what I hear around here, that''s within the normal range for a student doing weekend helper work. I''d care more about three other things: that it''s on the books (it is), that someone gives you a real safety talk before they put you in an attic, and that someone explains what you''re carrying and why. If you get those, you''re being paid twice.

Attics on a Saturday in summer are no joke. Stay safe.', true, 20, '2026-08-16T10:28:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('000c8470-be44-5bee-b2a7-aae33326bfa6', 'e3c5e260-b34e-5acc-86eb-f0eb5ebba898', 'df0dfff9-4016-5ddb-a8b6-c4029b1e30b2', 'i started at about that out of school, got bumped after 3 months when my foreman told the boss i was worth it. did they say anything about a raise once you graduate? and do they do service or only installs', false, 1, '2026-08-16T12:55:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e35b6b06-128f-535c-878e-5e32c288762f', 'e3c5e260-b34e-5acc-86eb-f0eb5ebba898', '63579434-616f-5a6d-8f1f-281437382d7a', 'Installs mostly, some maintenance in the fall. Didn''t ask about a raise yet, I''ll ask when I go in Saturday. Thanks brother.', false, 1, '2026-08-16T14:09:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('3c5478ee-4be6-5e23-a40a-42ddb455c098', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'discussion', 'Update on my $21/hr question: had the review', 'Sorry, this is long. A while back I asked whether $21/hr was low for a 2nd-year non-union plumber near Manville. I had my review on Friday.

I brought a written list of what I can do alone now: water heaters, toilets, most drain calls, two small repipes. I asked for $24 plus mileage. I got $23 and mileage at a set rate per mile, which is less than I asked for but more than I had. My boss said we''d "talk again in the spring."

Is it normal to land in the middle like that, or did I leave money on the table?', 'plumbing', 'Somerset County, NJ', 14, '2026-09-28T01:40:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('6b36875f-6b2e-5ed4-aaa4-77cf61b209ef', '3c5478ee-4be6-5e23-a40a-42ddb455c098', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I look for when I give a raise, and you did most of it: you came in with what you can do on your own, not what you think you deserve. Landing in the middle is normal; most owners expect to.

The part I''d lock down is "talk again in the spring." Ask him what specifically he wants to see by then, and write it down while you''re still in the room.', true, 22, '2026-09-28T23:12:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('04324abd-4b34-5914-b5b5-bff901e58907', '3c5478ee-4be6-5e23-a40a-42ddb455c098', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Good outcome. Two things to check now that it''s settled:
- Is the mileage on your pay stub, or cash in an envelope? It should be on paper
- Get the new rate in writing, even a text
The $2 matters, but the mileage is the part most guys forget to ask for.', false, 3, '2026-09-29T00:23:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('86d24471-0005-564d-9390-6d7b919984e8', '3c5478ee-4be6-5e23-a40a-42ddb455c098', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly that''s a solid review. I''ve had guys walk in asking for five dollars more with nothing to show me. You showed up with a list. Keep adding to it every month and spring takes care of itself.', false, 6, '2026-09-29T00:48:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('831b4247-c7e1-5caa-aa01-b703cb5989fd', '3c5478ee-4be6-5e23-a40a-42ddb455c098', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'nice... i asked for a raise in june with no list and got ''we''ll see''. doing the list thing next time', false, 2, '2026-09-29T03:16:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a6dc09cd-087c-56b0-b8b2-1b4d16c803f5', '3c5478ee-4be6-5e23-a40a-42ddb455c098', 'aa4aa383-9b0a-5294-809c-62f229f9606e', 'fair brother. the $40 number I threw out in your other thread was my buddy counting his whole union package, found out after. $23 and mileage sounds right from what I''ve heard since', false, 2, '2026-09-29T03:51:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('911c8819-0322-57fd-90c8-8c1886b8dcca', '3c5478ee-4be6-5e23-a40a-42ddb455c098', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'edit: thanks all. I texted him asking for the spring goals like haddad_mech said and he actually sent them back. Two items. Writing them on the inside of my truck visor.', false, 2, '2026-09-29T09:16:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'question', '3 years non-union. would applying to 164 mean taking a pay cut?', 'so i''m 3 years in at a small non-union shop near garfield. decent boss, no school though. been thinking about applying to the IBEW apprenticeship but from what i can tell a first year apprentice makes less per hour than i do now. i''m at $25 on the books, no benefits, no retirement. is the cut worth it? do they give you credit for the years you already have or do i start at zero? not trying to start a union vs non-union fight, just trying to do the math. thanks in advance', 'electrical', 'Bergen County, NJ', 35, '2026-09-22T09:29:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('f54606f9-2398-5222-8355-a17722e01bfc', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Fair question, and you''re doing the math the right way. Compare the whole package, not the hourly. Apprentice wages usually step up each year as a percentage of the journeyman rate, and on top of the check there''s health coverage, pension and annuity contributions, and the schooling, none of which you have now.

Whether they credit prior experience is a question for the apprenticeship office directly. I won''t guess for 164. Some programs have ways to place experienced applicants, but don''t count on it. Stay safe.', true, 9, '2026-09-22T23:54:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e87afbcd-6e9f-59a6-90f5-5cd3f5e93112', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'If you want the math to be honest, price out what you have now:
- Health insurance you''d buy on your own: get a real quote
- Retirement: $0 now, so that''s a real gap
- School: what night classes would cost you out of pocket
Add those to your $25 and then compare. Sometimes the cut is smaller than it looks. Sometimes it isn''t.', false, 3, '2026-09-23T03:47:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0e683856-00e1-5eca-843e-1d8a2d148a5e', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly, three years in a good non-union shop isn''t nothing. If your boss will sign off on your experience toward a license someday, that''s a path too. I went that way and it worked for me. But no school and no retirement at year 3 is the part I''d want fixed one way or the other.', false, 6, '2026-09-23T03:55:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('72087ca8-b98d-5b70-ae8d-e82a24417792', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', '02a13f50-be86-588b-966d-7ae10b7d64cd', 'don''t quit before you get in, the list can take forever... wait you didn''t say you were quitting lol. ignore me. but still, don''t quit early', false, 1, '2026-09-23T09:54:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6b79c4eb-f748-573e-b149-2c114dbef527', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'One thing from the hiring side: three years with nothing on paper is the weak spot either way. Start keeping a log of your work now and ask your boss to put your hours in writing. If you stay non-union and want a license someday, you''ll need it. If you apply, it helps at the interview.', false, 8, '2026-09-24T01:08:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('652e0079-6b79-5a54-a456-2346ac51b6c4', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', '2nd year in 164 here... I took a cut too, came from a non-union shop in Teaneck where I was making a little more. Year one was tight. Year two the check caught up and the benefits are real. That''s just me though', false, 5, '2026-09-24T02:25:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('eab15bb7-017f-50be-91a7-2dc364e6e3e7', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'appreciate it. the health insurance quote is a good point, never priced it. would a 1st year rate be like half of what a journeyman makes?', false, 1, '2026-09-24T09:43:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('678eb666-9806-555f-9e8b-6f87caa7b53e', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Roughly in that neighborhood for a first-year, from what I''ve seen, but each program sets its own percentages and steps. The local publishes its wage sheet. Look at the actual numbers instead of guessing, and ask the apprenticeship office.', false, 5, '2026-09-25T01:39:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('554e6286-d84d-568b-8385-0e6c6e131184', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', 'cee246a3-b9ec-55fd-8ac0-35c06eeed07f', '1st year 164 here, i came straight from vo-tech so i didn''t take a cut. but the night school alone would cost real money if you paid for it yourself. also the raises come on a schedule so you never have to go ask for one', false, 2, '2026-09-25T03:00:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('aad383a6-4bec-54bc-a0a9-ec22d965f1c5', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'idk man, i''m 4 years non-union and i make more than my cousin does as a union apprentice. but he has a pension and i have a 2011 silverado so', false, 1, '2026-09-25T09:49:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2de88e1f-6aac-54dc-af49-a798dae4cc94', 'f0e0ce35-a53d-52e5-9568-5167b0c7c2e6', 'dfb7bdec-5951-5bee-baad-add9b3294059', 'lol. ok, getting a health insurance quote this week and looking up the wage sheet before i decide anything. edit: priced it. way more than i thought.', false, 1, '2026-09-25T14:22:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('193847d3-926c-5ee7-8b85-32b742c96741', 'aa4aa383-9b0a-5294-809c-62f229f9606e', 'question', 'first year helper, no health insurance, no PTO. normal?', 'started at a residential hvac shop in woodbridge this summer. $18/hr on the books, no health insurance, no paid days off, and they said maybe benefits after a year. owner says that''s how every small shop does it. is that true or is he just saying it? not complaining about the hourly, just want to know what''s normal before I think about looking around brother', 'hvac', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 4, '2026-09-23T00:40:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0a658fbb-a4e4-5791-9042-43edd2201322', '193847d3-926c-5ee7-8b85-32b742c96741', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Common for small shops, not universal. What I see around Middlesex:
- Some shops start health insurance at 60 or 90 days
- Some never offer it and pay a bit more instead
- Paid time off for first-years is often a few days, if any
A one-year wait isn''t unusual. "Maybe" is the word I''d ask about. Ask him what the policy actually is and whether it''s written down anywhere.', true, 10, '2026-09-23T01:06:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('165c6b14-cfd4-5077-bde3-c45dd5c0896f', '193847d3-926c-5ee7-8b85-32b742c96741', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Lol my first shop in Pennsauken said benefits ''after a year'' and then I found out nobody had ever made it to a year... Ask how many guys are on the plan right now. That tells you more than the policy does', false, 3, '2026-09-24T00:18:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('27d3b385-44a5-544d-8c06-01d6f249c51a', '193847d3-926c-5ee7-8b85-32b742c96741', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Also confirm he''s carrying workers'' comp for you. As far as I know NJ employers are supposed to, and being on the books usually means yes, but ask. If you get hurt in an attic, that''s the coverage that matters first.', false, 3, '2026-09-25T00:50:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2e597141-b236-515c-b18a-d573b84cb253', '193847d3-926c-5ee7-8b85-32b742c96741', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'same at my shop in clifton, no insurance first year. but they''re paying for my 608 test and the practice tests and i get the van on call weeks, which i guess is worth something? did yours say anything about the 608? or tools', false, 3, '2026-09-25T11:01:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4460455f-9f9b-5e40-a982-d61157357950', '193847d3-926c-5ee7-8b85-32b742c96741', 'aa4aa383-9b0a-5294-809c-62f229f9606e', '608 yes, they paid for it. tools no. ok, I''ll ask him how many guys are actually on the plan. thanks brother', false, 1, '2026-09-25T11:13:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cef6d739-193b-5b03-9e00-bea2e894972d', '193847d3-926c-5ee7-8b85-32b742c96741', '31e0974e-aadd-529c-90fc-0385fc7c46a5', '3rd year in bound brook, mine kicked in at 90 days. so it really varies by shop. ask around at the supply house', false, 1, '2026-09-25T14:43:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f63632f6-9da3-5fc7-9163-ae1cab061e08', '193847d3-926c-5ee7-8b85-32b742c96741', 'aa4aa383-9b0a-5294-809c-62f229f9606e', 'update: asked. 4 out of 6 guys are on the plan, all of them past a year. so I guess it''s real. staying for now', false, 2, '2026-09-25T17:16:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'question', 'worked 58 hours during the heat wave, check came back all straight time', 'so last week was the heat wave and we were running no-cool calls from 6am til like 10 at night. i''m a helper at a small residential shop in clifton, i ride with the lead tech. i counted 58 hours. my check came back 58 hours at my regular rate, no overtime. when i asked the office she said the owner ''doesn''t do overtime for helpers, it evens out in the winter.'' is that a thing? is that even legal? i don''t want to get fired over this but thats 18 hours of time and a half i didn''t get', 'hvac', 'Passaic County, NJ', 15, '2026-08-07T21:28:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e20c3c5d-4fc1-55ef-8253-ac6e9a791d7e', '629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: as far as I know, most hourly employees in NJ are owed time and a half over 40 hours in a workweek, and "it evens out in the winter" isn''t how that works. Code is my area, not wage law, so check the NJ Department of Labor''s wage and hour pages or call them before you take my word for it.', false, 2, '2026-08-08T12:51:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5850ba51-3fb4-5247-ae64-d3c5d3f27466', '629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s how it works at my shop, and at every shop I''d put my name on: hourly helpers get time and a half after 40, period. Our payroll company wouldn''t let us do it any other way.

The state labor department is the place to check, like he said. Before you go there, ask the owner directly and calmly, in person, with your hours written down. Sometimes it''s an office mistake. Sometimes it isn''t, and then you know what kind of shop it is.', true, 14, '2026-08-09T00:00:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bd33bf16-93c7-50d0-a8ec-47d5c708e07e', '629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Agree with both. Keep your own record from now on:
- Start and end times every day, written down that day
- Which calls, which truck
- Screenshots of any texts about hours
If it ever turns into a dispute, notes you made at the time carry weight.', false, 4, '2026-08-09T02:31:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f5506879-5c94-5d0f-8832-f2299611dd46', '629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', 'my old non-union shop in teneck did ''comp time'' in the winter instead of OT... it never added up. one of the reasons I left', false, 1, '2026-08-09T09:13:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('175edc2f-1b72-5247-8d11-39a9a2016c6c', '629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'On our side the contract spells out overtime, so it isn''t a conversation. Whatever shop you''re in, your stub should show how your hours were paid. And 58 hours in attics in that heat: water, breaks, and come down if you feel off. Stay safe.', false, 8, '2026-08-09T09:59:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b76263f7-1937-5d4a-9b1d-4ad0cd67b311', '629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', '02a13f50-be86-588b-966d-7ae10b7d64cd', 'my boss pays OT but caps us at 50 in the summer... honestly i was mad about the cap until july happened', false, 1, '2026-08-09T11:40:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e9f6cbf5-4b7a-534a-a61e-83d41d7eb5e8', '629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', '8537b87b-2917-5fba-aac2-8e516880bdaf', 'sorry if this is dumb but does the same thing apply if you''re salaried? my buddy at another shop is ''salary'' as a helper and works 60 a week lol', false, 3, '2026-08-09T13:22:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1b8ba55b-0fc2-5738-9b8d-d6d0d9e019fe', '629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Not a dumb question.
- Calling someone salaried doesn''t automatically mean no overtime
- There are rules about which jobs can be exempt, and a helper on a truck usually isn''t what people mean by that, as far as I understand it
Same answer: the Department of Labor, not me.', false, 8, '2026-08-09T22:40:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9f3685c0-fe34-5833-9cfd-f90cff0a9b7f', '629bae00-a9e7-522d-99b9-ca00b2133996', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'update: asked the owner in person with my hours on paper like haddad_mech said. he said the office ''set it up wrong'' and it''ll be on the next check. not sure i believe the wrong part but ill take it', false, 1, '2026-08-10T01:59:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('465f5cb5-95ef-5640-8e4a-4bd8db189c8e', '393b9bbb-e88d-53b5-be6e-c1c847014fa4', 'question', 'brooklyn non-union helper pay vs local 1, what''s normal?', 'Apex grad, working for a small non-union shop out of Canarsie, mostly service and drain calls. Applied to Local 1 and waiting. I''m at $20 an hour on the books. My foreman says that''s good for the city for a first year helper. A guy I graduated with says he makes more at a shop in Queens doing new construction. What''s normal in the city for year one non-union? And is it worth waiting on the union or should I just stay put.', 'plumbing', 'Brooklyn, NY', 11, '2026-09-23T00:32:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('89151971-e355-52ad-bb8c-cdfcc9a0ac95', '465f5cb5-95ef-5640-8e4a-4bd8db189c8e', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different, and pay is all over the place. From what I see, and what I pay, a first-year helper at a small Brooklyn service shop is somewhere around where you are, give or take a couple of dollars. New construction sometimes pays more per hour, and it''s steady until it isn''t.

Don''t compare the hourly alone. Ask about overtime, transit or parking, and whether they''ll document your experience. If you ever want a license here, documented years under a licensed master are the whole game.', true, 21, '2026-09-23T01:40:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fc6cf5ea-a676-5dcd-824b-275c7da81ccb', '465f5cb5-95ef-5640-8e4a-4bd8db189c8e', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'local 1 first year here. not posting my rate but look up the wage sheet, it''s public. the benefits are the big part. took me 2 tries to get in lol', false, 1, '2026-09-23T11:28:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9d69b5f5-4351-52c9-ba14-99c8648a549d', '465f5cb5-95ef-5640-8e4a-4bd8db189c8e', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'I''m in Jersey, so I can''t speak to city numbers, but the same checklist applies:
- Hourly
- Overtime, and how often
- Health insurance
- Travel: tolls, parking, transit
- School
The Queens guy might be ahead on one line and behind on three.', false, 4, '2026-09-23T22:38:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('49d0e977-86c2-55ba-99ae-7dbdeba704de', '465f5cb5-95ef-5640-8e4a-4bd8db189c8e', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'jersey side, local 24 first year. i''ll just say my package looked way better on paper than my hourly did, which is kind of the point. don''t sit around waiting though, keep working', false, 1, '2026-09-24T01:45:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('05de9f7d-742c-5607-9d0a-638a79aa81c2', '465f5cb5-95ef-5640-8e4a-4bd8db189c8e', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'On ''should I wait'': you don''t have to choose. Keep working and keep the application alive. Here''s what I look for when I hire, union or not: somebody who kept working while they waited. A waiting list never trained anybody.', false, 2, '2026-09-24T10:06:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3c482436-d6ab-5772-801b-17e210eeea99', '465f5cb5-95ef-5640-8e4a-4bd8db189c8e', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'One more thing on documenting: keep your own copy of everything, even if your foreman is good about it. Shops close, masters retire, and you don''t want your years depending on someone answering the phone in 2032.', false, 5, '2026-09-25T00:52:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ec2b64c4-fc3e-58e4-b650-6e16cf7af543', '465f5cb5-95ef-5640-8e4a-4bd8db189c8e', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', '^ this. my uncle lost 3 years of paperwork when his old boss retired to florida lol', false, 2, '2026-09-25T15:43:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('1117b173-d505-585c-8e35-d1d0bb481a3e', '85d3dc63-b215-52ad-b741-7bace7266d53', 'question', 'anyone else''s hours get cut after labor day down the shore?', '1 yr in at a residential/light commercial hvac shop in egg harbor twp. all summer we were doing 55-60 hours. labor day hit and now i''m getting maybe 32 a week, some days they send me home at noon. boss says it picks back up when heating starts. is this normal for shore shops or is it just mine? trying to figure out if i need a second job for oct and nov brother', 'hvac', 'Atlantic County, NJ', 10, '2026-08-11T00:29:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('c91c9874-7c77-5352-9178-f8a6056ee1e6', '1117b173-d505-585c-8e35-d1d0bb481a3e', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'normal down here. summer you work, winter you learn. the shops that keep you at 40 in october are the ones with heating service and maintenance contracts. ask your boss if theres a fall tune-up push and volunteer for it. thats how i stayed busy my first few years', false, 6, '2026-08-11T09:58:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f2368386-1b8d-532f-b954-9c036c797308', '1117b173-d505-585c-8e35-d1d0bb481a3e', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Same pattern in Burlington, just less extreme. Next year, bank some of the summer overtime; that''s the real lesson. If you take a second job for a couple of months, tell your boss. Better than him finding out when he calls you in on a cold morning and you can''t come.', false, 3, '2026-08-11T23:33:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('9d74f742-ce05-5eb5-9cf8-4b7a6dabf6ec', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'tip', 'Side jobs, from the owner''s side: what happens when yours calls my office', 'Happened again this month, so I''ll write it down. A homeowner called us for a no-cool on a mini-split installed last year. Not our install. A helper from another shop put it in on weekends, cash. No permit, no proper evacuation, flare connections leaking. The homeowner wanted to know who to call about it, and the answer was nobody.

What it looks like from my side:
- The homeowner pays twice, once to him and once to us
- If your own boss gets that call, you''re probably done there
- Handling refrigerant without your 608 is its own problem, and having the card doesn''t make an unpermitted install legal
- You have no insurance, so whatever goes wrong is on you

I''m not telling anyone what to do on their own time. I''m telling you what it costs when it goes wrong.', 'hvac', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 13, '2026-08-23T13:29:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('8822b02b-28ae-5690-b678-3f67310abca4', '9d74f742-ce05-5eb5-9cf8-4b7a6dabf6ec', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it. On the electrical side of these, I see the disconnect and the circuit done wrong more than anything else. When unpermitted work turns up later, at a sale or after a problem, the homeowner is usually the one left holding the bill. Check which code edition is in effect and what the town requires before anyone touches a line set.', false, 7, '2026-08-24T00:47:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2cfedd58-c96d-5472-b514-127078b9e6ce', '9d74f742-ce05-5eb5-9cf8-4b7a6dabf6ec', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'sorry if this is dumb but what about stuff with no refrigerant, like cleaning coils and changing filters for neighbors? my neighbor keeps asking. thanks in advance', false, 2, '2026-08-28T14:47:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4197e370-3ca8-59d9-8fa8-eba2efca8312', '9d74f742-ce05-5eb5-9cf8-4b7a6dabf6ec', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Smaller exposure, same basic problem:
- You''re still uninsured if you fall off a ladder or break something
- "Just cleaning coils" turns into "while you''re here, can you look at this" fast
- Your boss may see it as taking his customers
Ask your boss if the shop wants the maintenance work. Usually they do, and you get the hours.', false, 4, '2026-08-29T14:37:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('1167b4a6-8483-509c-a55e-50de5e06326f', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'question', 'uncle wants me to wire his basement under a homeowner permit. is that allowed', 'my uncle in barnegat is finishing his basement and wants me to do the wiring on weekends. he says he can pull a homeowner permit and i''d just be helping him, and he''d pay me in pizza and gas money basically. i work for a remodel shop in manahawkin so i know how to do it, but i''m not licensed. is this actually allowed in nj or is the homeowner permit only if he does the work himself? would rather ask here than ask my boss.

edit: he owns the house and lives there, if that matters', 'electrical', 'Ocean County, NJ', 26, '2026-08-30T20:32:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d6f3896b-e4a1-5c68-83c4-ed435a695401', '0e1f3b61-0ba4-56b9-9844-cea31e8e2deb', 'question', 'Boss wants me on his Saturday cash jobs. Is that the same as side work?', 'Sorry if this is a dumb question. I''m a first-year helper at a small shop in Brick. My boss has started asking me to come out Saturdays on ''his'' jobs, which as far as I can tell are jobs that don''t go through the company. Cash, no paperwork, and he tells the customer not to worry about a permit. It''s $150 for the day, which is a lot for me right now. He''s licensed, so is it fine because it''s under him? Or is this the thing everyone warns about?', 'electrical', 'Ocean County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-18T02:55:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('593010bb-8a3c-54dc-9955-24706e5a9047', 'd6f3896b-e4a1-5c68-83c4-ed435a695401', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: his license doesn''t make skipping the permit fine. A licensed contractor is still supposed to pull permits where they''re required, and a job done off the company''s books probably isn''t on the company''s insurance either.

If you get hurt on a Saturday that officially didn''t happen, workers'' comp becomes a hard conversation. I''d say no politely. "I''ve got something on Saturdays" is enough.', true, 6, '2026-09-18T03:44:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b266d24c-d7ea-5432-a2dd-c5024ce9dfa3', 'd6f3896b-e4a1-5c68-83c4-ed435a695401', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly I''ve seen this go bad both ways. Somebody gets hurt, or the house sells and the buyer''s inspection turns up work with no permit, and suddenly everyone remembers who was there. $150 is real money at year one, I get it. Still not worth it.', false, 5, '2026-09-18T10:16:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cb149db2-2d5d-538f-8dac-7a195dc8fb36', 'd6f3896b-e4a1-5c68-83c4-ed435a695401', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'In the Army we''d say off the books means off the record, and nobody covers you off the record. I''d pass, brother.', false, 1, '2026-09-18T12:12:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b4d68558-3a76-5d64-ae4d-0e035ff02f02', 'd6f3896b-e4a1-5c68-83c4-ed435a695401', '0068d208-ce11-5170-b467-caa34a717104', 'Ocean County is small. You think the inspectors don''t know whose truck that is? Say no and keep the job. How long have you been there?', false, 1, '2026-09-18T16:35:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3abada9f-7dc3-56aa-ae43-c355bccf3fcb', 'd6f3896b-e4a1-5c68-83c4-ed435a695401', '0e1f3b61-0ba4-56b9-9844-cea31e8e2deb', 'About 4 months. Ok. Told him I have a family thing on Saturdays for now. He didn''t seem mad. Thanks for explaining instead of just yelling at me lol', false, 1, '2026-09-19T09:23:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'question', 'Landlord on my block wants me to do his apartments'' outlets. I''m a student', 'Trade program in Queens, graduating soon. My uncle''s friend owns a couple of 2-family houses in Ridgewood and found out I''m in the electrical program. He wants me to swap outlets, put in some GFCIs and replace a few fixtures before new tenants move in. Says he''ll pay $400 cash and "nobody checks." My foreman at my weekend job told me absolutely not but didn''t really say why. Is it really that bad if it''s small stuff?', 'electrical', 'Queens, NY', 24, '2026-09-20T18:42:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('48bc1d63-ccb6-5879-897e-c911c65e328f', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, your foreman''s right, and I''ll tell you why. Here in the city, getting paid to do electrical means a licensed master electrician is behind the job, and permits get pulled where they''re required. Rental apartments make it worse, not better.

A fire in a tenant''s unit gets traced back to your GFCI, and you''re the kid with no license and no insurance. Don''t.', true, 8, '2026-09-21T02:43:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('224e7722-811b-57f5-90da-c9d95f747c17', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'I''ll ask the dumb question for him: what if it''s only swapping a light fixture? That seems like nothing', false, 2, '2026-09-21T10:29:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a814b6f4-db95-51fc-a273-65e1631a02c2', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different, but not on this. Small stuff is where people get comfortable. And a landlord who says nobody checks is telling you exactly how he''ll treat you if something goes wrong. He''ll say he hired a professional and that you told him you were licensed.', false, 2, '2026-09-22T02:00:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('31249cea-cdce-57df-9d8e-bb0a7b027a1f', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'I never said I was licensed though. Never would either.', false, 2, '2026-09-22T10:22:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('49d0e2db-7baf-5353-bcf4-79dfb3968038', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'Doesn''t matter what you said. It matters what he says later, to an insurance adjuster.', false, 6, '2026-09-22T12:00:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('38be85c3-82a9-5fb3-9efd-f39719010432', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, and I''m on the Jersey side. When I see a fixture swap gone wrong, it''s almost never the fixture. It''s the box that wasn''t secured, the backstabbed device, the neutral that wasn''t where someone assumed. Small jobs fail the same ways big ones do, just with fewer people looking.', false, 5, '2026-09-22T13:19:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cc5a1bd9-e2d9-5006-90ac-b254d1fe150e', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'different state but i asked almost the same thing about my uncle''s basement a while back and nobody answered, so i''m reading this whole thread lol', false, 1, '2026-09-22T13:59:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a4635c13-3368-55a9-89a0-1ad336d317b2', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, $400 cash is the most expensive money you''ll ever make if it goes bad. 28 years in and I still pull permits on jobs I could do in my sleep. That''s the job.', false, 5, '2026-09-23T01:38:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d68d387b-8b5e-5b71-8075-12d9689b440a', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'Ok so the fixture is a no too. Noted. Asking for me as much as him honestly', false, 3, '2026-09-23T01:48:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f63f57c8-3ac6-5cd3-bde7-e454184cab20', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'Apex grad, working non-union in the Bronx. When I was in school a guy in my class did this exact thing for a landlord and got stiffed on the money. He couldn''t exactly complain to anyone. Just something to think about.', false, 2, '2026-09-23T03:48:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('db894e4a-04f8-5ecb-bd2b-60cf83413949', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'ccf9dc60-958f-5461-ad1b-ad7dd180a037', 'everybody in my building''s family asks me too... i just say my boss would fire me, which is true lol', false, 3, '2026-09-23T09:28:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2dc50717-0e48-590a-89ab-79f744bbca24', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'That''s a good line, stealing it. My uncle''s going to be annoyed though', false, 2, '2026-09-23T11:47:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e5c6d2b7-84e3-57a6-b526-febddeaa5d86', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Your uncle will get over it. Tell the landlord to hire a licensed electrician and ask if you can shadow the job. That''s how you turn this into something.', false, 3, '2026-09-23T15:18:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e94d2e71-a8e5-52e5-bc6f-075b29b7b54d', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'ce84b73a-6963-5f91-90b8-134f5200b157', 'update: told him no. Asked him who he''s hiring instead and he gave me the guy''s number. Calling him Saturday.', false, 1, '2026-09-23T16:03:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4b4c53b9-10ad-5195-ac80-2ab15568325d', '7f64c4d2-122e-582e-88d4-394b49293987', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Good. That''s the right move. Let me know how the call goes, brother.', false, 7, '2026-09-24T01:08:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('9a2efc82-7ef8-5833-a03c-e0af785397d7', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'question', 'Long-term question: what does insurance run for a one-truck plumbing shop?', '1st year in Local 24, so this is years away. idk if it''s weird to ask this early. My long-term plan is to top out, get my master, and eventually run a small service shop in Bergen. Everyone says insurance is the thing that kills new shops. What kinds do you need, and roughly what does it cost? Ballpark is fine. Just planning.', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 12, '2026-10-02T09:19:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('a4e45c9a-ed93-548e-97bd-9e3e3d7710ae', '9a2efc82-7ef8-5833-a03c-e0af785397d7', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Not too early. Ballparks are hard because it depends on trade, payroll, claims history and carrier, so get real quotes when you''re close. The kinds you''ll deal with:
- General liability
- Workers'' comp once you have employees
- Commercial auto for the truck
- Tools and equipment coverage
For a one-truck shop, expect the total to be one of your bigger fixed costs, not a rounding error. Talk to a broker who works with contractors, not your car insurance guy.', true, 14, '2026-10-02T10:49:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d4cc2760-b0de-533a-9579-a86b54ec6468', '9a2efc82-7ef8-5833-a03c-e0af785397d7', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'I''m in the electrical program at the vo-tech, and our teacher had us do a small-business project on this last spring. What surprised everyone was that the truck insurance alone came out higher than most people''s rent. Not plumbing specific, but probably similar.', false, 2, '2026-10-02T17:08:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5d91653a-77ef-560d-87ec-845942d0344b', '9a2efc82-7ef8-5833-a03c-e0af785397d7', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'my foreman ran his own shop for 6 years before he came in... he says insurance and chasing payments are the two reasons he came back', false, 1, '2026-10-02T17:57:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'question', 'me and a buddy want to start an LLC doing handyman + small electrical. is HIC enough?', 'ok so hear me out. my buddy is a carpenter, i''m a year out of vo-tech working for an electrical shop near asbury. we want to start an LLC on the side, register as a home improvement contractor with the state, and do bathroom refreshes, decks, and the "small electrical" like fixtures, outlets, fans. he says the HIC registration covers all of it as long as it''s under the LLC. is that right? and what insurance would we even need for something like that? we''re not trying to do panels or anything crazy', 'electrical', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 12, '2026-09-26T14:25:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('1d993024-40fd-5a1b-a70f-8f4d9743cc8a', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: as I understand NJ''s rules, home improvement contractor registration is not an electrical license and doesn''t cover electrical work. If you''re paid for it, a licensed electrical contractor has to be the one running it. "Small" isn''t a category in the code.

Call the Division of Consumer Affairs and ask them directly before you form anything.', true, 16, '2026-09-27T01:30:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b0297420-edd5-51b2-bc9e-7ba32614a05e', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Same in my trade. As I understand it:
- HIC registration covers general home improvement work
- Licensed trades (electrical, plumbing, HVACR) need the license, or a licensed contractor running the work
- An LLC is a business structure, not a license
Your buddy''s carpentry side may be fine under HIC. Check with Consumer Affairs for your exact case.', false, 9, '2026-09-27T02:53:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('13c9fd85-077f-5eaa-8034-7c8a0d1eaaf3', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'wait so he can do the decks but i can''t do the fans? even under the same company?', false, 2, '2026-09-27T03:13:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('69d3cbdc-4297-5d25-9c22-44cc706ad465', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', '> even under the same company?
yes. the company doesn''t make you licensed.', false, 5, '2026-09-27T10:19:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('edabe5c1-5c22-500d-9790-81247d5263b8', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'this is basically what my boss''s shop is. he''s licensed, his brother does the carpentry under the same company. the license is the part that makes it work', false, 1, '2026-09-27T11:01:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('610d9af9-85bc-5ae3-8883-1c5ed26d187e', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Also think about the fact that you already work for an electrical shop. Doing the same kind of work on the side, in the same area, is going to get back to your boss. Small state. Talk to him before you do anything; some owners will even help you find a path.', false, 4, '2026-09-27T11:18:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8efac6f4-8fac-5b1e-8ecd-3a22fbfc2949', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'my foreman says the same thing about plumbing. he says the fastest way to lose your shot at a license is getting caught doing licensed work without one. not sure if that''s true word for word but he was dead serious', false, 1, '2026-09-27T12:21:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('eed10e19-9807-5b44-a8c4-c1895676f9a9', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'ok so what if my buddy does the bathrooms and we just sub the electrical out to a licensed guy?', false, 2, '2026-09-27T17:01:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('33173aea-7052-5ab4-8319-82978788bf93', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly that''s how a lot of legit small outfits work. You pay the licensed EC, he pulls the permit and does or supervises the work. You learn by being on his jobs. Less money for you, but it''s clean, and you''re building a relationship with someone who might hire you or sign off on your hours.', false, 5, '2026-09-28T00:29:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5b7cadd1-5173-59de-afaf-b697496863a9', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'And on insurance, if you go that route:
- General liability for the LLC, with a carrier that knows contractors
- Every sub shows you a current certificate of insurance before they start
- Workers'' comp if you hire anyone
Get quotes before you price your first job. It will change your prices.', false, 4, '2026-09-28T00:39:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6e34d759-bff9-5e9c-863f-640b4147953b', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'One thing I''d push back on a little, thiago. Subbing out is clean, but a lot of the shops that sub for small outfits get burned on payment and stop doing it. Make sure the EC knows you pay on time, or you won''t find one twice. My father stopped subbing for two GCs in one year over that.', false, 2, '2026-09-28T02:09:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e2da21fa-1fcf-5f86-8878-6988d0f0e4e1', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Fair point. I''ve been the EC who got stiffed, more than once. Pay your subs.', false, 12, '2026-09-28T02:25:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ab45e137-0903-58e4-9383-d6838279810f', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'my buddy is not happy lol. he thought the LLC thing was a loophole', false, 2, '2026-09-28T09:33:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f0a64477-f10c-50aa-98da-8f9e40d5a26b', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'It''s the most common misunderstanding I hear. As I understand it, an LLC is about liability and taxes, and a lawyer or an accountant should tell you what it does and doesn''t protect. It doesn''t license anyone to do anything. Have him call Consumer Affairs too, so he hears it from them and not from strangers online.', false, 2, '2026-09-28T13:42:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dcea2aaf-fe84-5e92-9d09-ace52b9993c9', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'I asked the insurance half of this in another thread. Short answer was get real quotes, and it''s more than you think.', false, 2, '2026-09-28T13:55:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('845a33de-5696-5dec-9f1a-e54c7f174a97', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'Our teacher said something similar when a kid asked about LLCs. I wrote it down: the LLC is paperwork you filed, the license is a test you passed. Not his exact words, but close.', false, 5, '2026-09-28T16:26:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7c560c08-e5c3-509d-8628-7e926be45ca6', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'update: talked to my boss like mbell said. he laughed at the LLC part, then said if my buddy lands bathrooms the shop will do the electrical and i can be on those jobs. so that''s kind of a win?', false, 3, '2026-09-28T17:04:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a5d0e420-c55c-5caf-9ecb-b8c9e3dda91b', 'f3951955-2cde-5cfb-94d6-906122209ba0', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'That''s a big win. That''s how your name gets around. Sounds like a good boss, hang onto him.', false, 2, '2026-09-29T02:03:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('f55fe1b8-16c0-57b3-9db0-212cae5e0763', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'discussion', 'No kids in the trade. Who buys a 2-truck shop when you want out?', 'Business side question, for the owners and for any Juniors thinking long-term.

My father ran this shop for three decades and handed it to me. None of my kids want it. My nephew in Hamilton is in IT. So in ten years or so, who buys a 2-truck residential shop on the Hudson/Bergen line? The trucks and tools aren''t worth much. The customer list and the phone number are the whole business.

My father used to say a shop is just the people who still call you back. I half regret not thinking about this sooner. Anyone been through selling, or buying in?', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 10, '2026-08-13T22:38:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0cd15b30-2a85-57f5-bf1d-55a26207ca59', 'f55fe1b8-16c0-57b3-9db0-212cae5e0763', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'We''ve started thinking about this too. What I''ve learned so far:
- The license is personal; a buyer needs their own, or a licensed person running the work
- Your books need to be clean for years before anyone pays real money for goodwill
- The most likely buyer is someone already working for you
That last one means you start grooming someone now. Ten years goes fast.', false, 3, '2026-08-14T02:25:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('465c341d-a902-505e-9793-143cea504411', 'f55fe1b8-16c0-57b3-9db0-212cae5e0763', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'Not an owner, I haven''t even started yet, but I spent 11 years in insurance claims and saw a lot of small businesses get valued. Clean records and repeat customers were always what moved the number. Kash is right about the books.', false, 2, '2026-08-14T10:26:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1e168c07-b2f3-59bf-9579-8c5535196efc', 'f55fe1b8-16c0-57b3-9db0-212cae5e0763', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'The someone-already-working-for-you part is what I keep coming back to. I hired a vo-tech kid last year who might be that guy, if he doesn''t go union first. My father would laugh at me for worrying about any of this.', false, 4, '2026-08-16T14:12:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('c6a8a008-7dfb-5077-887b-4dc6f1e21550', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'question', 'Army vet, 35, want my own electrical shop in Queens someday. Realistic timeline?', 'Got out of the Army last year, now about a year in as a helper at a small shop in Queens. I''m 35. Long-term I want my own shop. From what I can tell I''d need a master electrician license in the city, and that takes years of documented experience. idk the exact number. Is own-shop-by-45 realistic? Also, does military electrical experience count for anything? I did generator and power distribution work, not building wiring.', 'electrical', 'Queens, NY', 9, '2026-09-10T23:25:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('b39507bb-dbb3-5298-b090-8c713d412221', 'c6a8a008-7dfb-5077-887b-4dc6f1e21550', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different from Jersey, and the master license is serious. Last I looked, the requirement was years of documented experience under a licensed master electrician, somewhere north of seven, plus the exams. Read the DOB licensing page for the current rules; they''ve changed since I did mine, and mine is plumbing, so check the electrical requirements specifically.

Whether military work counts, ask DOB directly. 45 isn''t crazy if you start documenting everything today.', true, 6, '2026-09-11T01:26:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5b98a07b-9edc-58d2-b458-03791814ff8c', 'c6a8a008-7dfb-5077-887b-4dc6f1e21550', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, and I''m on the Jersey side, but two things apply anywhere: keep every pay stub and a log of the work you did, and get your employer''s signature on it periodically, while they still remember you. People lose years of credit because nobody can verify them later.', false, 4, '2026-09-11T02:02:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2edad0e6-7b22-5091-9d4c-42f501bd4bd0', 'c6a8a008-7dfb-5077-887b-4dc6f1e21550', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, thank you for your service. Same advice on documenting. Also look into whether any veteran programs help with apprenticeship or exam costs. I don''t know the details, but a couple of guys on my job have used them.', false, 5, '2026-09-13T15:04:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('f5471fe1-75e0-587a-b2a9-8285f365b8c2', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'question', 'Planning way ahead: first work vehicle, used van or a pickup with a cap?', 'I''m in the electrical program at the county vo-tech, so I realize this is a long way off, but I like to plan. I''ve been saving from my weekend job, and my dad suggested I think about what I''d eventually need for a vehicle if I ever go out on my own. I see guys with box trucks, Transit vans, pickups with caps, and one man at the Wawa near Wayne who runs everything out of a Prius. For someone starting small in electrical, used van or pickup with a cap? I''d rather buy once.', 'electrical', 'Passaic County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-23T17:57:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e2e2e4a8-aadb-56c6-af4b-8e5cc494b84f', 'f5471fe1-75e0-587a-b2a9-8285f365b8c2', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Good instinct. From my own first truck:
- Used is fine. Reliability beats everything else; mine was 9 years old and never left me stranded
- A van keeps tools dry and locked; a pickup with a cap is a compromise for electrical
- Shelving costs more than you expect
- Commercial insurance and registration are part of the price
Buy it after you have the license and the work, not before.', true, 8, '2026-09-23T23:15:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8d03052c-aa8b-5457-96a9-b62ecdc47307', 'f5471fe1-75e0-587a-b2a9-8285f365b8c2', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'i think i''ve seen the prius guy lol. sorry, not helpful at all. thanks in advance for not deleting this', false, 1, '2026-09-24T01:02:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cc8fb007-e448-5136-b38b-1c6ad0194dde', 'f5471fe1-75e0-587a-b2a9-8285f365b8c2', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I look for when a new hire shows up in his own vehicle: organized, clean, nothing leaking. Customers judge you by what''s parked in their driveway before you say a word.', false, 6, '2026-09-24T02:39:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cd1377ad-d582-5608-996d-89740c61a49c', 'f5471fe1-75e0-587a-b2a9-8285f365b8c2', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'Noted on buying it after the license and the work. The savings stay in the bank for now. My dad will be relieved, honestly.', false, 2, '2026-09-24T03:58:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5ef2f650-c5e9-5bd0-916e-c45dae6783f7', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'question', 'My teacher says public school jobs pay way more. What is prevailing wage?', 'Before school let out my shop teacher was going on about how the summer school renovation jobs pay "prevailing wage" and that''s why everyone fights to get on them. I nodded. I have no idea what it means. Is it a union thing? Would I make more as a helper on one of those jobs? And why would a school pay more than a house? Explain it like I''m a vo-tech kid in Hamilton whose whole resume is one summer carrying wire, because that''s what I am.', 'electrical', 'Mercer County, NJ', 18, '2026-08-14T00:03:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('54c3b0a5-d874-5177-9b95-4ff1f6da170e', '5ef2f650-c5e9-5bd0-916e-c45dae6783f7', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Short version: on covered public jobs in NJ (schools, municipal buildings, a lot of publicly funded work), contractors have to pay at least the rates the state sets for each trade and county. Those rates are published by the state labor department.

It isn''t only a union thing. Non-union shops like mine do prevailing-wage work and pay the rates. The paperwork is certified payroll: every week, every worker, every hour. That''s part of why not every shop bids them.', true, 8, '2026-08-14T01:30:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8c4165a7-861d-5e43-b0e0-d5ff41273036', '5ef2f650-c5e9-5bd0-916e-c45dae6783f7', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'To add the helper part:
- Apprentice rates on those jobs generally depend on being in a registered apprenticeship program
- If you''re not in one, a shop may not be able to use you as an apprentice there at all
- Ask your teacher about it before you graduate
Check the details with the state, not with me.', false, 5, '2026-08-14T03:42:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8f743d56-a9ad-5241-a7a9-05dbbd87e3ea', '5ef2f650-c5e9-5bd0-916e-c45dae6783f7', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'the state sets the rate. the school isn''t being generous.', false, 7, '2026-08-16T15:55:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1dfd1c7a-0d7f-5faf-aff1-bff8538e4e74', '5ef2f650-c5e9-5bd0-916e-c45dae6783f7', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'OK that actually makes sense. So it''s less "schools pay more" and more "the state says you can''t pay less on public jobs." Asking my teacher about the registered apprenticeship part tomorrow and pretending I knew all along.', false, 1, '2026-08-16T17:04:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('297a461c-3ae2-581b-a3b7-4cd85c0fb33e', '02a13f50-be86-588b-966d-7ae10b7d64cd', 'question', 'shop won a summer school job... do I get the prevailing rate too?', 'so my shop just won a job replacing rooftop units at a middle school, we start next week while the kids are out... my boss said it''s prevailing wage but then said I''m still at my regular $22. I''m two years in, non-union. is that right?? I thought prevailing meant everyone on the job gets the rate. not trying to make trouble, just confused... also it''s going to be 95 on that roof lol', 'hvac', 'Bergen County, NJ', 4, '2026-07-25T18:53:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('c82f6160-4c6d-5af8-b8f3-df675bfc856e', '297a461c-3ae2-581b-a3b7-4cd85c0fb33e', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s how it works on our jobs, as I understand the rules: everyone doing the work on a prevailing-wage job is paid at least the published rate for their classification. Apprentice rates are only for apprentices in a registered program; otherwise you''d generally be classified and paid as a journeyman. Politely ask your boss which classification you''re listed under on the certified payroll. If the answer is fuzzy, the state labor department has the rules.', false, 3, '2026-07-26T00:06:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('81ef6075-a660-5a88-bca7-00f3459e3e2d', '297a461c-3ae2-581b-a3b7-4cd85c0fb33e', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', 'same thing happened to me on a township job. asked which classification i was under. got moved to the right rate on the next check. ask', false, 2, '2026-07-26T10:00:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('c23e33b6-21c8-5375-a52e-de89fa56029d', '27d51566-aafb-564c-8cfe-1a24a78998aa', 'question', 'what is the ''fringe'' line on my pay stub from a public job', 'did two weeks on a township building in middlesex with my shop. my stub that week had my regular rate, a higher prevailing rate for those hours, and a separate line that says fringe. idk what the fringe is or why part of it went to a benefits fund and part came to me as cash. is this normal or did payroll mess up

edit: the shop is non-union if that matters', 'hvac', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 8, '2026-07-28T00:22:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'tip', 'Prevailing wage vs PLAs: why the big public jobs look the way they do', 'This keeps coming up, so here''s the union-side view. I''d welcome the non-union contractors here to correct me where it''s different for them.

Prevailing wage is a floor. On covered public work, everyone gets at least the published rate for their trade and county, union or not.

A project labor agreement is a different thing. It''s an agreement for a specific project, usually a big one, about labor terms: hiring through the trades, how disputes get handled, no strikes. You''ll hear about them on large public construction.

If you''re an apprentice and you land on one of these jobs, a few things will be new: sign-in sheets, long safety orientations, and someone checking that your classification matches your paperwork. Bring your ID, bring your card, wear your glasses. Stay safe.', 'electrical', 'Morris County, NJ', 12, '2026-09-22T10:19:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('ece6f085-3eea-5b54-bc22-0356416f76da', 'ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Mostly right, and thanks for asking for the other side. One thing I''d adjust: it isn''t every public job. There are thresholds and exceptions, and the state''s site spells them out. From the non-union side, the certified payroll is the real cost of public work, not the wages. On PLAs, I''ll just say not every contractor thinks they''re good for competition, and leave it there.', false, 7, '2026-09-22T13:23:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('adf4b858-b153-55d5-870c-923d8226370b', 'ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Fair correction on the thresholds, and I appreciate you keeping it civil. Plenty of people on my side would say the same thing about PLAs from the other direction.', false, 2, '2026-09-23T00:00:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2df117d6-6249-5af8-a84b-6ce81d9ecba3', 'ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'From the inspection side: whatever the labor terms are, the code doesn''t change. I''ve seen people on public jobs assume the rules are different because the paperwork is. Check which code edition is in effect for the project, and read the project specs, which sometimes ask for more than code.', false, 3, '2026-09-23T10:12:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fef9a8ee-568c-595b-847f-1f01bed46264', 'ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'This is very helpful. My teacher mentioned PLAs once and moved on. When you say classification has to match your paperwork, does that mean a student couldn''t work on one of these at all?', false, 2, '2026-09-23T13:48:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d0dd998c-b02b-544e-8710-b837856aea74', 'ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Not at an apprentice rate unless you''re in a registered program, as I understand it. That''s a question for your instructor and the state''s rules, though. Finish school first. The jobs will still be there.', false, 3, '2026-09-23T14:25:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0fa7a294-6626-534c-ab63-0a5e30233042', 'ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', '1st year in 24, did a week on a public school job in july. the sign-in sheet thing is real. the safety orientation was 3 hours and half of it was ladders lol', false, 1, '2026-09-23T17:56:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('49d701f4-5bb3-593a-aa2b-6bf2c9713bdb', 'ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'the orientation on the big jobs is long... my foreman says that''s where they catch the guys who don''t belong there. bring your card', false, 2, '2026-09-23T21:13:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e5fbf484-4310-5492-96da-309b9eb9fff7', 'ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'certified payroll is why my old shop stopped bidding them. good jobs if your office can handle it.', false, 4, '2026-09-23T21:57:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e65806a4-2c45-5ed9-880f-3b49d27f405d', 'ee6504c1-792d-56df-aea3-92ede81e41df', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'saving this for when I graduate, didn''t know any of it. our class is going to get a lot of questions from me now', false, 2, '2026-09-24T00:42:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('c3d6d570-0bbb-5eee-a04f-4a590c2e5b43', 'a500e8c1-fe10-5f2f-a33e-6f510dd05201', 'question', 'Reading the wage sheet: how much of the ''package'' actually hits my check?', '3rd year apprentice in Local 9. My girlfriend saw the published package number for my year and asked why my check is so much smaller. Honestly, I couldn''t explain it well. I know part of it is health, pension, annuity and training, but I''d like to be able to explain it properly, and to compare it fairly when non-union friends tell me what they make. How do you all explain this to family? Thanks in advance.', 'plumbing', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 18, '2026-08-21T02:20:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('17ad1022-c707-5248-8fe1-e5d89809b9e0', 'c3d6d570-0bbb-5eee-a04f-4a590c2e5b43', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'the package is the wage plus what goes into the funds. your check is the wage part, minus taxes and dues. put the stub and the fund statements side by side for her.', true, 8, '2026-08-24T00:37:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('46297567-7460-5727-b3f8-1ee40c8b3be5', 'c3d6d570-0bbb-5eee-a04f-4a590c2e5b43', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Same structure on our side. When I explain it to family, I say the check is what you live on now, and the funds are the health care, retirement and school you''d otherwise pay for yourself. When a non-union friend quotes you an hourly number, ask what he pays for health insurance and what goes into his retirement. The conversation usually gets quieter.', false, 3, '2026-08-24T01:25:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('12151114-97e1-577e-97c0-f901a4f5c599', 'c3d6d570-0bbb-5eee-a04f-4a590c2e5b43', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'To be fair from the non-union side: a good non-union shop pays benefits too, structured differently. Compare total compensation, not labels. Some of my guys come out fine against a package; some shops around here offer nothing. It varies a lot.', false, 7, '2026-08-24T03:57:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1c30b05e-c032-5e33-acf6-542721ed1f2d', 'c3d6d570-0bbb-5eee-a04f-4a590c2e5b43', 'a500e8c1-fe10-5f2f-a33e-6f510dd05201', 'That helps, thank you. Going to print the stub and the fund statement and do the side by side with her this weekend.', false, 1, '2026-08-24T10:28:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('60ba3eb6-4ef0-5854-92a2-d36d1c5a2a12', '07676d29-9e30-5e27-b903-f9044b52fe4b', 'question', 'two weeks on a township job and my check almost doubled. now what', 'plumbing helper, 2 years, small shop near pleasantville. we just did two weeks on a township building, bathrooms and a new water heater room. prevailing wage. my check those weeks was almost double my normal. back on regular jobs now and its hard to go back lol. how do i get on more of those? do i need to switch shops? also i''m waiting on the union, would that be all public work?', 'plumbing', 'Atlantic County, NJ', 19, '2026-09-09T23:50:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('8ed011bd-ecd3-5013-b95e-26b579f7f5cb', '60ba3eb6-4ef0-5854-92a2-d36d1c5a2a12', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I look for when I staff public work: someone who shows up at 6, can pass a background check for schools, keeps a clean sign-in record, and doesn''t need babysitting on a site full of other trades.

If your shop only lands a couple of these a year, a shop that bids them regularly is where the steady hours are. Don''t quit over one good check, though. Ask your boss if he plans to bid more.', true, 15, '2026-09-10T00:17:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f264189f-6205-5198-802d-3a754a7edfb4', '60ba3eb6-4ef0-5854-92a2-d36d1c5a2a12', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'the union isn''t all public work. hospitals, pharma, plenty of private jobs. the rate is what it is either way.', false, 4, '2026-09-10T02:17:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2c41f230-d147-57d3-838b-55d6d43b2d4f', '60ba3eb6-4ef0-5854-92a2-d36d1c5a2a12', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'down here the public jobs come in waves, summer for schools mostly. rest of the year youre back at the regular rate. dont plan your rent around it', false, 7, '2026-09-11T01:14:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e0ec3d7f-6cf7-559a-92de-5a3b6f20a3f0', '60ba3eb6-4ef0-5854-92a2-d36d1c5a2a12', '9d863d1d-0f6f-5b8c-921d-d473f8721247', 'this is the first time i understood why my boss gets so excited about school jobs lol', false, 2, '2026-09-11T02:59:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ef64ba4a-2d7f-5dda-9556-511a072fb156', '60ba3eb6-4ef0-5854-92a2-d36d1c5a2a12', '07676d29-9e30-5e27-b903-f9044b52fe4b', 'fair, not quitting. asked my boss and he said they''re bidding 2 more this winter. i''ll ask to be on them', false, 2, '2026-09-11T09:03:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7f28b3a8-c149-5385-9b67-f2709cdad8a7', '60ba3eb6-4ef0-5854-92a2-d36d1c5a2a12', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Good. Make it easy for him to say yes. And keep your stubs from those weeks; they''re a good record of the work.', false, 6, '2026-09-14T01:42:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('afc43ee6-851a-51af-ae78-0086ceda24be', '76ffb6b2-6ae2-5434-982e-39a1a1bf28b2', 'question', 'Ex-teacher here: school district maintenance job vs working for a contractor?', 'Sorry if this is a strange one. I taught middle school for nine years before switching, and I''m a few months in as an electrical helper in Atlantic County. I still know people in the district, and they say the maintenance department hires electricians, with a pension, and summers that are actually busy. Pay looks lower than contractor work but steadier. Has anyone gone from a contractor to a school district or county maintenance job? What do you give up? Appreciate it.', 'electrical', 'Atlantic County, NJ', 19, '2026-08-22T13:16:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('500e222e-8cde-5cc8-a5e6-1f4c327e84d8', 'afc43ee6-851a-51af-ae78-0086ceda24be', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'I''ve lost a few good guys to districts and I don''t blame them. What you gain: steady hours, public benefits, home for dinner. What you lose: variety, overtime, and usually the fastest learning. Most district jobs want someone already licensed or well along, from what I''ve seen. Get your years in with a contractor first. The district job will still be there.', true, 27, '2026-08-22T15:12:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f7422af3-6eda-5490-b2ac-037037c84095', 'afc43ee6-851a-51af-ae78-0086ceda24be', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'my buddy did commercial for fifteen years then went to a school district down here. says it was the best thing he did for his back and the worst for his skills. he got bored. depends what you want', false, 2, '2026-08-22T22:23:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d5bc0e56-1694-5e46-b880-0c8e383354ed', 'afc43ee6-851a-51af-ae78-0086ceda24be', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'the pension math is real. do your years with a contractor first, then decide.', false, 6, '2026-08-22T23:41:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('eb6fb6dc-6839-581c-8555-674606f2f984', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'tip', 'Where the money from a $189 service call actually goes', 'Every year a new tech sees an invoice and asks why he makes $22 an hour when we charged $189 for forty minutes. Fair question. Here''s roughly how I explain it at my shop. Numbers differ everywhere; this is the shape, not a formula.
- The tech''s wage, plus payroll taxes and workers'' comp on top of it
- The truck: payment, fuel, insurance, repairs, the stock on the shelves
- The office: the person who answered the phone and scheduled you
- Drive time between calls that the customer never sees on the bill
- Callbacks, which we fix for free
- Slow weeks in October when the phones are quiet and everyone still gets paid
After all that, a healthy shop keeps a margin, and plenty of shops don''t. I''d rather you understand this before you go out on your own and price yourself out of business.', 'hvac', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 40, '2026-09-23T21:06:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('6a9d0b59-0de8-5dbe-a055-0c5a8d7d4c0a', 'eb6fb6dc-6839-581c-8555-674606f2f984', 'aa4aa383-9b0a-5294-809c-62f229f9606e', '> a healthy shop keeps a margin
ok but if the margin is there why does every owner say they''re broke lol', false, 2, '2026-09-23T22:28:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('be233b9b-3724-559d-96f0-5b2bb3997186', 'eb6fb6dc-6839-581c-8555-674606f2f984', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Because some of them are. Two things:
- A lot of owners pay themselves last
- Equipment margins and service margins are very different animals
I''m not saying every owner is honest about it. I''m saying the $189 isn''t profit.', false, 3, '2026-09-23T23:19:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1ccf2a33-9334-5d3d-baa8-4ea59fd9ca4d', 'eb6fb6dc-6839-581c-8555-674606f2f984', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Same on the mechanical side. The number new guys never see is unbilled time. Here''s what I look for in a tech who''s earned a raise: the one whose calls don''t come back. A callback is the most expensive hour we have.', false, 8, '2026-09-24T09:33:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b2c53ce8-98e1-5a9c-a694-40fc114f9d17', 'eb6fb6dc-6839-581c-8555-674606f2f984', '31e0974e-aadd-529c-90fc-0385fc7c46a5', 'idk, this actually helps. my boss charges about that and i always assumed he was pocketing $150 of it', false, 1, '2026-09-24T12:30:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e4a7d94f-0d38-5ca2-85c5-ea78852aa412', 'eb6fb6dc-6839-581c-8555-674606f2f984', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'so is drive time not paid for helpers?? or just not billed to the customer', false, 1, '2026-09-24T12:51:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e55879f3-6126-5a03-910a-a3431b279506', 'eb6fb6dc-6839-581c-8555-674606f2f984', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Not billed separately in a flat call fee. Different thing from your pay:
- Driving between calls during the workday should be paid to you as hours worked, as far as I know
- If it isn''t, that''s a conversation with your boss, and the state labor department has the details', false, 12, '2026-09-25T02:20:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fec575a6-9ef6-5ba1-a3f3-25965c579660', 'eb6fb6dc-6839-581c-8555-674606f2f984', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'add to the list: the 2am walk-in call where the restaurant pays net 60. owners float a lot of money nobody sees', false, 3, '2026-09-25T09:13:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('11f26e39-f8de-549c-918d-f681ab8da84f', 'eb6fb6dc-6839-581c-8555-674606f2f984', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', 'saving this. kash drew a version of this on a napkin for me once. makes more sense written down', false, 0, '2026-09-25T16:52:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('71d41f22-1402-59e4-9e60-9e69253f42ec', '049e3011-0b6d-5ddf-ad0e-83e84339599a', 'question', 'Left a job with benefits. How do helpers handle health insurance?', '1 year in, switched over from a call center. my old job covered health insurance for me and my wife. the new shop near voorhees doesn''t offer any yet. we''ve been on her plan but adding me is expensive. how are other helpers handling this? marketplace? spouse? going without? not looking for a lecture, just what people actually do.', 'other', 'Camden County, NJ', 9, '2026-08-30T00:15:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('4299da6a-5d61-58d4-8a4b-6e0e6b061e67', '71d41f22-1402-59e4-9e60-9e69253f42ec', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'What I see with new guys:
- Spouse''s plan, when it''s available
- The state marketplace, which can be subsidized depending on household income
- A shop that offers it, which is a reason to change shops on its own
Don''t go without. One ladder fall costs more than a year of premiums. Get a marketplace quote and compare it to the cost of adding you to her plan.', true, 19, '2026-08-30T03:01:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9808e46a-520c-53a4-81bc-5e210b3edec1', '71d41f22-1402-59e4-9e60-9e69253f42ec', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'my shop started it at 6 months... so they''re out there. ask around at the supply house when you''re ready to look', false, 2, '2026-08-30T03:19:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3e7f6281-a1c3-5499-bfc7-a78a5c4691e8', '71d41f22-1402-59e4-9e60-9e69253f42ec', '5ea91175-1b81-51fb-918c-7ad563230535', 'We did the marketplace my first year... it came out cheaper than I expected with the income drop. Worth getting the quote before you decide anything... I was about to ask this exact question myself', false, 1, '2026-08-30T03:42:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('30f80acf-d2a0-5635-99e1-5e7c25fe61c1', '71d41f22-1402-59e4-9e60-9e69253f42ec', '049e3011-0b6d-5ddf-ad0e-83e84339599a', 'marketplace quote came back lower than adding me to her plan. doing that. thanks', false, 1, '2026-08-30T09:17:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('55aa8bfd-3957-5f82-ab2f-a189e60a0c69', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'question', 'new shop wants me on a 1099 with my own van. red flag or normal', '4 years in, service and panel swaps. got an offer from a shop in wayne, more per hour than i make now, but they want me as a 1099 ''independent contractor'' and i''d use my own van, my own tools, my own gas. i''d still be on their schedule, in their shirt, running their calls. idk if that''s normal or a way to skip paying for stuff. anyone done 1099 in the trades in nj?', 'electrical', 'Passaic County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-13T14:39:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e3003081-be78-5b49-a395-ed296e6237f5', '55aa8bfd-3957-5f82-ab2f-a189e60a0c69', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it: NJ is strict about who counts as an independent contractor. As far as I know, the state uses a test where, among other things, you have to be free of their control and actually running your own independent business. Their schedule, their shirt and their calls sounds like an employee to me. Read the NJ Department of Labor''s material on misclassification, or talk to an accountant, before you sign anything.', true, 17, '2026-09-14T02:11:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f4f55f66-dc45-5e8c-bd6d-d2033af56521', '55aa8bfd-3957-5f82-ab2f-a189e60a0c69', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'From the owner''s side, here''s what a 1099 usually means you pay for yourself:
- Both halves of payroll taxes
- Your own insurance, and no workers'' comp if you get hurt
- Van, fuel, tools, phone
- No overtime
Subtract all of that from the higher rate before you compare. It''s often less money, not more.', false, 5, '2026-09-14T02:55:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c4cb3489-4f60-5050-8f39-3540f6fef488', '55aa8bfd-3957-5f82-ab2f-a189e60a0c69', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'yeah the gas alone is like $80 a week on that route. didnt even think about the tax part', false, 1, '2026-09-14T09:46:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('99e51930-e3f8-5077-a9c3-bd1aaf7a0781', '55aa8bfd-3957-5f82-ab2f-a189e60a0c69', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly, there are legit 1099 setups in this trade, but they look like a guy with his own license and his own customers subbing for someone. Not a 4-year tech in the owner''s shirt.', false, 10, '2026-09-14T16:47:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('30ba6c49-09d3-58a9-9270-a34f738283b9', '55aa8bfd-3957-5f82-ab2f-a189e60a0c69', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'my cousin did this in jersey city for a year and got destroyed at tax time lol. set money aside if you do it, thier office won''t remind you', false, 2, '2026-09-14T17:30:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('98f6a640-4de1-5b9f-b6ce-0891df6eca3b', '55aa8bfd-3957-5f82-ab2f-a189e60a0c69', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'different situation but my shop pays me cash, no paperwork at all. at least a 1099 is paper? or is that worse?', false, 1, '2026-09-14T21:00:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d5c97fa2-14d5-585b-9b1c-60a0549c6d76', '55aa8bfd-3957-5f82-ab2f-a189e60a0c69', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'A 1099 is paper, but if the relationship is really employment, it can be the wrong paper. That''s a different problem than cash, not necessarily a better one. Same answer for both of you: the state labor department or an accountant, not a forum.', false, 5, '2026-09-14T21:16:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5e26250d-32a8-5525-9fc4-9c2855fcc81e', '330afa2d-de1f-58bc-aedf-c06a7bea2cac', 'question', 'How much did you actually spend on tools your first two years?', 'Year one almost done at a non-union shop in Morris County. I added up my receipts for the guy who does my taxes and I''ve spent way more on tools than I thought: hand tools, a meter, a bag, and two pairs of boots that died. Is that normal? Does your shop give a tool allowance or is it all on you? And what do you wish you hadn''t bought?', 'electrical', 'Morris County, NJ', 15, '2026-09-14T00:26:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0f3b5eb9-a283-560d-bb14-248b2e56d966', '5e26250d-32a8-5525-9fc4-9c2855fcc81e', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Normal, and it''s the most common regret I hear: buying a kit before you know what you''ll use. Our apprentices get a basic list; anything beyond that is their choice. Buy quality on the things that protect you, like boots, glasses, gloves and a good tester. Everything else can wait until you''ve borrowed it three times. Stay safe.', true, 13, '2026-09-14T01:33:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4ea75e6c-3ad6-5864-81c3-fe17bd11a919', '5e26250d-32a8-5525-9fc4-9c2855fcc81e', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly, at my shop I give a small tool allowance once a year, and I know plenty of shops don''t. Ask. Worst they say is no.', false, 7, '2026-09-14T03:01:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e7a4d756-c0ee-5c4b-bcef-5cb96f53818b', '5e26250d-32a8-5525-9fc4-9c2855fcc81e', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', 'biggest waste for me was a big rolling toolbox in year one... it lives in my parents'' garage now. second biggest was a cheap meter I had to replace', false, 2, '2026-09-14T03:37:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6035d732-c55d-5897-b55c-1659132ce3d2', '5e26250d-32a8-5525-9fc4-9c2855fcc81e', 'a5ea5c20-fc92-530f-8795-0f342d0e503f', 'nobody tells you boots are a tool. two pairs a year for me on new construction, every year', false, 1, '2026-09-14T03:58:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0e2790e5-9346-57b2-9655-f00c5c4621de', '5e26250d-32a8-5525-9fc4-9c2855fcc81e', '330afa2d-de1f-58bc-aedf-c06a7bea2cac', 'Ok, asking about an allowance at my review. No rolling toolbox, noted. Did anyone ever deduct tools on taxes, or is that not a thing for employees?', false, 1, '2026-09-14T10:01:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'tip', 'For the Jersey apprentices on my crew: the commute, honestly', 'Half my apprentices live in Jersey, so I''ve heard every version of this. Here''s what I tell them.

Don''t drive in unless the job pays for parking or you have a spot. Between the crossing, the tolls and a garage in Midtown, you''re working the first hour of the day for free. Train or PATH, then walk.

Leave earlier than you think. A 7am start means on the floor at 7 with your glasses on, not walking in the door.

Don''t move to the city in year one. You don''t know where your jobs will be in two years, and rent will eat you alive.

And I''m not one to talk. My sister lives in Bayonne, and every Sunday after dinner I sit in tunnel traffic going home and swear never again. So I get it, brother.', 'electrical', 'Queens, NY', 14, '2026-09-21T00:33:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('f547e2a2-3e93-57a5-8e57-9e5cca7f105b', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', '8b6662c7-cfe4-56bc-ba9e-b7cdcd78d855', 'New Brunswick to Midtown on NJ Transit is like an hour and a half door to door. Is that normal for guys on your crew brother?', false, 1, '2026-09-21T01:36:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2a14b3ee-40d9-527f-bd5c-dbcd3b4c5b09', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Some of them do worse. The guys from down your way are on the first train out. It''s doable for a few years. It gets old.', false, 6, '2026-09-21T02:48:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e0e20c2e-b82c-51e1-917d-836db484a7ae', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'union city here, i can see the city from my window and the week we had a job over there it took me an hour because of the bus to the tunnel lol', false, 2, '2026-09-21T10:59:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a35f3270-c746-598a-a529-42b575b2d0d7', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different for us plumbers, we''re in the van all day, so parking is my whole life. Brooklyn street parking with a work van is a sport. For electricians in Midtown, take the train, absolutely.', false, 3, '2026-09-21T22:40:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4127ad35-360b-5da0-ad73-eaeb74b20dd9', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'bay ridge to anywhere in manhattan is also an hour lol, it''s not just jersey people', false, 2, '2026-09-22T01:50:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('84b634e9-d8d0-57a1-b637-6c30363fa2ed', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'Question from someone not in yet: do apprentices get any say in which jobs they''re sent to? Or could you end up in the city even if you apply in Jersey?', false, 3, '2026-09-22T09:21:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('29342c25-0eef-54dd-995e-61c49f728017', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Depends on the local and its jurisdiction. I can only speak for Local 3, and you go where the work is. If you apply in Jersey, ask that local how they assign.', false, 6, '2026-09-22T09:47:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ec6a5397-7480-5fb8-bb7b-b1917269b76b', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'My uncle commuted from Wayne to the city for 20 years on the bus. He says the trick is sleeping on the bus and never driving. He has not driven into Manhattan since the 90s.', false, 4, '2026-09-22T10:31:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('66918acd-b16b-5414-bd01-f14b8482fff4', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', '8b6662c7-cfe4-56bc-ba9e-b7cdcd78d855', 'Sleeping on the train I can definitely do. Already practicing on the way home', false, 1, '2026-09-22T11:46:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fa5b7183-bb4e-534f-ade5-2b1650797cda', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'the real trick is never missing the bus lol. miss one and you''re late for everything all day', false, 3, '2026-09-22T12:10:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ec331605-c017-5549-a745-6667f87e8732', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', '164 so I stay in Jersey, but my foreman did years in the city before he came over here... he says he doesn''t miss the trains, he misses the lunch spots', false, 3, '2026-09-22T16:11:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9a920fa7-6d2d-524f-9374-a5efc11a1a92', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Your foreman''s right about lunch. That''s the one thing Midtown has on Jersey.', false, 4, '2026-09-28T19:12:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dce9bed9-fbc2-511b-ac27-b32ab749e701', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'I grew up in Jersey and I''ll say this: the bagels are a tie and the pizza is closer than either side admits.', false, 4, '2026-09-28T22:08:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cd9cd506-371c-5e35-b5f2-264afce9d716', 'ef6c7c20-0986-510c-b1f2-3e4071b2c1bf', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'Appreciate the honest answers. Leaving the city question alone until I''m actually in somewhere.', false, 2, '2026-09-29T03:49:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('b45a780c-3cd8-57d6-9bf8-3a9f335f2edf', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'discussion', 'First week of the fall semester: 22 new faces, three have held a torch', 'Every September I swear I''ll stop being surprised, and every September I''m surprised. New class started this week. Twenty-two of them. Three have held a torch, and one of those set his sleeve on fire in the first hour. Nobody hurt, everybody learned something.

First thing I teach, before anything technical: where the extinguisher is and how to use it. Second: how to sweep a floor properly. They laugh at that one. They stop laughing when they find out how much of the job it is.

For anyone who trains helpers: what''s the first thing you make a new person learn? Ask me how I know it matters.', 'hvac', 'Passaic County, NJ', 27, '2026-08-24T01:57:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('d485a510-2e48-568b-9a64-d38b0b550aa2', 'b45a780c-3cd8-57d6-9bf8-3a9f335f2edf', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Where the main shutoff is, kid. Before anything else. Every house, every job, find the main and make sure it actually turns. That''s the job.', false, 2, '2026-08-25T01:24:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('649c7d22-ba2b-5a58-b3de-141322d5a839', 'b45a780c-3cd8-57d6-9bf8-3a9f335f2edf', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Lockout/tagout and how to verify a circuit is dead, before they touch a tool. Then glasses on every day, no arguments. Good luck with the 22. Stay safe.', false, 3, '2026-08-25T03:46:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d92df54f-8454-54b1-beac-788066735b94', 'b45a780c-3cd8-57d6-9bf8-3a9f335f2edf', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'So this one time in AC... first day on a hotel job I made the new kid learn where the exits were before anything else lol. Sounds dumb. He still got lost in the basement for an hour on day two', false, 5, '2026-08-26T01:33:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a1d5fb7e-fa54-56f7-9af5-c2c94a2d8979', 'b45a780c-3cd8-57d6-9bf8-3a9f335f2edf', '63579434-616f-5a6d-8f1f-281437382d7a', 'Student in a different county here, and our teacher did the extinguisher thing first too. Then we swept for a week. I understand why now.', false, 1, '2026-08-26T01:56:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d4d1a611-2a74-5742-8e12-992982826779', 'b45a780c-3cd8-57d6-9bf8-3a9f335f2edf', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Mine: show up ten minutes early and write down what you''re told. A notebook in the back pocket fixes half the problems I see with new helpers.', false, 5, '2026-08-26T10:01:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c3470d11-31de-5851-aad0-c4fe590ad5b5', 'b45a780c-3cd8-57d6-9bf8-3a9f335f2edf', '7faa1a09-27de-5125-aea4-eb8d826c963b', 'career switcher here. the notebook thing is real. my first month i wrote down everything my lead said and reread it at night. still do it', false, 1, '2026-08-26T12:35:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('b92ca386-8fbe-579b-9b27-863daf17d6b9', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'discussion', 'Got screamed at by a GC in front of the whole crew. Wasn''t even my mistake', 'Sorry, venting a little. We''re doing the plumbing on a kitchen and two baths in a gut reno in Hillsborough. The GC walked in this morning, saw the island drain wasn''t where the new cabinet layout had it, and screamed at me in front of the tile guys and the electricians. I''m the helper. My lead set it from the drawings we were given last month. The GC changed the layout and never told us. I just stood there. Should I have said something? I didn''t want to make it worse for my boss.', 'plumbing', 'Somerset County, NJ', 5, '2026-09-17T00:18:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('ec3e70ef-a0f1-5bff-a84b-8ce7afab9110', 'b92ca386-8fbe-579b-9b27-863daf17d6b9', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'You did fine by not arguing on the spot. Tell your lead exactly what happened, today, and let him handle it with the GC. That''s his job, not yours. Next time there''s a revised drawing, ask to see the date on it. Paper settles most of these. Keep your head down and stay safe.', true, 7, '2026-09-17T01:50:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('de39c65c-3f84-519c-9328-bc1ae3df61e2', 'b92ca386-8fbe-579b-9b27-863daf17d6b9', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'My father used to say the GC yells at whoever''s standing closest. It wasn''t about you. I''ve been the guy who yelled, early on, and I regret it. The good ones come back and apologize. This one might not.', false, 6, '2026-09-18T01:21:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5d3a1779-92ec-5203-92fd-0a9fbd0be3b2', 'b92ca386-8fbe-579b-9b27-863daf17d6b9', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'had the same thing happen in deptford over a vent. my lead backed me up. did yours?', false, 3, '2026-09-18T02:48:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('25c09be3-e14f-5d32-9f5b-72a4bcd24d80', 'b92ca386-8fbe-579b-9b27-863daf17d6b9', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'edit: my lead called the GC, showed him the old drawing, and the GC came back after lunch and said "my bad" to my lead. Not to me. But I''ll take it.', false, 3, '2026-09-18T03:12:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5a5da624-49cd-5344-9227-a4fdc2665f3c', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'discussion', 'Quit the Bronx shop today. Two weeks'' notice, no drama', 'Two years at a non-union shop in the Bronx while I wait on the list. The last few months a lot of things got unsafe, and I''ll leave it at that. I gave two weeks'' notice this morning, thanked the owner for the two years, and that was it. Starting at a shop in Queens that does commercial fit-outs next month. My mentor told me to leave clean and never say a bad word about them publicly, so that''s all I''ll say. Mostly posting because I''ve been nervous about this for a month.', 'electrical', 'Bronx, NY', 13, '2026-09-15T16:19:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('bbc5e6fc-ed67-5309-a4ef-789086b2bcb3', '5a5da624-49cd-5344-9227-a4fdc2665f3c', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Proud of you, brother. You left the right way. Nobody in this trade remembers why you left. They remember how.', false, 5, '2026-09-16T01:18:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('07d44492-d6f3-5db0-8396-53927ddb89c1', '5a5da624-49cd-5344-9227-a4fdc2665f3c', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Two weeks and a thank-you. You''d be surprised how many guys can''t manage that. The owner will remember it when somebody calls him for a reference, and somebody always does.', false, 3, '2026-09-16T02:26:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('859ec140-7831-58c8-a137-c9e7eea8dadc', '5a5da624-49cd-5344-9227-a4fdc2665f3c', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fwiw ''unsafe'' is reason enough, you don''t owe anybody details. good luck at the new place. fit-outs means you''ll see some low voltage, pay attention to it, it''s a real trade', false, 7, '2026-09-16T23:09:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('dbc7aeaa-4e92-59aa-8686-ddf2de71c2be', '3839ca6e-9b97-5146-a0ce-e1221e0f3b8e', 'discussion', 'first week running calls solo. no callbacks yet', '3 years riding with a lead and this week they gave me my own van and my own calls. pemberton, browns mills, mount holly. 14 calls in 5 days, mostly no-cools on the last hot days and two furnace checks. no callbacks yet. called my lead twice, once for weird thermostat wiring and once because i couldn''t find the attic access in a split level. he answered both times and didn''t make me feel stupid. anyway. that''s it. just wanted to tell people who get it', 'hvac', 'Burlington County, NJ', 5, '2026-08-12T01:26:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('13fb1b49-64b4-5c8c-8b0a-106ef6312e0a', 'dbc7aeaa-4e92-59aa-8686-ddf2de71c2be', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Nice!! A first solo week with no callbacks is a good week... my first solo week I called my lead eleven times. Twice is nothing lol. Keep calling when you need to', false, 6, '2026-08-12T03:06:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('74c68402-d7b9-565a-b50d-e6e4e00241ba', 'dbc7aeaa-4e92-59aa-8686-ddf2de71c2be', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s what I look for in a new service tech: calls the lead when he isn''t sure instead of guessing. You''re doing it right. Callbacks will come eventually; how you handle the first one is what matters.', false, 4, '2026-08-12T23:19:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0e657d64-d2c9-5dd8-8ee4-f1d21a045a3d', 'dbc7aeaa-4e92-59aa-8686-ddf2de71c2be', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Congratulations. One habit for the first year:
- Photo of the nameplate, the thermostat wiring and your readings on every call
When a callback does happen, you''ll know exactly what you left.', false, 4, '2026-08-13T23:22:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('b2f9784f-35d1-54c6-a312-9ff150dbad69', 'f335afa5-2456-517f-bd3e-8c28f1aaa9ec', 'discussion', 'union county roll call (the county, not the union lol)', 'anyone else from union county on here? i''m in rahway, 2nd year in local 9, which i realize makes the title confusing, union county and also union, i meant the county. i spend my days on water heaters from elizabeth to cranford. feels like everyone on here is either bergen or down the shore. sound off', 'other', 'Union County, NJ', 14, '2026-08-30T20:09:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('d0221fd6-9db6-5285-8c2e-42a67a5c74f4', 'b2f9784f-35d1-54c6-a312-9ff150dbad69', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', 'elizabeth. hvac, 1 yr in. probably passed your van on route 1 this morning', false, 1, '2026-08-30T22:50:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2635b95b-3f97-5a55-b019-e01d3e202f3e', 'b2f9784f-35d1-54c6-a312-9ff150dbad69', '0b536e7d-7d15-52d5-ae52-959dc9ae15ec', 'rahway too. non-union plumbing, boilers in the winter. small world, we probably use the same supply house', false, 1, '2026-08-31T03:05:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3f5ff7ea-2d6f-581c-8b21-428e0ed15fd5', 'b2f9784f-35d1-54c6-a312-9ff150dbad69', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Edison, so next door. I''m claiming honorary Union County status for every no-heat call I''ve run in Rahway over the years.', false, 12, '2026-08-31T09:24:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('36490025-2f92-52f3-a4dc-8b56059fd584', 'b2f9784f-35d1-54c6-a312-9ff150dbad69', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'Piscataway, is that close enough? Still undecided on a trade, but I drive through Rahway twice a week for ride-alongs, so I''m counting myself in.', false, 3, '2026-08-31T12:30:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', 'e84cafaf-f3fa-5f47-ab1f-78162ab3e2c3', 'discussion', 'anyone else from ocean county on here? feels like it''s all north jersey', 'vo-tech kid from manahawkin, trades program, haven''t picked a trade yet (leaning electrical because my foreman at my summer job was an electrician). feels like every thread on here is bergen and hudson. where''s ocean county at? toms river, brick, lakewood, barnegat, LBI, sound off. appreciate it', 'other', 'Ocean County, NJ', 40, '2026-09-25T21:50:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('6ade0973-4fe7-57ab-9e58-a07e36dffece', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', '0e1f3b61-0ba4-56b9-9844-cea31e8e2deb', 'Brick! First year electrical helper. Glad it''s not just me down here.', false, 0, '2026-09-27T15:57:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('68090258-4802-5261-a9fe-197c3e5d26af', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', 'd680c878-f79d-58ae-9875-7e9bdf0efa31', 'brick too, plumbing, 3 years. brother we''re everywhere, we''re just stuck in traffic on route 37 instead of posting', false, 1, '2026-09-27T16:18:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('052de247-d331-5e86-b368-7740947e1cfe', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'toms river. hvac, ocean county vo-tech grad, doing duct work and changeouts. hi', false, 1, '2026-09-27T17:25:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f655c5bf-29c4-5501-aa25-9c60c1bf8e20', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'manahawkin too. electrical helper, residential remodels. small world, which program are you in', false, 2, '2026-09-27T18:56:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('06817d54-7977-5148-8e8c-b183aabeef93', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', 'e84cafaf-f3fa-5f47-ab1f-78162ab3e2c3', 'the county vo-tech trades program, same as everyone lol. you?', false, 2, '2026-09-27T19:38:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6a6eac2d-d687-595e-b533-6b0af94ae26c', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'same school, couple years ahead of you. look into the evening classes when you''re done, they''re better than people think', false, 2, '2026-09-27T23:27:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bdd79bc0-3762-5c98-8a3d-444eadad0393', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', '0068d208-ce11-5170-b467-caa34a717104', 'Jackson here, 2nd year in Local 400. Which, for the Ocean County kids reading, is the IBEW local I believe covers this area, but check their site, because jurisdiction maps are confusing and I got it wrong the first time I looked', false, 1, '2026-09-27T23:56:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('56d4d63e-d067-5c16-9770-902a0f61fe96', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'I''m at the shore too, and that''s all I''ll say about where. Good to see the county represented. If any of you ever want to know why something failed inspection down here, start a thread.', false, 5, '2026-09-28T23:27:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('78524ac6-8eb5-502b-80e3-981c83566050', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Monmouth, so I''m the neighbor who says he isn''t from Ocean County but does half his work there. Honestly, half my raised-house jobs since Sandy have been in your county.', false, 6, '2026-09-29T02:19:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2a434196-9e8e-55da-9207-3907af7c5967', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'egg harbor twp. not ocean but close enough. you guys get the LBI restaurant calls before we do', false, 8, '2026-09-30T00:40:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('01820b6e-2f2b-5b6d-b2e4-8e6c4d528d77', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'anyone else get coffee at the wawa on route 37 every morning or is that just me', false, 1, '2026-09-30T01:09:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a88474ff-c9a0-5b5b-a82a-dbd8506e0443', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', 'd680c878-f79d-58ae-9875-7e9bdf0efa31', 'every wawa on 37 is the same wawa brother. they''re all connected underground', false, 4, '2026-09-30T10:09:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('597d4b9f-6f1d-5fd7-a828-2db52f78c3cf', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'can confirm. been to most of them this month on material runs for the shop', false, 2, '2026-09-30T11:18:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('512c6aaa-72c7-5ff7-b0ed-3d65d36b9fb5', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', 'asbury park, monmouth, but i''ll take any thread that isn''t bergen county lol', false, 1, '2026-09-30T12:06:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e5872e42-7782-5afb-bd38-f679342a05d0', 'c0f8d6aa-e93e-5477-8186-e7a292e44d48', 'e84cafaf-f3fa-5f47-ab1f-78162ab3e2c3', 'this is more of us than i thought. appreciate it everyone. if anyone''s foreman needs a helper over winter break, i''m around', false, 1, '2026-09-30T15:58:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('91d535d9-4392-5662-bfe0-c6eccdd7f1f7', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'discussion', 'My best helper got the call from the Local. Happy for him. Mostly.', 'The vo-tech kid I hired last year, best helper I''ve had in a long time. Shows up early, listens, asks the right questions. He applied to the plumbers'' local in the spring without telling me. Got the call this week. Starts in January.

I''m happy for him, and I mean that. I was in the union myself for a few years. I know exactly what he''s getting: real schooling, real benefits. My father used to say you can''t keep a good kid in a small shop, you can only be the shop he''s glad he started in.

Still. I''d started thinking he might be the one to take this place over someday. Back to the hiring pile. Anyone else lose their best guy this year?', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 15, '2026-09-15T01:39:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('aae8aa64-a366-5a8b-8e65-8f24434f38f4', '91d535d9-4392-5662-bfe0-c6eccdd7f1f7', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Every spring I lose students to the locals and every spring I''m proud and a little sad. You did your part. He''ll remember who taught him to carry a water heater properly.', false, 5, '2026-09-15T09:46:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f628961a-0b00-5a21-a38c-18f24efe7d53', '91d535d9-4392-5662-bfe0-c6eccdd7f1f7', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'the guy from deptford is still reading, just saying lol. appreciate the advice from the other thread either way', false, 4, '2026-09-15T10:33:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bcd9abe2-9f4f-5d5b-b0b0-42954a848443', '91d535d9-4392-5662-bfe0-c6eccdd7f1f7', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Congratulations to him. Sorry if this is a dumb question, but do shops ever stay in touch with guys who go union? Do they ever come back?', false, 1, '2026-09-15T17:29:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b7f197b7-9819-593b-9ffa-93dab5cd8650', '91d535d9-4392-5662-bfe0-c6eccdd7f1f7', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Some do. I did, didn''t I? Took me a few years. The door''s open for him, and I told him so.', false, 3, '2026-09-16T02:42:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '7180834c-9f0f-5d01-a84e-72ced4209a2c', 'discussion', 'Since the pork roll thread settled nothing... Wawa or QuickChek?', 'Sorry, I know there was already a whole pork roll war on here... but nobody settled the other one. I''m in Little Falls, I just started riding with a crew that does commercial bathrooms all over, and this week we were in Hamilton and the guys from down there acted like I insulted their mother when I said QuickChek coffee is better. So... Wawa or QuickChek? And is it a north/south thing or an actual coffee thing? Defend your answer, I''m buying coffee for the crew Friday and I need to pick a side...', 'other', 'Passaic County, NJ', 15, '2026-09-25T17:42:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('8a895913-c51c-5086-874d-da9ffbf5a76b', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Wawa. Not even a question... I''ve been going to the same Wawa in Cherry Hill for 15 years and they know my order lol. QuickChek is a nice gas station. Wawa is a lifestyle', false, 3, '2026-09-26T12:09:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('29ce83ae-c00c-54aa-8083-9740cdd6d9ad', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'QuickChek. I said it in the other thread and I''ll say it again. Up here it isn''t even a choice, it''s geography.', false, 8, '2026-09-27T00:46:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e9350f88-44ec-53f1-a2df-5767b605c062', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'I''m from Hamilton. I wasn''t there, but I would have been one of the guys acting insulted. Wawa. The hoagie line at 6am is a sacred place and you walked in and disrespected it.', false, 3, '2026-09-27T01:40:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5d4e28c3-49bb-5e18-a263-1c72f66ceaee', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '5ea91175-1b81-51fb-918c-7ad563230535', 'In my defense the handle was a joke... I live in Cherry Hill. I''m Wawa. I''m sorry to everyone who expected otherwise.', false, 1, '2026-09-27T02:52:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5e8b114c-e5bf-56c7-b2a0-54d52d26184f', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'fair lawn. my handle is also a lie, the closest wawa is a real drive. quickchek every morning. sorry', false, 2, '2026-09-27T03:30:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2afeace0-dcf2-55bd-920f-9af4050966b1', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, I''ve been drinking deli coffee in Lodi for 28 years. You''re all wrong. Buy the crew coffee at the deli by the supply house and nobody fights.', false, 3, '2026-09-28T00:22:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('56456f02-0bbf-5c7f-911f-d077b90b2ab1', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '7180834c-9f0f-5d01-a84e-72ced4209a2c', 'ziggy that is the most boss answer possible... but which one would you pick if you HAD to?', false, 1, '2026-09-28T01:34:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a84b2bf3-4725-571d-8ccc-22b080f20191', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'QuickChek, because it''s on my way. That''s the whole reason. Don''t tell anybody down south.', false, 5, '2026-09-28T02:51:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('296ee510-50d4-5aba-a803-6ea49edced9d', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'wawa. down here at 5am in july the wawa is the only thing open and its full of guys in work boots. thats your answer', false, 5, '2026-09-28T22:05:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6af573ba-481d-55f7-ae0f-13dab3937872', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '7faa1a09-27de-5125-aea4-eb8d826c963b', 'secaucus. my handle says taylor ham and my coffee says quickchek. consistent at least', false, 2, '2026-09-28T23:14:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ad77d66f-9ee7-5fed-ba8b-f6ebeb7f7b4c', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '02a13f50-be86-588b-966d-7ae10b7d64cd', 'hackensack, but my mom''s from toms river so we drive past six wawas to see my grandma... honestly wawa coffee is better and the quickchek sandwiches are better, fight me', false, 3, '2026-09-28T23:42:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9772b7fb-2294-5877-b457-18a13a4f82de', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Ok Bergen_Ducts gets a pass because his mom raised him right... the rest of you up north are still lost', false, 2, '2026-09-29T10:15:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('73865dcc-8fae-5598-baee-7c65ea285e2c', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'I polled my class this morning instead of teaching them anything. Fourteen QuickChek, eight Wawa, and one student who said 7-Eleven and now has to sit in the back.', false, 7, '2026-09-30T01:42:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('33d8e76b-2fe9-5201-8d93-79a8f9873918', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'montclair, quickchek during the week. but on the parkway down the shore it''s wawa, everybody knows the rules', false, 0, '2026-09-30T10:25:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bf7852ed-4afe-513e-b26d-1fa5baeed334', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'toms river. wawa. same answer as the pork roll thread. consistency matters', false, 1, '2026-09-30T13:39:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b4a7ae68-d823-51b3-b715-f2213f1ba0d7', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'I''ll stay out of this one. I''ll only say a cold coffee on a hot jobsite is fine as long as you''re drinking water too. Stay hydrated, stay safe.', false, 7, '2026-09-30T23:11:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('68029bf8-bcd4-58e8-810e-d3f668db3105', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'bayonne. quickchek. brother how is this even a debate north of 195', false, 3, '2026-10-01T00:18:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cb2eb521-5faa-5ea4-864e-659d080433cd', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'cherry hill... wawa. i didn''t know quickchek was a real place until i was 19 lol', false, 1, '2026-10-01T10:08:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1073013f-54b6-5acf-bf3c-5cfcac4e8f18', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'I keep a spreadsheet of coffee stops on the way to my weekend job, mostly as a joke at this point, and statistically my best mornings have been Wawa days. That isn''t science. It isn''t nothing either.', false, 1, '2026-10-01T10:14:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a4ebcdb8-7d9a-598b-b628-2f755f5aae0a', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'the coffee on route 1 jobsites comes off a truck. drink it and go to work.', false, 4, '2026-10-01T10:46:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fd276a2b-49da-5a24-9183-36dac8d69d64', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '493faab8-51d6-584c-8d92-65b67edb36f6', 'glassboro. wawa. didn''t know this was even a question until this thread. edit: my teacher just said quickchek has better coffee and i don''t know what to believe anymore', false, 1, '2026-10-01T14:50:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d70e21a8-bbb5-5b5f-9bea-30c8bcf2ce2c', '4fc4d370-b3bd-543e-96e4-877dc495707f', '7180834c-9f0f-5d01-a84e-72ced4209a2c', 'ok final count from this thread: north says quickchek, south says wawa, ziggy says deli. I''m getting the deli. nobody can be mad at the deli...', false, 1, '2026-10-01T16:21:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('a576c208-a266-5a7a-b530-379f6aa6e3c8', 'fb3a0b82-da77-5dd7-9a89-e099391b6ce7', 'question', 'Boss threw a pipe wrench across the basement. Quit on the spot.', 'Two years out of the county vo-tech, 14 months at this shop in Essex. All demo, all carrying, and a boss who throws tools when he''s in a mood. Today it was a pipe wrench across a basement. Didn''t hit anybody. I put my stuff in my car, told him I was done, and drove home. Already have an interview Thursday with a shop in Montclair that does service. Did I mess up by not giving notice? Should I call him and smooth it over or just let it go?', 'plumbing', 'Essex County, NJ', 6, '2026-08-29T13:28:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0acf4b35-f099-59fb-b00e-b05e0912b082', 'a576c208-a266-5a7a-b530-379f6aa6e3c8', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question? Because "did I mess up" and "should I call him" have different answers.

Did you mess up: no. Someone throwing a pipe wrench in a basement is a safety problem, not a mood. Should you call: a short text saying you won''t be back and where to send your last check is enough.', true, 14, '2026-08-30T00:12:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9f9608f7-0bc6-538e-ae41-9eec982d74f7', 'a576c208-a266-5a7a-b530-379f6aa6e3c8', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Don''t trash him around the supply houses, though, even if he deserves it. People will hear about the wrench without your help. You just be the guy who shows up Thursday.', false, 6, '2026-08-30T02:35:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7dec0305-ba96-57c4-a6a0-eef35fb8ab21', 'a576c208-a266-5a7a-b530-379f6aa6e3c8', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'montclair has a few decent service shops. good luck thursday. wear the clean boots', false, 1, '2026-08-30T03:27:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0d3ba61e-23be-59fd-b9b0-093f2c4ab116', 'a576c208-a266-5a7a-b530-379f6aa6e3c8', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Agree with both. Thrown tools are how people get hurt, and you don''t owe notice to someone who makes the site unsafe. Write down the date and what happened, in case it ever matters for anything.', false, 5, '2026-08-30T03:36:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e5df06bb-261b-5527-a5ee-14a0403becf4', 'a576c208-a266-5a7a-b530-379f6aa6e3c8', 'fb3a0b82-da77-5dd7-9a89-e099391b6ce7', 'Sent the text. He replied with a thumbs up. That''s the most communication I''ve gotten from him in a year. Interview''s Thursday, boots are clean.', false, 2, '2026-08-30T09:18:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('7059f13b-0571-5d25-beac-ee7e54a889b5', '63579434-616f-5a6d-8f1f-281437382d7a', 'discussion', 'Got the 608 Universal on the first try (core was the hard part)', 'Took the EPA 608 at a supply house testing session Saturday and passed Universal. Core was the hardest section, like everyone says. Big thanks to ms_almonte, who told me to drill Core until I could recite the dates in my sleep. Still a vo-tech student, but now I''m allowed to actually hook up gauges with my lead watching. The shop I''m doing Saturdays at said they''d bump me a dollar once I had it, so we''ll see if they remember.', 'hvac', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 4, '2026-10-05T01:14:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('863d4b67-6bbc-54b8-93a2-d02ad8a37554', '093c22fa-177a-57f7-9eba-10a325ebde80', 'discussion', 'First heating call of the season and the thermostat was set to COOL', 'First cold morning this week and the phones at the shop went off. My first heating call of the season, in Roselle: "furnace blowing cold air." I pulled the panel, checked the flame sensor, checked the inducer, checked the filter. Twenty minutes in, the homeowner''s daughter asked if the thermostat was supposed to say COOL. It was. Switched it to HEAT and the furnace fired right up. We still charged the service fee because the office said so, and I felt terrible. Lol. Two years in and I still fell for it.', 'hvac', 'Union County, NJ', 10, '2026-10-02T03:19:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('fbb57f2d-1893-53b3-ac1e-05e7def75706', '863d4b67-6bbc-54b8-93a2-d02ad8a37554', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Lol everybody has one of these... thermostat first is the oldest lesson in the book and we all learn it the hard way anyway. Welcome to heating season', false, 11, '2026-10-05T02:36:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b8ec3b3b-5aee-5919-a7e5-b437f2aa1a70', '863d4b67-6bbc-54b8-93a2-d02ad8a37554', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Don''t feel terrible about the fee. You drove there, diagnosed it, and checked the flame sensor and filter while you were in there, which is real work. Two things I''d do:
- Tell the customer what you checked, so they know they got something
- Write "tstat in cool" on the ticket so the office starts asking that question on the phone
The first cold week is full of these.', false, 5, '2026-10-05T02:43:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('798f22a1-859b-5020-81cd-50b02443d3a8', '863d4b67-6bbc-54b8-93a2-d02ad8a37554', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First thing I tell students on a no-heat: talk to the thermostat before you talk to the furnace. Second: ask the homeowner what changed since the last time it worked. Ask me how I know you''ll still forget once a year.', false, 15, '2026-10-05T02:56:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fbbb1487-55b4-55f4-b55a-db5ce7629d8f', '863d4b67-6bbc-54b8-93a2-d02ad8a37554', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', 'did the exact same thing last week in elizabeth. except it was the fan set to ON not AUTO. homeowner thought it was broken because it blew cold between cycles', false, 3, '2026-10-05T03:08:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('93d646da-cfae-521b-b631-c31027958524', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'discussion', 'Got the call. Interview for the IBEW apprenticeship is next month', 'Applied over the summer because my shop teacher would not stop bringing it up. Took the aptitude test. Got a call today with an interview date. I was at the Wawa when my phone rang and almost dropped my coffee. Not in yet, I know. But I didn''t think I''d get this far. What do I wear and what do they ask?', 'electrical', 'Essex County, NJ', 8, '2026-09-30T09:11:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('650872f7-5c22-5b0f-8e84-815eebfa9dd1', '93d646da-cfae-521b-b631-c31027958524', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, congrats. That''s a big step. I can only speak for how mine went years ago: clean simple clothes, on time means early, and be honest. They want to know you''ll show up and listen. Don''t pretend you know more than you do.', false, 5, '2026-09-30T13:39:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f9c9048b-5b7a-5ade-9451-19a4d1d17017', '93d646da-cfae-521b-b631-c31027958524', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Congratulations. Bring proof of any work or school you have, even weekend helper hours. Know why you want this trade in one or two sentences. And when they ask about safety, mean it. Stay safe.', false, 4, '2026-10-01T01:18:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('31493df4-c2ad-502f-b47c-2e3837200524', '93d646da-cfae-521b-b631-c31027958524', '5ad43be5-8875-5ab7-aeb8-e83457c681fe', '1st year 164. i wore a button down and was the most overdressed guy in the room lol. still got in. just be on time', false, 2, '2026-10-01T02:18:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0332fb77-6d4c-5dbc-89a4-2bf0d8c87362', '93d646da-cfae-521b-b631-c31027958524', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Practice saying your answers out loud before the day. My students who do mock interviews with me always do better than the ones who wing it. Ask me how I know.', false, 3, '2026-10-01T03:13:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('67d23a57-f65c-5e0f-b768-aaa8ced0a0ea', '93d646da-cfae-521b-b631-c31027958524', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'congrats brother. hvac guy here but rooting for you, update us after the interview', false, 1, '2026-10-01T03:39:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('7c6e56bd-3abb-58bd-b52a-d51a9f8bfe09', '86afdff7-a622-5314-99e0-81558cc06b11', 'discussion', 'Accepted into the steamfitters'' apprenticeship. I start in January.', 'Sorry if this isn''t the right place for it. I''m two years out of the Morris County vo-tech HVAC program. I applied to the steamfitters'' apprenticeship last spring, did the test and the interview, and got the acceptance call today. I start in January. My parents didn''t really understand why I was so excited until I explained the benefits part. Anyway, I wanted to tell people who would understand. If anyone has advice for the first year, thanks in advance.', 'hvac', 'Morris County, NJ', 13, '2026-09-30T00:38:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5eaa391b-2a5b-54d5-a987-d872f3d41753', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'question', 'GC''s super ripped into me on a JC jobsite. This time I deserved it', 'Doing a ductless install in an apartment renovation in Jersey City. I left a ceiling access open and a bag of insulation in the hallway overnight. Fire inspector walked through first thing in the morning. The GC''s super found me at 7am and let me have it in front of the drywall guys. He was right. I was embarrassed. Apologized, cleaned it up. Sorry if this is a dumb post, I''m just stewing on it. How do you get over getting yelled at when it actually was your fault?', 'hvac', 'Hudson County, NJ', 13, '2026-08-07T16:00:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('4866ce10-80b4-5e23-9e2f-b36f35dff7ec', '5eaa391b-2a5b-54d5-a987-d872f3d41753', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First: you owned it and fixed it. That''s most of it.

Second: tomorrow, be the first one cleaning up at the end of the day, without being asked, where he can see it.

Third: let it go by the weekend. Every one of us has a story like this. Ask me how I know.', true, 15, '2026-08-10T02:56:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f3b168e7-7d73-5da1-baf6-4ad6eb864978', '5eaa391b-2a5b-54d5-a987-d872f3d41753', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Open ceilings and material in an egress path are a real problem on a multifamily job, so he wasn''t wrong to be upset. Take the lesson, ignore the tone. Do an end-of-day walk every day: access panels closed, path clear. Stay safe.', false, 7, '2026-08-10T23:38:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('514601a2-d11a-5524-b004-d90e64cb0486', '5eaa391b-2a5b-54d5-a987-d872f3d41753', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'idk, getting yelled at when you were wrong is alot easier than when you weren''t. at least you know what to fix', false, 2, '2026-08-11T02:07:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dafb73e9-5c08-51e4-bbdd-00e1d7004331', '5eaa391b-2a5b-54d5-a987-d872f3d41753', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'fair. did the end of day walk today. super nodded at me on the way out. that''s probably as good as it gets', false, 2, '2026-08-11T09:10:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('25186afe-2cb4-551e-b0b4-cddc91e843dd', 'd680c878-f79d-58ae-9875-7e9bdf0efa31', 'discussion', 'Rain rant: nine days of mud on an underground job in Jackson', 'Not a question, I just need to yell. New construction in Jackson, we''re supposed to be setting underground for six houses. It has rained nine of the last eleven days. The trench is soup. The GC wants it done by Friday anyway. My boots weigh ten pounds each and I''ve lost a glove in the mud every single day. How do you guys keep your stuff dry? Does anyone own boots that actually survive this, brother?', 'plumbing', 'Ocean County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-18T09:27:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('51e73c26-9044-5491-b815-4633e2b6eb94', '25186afe-2cb4-551e-b0b4-cddc91e843dd', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'rotate two pairs of boots. one dries by the heater overnight while you destroy the other one. thats the whole secret', false, 7, '2026-09-18T10:07:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ecdb157c-ecab-57b5-87ed-d79ffc04950e', '25186afe-2cb4-551e-b0b4-cddc91e843dd', '0e1f3b61-0ba4-56b9-9844-cea31e8e2deb', 'My handle is literally about this. On rain days my boss sends us to restock the van. Underground guys don''t get that luxury I guess.', false, 1, '2026-09-18T11:38:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d83c029d-097a-5663-ba97-86acf4812dbe', '25186afe-2cb4-551e-b0b4-cddc91e843dd', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kid, mud''s part of it. Rubber boots over your work boots on trench days, and a bucket with a lid for your tools. And don''t let the GC rush you into a bad joint because of a deadline. The inspector won''t care that it rained. That''s the job.', false, 11, '2026-09-19T12:44:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('24713ba4-a659-5e32-80af-cc3a8459c242', '25186afe-2cb4-551e-b0b4-cddc91e843dd', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'Electrical vo-tech kid here. I thought the attic in July was the worst thing in the trades. This sounds worse.', false, 1, '2026-09-19T14:41:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('70fa150b-bce9-55a2-b944-cf9574d7fd7a', '25186afe-2cb4-551e-b0b4-cddc91e843dd', 'd680c878-f79d-58ae-9875-7e9bdf0efa31', 'attic in july is worse for like 2 months. mud is worse the rest of the year. both suck brother', false, 2, '2026-09-19T15:03:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a0da431c-752c-5a0c-bdd2-300196848947', '25186afe-2cb4-551e-b0b4-cddc91e843dd', '0068d208-ce11-5170-b467-caa34a717104', 'I''m in Jackson too and it''s been miserable. Our new-construction job got pushed a week because nobody could get trucks down the access road.', false, 3, '2026-09-19T19:54:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4f6c1b84-df2d-5d9d-97f9-b1ef9a7c1ed7', '25186afe-2cb4-551e-b0b4-cddc91e843dd', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Lol we once did a rooftop changeout in a nor''easter because the crane was already paid for... nobody should do that. Stay dry out there', false, 6, '2026-09-20T01:01:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('16159665-42e0-5c81-a718-c16ed3b9e29b', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'discussion', 'It was 97 outside and I swear 140 in that attic', 'Summer job, helping an electrical contractor while school''s out. Today we ran a new circuit for a bathroom fan in a Cape in Hamilton, which meant the attic. In the heat wave. My shirt was soaked through in four minutes. I drank three bottles of water and my boss made me come down every 20 minutes, which I was mad about until I got dizzy on the ladder coming down the last time. I''m fine. Sat in the truck with the AC on for a while. Is this just what summers are? How do you all do this for 20 years?', 'electrical', 'Mercer County, NJ', 7, '2026-08-01T13:20:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('295d9ca4-5259-577a-970d-8ccdd15a25be', '16159665-42e0-5c81-a718-c16ed3b9e29b', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Your boss made the right call, and I''m glad he did. Heat illness sneaks up on people, and dizziness on a ladder is exactly how someone gets hurt. Do attic work early in the morning, take breaks before you need them, water plus something with electrolytes. If you feel off, you come down. Stay safe.', false, 5, '2026-08-01T18:31:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5c50efac-7959-5bd4-8caa-f5babfd7c157', '16159665-42e0-5c81-a718-c16ed3b9e29b', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'try a walk-in compressor on a boardwalk roof in july. at least your attic had shade lol', false, 4, '2026-08-01T21:05:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ac8a80e7-1310-56da-9668-b60ca7602238', '16159665-42e0-5c81-a718-c16ed3b9e29b', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly the shore attics are the worst. Raised houses, dark shingles, no ventilation. I schedule attic work before 10am in July and August now, period. Took me way too long to learn that.', false, 15, '2026-08-01T22:56:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c67a8044-463f-5119-9d09-aa7c44da7eaa', '16159665-42e0-5c81-a718-c16ed3b9e29b', '2f048a7b-273e-574a-911a-7232a6136051', '20 years? i''m 4 years in and i already bought a cooling towel and a little fan that clips on my hard hat. no shame', false, 5, '2026-08-02T01:58:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('58bea4ba-e9b3-5c9e-a56b-8fc2364e3456', '16159665-42e0-5c81-a718-c16ed3b9e29b', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'hvac helper in clifton, we did 3 attic air handlers this week. my handle was a joke when i made it. it''s not a joke anymore', false, 1, '2026-08-02T02:48:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bb9fb586-3bca-56f6-bf33-0c7acb046106', '16159665-42e0-5c81-a718-c16ed3b9e29b', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'Ordering the cooling towel. My boss also said nobody gets a medal for staying up there. Writing that on my tool bag.', false, 1, '2026-08-02T09:16:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b798fd30-9b1b-5820-8674-ac6ffb322a06', '16159665-42e0-5c81-a718-c16ed3b9e29b', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Lol that''s a good boss... So this one time in AC, a guy on my crew didn''t come down when he should have and we had to help him out of the attic. He was ok. Come down when your boss says come down', false, 5, '2026-08-09T20:50:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('329c7ec2-f1ea-5740-9c6a-f279e67a3527', '16159665-42e0-5c81-a718-c16ed3b9e29b', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'One thing from my side, since I inspect a lot of summer attic work: when you''re miserable, you rush, and rushed connections are what fail later. Take the break, then make the connection right. Heat makes people skip steps.', false, 14, '2026-08-09T21:45:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('c9afaaa6-e409-5be8-953a-37358ea4becb', '9fe65554-dd4f-5c8b-9708-65d0c765a948', 'question', 'Homeowner tried to hand me a $20 tip. Do you take it?', 'First month as a helper at a shop near Long Branch. We fixed a leak under an older lady''s kitchen sink today, and while we were packing up she tried to hand me a $20 and a bottle of water. I took the water and said no to the money because idk what the rule is. My lead laughed at me in the truck. Is it ok to take tips? Does the shop care? Do you split it with your lead?', 'plumbing', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 17, '2026-10-01T01:52:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('53ec7e06-be3e-5f49-bf78-8fe319262ce9', 'c9afaaa6-e409-5be8-953a-37358ea4becb', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly, at my shop the rule is simple: if a customer insists, say thank you and take it, and never ask or hint. Some shops have a no-tip policy, so ask your boss once and then you know. Splitting with your lead is a nice move when he did most of the work, which in month one, he probably did.', true, 11, '2026-10-02T01:50:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7d94fcb6-5825-5a03-b4be-39769c8b42ee', 'c9afaaa6-e409-5be8-953a-37358ea4becb', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Take the water every time, kid. Take the money if she insists twice. Never take it from someone who looks like they can''t afford it. That''s the job.', false, 5, '2026-10-03T14:01:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f1e01e7e-5e27-549a-a278-6df8f4c49e0e', 'c9afaaa6-e409-5be8-953a-37358ea4becb', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'my foreman says a tip means the customer liked you, it''s not a payment. he gives it to whoever did the cleanup. no idea if that''s a thing everywhere', false, 1, '2026-10-03T15:50:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d2131c92-5bdb-536b-8ba7-a96fc33ce3c9', 'c9afaaa6-e409-5be8-953a-37358ea4becb', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Down here in summer it''s cold Gatorade and leftover hoagies... I''ve been tipped in tomatoes from a guy''s garden. Took the tomatoes lol', false, 6, '2026-10-03T16:09:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9ace578f-b2ee-5835-acdf-052cadc80cd4', 'c9afaaa6-e409-5be8-953a-37358ea4becb', '9fe65554-dd4f-5c8b-9708-65d0c765a948', 'ok asked my boss. he said keep it if they insist, nothing over $20, and buy the lead a coffee. so now i owe my lead a coffee for a tip i didn''t even take lol', false, 4, '2026-10-04T09:34:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('5e530bcb-384a-50d9-bb34-6e2d0ff6ccc3', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'discussion', 'Customer called the office and asked for me by name', '4 years in, running service on my own in Hudson. I''m not a talker. Customers usually ask for my boss or the other guy, the one who can talk to anybody. Today the office said a lady in Weehawken called back for a second job and asked for "the quiet one who explained the water heater." Small thing. Made my week. The explanation was me drawing on a piece of cardboard because I''m better at that than talking lol.', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 27, '2026-07-27T01:26:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('0744b255-3d04-502a-a4c2-7c8cc704c330', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'discussion', 'A first-year asked ME how to bend an offset today...', '4th year in 164... today a brand new first-year on our job asked me how to bend an offset and I just showed him without thinking about it. Then I realized I was him three years ago, asking the same thing and wasting half a stick of EMT. My foreman saw it and said "see, you''re useful now." Weird feeling... anyway, I top out next year. Just wanted to say it somewhere', 'electrical', 'Bergen County, NJ', 4, '2026-09-09T01:45:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('d56b4c96-15f5-594c-a70f-cf7d2ae36ea3', '0744b255-3d04-502a-a4c2-7c8cc704c330', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'That''s the moment. Teaching someone is how you find out you actually know it. Keep doing it, and teach him the safety part along with the bend. Stay safe.', false, 3, '2026-09-09T02:53:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('744e59d1-3765-5510-b140-61fcca3aed9d', '0744b255-3d04-502a-a4c2-7c8cc704c330', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Good. The apprentices who teach well usually make the best journeymen. Teach him why, not just how. ''Because that''s how we do it'' is how bad habits travel from crew to crew.', false, 12, '2026-09-09T09:14:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('adbc68cd-802c-5048-b450-50965a49664c', '0744b255-3d04-502a-a4c2-7c8cc704c330', 'eb2e65c4-6237-58c3-874e-6d74de571429', '2nd year 164 here, still the one asking lol. i hope somebody on my job is this nice', false, 2, '2026-09-09T10:02:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('340fc854-bc4f-55d8-8655-5c8b5c595f80', '0744b255-3d04-502a-a4c2-7c8cc704c330', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'appreciate it... and yeah, the safety part, I made him put his glasses on first. learned that one from my foreman too', false, 2, '2026-09-09T12:25:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('1f46e837-d525-5d25-915d-b415188bd0aa', 'ea9bf166-53e3-541b-9f3a-28d296966e19', 'discussion', 'Week one done. Everything hurts and I''m weirdly happy', 'Left insurance claims last month, I''m 28, and I started as a plumbing helper at a shop out of Glassboro on Monday. Five days of carrying cast iron out of a basement in Pitman and hauling a water heater up some stairs. My hands are wrecked, my back is wrecked, I fell asleep at 8:30 every night. And I haven''t checked a work email in a week. Don''t know if I''ll last. Anyway. Week one, done.', 'plumbing', 'Gloucester County, NJ', 4, '2026-09-29T23:55:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('609ba189-b563-5706-9228-d00f59837191', '1f46e837-d525-5d25-915d-b415188bd0aa', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Week one is the worst one, physically. Your body catches up in about a month. I switched over from restaurant management at 26 and I remember falling asleep in my boots. It gets better. Keep going.', false, 4, '2026-09-30T03:16:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e77700ae-3ceb-52ff-8b94-41780f8e4156', '1f46e837-d525-5d25-915d-b415188bd0aa', '9d863d1d-0f6f-5b8c-921d-d473f8721247', 'career switcher too. week 1 i couldn''t close my hands in the morning lol. by week 6 i was fine', false, 2, '2026-09-30T09:41:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9d317cff-7fef-5833-9470-aab3cd924102', '1f46e837-d525-5d25-915d-b415188bd0aa', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'pitman basements are no joke... welcome. it gets easier, or you just stop noticing', false, 1, '2026-09-30T11:14:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('1255e92f-42fa-5599-90f6-9fd527aa2667', '4c3c92ef-9ba5-56b3-90e4-5341be547a4a', 'discussion', 'worked all of labor day weekend on strip mall rooftops. rant incoming', 'everybody i know was at the beach labor day weekend. me? three days straight of rooftop units on strip malls around neptune and ocean township, 90+ and humid, and every RTU in monmouth county decided to die the same weekend. one roof had no hatch so it was an extension ladder in the heat with a bag of tools. made good OT. hate everything. appreciate you guys reading this far', 'hvac', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 40, '2026-08-11T23:28:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e00a2754-45cc-5810-9393-c5f371762b4d', '1255e92f-42fa-5599-90f6-9fd527aa2667', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Labor Day weekend in HVAC is a tradition... nobody in this trade is at a barbecue lol. Congrats on surviving it', false, 2, '2026-08-13T01:55:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('750b40ea-f6af-5531-9e8c-e446ffe64507', '1255e92f-42fa-5599-90f6-9fd527aa2667', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'same weekend every year down here, ice machines and walk-ins on the boardwalk nonstop. the tuesday after labor day everything goes quiet and you sleep for a week', false, 1, '2026-08-13T03:05:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('061e52f2-fb55-520f-bec8-bfbfd802776c', '1255e92f-42fa-5599-90f6-9fd527aa2667', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Holiday weekends are where the money gets made and where techs burn out. If you work a lot of them:
- Ask how holiday pay works before the weekend, not after
- Bank some of that OT
- Take a day when it slows down, and ask for it in writing', false, 4, '2026-08-13T10:11:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('13d5435c-4fa4-58ec-b8a7-73d80c7d0982', '1255e92f-42fa-5599-90f6-9fd527aa2667', '7ae3dcf8-1c9a-56f2-bc63-f1efe2a2d403', 'bound brook. same. 3 rooftops sunday. nobody told me labor day means actual labor lol', false, 1, '2026-08-13T12:30:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('678ba6f3-6022-5acd-9921-640c56f706b9', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'discussion', 'Hudson County, where you at? Bayonne checking in', 'Feels like half this place is Bergen and the shore. Hudson County roll call. I''m in Bayonne, plumbing helper, a year in, mostly old buildings and a lot of walkups. Where are the Hudson people? JC, Hoboken, Union City, North Bergen, Kearny, Secaucus, brother, sound off. Bonus points if you''ve ever parked a work van in Hoboken without a ticket.', 'other', 'Hudson County, NJ', 7, '2026-08-28T01:26:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('61099c09-722a-554a-8bd7-66c291fccb3f', '678ba6f3-6022-5acd-9921-640c56f706b9', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Jersey City. Seventeen years of multifamily and co-ops. And no. Nobody parks a work van in Hoboken legally. It''s a myth.', false, 2, '2026-08-28T10:06:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7a38770e-26bb-5a4b-bcaf-6f438a6ab296', '678ba6f3-6022-5acd-9921-640c56f706b9', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'Bayonne too. HVAC, 2 years. we''ve probably been in the same building', false, 1, '2026-08-28T11:22:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d76f4ac6-933c-5f86-9fc1-fff405c56e4a', '678ba6f3-6022-5acd-9921-640c56f706b9', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'union city. service plumbing. hi lol, didn''t know there were this many of us', false, 1, '2026-08-28T13:58:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dbdb528e-0047-5824-a2d7-f174987c8521', '678ba6f3-6022-5acd-9921-640c56f706b9', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'union city as well, electrical helper. parking in hoboken got me two tickets in one week lol', false, 2, '2026-08-28T14:37:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1e8ae09a-9fde-5201-b2d2-481534e27112', '678ba6f3-6022-5acd-9921-640c56f706b9', '7faa1a09-27de-5125-aea4-eb8d826c963b', 'secaucus. career switcher, hvac. secaucus is hudson county even if everyone forgets', false, 1, '2026-08-28T20:34:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('008d6997-b3a4-568d-8348-7678b9a05bb5', '678ba6f3-6022-5acd-9921-640c56f706b9', '2f048a7b-273e-574a-911a-7232a6136051', 'north bergen, 4 years, service. sorry for the dumb add but anyone know a supply house in jc that opens before 7', false, 3, '2026-09-06T11:57:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('03f5c62b-6fea-5c68-a979-6d08957109e0', '678ba6f3-6022-5acd-9921-640c56f706b9', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Kearny, right on the line with Bergen, so I claim both counties like my father did. Good to see this many of you. If any of you ever want to talk old Hudson buildings, I''ve been in most of them.', false, 6, '2026-09-07T00:41:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dac7eda6-c3c4-5028-918d-bc2fa9ba3f9b', '678ba6f3-6022-5acd-9921-640c56f706b9', 'acfd4b6b-76e3-5ba1-a2a5-522d4e1a65b6', 'more of us than I thought brother. and yes my handle says Kearny and I live in Bayonne. long story, don''t ask', false, 2, '2026-09-07T01:53:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('add5a549-4c12-5c39-bb88-549d15f53c6f', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'tip', 'Torch work in old houses: stick around after you put the torch down', 'Had a helper sweat a couple of fittings on a boiler near a joist bay in Lodi last week. Nice joints. We packed up, I went back down for a tool I forgot, and I smelled it before I saw it. The old wood and the dust up in that bay had been smoldering the whole time.

Nobody got hurt and the house is fine. But here''s what everybody on my trucks does now, and what I should have made him do:

Fire cloth behind the joint before you light the torch, not after. Wet down old framing if it''s dry as paper. Spray bottle and an extinguisher on the floor next to you, not out on the truck. And when you''re done, stay and watch it for half an hour. Put your hand near the wood. Look up into the bay with a light.

Old balloon-frame houses in Bergen have bays that run open floor to floor. A spark goes up there and you won''t see it until it''s a real problem.

Thirty minutes of watching is cheap. That''s the job.', 'plumbing', 'Bergen County, NJ', 15, '2026-09-17T01:54:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('18710dec-c832-5ca2-8111-e716276d1ad1', 'add5a549-4c12-5c39-bb88-549d15f53c6f', 'fb3a0b82-da77-5dd7-9a89-e099391b6ce7', 'Good one. What kind of fire cloth do you guys actually use, the cheap felt ones from the supply house or the pricier ones? And do you wet the wood every single time or only when it''s old?', false, 1, '2026-09-17T09:03:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('baa14742-5883-537d-87c0-c9d389b21045', 'add5a549-4c12-5c39-bb88-549d15f53c6f', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'The felt ones are fine for half inch and three quarter copper if you keep them in good shape. I spray old wood every time, it costs nothing. And check the other side of the wall. Hoboken brownstones share party walls, and the smoke shows up in the neighbor''s place first.', false, 2, '2026-09-17T11:10:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b8eb2d63-4355-5993-9389-f971739b6435', 'add5a549-4c12-5c39-bb88-549d15f53c6f', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First thing I teach before anyone touches a torch: know where the extinguisher is and what''s on the other side of the wall. Second: you''re not done when the joint is done. Students hate the waiting part. Ask me how I know it matters.', false, 3, '2026-09-18T01:57:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('8dcf7115-dc45-57bf-ac6d-e3f11e5c1a63', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'question', 'Press coupling spit water under test... boss says I never pressed it', 'So we did a small repipe in a ranch in Cherry Hill, all press, and when the boss put it under test one of my 3/4 couplings was spitting... he took one look and said I never pressed it. I swear I did. Then he showed me the pipe and there was no depth mark, because I skipped marking on couplings since "I could feel it seat"...

Couple questions. Is it normal for an unpressed fitting to leak like that or did I just get lucky? And if I DID press it and it still leaked, what else causes that? Trying to not do this twice

edit: boss redid it, passed. buying a marker for every pouch I own', 'plumbing', 'Camden County, NJ', 6, '2026-08-17T00:51:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('d1b535cf-adc2-5b81-9b17-fe35ae9bfd3a', '8dcf7115-dc45-57bf-ac6d-e3f11e5c1a63', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'You got lucky in the right way. A lot of the press fittings on the market now are designed to leak when they haven''t been pressed, so you find them under test instead of months later behind drywall. It did its job.

If a fitting is pressed and still leaks, the usual causes on our jobs: the pipe wasn''t fully inserted, a burr or a rough cut nicked the O-ring, dirt on the pipe, a dented or out-of-round end, or the wrong jaw for the size. Cut square, deburr, wipe, mark, insert to the mark, press. Every time.

Here''s what I look for when I hire, by the way: somebody who marks depth on couplings too.', false, 7, '2026-08-17T02:30:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('63febe3b-8122-5e16-b88e-051fb7ccfc78', '8dcf7115-dc45-57bf-ac6d-e3f11e5c1a63', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'my uncle makes me mark depth and then he checks the mark after the press before he lets me move on. annoying but it works', false, 4, '2026-08-17T03:26:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('943dffae-dde6-5f94-938b-df051ef05670', 'de452d6f-92dd-5609-97a4-463b06fafe39', 'question', 'Why does my lead flow nitrogen when we braze linesets?', 'Sorry if this is a dumb one. Doing a lot of AC changeouts in Bayonne and JC this summer. Every time we braze the lineset my lead hooks up the nitrogen bottle with a regulator and has a little flow going through the pipe while I braze. He told me "so you don''t make crud" and walked off. What crud? In school we just brazed. Is this actually a big deal or is it one of those things one guy does?', 'hvac', 'Hudson County, NJ', 27, '2026-08-13T02:35:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('efeb8a3c-56c1-52d6-8924-fbeba95ad751', '943dffae-dde6-5f94-938b-df051ef05670', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Not a one-guy thing... it''s a big deal lol. Copper heated with air inside it grows black oxide scale on the inside wall. Later that scale flakes off and goes where you don''t want it: the metering device, the screens, the compressor oil. A low flow of nitrogen pushes the oxygen out so the inside stays clean. So this one time in AC I cut open a line on a casino job where nobody flowed nitrogen and it looked like the inside of a chimney. Low flow, through a regulator, just enough to feel on your hand.', false, 2, '2026-08-14T00:25:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d7865767-bebd-53d4-a83c-839c7aaead09', '943dffae-dde6-5f94-938b-df051ef05670', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Plumber''s side of it, kid: on water we sweat with soft solder and nobody cares about a little oxide inside. Refrigerant is brazed and the system is sealed, so whatever''s inside stays inside forever. Different animal. Listen to your lead on this one.', false, 2, '2026-08-14T01:23:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('22ef1b2b-8b79-5b08-9ee1-89f53ba0d4d6', '566a4ee6-0294-5f38-93a7-c5e3a7297ddd', 'question', 'mini-split flare connection leaking on a brand new install', 'apologies if this is basic. we installed a single zone mini-split in a split-level in woodbridge last week. pulled a vacuum, it held for a few minutes, released the refrigerant, and two days later the customer says it''s blowing warm. my lead found the liquid line flare at the indoor head leaking. i made that flare. what usually causes a flare to leak, and how do you know a flare is good before you tighten it? i would like to stop guessing on these.', 'hvac', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 8, '2026-08-12T17:33:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('113e3b7f-15f0-5019-afb9-625d06dd088d', '22ef1b2b-8b79-5b08-9ee1-89f53ba0d4d6', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Flare leaks are almost always one of these:
- Cut not square, or not deburred (or deburred so hard the wall got thin)
- Flare nut not on the pipe before you flared it (everyone does it once)
- Wrong flare size, or an off-center flare from a worn tool
- Not torqued to the manufacturer''s spec. Too loose leaks, too tight cracks the flare
- Dirt or a scratch on the flare face

Before you tighten it, look at it: smooth, even, no cracks, sits flat on the cone. Torque wrench and the number from the install manual. Then a nitrogen pressure test and a vacuum on a micron gauge, held long enough to mean something. A few minutes isn''t a decay test.

A callback like this eats the margin on the whole install, so it''s worth getting right.', true, 18, '2026-08-12T19:35:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2d640407-715f-5799-8968-4839ef95e315', '22ef1b2b-8b79-5b08-9ee1-89f53ba0d4d6', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Plumber here, so take it for what it''s worth. My father used to say a flare is a sealing face, not a thread joint. Don''t put pipe dope or tape anywhere near it. I watched a guy do that on a gas flare once and I''m still mad about it.', false, 5, '2026-08-12T22:29:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bc6bd99c-fdb0-5171-b11a-a044edb4f5f6', '22ef1b2b-8b79-5b08-9ee1-89f53ba0d4d6', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'torque wrench. every time. the guys who do flares by feel in july are the ones i see again in august. if you have to redo one, cut it off and flare it fresh, don''t just crank it tighter and hope', false, 2, '2026-08-12T22:46:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('7bd97362-a6d3-51ef-9821-9918cea2c490', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'question', 'Brownstone gas job: why are we still threading black iron?', '1st year. On a brownstone gut reno in Park Slope with my journeyman, running new gas from the meter in the cellar up to the kitchen on the parlor floor. All black iron, threaded, and I''m the one cutting and threading all day lol. The water side of the same job is all press and it goes like 5x faster.

So why not press the gas too? Journeyman just says "not on this job" and "the inspection is the inspection." Is it a code thing in the city, a cost thing, or is he just old school? Not trying to do anything myself, just want to understand what I''m doing.', 'plumbing', 'Brooklyn, NY', 10, '2026-09-21T01:06:44+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('7573527d-546a-5572-acc8-7e58241623de', '7bd97362-a6d3-51ef-9821-9918cea2c490', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different, and gas is where it''s most different. Gas work here has to be done under a licensed master plumber, the workers need their own DOB gas qualification, and the work gets inspected and tested before the utility will turn anything on. A lot of buildings also have periodic gas piping inspections now, so old brownstone lines get looked at much more than they used to.

On press for gas: some press systems are made and listed for gas, and I''ve seen them used. Whether a given job can use one is something I check against the current code and DOB requirements every time. I won''t tell you yes from memory, and your journeyman made that call for this job.

Ask him to show you how he checks a thread. That''s the part worth learning.', true, 24, '2026-09-21T10:01:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('067ef3c5-2c38-5b6f-9107-b15d4419d995', '7bd97362-a6d3-51ef-9821-9918cea2c490', '07676d29-9e30-5e27-b903-f9044b52fe4b', 'jersey side, 2 years in and my boss still won''t let me near gas. i carry the pipe and clean up', false, 2, '2026-09-21T10:20:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('754b8c31-6f70-5d1c-af2a-ad34e7541297', '7bd97362-a6d3-51ef-9821-9918cea2c490', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question: why black iron, or why him and not you? Black iron because that''s what he''s confident will pass on that job. Him because you''re a 1st year and it''s gas. Learn to cut a clean thread. Same deal in Jersey City brownstones.', false, 2, '2026-09-22T02:31:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('31afe3c5-f794-5786-8c83-a46178cb4533', '7bd97362-a6d3-51ef-9821-9918cea2c490', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Jersey side we still thread most gas too, kid. Press is fine when it''s the right listed system and the inspector''s good with it. Your journeyman''s being careful with somebody else''s house on a gas job. That''s the job.', false, 4, '2026-09-26T22:31:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3b8d26fc-5388-5db8-abb4-baa70a1a5fa0', '7bd97362-a6d3-51ef-9821-9918cea2c490', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'update: asked him. he said every press system for gas he''s seen needs its own fittings and jaws and the company doesn''t own them yet lol. so it''s both. he let me stand with him on the pressure test though', false, 2, '2026-09-26T23:06:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'ccf9dc60-958f-5461-ad1b-ad7dd180a037', 'question', 'Plumber says the water pipe bond is pointless now that it''s PEX', 'non union apprentice in brooklyn... we''re on a 3-family townhouse new build in east flatbush. copper water service comes in from the street to the meter, then the plumber ran everything after the meter in PEX. my foreman wants the water bond done a certain way and the plumber is laughing at him, says "it''s all plastic brother, there''s nothing to bond, that''s from the 80s."

my foreman just said "do it anyway." I''d like to actually understand who''s right because they''re both going to ask me to do stuff on this job... is the plumber right that PEX means no water bond? and why does the meter matter at all? thanks in advance', 'electrical', 'Brooklyn, NY', 20, '2026-09-21T22:49:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('7d8c4ba6-b6eb-5333-a5dd-1a1e750acd69', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'following. our shop just clamps to whatever copper is near the panel and calls it a day, now im wondering', false, 2, '2026-09-22T01:25:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('afbc6b73-0c2d-557d-9cd5-06e9671b8f9b', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Two separate questions, and the plumber and your foreman are each answering a different one.

One: is the water service an electrode? If the pipe coming in from the street is metal and in the earth long enough, it counts as a grounding electrode, it gets connected close to where it enters, and the connection can''t depend on the meter, so there''s a jumper around it. If the service is plastic, it isn''t an electrode and you need others.

Two: is there metal water piping inside that has to be bonded? If the inside is all PEX, there may be very little. But a copper service up to the meter is metal piping either way.

You''re in the city, so it''s the NYC Electrical Code with its own amendments, and I inspect in Jersey. Check which code edition applies to your permit, and ask your foreman.', true, 36, '2026-09-22T03:37:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cc04003c-3a76-5267-b5ee-83d4fd4d938e', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different on paper, but the physics is the same. On my townhouse jobs the service comes in copper to the meter, the electrician bonds it near the entry with a jumper around the meter, and after that we go PEX. Nobody argues about it on my jobs.', false, 9, '2026-09-23T00:26:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e4ad87cb-f59a-5c6a-8286-17d8d06499d1', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'My father used to say never cut a water pipe without a jumper on it first. If there''s an open neutral on the street, the current goes looking for a path, and the plumber holding both ends of a cut pipe becomes the path. I keep a jumper cable with two clamps on my truck for exactly this.', false, 5, '2026-09-23T01:04:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c9ffa4e2-50ee-54ac-8f71-ca92e5b620c8', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'wait so if it''s all pex then there''s nothing to bond and the plumber is right? our shop teacher said pex basically killed the water pipe ground. so the plumber kind of has a point', false, 3, '2026-09-23T09:05:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b2fb4fd1-5d59-500f-87f0-9c2b28db4eb9', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', '> pex basically killed the water pipe ground

Partly. It changed what''s there to bond. If there''s no metal water piping, there''s nothing to bond on that system. But on his job the service is copper up to the meter, so that copper is still in play. The answer is always what''s actually in the building, not what someone says is in it.', false, 6, '2026-09-23T09:28:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bda8dca5-2362-5748-b599-4bbc7a335118', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Whatever the answer on paper, treat that pipe as possibly energized until you''ve proven otherwise. I''ve watched a meter get swapped in an occupied building with no jumper on and the plumber got bit. A jumper and gloves cost nothing. Stay safe.', false, 4, '2026-09-23T10:46:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f5b18051-f355-573f-8073-178796cf08b8', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question: who''s right, or who has to do it? On my jobs the bond is the electrician''s. My part is not removing it, and putting a jumper on before I cut anything.', false, 3, '2026-09-24T01:22:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0910bcd2-fdac-5374-bef0-1c7dd723244b', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, in the high-rises it''s the same story, just bigger. Bonding on the water risers, the gas, the steel. Nobody on my job touches a bond without the foreman knowing.', false, 3, '2026-09-24T02:00:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6b777b55-a9ef-538e-a201-b4cc4a8bf89c', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'ccf9dc60-958f-5461-ad1b-ad7dd180a037', 'ok this is making more sense... so the plumber is half right? the pex isn''t anything to bond but the copper service before the meter still is. thanks for the patience lol', false, 1, '2026-09-24T09:29:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ee8dc565-68b4-5cee-86c1-e7b38035148d', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Half right is how most job-site arguments end up, kid. Tell the plumber to put a jumper across before he swaps that meter, and tell your foreman where the bond is so nobody "cleans it up" later. That''s the job.', false, 3, '2026-09-24T23:16:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('641a1659-8c7c-555b-8e03-b252aa4550f1', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'Apex grad here. We were taught the clamp goes on the street side, within the first few feet of where the pipe enters the building, not on some random pipe near the panel. Appreciate everyone explaining the jumper part, that one we didn''t really cover.', false, 2, '2026-09-25T03:40:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cd8af30d-36e1-5391-9ae6-e84ffb68fed9', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly I see the flip side of this down the shore. After Sandy a lot of houses got repiped in PEX and the old water bond got left clamped to a stub of copper going nowhere. Looks official, does nothing.', false, 3, '2026-09-28T00:15:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e54895fe-a7b7-5ec4-9860-f5c41b716d87', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'edit to my earlier post: asked my boss. he said we clamp the service copper near where it comes in, and he just bought the plumbers a jumper lol. so "whatever copper is near the panel" was me not paying attention', false, 1, '2026-09-28T02:38:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('48480c4b-85cd-5eee-ac4d-5c3c68af71cd', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', '164f7cb1-65cc-51f3-b008-aac80476859c', 'Career switcher in Ozone Park here. idk if this is a dumb question but what about the gas pipe, brother? Does that get bonded too or is that a different thing?', false, 2, '2026-09-28T12:20:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('52f6d055-25a5-5114-ba3a-4e1036e11dfa', 'cae6798b-a594-5762-98a9-6e03dc07c3a2', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'Gas is its own question. Metal gas piping gets bonded too, and the yellow flexible gas tubing has its own bonding requirements from the manufacturer and the code. In the city I let the electrician and the inspector settle exactly how. Gas bonding is not a place to get creative.', false, 6, '2026-09-29T00:28:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('bbb065a4-9755-5b66-92a5-bc2ea9cc597b', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'question', 'Set screw or compression EMT fittings? Our instructor won''t just say', 'Ok so context, I''m in a trade program in Queens, senior year, we''re doing conduit right now and I''m the kid who actually likes bending (hence the name). We''ve been using set screw connectors and couplings on everything in the shop. Today the instructor handed out compression fittings for the "outdoor" mockup, and when I asked when you use which, he said "when the job tells you." Which is not an answer.

Is it just wet vs dry? Is compression better everywhere and set screw is just cheaper? And what do you use in concrete? Thanks in advance, I just want to understand it before I''m on a real job looking stupid.', 'electrical', 'Brooklyn, NY', 15, '2026-09-29T02:30:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('810767f4-e871-5950-911b-49c4c73c1428', 'bbb065a4-9755-5b66-92a5-bc2ea9cc597b', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Your instructor is right, but here''s the longer version. Set screw fittings are generally for dry locations. Wet and damp locations, outdoors, anywhere water can get in, you want fittings listed for that use, which usually means raintight compression. Embedded in concrete, you need fittings listed as concrete-tight. The listing on the box tells you where it''s allowed, so read it.

Field side: compression costs more and takes longer, and a nut that wasn''t tightened will pull apart. Set screws strip if you lean on them. On our data center jobs it''s set screw inside the building and compression for anything outdoors or on the roof. Stay safe, and enjoy the bending. It''s a skill people pay for.', true, 16, '2026-09-30T01:50:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7feb816e-dc43-5b24-8a3c-71a91dae3de4', 'bbb065a4-9755-5b66-92a5-bc2ea9cc597b', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Plumber here. Compression fittings are my whole world and they leak if you don''t tighten them. Apparently it''s the same idea for you guys.', false, 3, '2026-09-30T09:15:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('74804d40-d565-5b42-ae1b-21cbe724397e', 'bbb065a4-9755-5b66-92a5-bc2ea9cc597b', '97f0c7e0-52b2-5ed3-badd-056a31d2b427', '1st year out of vo-tech in jersey. we did a whole porch in set screw and the inspector made us redo it in raintight. so yeah wet vs dry is real. does anybody actually use concrete tight on residential?', false, 5, '2026-09-30T16:25:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5efcc0b2-a7f1-5dbb-8fd0-84fc1b927f26', 'bbb065a4-9755-5b66-92a5-bc2ea9cc597b', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'Our shop teacher at the vo-tech says the same thing as yours. Read the box. We literally got quizzed on box labels.', false, 2, '2026-09-30T20:42:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4fef0590-a9a3-5a56-b761-7901272baf6b', 'bbb065a4-9755-5b66-92a5-bc2ea9cc597b', 'cbe525cf-5b87-54d7-b315-7c60d722e874', 'sorry, plumbing guy on staten island, but why emt outdoors at all and not pvc? is that a cost thing or a code thing', false, 1, '2026-10-01T01:28:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b74bb205-5ff1-58ff-8a4b-26de497cee92', 'bbb065a4-9755-5b66-92a5-bc2ea9cc597b', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly down the shore I run a lot of PVC outdoors because salt air eats steel. EMT outside works with the right fittings, it just rusts near the ocean. Depends on the job and the spec. And to the other question, yes, concrete-tight on residential when there''s conduit in a slab, garages mostly.', false, 1, '2026-10-01T02:26:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('07f88e82-439f-5549-af16-bfadeaa9cd64', 'bbb065a4-9755-5b66-92a5-bc2ea9cc597b', '68fc283f-e408-5f1b-b3d2-1284762d935d', 'This is the answer I wanted. Read the listing, wet vs dry, concrete tight in concrete, and the beach eats everything. Bringing box labels to class tomorrow lol', false, 3, '2026-10-01T02:51:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('9dcaaeb9-8a68-5185-8e05-477fa957c694', '9fe65554-dd4f-5c8b-9708-65d0c765a948', 'question', 'swapped one hallway switch and now the light only works from one end', 'plumbing guy here so go easy. my mom''s hallway in long branch has a light switch at both ends. one switch was cracked so I bought a new one at the hardware store, breaker off, swapped it wire for wire (I thought). now the light only works from the new switch when the other one is in one position, and sometimes not at all. did I buy the wrong switch or wire it wrong? idk why it would care which screw. also is this a call-an-electrician thing at this point

edit: it was the dark screw thing. thanks', 'electrical', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 2, '2026-09-26T15:18:43+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('167c49e6-ee4d-5f28-a3b8-33c93ce65a9b', '9dcaaeb9-8a68-5185-8e05-477fa957c694', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly this is the most common 3-way mistake there is, don''t feel bad. A 3-way has one darker screw (the common) and two lighter ones (the travelers). Your new switch probably has the common in a different spot than the old one, so the wire that was on the old common ended up on a traveler screw. Breaker off, verify dead with a tester, then find that wire. If you didn''t mark it, that''s where it gets harder. If the wiring is cloth or crumbly, stop and call someone. Long Branch has plenty of hallways like that.', false, 4, '2026-09-26T22:06:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4e2aaa54-78c9-5bac-a8c3-884d115f70fc', '9dcaaeb9-8a68-5185-8e05-477fa957c694', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'To your second question: if you can''t sort it out with the power off and a tester, that''s the point to call an electrician. Next time, put a piece of tape on the wire from the dark screw before anything comes off.', false, 4, '2026-09-27T02:05:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b7e1b0f3-c9d3-58ec-9232-dfc6e0060c88', '9dcaaeb9-8a68-5185-8e05-477fa957c694', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'same thing happened to me in my apartment in deptford. it was the common. took me an hour. appreciate it, learned something too', false, 1, '2026-09-27T02:51:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('cfc0653d-cd51-5028-894a-3c1d3dab1b9a', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'question', 'what does a 4-way switch actually do in the middle?', 'UA 1st year, plumbing, so this is pure curiosity. The electrician on our job (commercial bathrooms in a building in Montclair, long corridor outside them) was explaining the corridor lights at lunch. 3-way at each end, I followed that from the other thread on here. Then he said there''s a 4-way in the middle and it "flips the travelers" and he lost me. Flips them how? Why can''t you just put a third 3-way in the middle?', 'electrical', 'Essex County, NJ', 3, '2026-08-14T03:51:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('90b6df32-dd16-5b7a-a4dc-0d43736bf73a', 'cfc0653d-cd51-5028-894a-3c1d3dab1b9a', '95c564b5-4a82-5ef3-b8b5-c0622870a9bc', 'IBEW 2nd year here... the way my foreman explained it: both travelers come into the 4-way, and the 4-way either passes them straight through or crosses them over, so traveler A goes out on B and B goes out on A. Flipping it swaps which traveler is live at the far end... so any switch can change the light. A 3-way only has one common and two travelers, it can''t do the swap, which is why the middle one has to be a 4-way. You can put as many 4-ways in a row as you want between the two 3-ways.', true, 6, '2026-08-14T10:16:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('781c8970-969d-5cdf-b03f-7d5645ae0d63', 'cfc0653d-cd51-5028-894a-3c1d3dab1b9a', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly that''s one of the better explanations I''ve seen. Draw it: two 3-ways on the ends, the 4-way in the middle, and trace it with your finger in every position.', false, 3, '2026-08-14T15:36:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6d4ef16a-e385-53b9-a30d-8139db678043', 'cfc0653d-cd51-5028-894a-3c1d3dab1b9a', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'One thing to add for when you see these in the field: check the 4-way''s instructions for which screws are the pair in and which are the pair out. They aren''t always laid out the same, and mixing them up gives you exactly the "works sometimes" complaint.', false, 2, '2026-08-16T16:37:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9562f9a5-85fc-54cf-a86e-3778d1a8ea99', 'cfc0653d-cd51-5028-894a-3c1d3dab1b9a', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'ok the crossing over thing finally clicked. kind of like a diverter on a manifold, sort of. thanks guys, back to toilets', false, 1, '2026-08-16T22:07:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('986de375-3a71-5dec-8c24-c9f5142d5a47', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'question', 're-identifying the white wire on a switch loop, is tape enough', 'residential remodel in manahawkin. old part of the house has a ceiling light fed at the fixture, with a 2-wire cable down to the switch. my boss wraps black tape on the white at both ends and moves on. in school they mentioned something about needing a neutral at switches now. is the tape enough on an existing loop, and does the newer code mean we have to rewire it when we touch it?', 'electrical', 'Ocean County, NJ', 3, '2026-08-20T01:06:59+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0bf3d3b4-3019-5625-8889-faecbc2b0d04', '986de375-3a71-5dec-8c24-c9f5142d5a47', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Re-identifying the white with tape or another permanent marking, wherever it''s visible and accessible, is the long-standing way to use it as a hot in a switch loop. In a loop the white is supposed to be the supply going to the switch, not the return to the light.

The neutral-at-the-switch requirement applies to switch locations in the code editions that have it, with exceptions. Whether touching an existing loop pulls you into it depends on the edition and the scope of the permit, so check which code edition is in effect and ask your inspector before you assume.', false, 2, '2026-08-20T22:02:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('78d10081-5399-5001-b7b9-bba38848d503', '986de375-3a71-5dec-8c24-c9f5142d5a47', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly on remodels, if the wall''s already open we pull a new 14/3. Costs you ten minutes and the next guy who wants a smart switch there will thank you.', false, 6, '2026-08-21T00:30:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('ee8ca3c6-8849-50c9-8269-e632dca00172', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'question', 'Prewar Bronx building: fixture is hot with both 3-ways off', 'Working non-union in the Bronx, mostly apartment renovations in prewar buildings. Today we were replacing a hallway fixture in a unit in Kingsbridge. Both 3-way switches off, and I checked the fixture with my non-contact tester anyway and it lit up on both wires. My mechanic checked with a meter, said there was voltage to ground on both conductors, then said "it''s a Carter, leave it and call the office."

I have never heard of a Carter system. We did 3-ways at Apex and none of this matched. What is it, and why would both wires be hot with the light off? Appreciate any explanation.

edit: nobody touched anything live. He made us stop and the office is sending someone to look at it.', 'electrical', 'Bronx, NY', 15, '2026-08-09T18:02:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('6966e06d-748d-5e8c-b96b-fe24e4509922', 'ee8ca3c6-8849-50c9-8269-e632dca00172', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Brother, your mechanic did exactly right. A Carter system is an old way of wiring 3-ways where the travelers carry the hot and the neutral, and each switch picks which one goes to its side of the light. Light''s on when one side gets hot and the other gets neutral. Light''s off when both sides get the same thing, and that can be both hot. So "off" doesn''t mean dead.

It''s been prohibited for new work for a long time, I couldn''t tell you the year. You still run into it in old buildings up here. You don''t fix it by swapping a switch. It gets rewired properly, under a permit, by whoever the office sends.', true, 5, '2026-08-09T21:54:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2a615c67-9ce0-56fe-9187-20984ee6a507', 'ee8ca3c6-8849-50c9-8269-e632dca00172', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Good catch testing a fixture you''d been told was off. That''s the whole lesson. I inspect in Jersey, not the city, so I won''t speak to the NYC code, but I''ve seen a couple of these in very old houses at the shore. Same answer: rewire it, don''t patch it.', false, 3, '2026-08-18T00:58:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4901c9c8-611f-547e-9ddf-aecfe31c85c2', 'ee8ca3c6-8849-50c9-8269-e632dca00172', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'This is why we test before we touch on every job, even when somebody swears it''s off. Verify with a meter you''ve just checked on a known live source. Stay safe.', false, 3, '2026-08-19T01:30:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8e1427f9-4f5e-54bf-ae82-0efa99393e32', 'ee8ca3c6-8849-50c9-8269-e632dca00172', '925c5853-2eed-5ea8-b420-8c4feaf88498', 'I''m just starting out as a career switcher and I would have assumed off meant off. Glad I read this before my first really old house.', false, 1, '2026-08-19T03:01:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c99c904c-accb-575a-9f05-c49479941688', 'ee8ca3c6-8849-50c9-8269-e632dca00172', '0417a72d-2e53-5b0b-98c3-929f1e404a87', 'Appreciate it, all of you. Going to look up the diagram tonight so I recognize it next time.', false, 4, '2026-08-19T03:06:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', '6b3a1896-cd39-5ae1-8351-8817f445313d', 'question', 'smart switch needs a neutral, can i just use the bare ground?', 'plumbing guy, mostly demo right now lol. my mom wants a smart switch for the porch light at her house in lawrence. got it out of the box and it wants a neutral. switch box has a black, a white taped black, and a bare copper. guy at the store said "some people use the ground as the neutral, it''s fine, it only draws like nothing." is that ok or no. not doing anything till somebody tells me', 'electrical', 'Mercer County, NJ', 9, '2026-08-19T00:49:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('180ace50-3593-5e2f-a084-80d488469a3d', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'No. Don''t. The equipment ground is not a current-carrying conductor. It''s there to carry fault current long enough to trip the breaker. Put normal current on it and every grounded thing on that circuit, metal boxes, fixture housings, appliance frames, carries a little current all the time, and if that ground path ever opens, those parts can sit at line voltage with nobody knowing. Small current doesn''t make it fine.

What you described, a black and a white taped black, sounds like a switch loop: no neutral in that box. Your options are a smart switch listed to work without a neutral, a smart bulb in the fixture, or a new cable with a neutral to that box. Breaker off and tested dead before anything comes apart.', true, 15, '2026-08-19T02:36:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('18a03dc7-4f35-5e08-b36e-a6edf93bef4e', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'honestly people do it all the time, my cousin did it in his whole house. a smart switch pulls a few milliamps, nothing is going to happen. no inspector is ever coming back to look at a porch switch', false, 3, '2026-08-19T03:40:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9b787459-c182-5ef9-9699-b936ae966e60', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly I''ve been on service calls where the "few milliamps" guy did his whole house, and we found it because the GFCIs and AFCIs kept tripping. It''s not about the inspector coming back. It''s about whoever touches that fixture someday when the ground''s loose. Don''t.', false, 10, '2026-08-19T10:06:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f1025e93-7c19-5d8e-888c-6e0929538a95', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Agree with both of them. And whatever you end up doing, kill the breaker and verify dead with a tester you''ve checked. Porch lights sometimes share an outdoor circuit with things you wouldn''t expect. Stay safe.', false, 3, '2026-08-19T15:45:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a3a43978-0cd2-5576-8510-21cb5ca4cc94', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fwiw the no-neutral smart switches are a real product, listed, and they work by trickling a tiny bit of current through the bulb instead of through the ground. downside is some leds flicker or glow with them. low voltage guy here, we run into this all the time on retrofits', false, 3, '2026-08-20T00:48:56+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d2a0f659-6823-557b-a3ba-e2d84ad296e1', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Sorry if this is a dumb question, but how would you even tell the white is taped because it''s a switch loop and not just somebody''s random tape?', false, 1, '2026-08-25T16:08:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dbe8e51e-2e63-568f-a514-1d8af6ea2769', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Not dumb. Breaker off, open the fixture box and look. In a switch loop the white from the switch cable is spliced to a hot, not to the other whites. If you can''t tell, assume it isn''t a neutral.', false, 7, '2026-08-26T00:17:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d21cd12b-0fcc-5483-8fa3-f5738ac1d4b3', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'UA here, and this is the same conversation we have about tying a vent into a drain because "it works." works until it doesn''t', false, 1, '2026-08-26T00:48:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9be4b714-8b84-58ec-a7f6-5d8fcc8c94a7', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', '8498b67e-8832-52a9-854b-bbe6514f03b3', 'smart bulb is the easy answer. we had them at the bar i used to work at, zero wiring, never had a problem', false, 4, '2026-08-26T01:09:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f661fc08-a065-580e-8e44-2237610c7bd3', 'd6bcd143-986b-53aa-a041-d4e3b55794de', '6b3a1896-cd39-5ae1-8351-8817f445313d', 'update: got the no neutral one that says it''s listed for that. my foreman''s brother is an electrician, he came by and put it in. porch light works from the phone. mom happy. thanks', false, 3, '2026-08-26T03:46:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('971782f2-b9f6-5e77-83da-ed8d2371098a', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'question', 'LED bulbs on the basement stairs glow when the switches are off', 'Helping my uncle again this weekend. His basement stairs have a light with a switch at the top and the bottom. He swapped the old bulbs for LEDs and now with both switches off they glow really faint, like a nightlight. He says it''s cheap bulbs and to ignore it. I''m a plumbing kid so I don''t really know electrical, but it bugs me. Is that a bulb thing or is something wired wrong? Should I be worried about it', 'electrical', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 8, '2026-09-16T00:32:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('fc10d28c-0806-53be-aae4-57bb3ef8367a', '971782f2-b9f6-5e77-83da-ed8d2371098a', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'had this in my apartment, swapped brands and it went away. so cheap bulbs, or was something else going on with mine too?', false, 1, '2026-09-16T02:49:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f48bd0c3-98af-5907-ad21-b2f8d0b41b9f', '971782f2-b9f6-5e77-83da-ed8d2371098a', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Could be the bulbs, could be the wiring, and it''s worth knowing which. The common harmless cause: on a 3-way the two travelers run side by side in the same cable, and on a long run a little voltage couples from one to the other. An incandescent never shows it. An LED needs so little that it glows. Lighted switches do the same thing.

The cause you want to rule out is the switches breaking the neutral instead of the hot. Then the fixture is still hot when it''s off, and somebody changing a bulb gets a surprise. Have someone qualified check it with a meter. If it''s coupling, a different bulb or a small device made for this usually fixes it. Stay safe.', false, 8, '2026-09-16T03:05:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('71cc492f-0c5b-5df6-bcfc-f2edaea90e56', '971782f2-b9f6-5e77-83da-ed8d2371098a', 'c2dab74b-64e9-5d5a-a3d4-8fef7f96548d', 'my parents had this in Montclair, turned out to be the lighted switch at the bottom of the stairs. took it out, glow gone', false, 1, '2026-09-16T09:04:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dc9dfcca-fc7a-542a-a4d2-539cde91807c', '971782f2-b9f6-5e77-83da-ed8d2371098a', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question? "Should I be worried" is the real one, and the answer is: not until somebody checks it. Have your uncle get an electrician to look. It''s a short visit.', false, 7, '2026-09-16T11:10:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '0e1f3b61-0ba4-56b9-9844-cea31e8e2deb', 'question', 'Bedroom AFCI at my dad''s place trips every couple nights. Just swap it?', 'Sorry if this is a dumb question, I''m about a month in as a helper in Brick. My dad had his panel replaced in the spring by an electrician (not my boss) and now the breaker for the back bedroom trips every two or three nights. Always at night, sometimes with nothing on but a fan and a phone charger. It''s one of the breakers with the test button.

My dad''s answer is "you work for an electrician now, put a regular breaker in." I said I''d ask first. The house is a 60s ranch, some of the wiring is original. Is the breaker just bad? Is it the fan? What would you even check?', 'electrical', 'Ocean County, NJ', 7, '2026-09-18T10:11:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('55353483-a0e8-590e-8934-de194b7d977f', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'Not an expert, I''m in vo-tech, but in our class we learned breakers trip when the load is too high. If it''s a 15 amp, maybe it just needs to be a 20 amp so it stops tripping. That seems like the simplest thing to try first.', false, 1, '2026-09-18T14:18:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c32c6df6-f059-506c-b4b7-1af8afbbe616', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Please don''t. The breaker size is set by the wire, not by what you want to plug in. If that bedroom is wired in 14 gauge, a 20 amp breaker lets the wire overheat before it trips, and that''s how fires start. And a breaker that trips with a fan and a phone charger on isn''t tripping on load anyway.', false, 2, '2026-09-19T15:08:50+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8f2c9464-546e-5f58-a25b-933e2b45851a', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'Understood, thank you for the correction. I didn''t realize the wire was what set it.', false, 1, '2026-09-19T16:29:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8b4f9634-d7ad-5a59-b44f-b596eddf059e', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly the first generation of these nuisance tripped like crazy and I cursed them on every Sandy rebuild. The newer ones are a lot better, but I still see the odd one that just doesn''t like a certain fan motor or treadmill.', false, 2, '2026-09-19T22:08:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4c40564c-1ba8-521d-b996-166c96cfa2fe', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Thiago''s right that the early ones had problems. What I see now, most trips are telling you something real. Field version of what I''d check, in order:

Is it a combination type that also senses ground faults? Many are. Then a neutral from that bedroom shared with another circuit somewhere, or a neutral touching ground in a box, will trip it, and a 60s ranch that''s been added onto is exactly where that hides. Next, a loose connection or a backstabbed receptacle on the run. Then damaged cable: a nail, a staple driven too tight. Then the loads. Unplug the fan for a week and see.

And don''t put a regular breaker in. That panel was just replaced under a permit, so call the electrician who did it back. It''s very likely theirs to solve.', true, 10, '2026-09-19T23:03:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e1a13192-7b4f-5334-9550-9444c8a9df76', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', 'b0196b88-78da-56e7-a196-a68a24255d52', 'hvac not electrical, but my house in toms river did this and it turned out to be the window ac. new ac, no more trips. thanks in advance for not laughing', false, 2, '2026-09-19T23:46:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3f07e673-2f99-5339-9462-d4b26a6cf88a', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'plumbing guy in deptford. question for the electricians: how would he even find a shared neutral, is it just opening every box? appreciate it', false, 1, '2026-09-20T01:13:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('caf9bf0a-1c80-5b52-ad5e-16f0cc7a0cea', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Pretty much, plus some tricks. Circuit off, look at how the neutrals land in the panel, open the boxes on that run and the ones next to it. In an old ranch you''re also in the attic looking for junction boxes nobody remembers. It''s a couple of hours, not a couple of minutes.', false, 7, '2026-09-23T01:35:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c7b9a9e0-a33b-54a1-83ed-587b31b978a6', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'service guy here. most of these i find a neutral tied together in a box in the attic or the basement. idk why people did that, saved a wire nut i guess', false, 3, '2026-09-23T02:09:27+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9c79c7c8-0c0b-5ee3-b3d4-0ed1a4be61a6', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'So this one time in AC... hotel room kept tripping and it was the guest running a hair dryer and a space heater on the same outlet lol. Not saying that''s your dad, but ask what''s plugged in back there.', false, 3, '2026-09-24T00:23:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('801f24a4-d2c1-53ae-b173-61a92a7c1e18', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '73081253-0d5b-5c2b-8196-6cb9a7bf4f61', 'sorry if dumb but does the breaker tell you anything about why it tripped? some of ours have lights that blink after', false, 1, '2026-09-24T10:11:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2f8a27ad-a1fe-5535-a170-3a8dd87502cf', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', 'cf6e05ac-e35b-5a04-98bd-da5715daa930', 'yeah some of them do, depends on the brand. there''s a code on the label or the manufacturer sheet, like arc vs ground fault. look it up for whatever''s in his panel before you start opening boxes', false, 6, '2026-09-24T12:04:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7c0e456b-6e57-57df-a382-fa24e204dc0f', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '0e1f3b61-0ba4-56b9-9844-cea31e8e2deb', 'update: unplugged the fan all week and it still tripped, so dad gave in and called the electrician back. He found the bedroom neutral tied in with the hallway circuit''s neutral in a junction box in the attic, from some old add-on. Separated them, no trips since. Mom says thanks too, she was tired of resetting it.', false, 2, '2026-10-03T11:29:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4e22de85-d6f7-5826-a485-4792d63fb100', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'There it is. Shared neutral in the attic. Good on you for asking before swapping the breaker.', false, 5, '2026-10-03T14:54:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a7a473db-a008-5f9d-99c2-b553b39cb000', 'b2f93ab7-f9f5-5d5c-a76a-bc6b3584d3af', '07e07098-eb41-5892-8d05-db2a210fb5e8', 'saving this one... my foreman always says the breaker is just the messenger. appreciate it', false, 2, '2026-10-03T18:01:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('2dedca72-dc1f-5133-8a20-a7b6d68b6c46', '15a35d13-ce46-5ce0-8883-c803eafa1f49', 'question', 'Vacuum pump keeps tripping a bedroom AFCI on install day', 'End of my first week at the new job, sorry if this is obvious to everyone. We were doing a ductless head in a back bedroom in Washington Township and I plugged the vacuum pump into the bedroom outlet. Tripped the breaker within a minute. Reset it, tripped again. Lead told me to run a cord from the garage instead and it was fine.

Homeowner was annoyed and asked me if something''s wrong with her house, and I definately had no idea what to say. Is it the pump, the breaker, or her wiring? And what do you tell the customer in that moment without sounding like an idiot?', 'hvac', 'Camden County, NJ', 10, '2026-10-04T18:27:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('bd830f4f-9e0e-5b31-9088-ea8808c6026a', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'question', 'how does an AFCI actually tell a bad arc from a light switch?', 'ok so last year in class we covered AFCIs and the teacher said they detect "dangerous arcing." but every time you flip a switch or plug something in there''s a little arc, and a brushed motor like a drill arcs constantly. so how does the breaker know which arc is the bad one? is it just guessing off some pattern? because from what I hear on here they trip on random stuff and miss other stuff, so I''m skeptical. also the teacher couldn''t really answer it so here I am', 'electrical', 'Mercer County, NJ', 3, '2026-07-27T02:14:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('3656d1fb-7181-5e40-a827-69f3350c079d', 'bd830f4f-9e0e-5b31-9088-ea8808c6026a', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Good question, and the skepticism is reasonable. In plain terms: the breaker has electronics that watch the current waveform for the signature of a dangerous arc, the erratic high-frequency noise and the pattern a loose or damaged conductor makes over time, as opposed to the brief, predictable arc of a switch or the steady noise of a motor. Combination types look for arcing in series, like a loose connection, and from line to neutral or ground, like damaged insulation. Many also sense ground faults.

It is pattern recognition, so it isn''t perfect. Some motors and electronics look suspicious to some models. That''s part of why the designs keep getting updated.', false, 2, '2026-07-27T22:37:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a67dc698-54b2-5abc-8106-e5f734c644fe', 'bd830f4f-9e0e-5b31-9088-ea8808c6026a', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Plumbing guy, but that was a better explanation than I''ve gotten from two years of listening to electricians complain about them. Thanks for asking it.', false, 7, '2026-07-28T01:12:29+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('b6ecab53-8a80-5f37-b4e8-c7fcc565dab6', '2f048a7b-273e-574a-911a-7232a6136051', 'question', 'new lower element in an electric water heater and the breaker trips instantly', 'sorry if this is a dumb one, 4 years in and i mostly do gas tanks. condo in north bergen, electric 40 gallon, no hot water. tested and the lower element was bad so i swapped it. drained it, new element in, filled it up, turned the breaker back on and it tripped right away. reset, tripped again. didn''t touch anything else. is the new element bad out of the box or did i do something', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 5, '2026-09-16T00:50:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('38c6e28f-95d0-5ad5-afe1-7701ffcc0f00', 'b6ecab53-8a80-5f37-b4e8-c7fcc565dab6', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'First question, kid: did you open a hot faucet and let it run until the water came out solid, no spitting, before the breaker went on? If the top of that tank had air in it, the upper element runs dry and dies, and sometimes takes the breaker with it.

Second: an instant trip usually means a short, not a weak element. Breaker off, verify dead at the heater, pull the wires off the element and check it with your meter. Across the two terminals you should read some ohms, roughly 10 to 17 depending on the wattage. From either terminal to the tank should read open. While you''re in there, look hard at the wires you pushed back under that cover. That''s the job.', true, 12, '2026-09-16T02:59:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c583ca3f-7b59-51a4-b233-048132e83c08', 'b6ecab53-8a80-5f37-b4e8-c7fcc565dab6', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Agree with all of that. From the electrical side, a straight short to ground trips any breaker instantly, and the usual spot after an element swap is a conductor pinched by the cover or nicked on the bracket. Check the insulation on both leads before you close it up.', false, 7, '2026-09-16T22:55:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('857ec699-f2cb-55eb-b0cd-6d64a128e6e9', 'b6ecab53-8a80-5f37-b4e8-c7fcc565dab6', '0b536e7d-7d15-52d5-ae52-959dc9ae15ec', 'burned up my first element that way, breaker went on before the tank was full. seconds and done. my foreman makes me bleed every tank now', false, 1, '2026-09-16T23:23:20+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5b521d78-7a88-5712-8080-d680d38b8960', 'b6ecab53-8a80-5f37-b4e8-c7fcc565dab6', '2f048a7b-273e-574a-911a-7232a6136051', 'update: it was the wire. the lower lead got jammed against the edge of the bracket when i stuffed the insulation back in, cut right through. new piece of wire, works fine. element was ok the whole time', false, 2, '2026-09-17T10:21:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('735a7aed-d120-5d21-9926-94d322f4df7f', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'question', 'New dishwasher trips the GFCI on the dry cycle. On us or the electrician?', '1st year, Local 1. Last week my journeyman had me do the water and drain on a dishwasher in a Bay Ridge apartment, the electrician did the circuit. Customer called back: it runs through wash and rinse fine, then the GFCI trips on the heated dry. Electrician says it''s the appliance. Customer''s blaming us because we were the last ones under there lol.

Is there any way a water connection trips a GFCI, or is this not our problem?', 'plumbing', 'Brooklyn, NY', 9, '2026-09-30T09:13:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('38a2570e-603c-579a-ba6d-44cc62fc88ba', '735a7aed-d120-5d21-9926-94d322f4df7f', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'It can absolutely be your problem without being your circuit. A GFCI trips when current leaks to ground. Two common causes on a new dishwasher: the heating element leaking current once it gets hot, which is the appliance, and water getting into the junction box under the front, which can be a weeping supply fitting right above it.', false, 2, '2026-10-01T00:41:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('92cc9e96-680f-5b29-ab31-88b006473011', '735a7aed-d120-5d21-9926-94d322f4df7f', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'had a callback like this in cherry hill... the elbow on the supply was weeping onto everything, you couldn''t see it unless the kick plate was off and it was running', false, 1, '2026-10-01T03:46:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9dca6799-a05c-568e-a413-78f3dabce666', '735a7aed-d120-5d21-9926-94d322f4df7f', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly the dry-cycle detail is the clue. Heat makes a failing element leak, and heat plus a little water in a box makes a GFCI unhappy. Look at your fitting first because it''s free: dry the whole area, run a cycle with the kick plate off, flashlight on the connection. If it''s bone dry and it still trips on heat, it''s the appliance and the customer calls the manufacturer. Either way, nobody bypasses the GFCI.', true, 18, '2026-10-02T02:56:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1726053f-5882-5537-b70c-8492344ce0af', '735a7aed-d120-5d21-9926-94d322f4df7f', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'My uncle tapes the threaded side of the dishwasher elbow (never the compression side) and checks it with a paper towel after the first fill. The paper towel shows drips you can''t see.', false, 2, '2026-10-02T10:16:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('efdde473-06c9-594d-b1d8-8452d25ab1a3', '735a7aed-d120-5d21-9926-94d322f4df7f', 'cc7452bc-0849-5059-bec8-af72afd6cf73', 'update: went back with my journeyman. elbow was weeping right onto the j-box. redid it, ran two full cycles, no trip. so yeah it was us lol. paper towel trick is going in my bag', false, 2, '2026-10-02T10:49:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('b9ea07ec-a896-5b53-864f-3c3bc86ca60a', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'tip', 'Sump pumps on GFCI: what I tell homeowners after every big storm', 'Every big rain, I hear the same complaint: "the GFCI tripped and my basement flooded, why does code make me do this?" Here''s how I explain it.

Current code editions want GFCI protection on basement receptacles, and the old exception that let a single dedicated sump receptacle skip it went away several cycles back. Check which code edition is in effect for your permit, because an older install may have been legal when it went in.

A GFCI that trips on a sump pump is usually telling you something. Pumps sit in water, and as they age the windings and cords leak current. That leak is exactly the thing that kills people in wet basements.

So the answer I give isn''t "remove the GFCI." It''s: put a high-water alarm in the pit, think hard about a battery backup pump, test the GFCI and the pump before storm season, and replace a pump that keeps tripping it. Not legal advice, just how I''d look at it after too many flooded basements.', 'electrical', 'Ocean County, NJ', 23, '2026-10-01T22:09:18+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('804a7c13-aa45-50f4-a7f2-2f57c2d3b4fe', 'b9ea07ec-a896-5b53-864f-3c3bc86ca60a', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly I''m torn on this one and I''ll say it. After Ida I had three customers with flooded basements, and every one was a tripped GFCI on the sump. I install it the way the code says, but I push the alarm and the backup pump hard, because a GFCI by itself is a bad plan in a basement that floods.', false, 3, '2026-10-02T02:05:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('84e7ff10-5947-5118-ace3-131336e6a38c', 'b9ea07ec-a896-5b53-864f-3c3bc86ca60a', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Fair, and we''re not that far apart. The GFCI isn''t the plan, it''s the protection. The alarm and the backup pump are the plan.', false, 1, '2026-10-02T03:57:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7bd3e6aa-fa77-512c-b262-d8f290f283ba', 'b9ea07ec-a896-5b53-864f-3c3bc86ca60a', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Plumber''s side: half the pumps I pull that were tripping GFCIs have a cord that''s been sitting in water or a motor on its way out. Replace the pump, check the check valve while you''re there, and the trips go away. A good pump tripping a good GFCI is rare.', false, 3, '2026-10-03T12:14:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8c549482-7988-5c5f-b333-bdd4bb696d5c', 'b9ea07ec-a896-5b53-864f-3c3bc86ca60a', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'As a student, may I ask why not put the sump on its own hardwired circuit with no receptacle at all? Wouldn''t that avoid the GFCI question entirely?', false, 3, '2026-10-03T15:01:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ea625228-d04f-5b81-81ec-864d7cbaad9a', 'b9ea07ec-a896-5b53-864f-3c3bc86ca60a', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Good question. Depending on the pump, the code edition and what your local office accepts, hardwiring can change the analysis, but most pumps are cord-and-plug so they can be swapped fast at 2am. Ask the inspector before you plan around it. I wouldn''t treat it as a loophole.', false, 5, '2026-10-03T15:34:25+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('e742905c-25d9-5eaa-b402-206f07cd83fd', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'tip', 'Target superheat needs indoor wet bulb. Students, buy the probe.', 'Every summer a few of my former students come back from their first jobs saying they "checked the superheat" on a piston system and it was fine. Then I ask what their target was and they look at me.

First, superheat by itself is just a number. On a fixed orifice system you compare it to a target, and the target comes from the manufacturer''s chart or a target superheat chart, using indoor wet bulb and outdoor dry bulb.

Second, wet bulb, not dry bulb. Wet bulb tells you how much moisture the coil is dealing with, and that moves the target a lot. A sticky July afternoon in Paterson and a dry day in September want different numbers.

Third, measure the return air at the unit, not in the hallway.

Buy a decent wet bulb probe before you buy the fancy gauges. Ask me how I know which one matters more.', 'hvac', 'Passaic County, NJ', 9, '2026-08-02T14:13:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('45b44c70-fabe-5775-bdae-04f03f856a98', '5ea91175-1b81-51fb-918c-7ad563230535', 'question', 'Should gauges go on every system at a maintenance visit?', 'Night program student here... I''ve been doing a ride-along with a tech this summer through a friend. At every maintenance visit he puts gauges on. My instructor says don''t hook up gauges on a system that''s working unless you have a reason, because you lose refrigerant every time... The tech says you can''t know it''s working without them.

Who''s right? Or is it one of those "depends" answers... I''d like to understand the reasoning so I don''t pick up a bad habit early. Thanks in advance.', 'hvac', 'Camden County, NJ', 5, '2026-08-13T01:38:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('85659693-8c18-5517-9687-6b5b38d19189', '45b44c70-fabe-5775-bdae-04f03f856a98', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Your instructor is closer, in my opinion:
- Every connection is a chance for a leak, a contaminated port, or a valve core that doesn''t reseat
- On a small system, what''s left in the hoses is a real share of the charge if you don''t handle it properly
- You can learn a lot without them: temperature split, line temperatures, amp draw, airflow, a clean coil
- When those tell you something''s off, then connect, with low-loss fittings

Plenty of good techs disagree with me on this, and that''s fine. Just have a reason for every connection.', false, 6, '2026-08-13T03:05:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('3cd32409-4c5c-5fcb-8038-3e9dc2a3be57', '45b44c70-fabe-5775-bdae-04f03f856a98', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'I''m one of the ones who disagrees lol... I don''t put hoses on every visit, but I do put clamp-on temp probes and wireless pressure probes on most systems. Low loss, and I''d rather see real numbers than guess from a temperature split. So this one time in AC the split looked fine on a rooftop unit and the superheat said it was way short on charge. The split doesn''t tell you everything.', false, 1, '2026-08-13T22:10:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fef38965-e5f9-50da-a01d-94c06bc1401d', '45b44c70-fabe-5775-bdae-04f03f856a98', 'f32d81a7-003f-51fe-bfbf-bf9a8f5e3ca8', 'we put a gauge on every water heater and boiler job, static pressure on the house, takes a minute... is hvac different?', false, 1, '2026-08-14T02:17:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1bad33ff-af96-58ba-916c-0567c2577a39', '45b44c70-fabe-5775-bdae-04f03f856a98', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'he''s asking about refrigerant gauges, not water pressure lol. different thing. on walk-ins i only connect when the box tells me something''s wrong. every connection is a leak waiting for july', false, 4, '2026-08-14T03:02:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('81666fc1-63b2-5b8e-8bd2-5216755296a2', '45b44c70-fabe-5775-bdae-04f03f856a98', '56ebe677-1060-5479-89c5-55faedf03943', 'Taking a night class too and we got told the same thing as your instructor. Interesting that the field guys split on it.', false, 2, '2026-08-14T03:33:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('22701fbb-f3c9-57a2-b434-7c1e0c46e989', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'question', 'where can a condensate pump actually drain in a finished basement', 'ok so long story, we''re doing a furnace and coil swap in a split-level in clifton and the basement is getting finished. right now the condensate pump just dumps into the laundry sink with the tube clipped on the edge. homeowner wants it "hidden," so the contractor finishing the basement asked if we can run it into the washer standpipe or tie it into the sump pit. my lead said "depends" (of course) and that it''s the inspector''s call. what are the normal options and which ones get people in trouble? also does the pump need anything wired to it besides the plug', 'hvac', 'Passaic County, NJ', 4, '2026-08-23T01:28:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('8d8deea0-2c9a-50fd-a388-d82ccd3c9e96', '22701fbb-f3c9-57a2-b434-7c1e0c46e989', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First thing my students forget: condensate is waste, and where it goes is a plumbing code question in your town, so the inspector really is the answer. Second: whatever it drains into, don''t make a direct connection to a drain without an air gap or air break. You don''t want sewer gas coming back up the tube, or a backup pushing into the pump.', false, 8, '2026-08-23T22:51:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bb147edf-38b8-5d25-b218-09a7eef7f9b6', '22701fbb-f3c9-57a2-b434-7c1e0c46e989', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Field version, around here:
- Laundry tub, or a standpipe with an air gap, is the common option and usually accepted. Check locally
- The sump pit gets used a lot and some towns don''t allow it. Ask before you do it
- Never glue it straight into a drain or a vent with no trap and no air gap
- Wire the pump''s safety switch so the AC shuts off if the pump fails. Most pumps have the switch; plenty of installers never connect it
- Leave access. Finished basements bury pumps behind drywall and then it''s a callback

The safety switch is the one that saves the new floor.', true, 22, '2026-08-23T23:34:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8e9731bf-6369-50a0-9dae-133d3599f943', '22701fbb-f3c9-57a2-b434-7c1e0c46e989', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'brother we had one in paterson where the pump was buried inside a soffit, took my lead an hour just to find it. leave it where you can get to it', false, 3, '2026-08-24T01:07:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('363bd9f8-eb80-5f53-8ff7-a35d4bc7131d', '22701fbb-f3c9-57a2-b434-7c1e0c46e989', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'update: inspector was fine with the standpipe with an air gap. we wired the safety switch into the furnace control so the ac stops if the pump dies. contractor is building a little access door. thanks everyone', false, 1, '2026-08-24T02:19:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('58bdaccf-b8e0-5c9d-8e1d-25b43fdfe062', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'question', 'Electrical student: why does the HVAC float switch cut the thermostat wire?', 'Electrical student at the county vo-tech, Nutley. I''ve been shadowing an HVAC tech friend of my dad''s on Saturdays. He put a float switch on an AC drain pan and wired it into the thin thermostat wire, not the power. In class everything we do is 120 or 240, so I asked why not just cut power to the unit. He said "it''s the control side." Can someone explain why it''s done that way, and which wire it goes on?', 'hvac', 'Essex County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-29T09:42:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('4efc328c-dae3-50e4-a7b5-c36ec46fe515', '58bdaccf-b8e0-5c9d-8e1d-25b43fdfe062', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', '"Control side" is the right answer. Here''s why:
- The thermostat wiring is 24 volts and tells the system when to run. Open one wire and the call for cooling stops
- Most of those float switches are made for low-voltage control wiring, not for the line voltage the equipment runs on
- It usually goes in series with the R or the Y, depending on what you want shut down and what the instructions say
- Killing line power can also shut off things you might want running, like the blower

Follow the switch instructions and the equipment''s wiring diagram, not a rule of thumb.', false, 4, '2026-09-29T10:16:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4c3afba7-2bf6-530b-b47f-ab5c2e8f6d97', '58bdaccf-b8e0-5c9d-8e1d-25b43fdfe062', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'And low voltage still deserves respect. First thing my students do on 24 volt wiring is short R to C and blow the little fuse on the control board. Second thing they do is swear it wasn''t them. Ask me how I know.', false, 14, '2026-09-30T00:49:57+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2f401d11-ac79-51fe-a657-0bcdb92f3fc9', '58bdaccf-b8e0-5c9d-8e1d-25b43fdfe062', 'fd687687-b565-5339-995d-3a85eb69c2f8', 'fwiw controls is a whole trade built on exactly this. a small signal decides what the big equipment does. if that part interests you, look at low voltage and controls. the work is mostly indoors in august too', false, 2, '2026-09-30T01:06:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('4ef4b960-fbf7-55b4-9bf6-1630069707dd', '15a35d13-ce46-5ce0-8883-c803eafa1f49', 'question', 'First fall startups: high-efficiency furnace drain lines, what size and how much pitch?', 'Haven''t started yet, but my new shop let me ride along on fall startups this week, sorry for the basic question. We''re doing fall startups and maintenance, and two furnaces this week had condensate problems. One in a garage in Sicklerville where the line ran dead flat and was half full of slime, one in Blackwood where somebody necked the drain down to 1/2 inch tubing because "it''s just a furnace." That one was shutting off on the pressure switch.

My lead fixed both, but I want the rules in my head. What size should the line be, how much pitch, and does it need a trap if the furnace has one built in? And what about the garage one freezing this winter? Damn, I thought heating was going to be the easy season.', 'hvac', 'Camden County, NJ', 9, '2026-09-15T00:37:04+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('d982338f-5f75-51c3-a2ed-7f6a0655f7da', '4ef4b960-fbf7-55b4-9bf6-1630069707dd', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'First: don''t neck it down. The mechanical code I learned on wants condensate drains no smaller than 3/4 inch and no smaller than the equipment''s connection, all the way to where they end. Check which edition your town enforces and the furnace manual, because the manual can ask for more.

Second: pitch. At least an eighth of an inch per foot, more if you can get it. Flat lines grow exactly the slime you saw.

Third: traps. Most condensing furnaces have their own trap, and the manual will usually tell you not to add a second one in series, because a double trap can air-lock. Read it for that model.

Fourth: the garage. Protect it from freezing the way the manual says, or reroute it inside. Ask me how I know what a frozen line does in January.', true, 14, '2026-09-15T03:47:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a289a5f8-8d2b-5e00-a4c7-0b113c8bd686', '4ef4b960-fbf7-55b4-9bf6-1630069707dd', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Two more from the business side:
- Condensate from a condensing furnace is acidic. If it''s going into a cast iron drain or onto a floor, talk about a neutralizer. Customers like hearing why
- Fall startups are where you clean the trap and the line and pour test it. That prevents the January no-heat call, which costs you more than the visit pays', false, 6, '2026-09-15T23:37:28+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d07c378d-aab5-52d6-8294-c2db7b18c1e2', '4ef4b960-fbf7-55b4-9bf6-1630069707dd', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'plumbing side, we see these tied into floor drains and laundry tubs. is there a rule on where it can go, or is it the same as an AC drain? appreciate it', false, 1, '2026-09-15T23:49:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('be13bfde-8884-54e7-ac22-6504f4dad986', '4ef4b960-fbf7-55b4-9bf6-1630069707dd', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Same idea as the AC drain, where it lands is the inspector''s call, and an air gap if it''s going to a drain... So this one time in Gloucester a whole basement smelled like sewer every fall. Somebody glued the furnace drain straight into the stack, and the furnace''s trap dried out every summer. Fix took ten minutes, finding it took two hours lol.', false, 2, '2026-09-16T01:20:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('70502ac9-8e53-589d-a6ad-56b512d955ba', '4ef4b960-fbf7-55b4-9bf6-1630069707dd', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'drain lines freeze down here too, not just up north. had a walk-in freezer in somers point go down on the coldest night because the drain line ran through an unheated hallway with no heat tape. winter is when you learn', false, 3, '2026-09-16T02:36:03+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('40986189-773b-5d89-98a8-0b2b363c60db', '4ef4b960-fbf7-55b4-9bf6-1630069707dd', '15a35d13-ce46-5ce0-8883-c803eafa1f49', 'This is gold, thank you. Writing "3/4, eighth inch per foot, read the trap section" on the inside of my van door. Lead says that''s how he learned too.', false, 2, '2026-09-16T03:52:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'discussion', 'Midtown tower going all heat pump. How do these do 40 floors up in January?', 'Question for the mechanical guys. The office tower in Midtown I''m on is ripping out the old steam and going all electric heat pumps, because of the city''s emissions law from what the owners say. My side is new feeders up the risers, a lot more amps on every floor than the building was ever built for. Fine. That''s our work.

What I want to know from the mechanical side: rooftop and setback units up there get wind like you wouldn''t believe. On a 10 degree January night, 40 floors up, with wind, do these things actually keep up? Or are we going to be back in two winters adding electric heat and more feeders? Asking because I''m the one who''ll be up there.

Also the 7 train is down again, so I have time to read.', 'hvac', 'Queens, NY', 34, '2026-09-23T02:55:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('70d9734d-dd66-5cfc-9c46-fd7ce323b512', 'bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Not a high-rise guy, but these are the questions I''d ask the engineer:
- What''s the rated capacity at the design low temperature, not at 47 degrees? Cold-climate equipment publishes it
- Is there backup or supplemental heat in the design, and is that load already in your feeder calc?
- Defrost: where does the water go, and does it freeze on the roof?
- Who services them, and can they get to them in February?

If the engineer has answers to all of those, you''re probably fine.', false, 3, '2026-09-23T10:29:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('1c2ee24c-15da-53fd-9a54-7b5cce8248db', 'bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Data center side, we see the same thing: every mechanical change ends up being an electrical change. Get the supplemental heat into the load calc now, not as a change order later.', false, 5, '2026-09-23T23:25:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0a22d551-5962-5f91-b448-025dacb511c0', 'bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'So this one time in AC... the casino I worked at had rooftop heat pump units on the garage that iced up every time the wind came off the ocean in February lol. Wind matters. The engineers who''ve done tall buildings use screens or put the units on mechanical floors instead of out in the open.', false, 3, '2026-09-25T00:10:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('aab0bbf4-c26a-5838-b802-5e108515eda9', 'bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'From the inspection side, and I don''t inspect in the city: the load calculation and the equipment nameplates will tell the story. Whatever the mechanical engineer says about supplemental heat should show up on the electrical drawings. If it doesn''t, ask.', false, 6, '2026-09-26T13:58:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c0562be0-51ec-5218-8958-d5d02a64f410', 'bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', '48b61243-8eaf-5f00-b8aa-9268dc17b5af', 'staten island apprentice here, brother. our shop wired a bunch of heat pumps in houses out here last winter and they kept up fine. in houses though. no idea about 40 floors up', false, 2, '2026-09-26T16:27:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b18cf732-8c2d-56f4-ade3-cef71c7d30b7', 'bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'Student question, possibly off topic: why not geothermal for a building like that? We read about it in class and it seemed like it avoids the cold air problem entirely.', false, 3, '2026-09-26T20:20:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ac947ed2-8caf-5103-879a-654250500685', 'bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Not off topic, brother. You need somewhere to drill, and in Midtown there''s a subway and a lot of foundation under you. Some buildings in the city do it. Not ours.', false, 6, '2026-09-29T13:12:17+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0ecbdfd3-16c5-5363-860b-92f2171493b9', 'bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'following this one. our shop in manahawkin does more heat pumps every month and nobody talks about the electrical side until the panel is full', false, 3, '2026-09-29T13:51:42+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('bf0acd9e-3b4d-57e5-b3a3-ec3118cfd0a5', 'bb5a34f6-9153-56e4-aa98-b39e6e407710', 'ba9dfbf5-d7ef-52a7-bf4e-18535f122bce', 'Appreciate it. Sent the engineer Kash''s list. Answer on defrost was "we''ll look into it." So that''s going great.', false, 4, '2026-09-29T19:53:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '76ffb6b2-6ae2-5434-982e-39a1a1bf28b2', 'question', 'Galloway colonial on propane: cold-climate heat pump or keep the furnace?', 'Sorry if this belongs somewhere else. I''m brand new on the electrical side, career switcher, but this one is my own house. 90s colonial in Galloway, no gas on our street, propane furnace and a central AC that''s on its last legs. The propane bill last winter was ugly. My wife wants to go heat pump since we have to replace the AC anyway.

Everybody I talk to says something different. One guy says heat pumps don''t work when it''s cold. One says get rid of the furnace. One says keep the furnace as backup. And since I''m "the electrical guy" now, everyone asks me if our 150 amp panel can handle it, and I don''t know.

What would you actually do here? Appreciate it.', 'hvac', 'Atlantic County, NJ', 29, '2026-09-09T09:32:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('c50ac097-580b-5d25-820e-9d4b9b4eb63a', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'my old boss said heat pumps quit working under like 30 degrees and then you''re on strip heat and the electric bill kills you. so keep the furnace', false, 3, '2026-09-09T09:58:34+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('046e731b-8c2a-5abe-b7d0-cf95198e0f69', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'That was true of a lot of older units. It isn''t true of current cold-climate equipment:
- Cold-climate heat pumps are rated to put out real heat at 5°F. Look at the published capacity at your design temperature, not the brochure
- Size it from a heat load calculation on your house, not from the old furnace''s number
- Ductwork that was fine for AC can be marginal for heating airflow, so have someone check it
- NJ Clean Energy and utility rebates change often. Look up what''s current before you sign anything', false, 2, '2026-09-09T23:40:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fe399e17-8c8f-5f0c-b84b-af58d063f579', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'I''d do it a little differently from Kash, with respect. In your situation, with a furnace that still works, I''d look hard at dual fuel: a heat pump for most of the season and the propane furnace for the coldest nights. You give up a little efficiency on those nights, you keep a backup if the heat pump goes down in January, and you don''t need electric strips loading your panel.

If the furnace were old too, a properly sized cold-climate heat pump with strips can absolutely carry a house in Atlantic County. Either way, step one is the load calculation. Anybody quoting you without one is guessing.', true, 10, '2026-09-11T01:59:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('05e7bb8a-a910-5030-8286-34f235a6b5a9', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Fair point. With a furnace that has life left, dual fuel is a good answer and I quote it all the time. I was answering the "they don''t work when it''s cold" part.', false, 5, '2026-09-13T17:12:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('9640bcf4-a679-579d-a035-296b9c08d8d1', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'On the panel: 150 amps might be fine. You find out with a load calculation for the whole house, done by an electrician, not by adding up breaker handles. The heat pump nameplate gives you the minimum circuit ampacity and the max breaker size. Strip heat is usually what pushes a panel over.', false, 6, '2026-09-13T23:05:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('334e331d-0c48-55ef-b43a-493c732b6e48', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'egg harbor twp here, same story on half my street, propane and no gas line. the ones who went heat pump with the furnace as backup are happy. and our design temp down here isn''t north jersey''s', false, 9, '2026-09-13T23:23:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('0de07030-8377-538d-8dcf-e78843be59cd', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'So this one time in AC... I did a heat pump in Absecon for a guy who swore it would never keep up, and he called me in February just to ask why the house felt so even lol. It runs longer and lower than a furnace. Tell your wife to expect that.', false, 3, '2026-09-14T03:59:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('83f95018-4ac4-54e1-a865-7e4a10b8fe7e', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Permits for both the mechanical and the electrical side. And if strips are part of it, make sure that circuit is in the load calculation, not added later.', false, 2, '2026-09-14T09:20:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ecbd6635-a098-55a8-9a3d-427dca7ac36c', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '4c3c92ef-9ba5-56b3-90e4-5341be547a4a', '3rd year hvac in monmouth, we put in alot of these now. warn her the air at the register feels cooler than a furnace, like 90 something instead of way hotter. totally normal, but people call about it', false, 1, '2026-09-14T12:32:00+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e66a1cd8-5300-56fc-8601-04254d491493', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '76ffb6b2-6ae2-5434-982e-39a1a1bf28b2', 'This is way more than I expected, appreciate it. So: load calc first, look at dual fuel since the furnace is only 8 years old, panel calc by an actual electrician. Not by me lol.', false, 1, '2026-09-14T14:43:40+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e9b40ec9-2e1e-55b7-91ec-66a51fc4e84e', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '676c05ba-1e88-599b-baa4-e2902fae7bcd', 'ok i stand corrected on the 30 degree thing. old boss was going off old units i guess', false, 1, '2026-09-14T16:15:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8d30911a-3080-5749-879a-42ce566656ef', '176242ae-3898-5650-bad9-d870889392d2', '76ffb6b2-6ae2-5434-982e-39a1a1bf28b2', 'update: had two companies do load calcs. both came back with a cold-climate unit and keeping the furnace as backup. electrician''s calc says the 150 is ok without strips. signing next week', false, 2, '2026-09-15T00:26:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'discussion', 'Cape Cods: ductless heads upstairs or a ducted unit in the kneewall?', 'Settle a fight at my shop... we''re doing a lot of Capes in Gloucester and Camden County this summer, upstairs is 85 by 3pm and there''s no ductwork up there. Half our guys sell a head in every bedroom. The other half want a small ducted air handler in the kneewall or the attic with short runs to each room.

So this one time in AC I put three heads in a Cape and the customer called the next summer saying the kid''s room was freezing and clammy and the other two were fine lol. Oversized head in a tiny room.

What do you guys do and how do you decide? Not looking for a brand war.', 'hvac', 'Camden County, NJ', 7, '2026-08-24T00:50:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('9308efb3-d708-5181-b745-d4207189433f', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'How I decide:
- Small bedrooms: the smallest wall head is often too big for them, so it short-cycles and doesn''t pull moisture out. That favors ducted
- Kneewall space: if there''s room for an air handler with short, sealed runs and a real return, ducted is quieter and cleaner looking
- If the kneewall is cramped, or the customer wants room-by-room control, heads
- Either way, the insulation in those kneewalls is usually terrible, so price the air sealing in

Margins are better on the ducted job if you price the labor honestly.', false, 5, '2026-08-25T01:19:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cf1ce07a-c1c8-57c7-a3fd-b369b4391b78', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Here''s how it plays out for us: the ducted kneewall unit is the better system when there''s room, but it takes a tech who can actually design duct. Heads are more forgiving for a crew that''s still learning. I sell the system my people can install well.', false, 3, '2026-08-25T02:17:08+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f9bf77ae-7a24-5d10-9d20-3d5c8d47b99c', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'we did a cape in clifton with one ducted unit in the attic over the dormer and it was so quiet the customer thought it was off. getting up there in july was brutal though', false, 2, '2026-08-28T11:02:39+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('dad8655b-19a2-55fc-ab3e-a99dc12988fc', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '889c860e-644c-5ba0-8dcd-6de744328e67', 'attic air handler in a cape in july, enjoy. whatever you pick, put a pan and a float switch under it. i''ve seen what a kneewall full of water does to a ceiling', false, 3, '2026-08-28T12:33:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('383dfb0f-d7d7-5791-b290-860e9d72fda9', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '7a6f6003-76c1-5962-a01c-a6cddfc8f26b', 'Honestly on the raised houses at the shore after Sandy we did a lot of heads, because there was nowhere to put anything. Not Capes, but the same problem: no space, no ducts.', false, 5, '2026-08-28T13:34:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('2c8b52ce-99df-5b15-958a-87b7e2b13ef6', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '76ffb6b2-6ae2-5434-982e-39a1a1bf28b2', 'Electrical side question, sorry if dumb: does one ducted unit mean one circuit instead of three? That''s a lot less work on our end.', false, 3, '2026-08-28T13:56:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('057b4417-7e19-5746-943d-902aeffeea25', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Depends on the setup. A multi-zone outdoor unit usually powers its heads through the interconnect, so that''s one circuit to the outdoor unit. Three separate single-zone systems are three circuits. Follow the install manual either way.', false, 3, '2026-08-30T18:08:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d8b846e4-0f3e-5922-b8b9-db5546fe7b09', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '7faa1a09-27de-5125-aea4-eb8d826c963b', 'customer question i get a lot in secaucus: do the heads look bad? and can you hide the linesets on the outside of a cape without it looking like spaghetti?', false, 2, '2026-08-30T23:11:02+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fdf95284-452e-5401-8c2c-43ba2011305e', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Lol the spaghetti question... lineset covers, run them on the back of the house, and talk about it before the install, not after. Some people hate the look of a head no matter what. Those are your ducted customers.', false, 8, '2026-08-31T03:07:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e9e5bfd6-a638-5f14-ac8c-466e2a0845f1', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', 'first summer in hvac, we did 6 capes in union county, all heads. didn''t know ducted in a kneewall was even an option. learning', false, 2, '2026-08-31T03:28:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('f88e7665-2276-5203-9275-1a14954a4406', 'f10784c2-d227-5839-b34c-dd911ead733f', 'dfa0289e-7f8a-53dc-8191-16f6fb52934f', 'Good thread, I''m stealing it for class. What students should take away is that you decide from the house: the room sizes, the space, the insulation, the customer. Not from whatever your shop usually sells.', false, 5, '2026-08-31T03:44:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d4250407-95cd-534e-98e5-d6e58ed75660', 'bca8fe2b-edd9-5242-b82f-a38ae629144b', 'question', 'Parents'' Cape is getting mini-splits. What''s the electrician''s part?', 'my parents'' cape in hamilton is getting a 3-zone mini-split next month and the hvac company said "you''ll need an electrician for the power." my dad looked at me because I''m in the electrical program at vo-tech, which, no, I''m a student. but I want to understand what the electrician is actually going to do so I can watch and not be useless. like how do they know what size breaker, what''s the box on the wall outside for, and does it need a GFCI? our book says something about outdoor GFCI but my teacher said it''s complicated', 'electrical', 'Mercer County, NJ', 5, '2026-08-19T23:51:22+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('017e8933-eb84-553c-9828-ce94538a310b', 'd4250407-95cd-534e-98e5-d6e58ed75660', '7e21e2e2-cb66-59f4-81f1-b1897975777a', 'Your teacher''s right that it''s complicated. Here''s the outline. Wire and breaker size come from the outdoor unit''s nameplate: the minimum circuit ampacity sets the wire, the maximum overcurrent protection sets the largest breaker allowed. The box outside is the disconnect, which the code wants within sight of the unit so a tech can kill it while working on it.

The GFCI part: a recent code edition expanded GFCI requirements for outdoor outlets in a way that caught HVAC equipment, a lot of inverter units nuisance tripped, and there were changes and local amendments afterward. Check which code edition is in effect for your parents'' permit. That''s a question for the inspector, not the internet.', false, 6, '2026-08-20T09:18:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('a2a19ae8-1a7d-55c8-93f8-d06329161adf', 'd4250407-95cd-534e-98e5-d6e58ed75660', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'From the HVAC side, also watch the interconnect between the outdoor unit and the heads. Most multi-zone units power the heads from the outdoor unit through that cable, and the manual specifies the wire. Nobody should be using leftover thermostat wire for it.', false, 11, '2026-08-21T00:35:19+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('72f2a929-f340-5a75-a514-689bac4118fe', 'd4250407-95cd-534e-98e5-d6e58ed75660', '64503839-3306-52e3-b438-2a84e1d5f38d', 'Watch where the condensate from each head goes too. Not electrical, but my uncle got called to a Cape where a head was draining into the wall cavity lol', false, 1, '2026-08-21T13:07:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('91bed52b-3dc9-5048-b7df-51bb7c678e1c', 'd4250407-95cd-534e-98e5-d6e58ed75660', '941687d4-f84d-584c-8d35-d12345914cae', 'we just did 3 of these in elizabeth. electrician was there like 2 hours total, disconnect, whip, breaker, done. we ran the interconnect ourselves', false, 1, '2026-08-21T17:22:31+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('aefbdb49-d821-5cca-a432-92320bd62790', 'a500e8c1-fe10-5f2f-a33e-6f510dd05201', 'question', 'One multi-zone outdoor unit or separate single-zone systems for my Cape?', 'This is for my own house, not a job. Cape in Middletown, upstairs has two bedrooms and a small bath, downstairs has the original oil-fired baseboard and window units. We''re finally doing mini-splits before next summer.

I have two quotes. One is a single multi-zone outdoor unit with three heads. The other is three separate single-zone systems, one for each bedroom plus one for the living room, so three outdoor units. The second is more money and more equipment on the side of the house.

The salesman on the first one says multi-zone is "the same thing, just one box." I''m a plumber, so I get suspicious when someone says that. What are the actual tradeoffs? Thanks in advance.', 'hvac', 'Monmouth County, NJ', 13, '2026-09-14T16:50:55+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('59c59d2e-851b-5dde-b9fe-6cd3c7d50e70', 'aefbdb49-d821-5cca-a432-92320bd62790', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'It''s not the same thing:
- One multi-zone outdoor unit fails, every room is down. Separate systems fail one at a time
- Multi-zone units often run less efficiently when only one small head is calling, which in a bedroom is most of the night
- Single-zone units usually have better low-temperature heating ratings, if you care about heat
- Multi-zone is fewer boxes outside and one circuit, which some houses need

For three rooms I lean singles if the budget and the wall space allow. For five rooms in a small house, multi-zone starts making more sense.', false, 3, '2026-09-14T22:42:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7dcca09d-79a3-55fd-8de8-c420e04bb3e7', 'aefbdb49-d821-5cca-a432-92320bd62790', '98e78eb6-decf-5515-a59c-8be11a84fa4d', 'Agree with Kash mostly... the one thing I''d add is ask both companies for the head sizes, room by room. Small bedroom with a big head is the callback I see the most lol', false, 3, '2026-09-15T00:10:52+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('332f7e93-464c-5b69-abf9-39a563f89509', 'aefbdb49-d821-5cca-a432-92320bd62790', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Sorry if this is off topic, but since the downstairs is oil baseboard, would they replace that too, or do people keep the boiler for heat?', false, 4, '2026-09-23T23:06:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('10c8992f-4b2f-588e-b97d-cb5b97b1878b', 'aefbdb49-d821-5cca-a432-92320bd62790', 'a500e8c1-fe10-5f2f-a33e-6f510dd05201', 'We''re keeping the boiler for now. Getting the upstairs comfortable is the goal this year, heat can be the next project.', false, 1, '2026-09-24T00:37:41+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6e9e7d1d-8a81-529f-ac1b-28425acce633', 'aefbdb49-d821-5cca-a432-92320bd62790', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'plumbing in deptford. my parents went multi-zone and the outdoor unit died last july, whole house hot for a week waiting on a part. appreciate the singles point', false, 1, '2026-09-24T03:08:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('030e304b-c8a1-5332-9410-64d44a008b7f', 'aefbdb49-d821-5cca-a432-92320bd62790', 'ac073e3f-468a-564a-9831-abbcb2c2a679', 'Electrical side... three singles is three circuits and three disconnects... ask who''s doing the electric and whether it''s in the price', false, 2, '2026-09-24T10:02:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('36b435b1-82fd-5b2d-9669-521aa1791f0c', 'aefbdb49-d821-5cca-a432-92320bd62790', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'UA 24 1st year. Asking for the same reason, my parents have a Cape in Fair Lawn. Following.', false, 1, '2026-09-24T11:54:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b792ddf5-2c0b-519a-bea8-a34ec1e27bb2', 'aefbdb49-d821-5cca-a432-92320bd62790', 'a500e8c1-fe10-5f2f-a33e-6f510dd05201', 'update: asked both for head sizes. The multi-zone quote had a head in the small bedroom about twice what the other company sized. Going with the singles.', false, 1, '2026-09-24T12:06:49+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('acb1f71c-189a-59fe-9494-18a4d7b97213', '9d863d1d-0f6f-5b8c-921d-d473f8721247', 'question', 'what actually happens in an oil to gas conversion, start to finish', 'career switcher, night class, ewing. my neighbor is converting from oil and asked me what''s involved since i''m "in plumbing now" lol. i have no idea and ziggy''s on a job all week so asking here. who does what, how long does it take, and what happens to the tank in the basement? just want the big picture so i don''t say something dumb to him', 'plumbing', 'Mercer County, NJ', 25, '2026-09-18T00:58:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('0649bd63-df66-57ba-aa22-afd4521fdd8c', 'acb1f71c-189a-59fe-9494-18a4d7b97213', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Big picture, roughly in order:
- Utility first: is gas available on the street, and how long for a service and a meter. That timeline drives everything
- Equipment: a new gas boiler or furnace is the usual answer. Converting the old oil boiler with a gas burner is possible but less common
- Venting: a liner for the chimney, or a direct-vent unit out the side wall
- Gas piping sized from the meter to everything that will burn gas
- Permits and inspections before the utility turns it on
- The oil tank: removed or properly abandoned, depending on the town and where it is

A licensed contractor for all of it. Your neighbor''s job is to pick someone good, not to figure it out.', false, 4, '2026-09-18T03:11:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d2e4a44e-53c9-5375-95e9-ffd130fbdcd0', 'acb1f71c-189a-59fe-9494-18a4d7b97213', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Kash covered it. One thing for you, kid: next time the neighbor asks, the right answer is "call two licensed shops and ask them about the chimney and the tank." Knowing what to ask is half of it. That''s the job.', false, 3, '2026-09-22T10:09:58+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('57605d31-0a70-5a4b-a259-90abdd0ff9f9', 'acb1f71c-189a-59fe-9494-18a4d7b97213', '0fb22325-72e4-5c91-9bea-1a069ad5e037', 'UA 24 here, 1st year. We did two of these in Fair Lawn this summer. The tank part took longer than the boiler both times. Idk why but every time.', false, 2, '2026-09-22T13:39:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('7a7b79c2-0486-5e0a-b82b-f7fb83780cf2', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'question', 'Three conversion quotes, three different answers on the chimney', 'Different kind of question from me. We''re finally converting our own house in Piscataway from oil to gas: split-level, oil boiler with baseboard, hot water off a tankless coil in the boiler. Got three quotes and they disagree on the chimney.

Quote 1: new gas boiler and a new gas water heater, both into the chimney with a new liner.
Quote 2: high-efficiency boiler vented out the side wall in plastic, new water heater into the existing chimney, no liner.
Quote 3: high-efficiency boiler out the side wall, a separate sidewall-vented water heater, chimney not used at all.

Quote 2 is cheapest. Quote 1''s guy says Quote 2 is going to cause problems. Who''s right, and why does the chimney matter so much? Appreciate it. Joy told me to get more than one quote, so here we are. Still doing ride-alongs too, so this is half for the house and half for me.', 'plumbing', 'Middlesex County, NJ', 6, '2026-09-09T22:46:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('40bb6eb5-998b-5b4f-903c-50ab0a3a50c6', '7a7b79c2-0486-5e0a-b82b-f7fb83780cf2', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Quote 1''s guy is pointing at a real problem, kid. That old chimney was sized for an oil boiler sending a lot of hot exhaust up it. Take the boiler out, and a gas water heater alone in that big flue is what we call an orphaned water heater. Not enough heat to draft right, so the flue gas cools and condenses, and you get weak draft, moisture eating the masonry, and possibly exhaust spilling into the basement.

That''s why conversions get a liner sized for whatever''s left in the chimney, or take the chimney out of the picture like Quote 3. Quote 2 could be fine if they actually checked that chimney, so ask them exactly how. If the answer is "it''ll be fine," that''s a no.

And CO detectors on every floor, whoever you pick.', true, 5, '2026-09-10T02:10:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('05810861-057d-5f9e-b521-90719e4c5c9b', '7a7b79c2-0486-5e0a-b82b-f7fb83780cf2', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'What I''d ask all three:
- Did you do a heat loss, or are you matching the old boiler''s size? Old oil boilers are usually oversized
- Who removes or abandons the oil tank, and is it in the price?
- Who handles the gas service with the utility?
- What''s the warranty on the installation, not just the equipment?', false, 3, '2026-09-10T02:40:13+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6af0b609-9c31-501f-83c0-ca9964f5360b', '7a7b79c2-0486-5e0a-b82b-f7fb83780cf2', '6b3a1896-cd39-5ae1-8351-8817f445313d', 'my foreman did one of these in lawrence where the water heater got left orphaned in the chimney. went back in november because the co alarm kept going off lol. relined it', false, 0, '2026-09-10T14:46:38+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('fc66d1b1-c7e4-55ac-9609-bff550015c5f', '7a7b79c2-0486-5e0a-b82b-f7fb83780cf2', '4608a194-8038-5aed-92b1-9105192f876b', 'Sorry, newer guy question. Is the side wall vent the white plastic pipe sticking out of the side of houses? I always wondered what those were.', false, 2, '2026-09-10T17:41:51+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7b4c9f78-815d-5d47-9658-20a2176d02a1', '7a7b79c2-0486-5e0a-b82b-f7fb83780cf2', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'Thanks Ziggy, this is exactly what I needed. Going to ask Quote 2 how they checked the chimney.

edit: Quote 2 said they''d "see when they get there." Going with Quote 3.', false, 1, '2026-09-10T21:11:47+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e13e553c-fdd4-5899-8a44-76db5573115b', '7a7b79c2-0486-5e0a-b82b-f7fb83780cf2', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'Good call. "We''ll see when we get there" on venting is the answer that gets people hurt. And benplumb, yes, usually PVC or a similar plastic on high-efficiency equipment, whatever the manufacturer specifies.', false, 3, '2026-09-11T00:18:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'question', 'Customer wants the old oil tank left in the basement after the gas conversion', 'Service tech, Union City. Finishing a conversion next week in a two-family in Weehawken. Customer wants the 275 gallon oil tank in the basement just left there, empty, "for later." Then he tells me the home inspector on another house he''s buying found a buried tank in the yard during the tank sweep, and the seller says "it was abandoned years ago."

Boss is out till Monday and I''m bad at talking to customers lol. What do I tell him on both? I know we don''t do tank work, I just don''t want to sound like an idiot.', 'plumbing', 'Hudson County, NJ', 7, '2026-09-25T01:47:10+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('edbc04c7-f92d-5bb5-8cdf-819e4a3dc6a1', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Basement tank first. Empty is never empty, kid. There''s always sludge and some oil in the bottom. Leave it and it leaks someday, or the next buyer''s inspector flags it. On most of our conversions the tank comes out: pumped, cleaned, cut up, hauled. Your town may want a permit for the removal. Tell him your boss will price it, and don''t let him keep it "for later."', false, 8, '2026-09-26T15:39:54+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('6988bf4f-a836-534f-9946-a1fa2acc75db', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'ed01b27e-7f0b-586c-bcb9-397a7d11f3fe', 'our boss in woodbridge puts the tank removal right in the conversion quote so the customer can''t skip it. saves you this exact conversation. appreciate the thread', false, 1, '2026-09-26T16:39:15+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('cd35fe9a-38ba-5fa6-9f85-46416989fc31', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'On the buried tank, from my experience in NJ:
- Ask the seller for paperwork. "Abandoned" without a permit and closure paperwork from the town means very little
- If there''s any sign of a leak, it becomes a cleanup, and in NJ that brings in DEP rules and certified contractors
- His attorney and insurance company should hear about it before closing, not after
- None of this is yours to sort out. Send him to his attorney and a tank company', false, 7, '2026-09-26T18:41:16+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c67ecf8e-9c22-50a3-95b4-7c92f5e4aced', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'And on the buried one, I''d want it pulled and the soil tested before I bought that house.', false, 7, '2026-09-26T23:43:21+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('d8ca09dd-ce74-51e7-8105-23daa433f4fe', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'Respectfully, Ziggy, pulling isn''t always the answer on buried tanks. Some are under a porch, an addition or a driveway, and abandonment in place, done properly with a permit and soil sampling, is what gets done. The paperwork is the thing. Depends on the town.', false, 4, '2026-09-27T00:08:26+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b8fbae6d-3035-5f4b-b8f8-cb8df0730a8f', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'Fair, Rui. If it can''t come out, it''s done on paper. My point is "abandoned years ago" with no paper isn''t abandoned.', false, 4, '2026-09-27T01:22:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('929b6f27-293d-5470-8aa6-b6ba960fb1b7', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question? You asked two. Basement: it should come out, your boss prices it. Yard: not your job, send him to a lawyer and a tank outfit. Two sentences, then stop talking.', false, 9, '2026-09-27T03:16:45+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('7a43a7ad-ed64-5ed6-ade9-96773ee681e9', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', '> Two sentences, then stop talking.

lol that''s the part i need', false, 1, '2026-09-27T10:01:32+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('967c3436-c070-5e7b-925f-17fa5fcbe418', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'c588b587-bf00-57ce-81f7-e7c7089fe77a', 'In the city it''s different in the details. Some older buildings still have oil tanks in the cellar or a vault, and the rules and who you call are city ones. Same principle though. Nobody believes "empty" and nobody believes "abandoned" without paperwork.', false, 3, '2026-09-28T00:08:53+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('103fd651-60ed-5037-8243-7b48ea1db6b4', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', '3823cb41-9c6e-5a35-b2fe-2195a85f097d', 'dumb question, why is a buried tank such a big deal if it''s just sitting there? like if it''s not leaking what''s the problem? and who even checks', false, 1, '2026-09-28T01:11:46+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('52d32606-3cbb-5838-9724-28dbeb716bd7', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Because old steel in wet soil eventually leaks, and nobody knows when. When it does, the cleanup can get very expensive, and it can land on the homeowner. That''s why buyers here do tank sweeps, and why sellers get nervous about them.', false, 6, '2026-09-28T02:22:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('5811db1e-7a6f-512f-b2a3-f22737145fd2', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', '36257d38-c53a-5d62-8935-a80bec20e7a6', 'had one in deptford where the customer''s homeowners insurance didn''t cover the leak. paid out of pocket. appreciate this thread', false, 3, '2026-09-28T03:50:06+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8cbfcff5-81c7-5efa-b99e-b9456d72cfb8', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', '86afdff7-a622-5314-99e0-81558cc06b11', 'Apologies if this is basic. In Morris County a lot of houses still have oil. Is tank removal something HVAC companies do, or is it always a separate company? Thanks in advance.', false, 2, '2026-09-28T10:13:01+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('808ddaa0-459b-57b8-b0d2-af5492482b48', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', '688739f6-9783-5e53-a5b2-f60373e11c3f', 'Mostly separate. On our commercial jobs it''s always a sub with its own insurance for that work. Here''s what I look for in that sub: their permits and paperwork, every time.', false, 5, '2026-09-28T18:59:37+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('ffea2feb-2961-54fd-925a-86d54df12aec', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'd564dd78-7316-5c47-b918-c6f2fba61791', 'Electrical side note: the oil burner circuit and its emergency switch should be removed or properly reused during the conversion. I''ve seen dead burner switches left at the top of the stairs for decades confusing everybody. Label it or remove it.', false, 8, '2026-09-28T23:18:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('e57d6076-2b33-5504-9f2d-2f74d2a5ede9', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'd680c878-f79d-58ae-9875-7e9bdf0efa31', 'brother we pulled an "empty" one out of a basement in brick last month, bottom had a few inches of sludge. smelled for days. who even takes that stuff?', false, 1, '2026-09-29T02:57:48+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('922e0bc0-74cc-55a9-9527-41546cc3519c', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', '70b2faae-ab2e-52c1-bf66-ddf5234d3a4a', 'talked to him today. basement tank is coming out, boss is pricing it. told him the yard one is a lawyer question. he actually listened lol. thier inspector already told them the same thing so that helped', false, 1, '2026-09-29T09:25:35+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('4c81ceb4-2279-5742-b12d-fb210d553704', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'c550f38e-1f91-59eb-8c3f-2566dca5af92', 'That''s how you do it. My father used to say the customer remembers how you said it more than what you said.', false, 6, '2026-09-29T23:39:23+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('07726cf0-36a3-583f-8106-428e0e0f9e57', '00b0616c-cbc5-53d9-88c0-568f2d569336', 'b6ca1269-6db2-5f6b-8338-7d2000b90bb5', 'We''re in the middle of our own conversion and tank removal was in all three quotes. Reading this, I''m glad it was.', false, 1, '2026-09-29T23:44:36+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('d1c03299-46bd-5186-8847-db2be043779b', 'fb3a0b82-da77-5dd7-9a89-e099391b6ce7', 'question', 'Sizing gas pipe for a conversion: why does everyone talk about the longest run?', '2 years in, Bloomfield. We''re doing a bunch of oil to gas conversions this fall and I''m finally being let near the gas piping, carrying and cutting at least. My journeyman sized the pipe for a house with a boiler, a water heater and a range and kept saying "the longest run" and "total BTU." Why the longest run and not each run on its own? And why does it matter if the pipe''s a little small, the gas still gets there right?

Not planning on doing any of this myself. I just want to understand it before somebody quizzes me on the job.', 'plumbing', 'Essex County, NJ', 6, '2026-09-25T00:25:11+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into replies (id, post_id, author_id, body, is_accepted, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values
  ('e00aba54-5357-546c-aa55-3fbc1ae61224', 'd1c03299-46bd-5186-8847-db2be043779b', 'f84fe0e8-873f-58b7-9893-f236cf66d827', 'What''s your actual question? Two, I count.

Why it matters: undersized pipe means not enough gas reaches the appliance when everything runs at once. The burner runs starved, burns badly, and can make carbon monoxide. "Gets there" isn''t enough. It has to get there at the right pressure.

Why the longest run: the common method in the code tables sizes every section using the total length from the meter to the farthest appliance, and the BTU load that section carries. It''s conservative on purpose. Your journeyman reads the table for that gas pressure and pipe material.

He does the sizing, the master signs for it, the inspector checks it, and it gets tested before the utility turns anything on.', true, 9, '2026-09-27T14:26:30+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('455edb26-1adf-5a74-9089-cfa00a64bbf0', 'd1c03299-46bd-5186-8847-db2be043779b', 'dfb0e5bf-fb0b-52d1-b931-e53488254b99', 'And the load is the input rating off each appliance''s nameplate, not a guess. Add them up and think about what they might add later, a dryer, a generator. Cheaper to run it right once, kid.', false, 5, '2026-09-28T01:00:33+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('406fafd8-cfbc-583f-8eea-218be372fedb', 'd1c03299-46bd-5186-8847-db2be043779b', '3072c22d-47f7-516e-977e-a20a20174e03', 'use the table for your pressure and material. test it. get it inspected. don''t light anything that wasn''t tested.', false, 4, '2026-09-28T01:25:24+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('b98db5a2-81c2-5e82-b543-9fb8a0b09796', 'd1c03299-46bd-5186-8847-db2be043779b', '33e17845-6ab1-5cde-a00b-47a97ff6cc5c', 'brother hvac helper in paterson here. we see undersized gas on furnace calls all the time, burner looks lazy and yellow. now i know why', false, 6, '2026-09-28T03:41:09+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('8821e34d-95ed-5c45-bb39-83f6bf14b01a', 'd1c03299-46bd-5186-8847-db2be043779b', 'fe4d315d-7d19-5d5d-82ae-1887fac966ee', 'electrical guy here but the yellow flexible gas pipe needs to get bonded right? our shop got called about that on a conversion lol', false, 2, '2026-09-28T10:04:14+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('c568b8a9-2311-5a4e-938b-d505fbb53b72', 'd1c03299-46bd-5186-8847-db2be043779b', '6a71c949-16d2-52fe-9c8c-0a623c8c3e66', 'Yes. CSST comes with its own bonding instructions, the code has a say too, and it matters mostly because of lightning. It gets bonded the way the manufacturer and your local code say. Nobody should be making that one up on site.', false, 7, '2026-09-28T10:07:12+00:00', 'fm-2026-10'),
  ('02ba38dd-0856-5023-abc6-931bb4cedd91', 'd1c03299-46bd-5186-8847-db2be043779b', 'f9633309-87d0-527e-a554-00484a219079', 'Our shop teacher mentioned bonding that yellow gas tubing last week. Didn''t understand why until this thread.', false, 1, '2026-09-28T11:26:05+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
insert into posts (id, author_id, type, title, body, trade, region, helpful_count, created_at, seed_batch_id) values ('914a77a7-b2b7-5ba8-83ee-a42f2e3346a8', '4c3416a3-87d3-52fd-a7e0-49bb8a5fef4c', 'question', 'What is the red switch plate at the top of my basement stairs for?', 'Vo-tech student, electrical, Passaic County class of ''27. This is about my grandparents'' house in Wayne, which I''ve been looking at much more carefully since I started the program. At the top of the basement stairs there''s a switch with a red plate that says something like "burner emergency." My grandfather says it''s for the oil burner. They converted to gas a few years ago and the boiler is new.

Does that switch still do anything now? Is it supposed to stay with a gas boiler, and if so, why is it at the top of the stairs and not next to the boiler? I''m only asking out of curiosity, I''m not planning to touch it.', 'hvac', 'Passaic County, NJ', 31, '2026-10-05T01:21:07+00:00', 'fm-2026-10');
